const e={P2C00:["Fuel Pressure Regulator C Performance","P2C00 reports that a third fuel pressure regulator, labelled C, cannot hold the pressure the engine module asks for, although its circuit tests fine. Letters beyond A and B are only needed on fuel systems with several pressure control elements, for example engines with two high-pressure pumps or separate control of low and high pressure. No manufacturer documents P2C00 publicly;",["Regulator C or the pump it controls worn or sticking","Insufficient feed pressure to the controlled pump","Fuel pressure sensor drifting, so the regulator appears off target"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power at high load","Extended cranking"],3,3,["P2C01","P233A","P2293","P0089"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C01:["Fuel Pressure Regulator D Performance","GM uses P2C01 in its 2023 and 2024 summary tables 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 for an engine control module that drives two fuel quantity control valves on the high-pressure side: P0089 covers the first, P2C01 the second, labelled regulator D. The ECM compares the filtered output of the high-pressure controller with fixed bounds.",["Second high-pressure pump or its quantity control valve worn or sticking","Low tank level or weak low-pressure supply","Rail pressure sensor reading implausibly"],["Check engine light on after two trips","Reduced power or stumbling at full load","Hard or slow starting"],3,3,["P2C02","P2C00","P0089","P0087","P0088"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ D — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C02:["Fuel Pressure Regulator D Control Circuit/Open","P2C02 is the open-circuit check on the control line of fuel pressure regulator D. In GM's tables 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 this is the second fuel quantity control valve of the high-pressure system, the twin of the valve watched by P0090. While the driver is switched off, the ECM expects a defined voltage on the line;",["Broken wire or loose terminal in the valve circuit","Corroded or unplugged connector at the high-pressure pump","Open coil in the quantity control valve"],["Check engine light on","Power reduction because one pump is no longer controlled","Possible rail pressure fault codes alongside"],2,3,["P2C03","P2C04","P2C01","P0090"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ D — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2C03:["Fuel Pressure Regulator D Control Circuit Low","P2C03 is set when the switched low side of the regulator D control circuit has contact with ground. GM documents it in 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 for the second fuel quantity control valve, where it mirrors P0091 of the first valve. With the driver off, a healthy circuit shows a voltage on this line; if it is pulled low, the ECM concludes that less than about 0.5 ohm separates the pin from ground.",["Low-side wire chafed through to ground","Damaged or wet valve connector","Internal short in the quantity control valve"],["Check engine light on","Reduced engine power","Rough running at high load"],2,3,["P2C02","P2C04","P0091","P233B"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2C04:["Fuel Pressure Regulator D Control Circuit High","P2C04 covers the opposite electrical fault to P2C03: the switched ground end of the regulator D circuit is connected to battery voltage. In GM's 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 tables the circuit belongs to the second fuel quantity control valve, counterpart of P0092 on the first.",["Low-side wire shorted to a supply voltage","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the valve connector","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power, possibly limp mode","Engine may hesitate under load"],2,3,["P2C02","P2C03","P0092","P233C"],"וסת לחץ דלק‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2C05:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Bank 1","Engines with switchable cam lobes use small solenoid actuators that push a pin into a groove of a sliding cam sleeve; a feedback signal confirms that the pin has moved. P2C05 is the general circuit fault for feedback A on the intake camshaft (camshaft A) of bank 1.",["Engine harness chafed, sometimes with blown fuses (GM L3B bulletins)","Loose or corroded connector at the profile actuator","Open circuit inside the actuator or its feedback element"],["Check engine light on immediately","Cam lift switching and cylinder deactivation unavailable, slightly reduced power or economy","With harness damage, many other codes and possibly no start"],2,3,["P2C06","P2C07","P2C08","P2C09","P2B33"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P2C06:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor A Range/Performance Bank 1","P2C06 deals with a feedback signal that is electrically intact but makes no sense. On GM's 2.7 L L3B, the ECM follows each shift of the intake profile actuator A on bank 1 through three Hall feedback states: extending once the reading falls below 55, extended below 45 and retracted, back at home, above 68.",["Actuator pin sticking or slow because of wear or dirty oil","Worn groove or sliding sleeve on the intake camshaft","Hall feedback element in the actuator giving wrong values"],["Check engine light on immediately","Lift switching disabled, engine stays on one cam profile","Possible ticking noise from the cylinder head"],2,3,["P2C05","P2C07","P2C08","P2C0A","P2B40"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2C07:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Low Bank 1","On GM's 2.7 L turbo four L3B (Silverado and Sierra 1500 from 2019) each of the four intake sliding-cam actuators reports its pin travel through a Hall element; GM calls the first one intake Hall sensor 1, which is position sensor A in J2012 terms. P2C07 means this circuit is pulled to ground.",["Engine harness chafed through to ground, e.g. over the camshaft carrier cover","Internal short to ground in the profile actuator or its Hall element","Oil or water in the actuator connector bridging to ground"],["Check engine light on from the first drive","Engine stays on one lift profile, no cylinder deactivation, slightly higher consumption","With harness damage, possibly blown fuses and many further codes"],2,3,["P2C05","P2C06","P2C08","P2C0B","P2C14"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C08:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit High Bank 1","P2C08 flags a short to voltage on position sensor A, the Hall feedback of the first intake profile actuator on bank 1. GM's L3B 2.7 L four runs this check the other way round from the ground test: the output stage is switched off, and if the line still shows 0.5 ohm or less towards controller power, 4 of 5 such readings above 11 V store a Type A code with immediate MIL (19OBDG03D, again 25OBDG03B).",["Chafed engine harness touching a live circuit (GM bulletins PIT5677, 21-NA-149)","Internal short to supply inside the actuator or its feedback element","Faulty output stage in the ECM"],["MIL lit immediately","No valve lift change and no cylinder deactivation","After harness damage also rough running, reduced power or no start"],2,3,["P2C05","P2C07","P2C0C","P2C10","P2C15"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C09:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Bank 1","Position sensor B belongs to the second of the four intake actuators that slide the cam sleeves on GM's L3B; GM's tables call it intake Hall sensor 2. The sensors are thus one per actuator, not one per lift step: sensors A to C get J2012 codes, while GM puts the fourth (sensor D) under its own codes P30B0 to P30B3. P2C09 is the open-circuit test for sensor B.",["Loose, unplugged or corroded connector on actuator 2","Wire broken by harness chafing on the camshaft carrier (GM L3B bulletins)","Open circuit inside the actuator or its Hall element"],["Check engine light on in the first trip","Lift switching and cylinder deactivation locked out","Usually no noticeable change in driving apart from fuel use"],2,3,["P2C05","P2C0A","P2C0B","P2C0C","P2C0D","P2C16"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P2C0A:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor B Range/Performance Bank 1","Here the wiring of position sensor B is intact, but its report does not match what the second intake actuator on bank 1 was told to do. On the L3B, GM follows every shift through three Hall readings: below 55 while the pin is moving out, below 45 once fully out, and above 68 when it is back home.",["Pin of actuator 2 sticking or slow (wear, sludge, wrong oil)","Worn shift groove or detent on the intake cam sleeve","Hall element in the actuator reporting implausible levels"],["MIL on at once","Engine kept on a fixed cam profile, no cylinder deactivation","Possible ticking from the camshaft carrier or slightly uneven idle"],2,3,["P2C06","P2C09","P2C0E","P2C17"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2C0B:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Low Bank 1","P2C0B reports that the circuit of position sensor B, the Hall feedback of the second intake actuator on bank 1, is shorted to ground. GM's L3B 2.7 L uses it with a resistance test while the output is on: at 0.5 ohm or less from signal to ground, 4 of 5 failed samples with supply over 11 V store a Type A code and the MIL comes on immediately (19OBDG03D, 25OBDG03B).",["Insulation of the sensor B line worn through against engine metal","Shorted actuator 2 or its integrated Hall element","Moisture or oil in the connector"],["Check engine light on straight away","Valve lift no longer changes, fuel use may rise"],2,3,["P2C07","P2C09","P2C0A","P2C0C","P2C0F","P2C18"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C0C:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit High Bank 1","A short from the sensor B line to a voltage source triggers P2C0C. The sensor is the Hall feedback built into the second intake profile actuator on bank 1. For the L3B four in 2019 and later Silverado and Sierra 1500 trucks, GM tests with the output stage off;",["Chafed harness bringing the line against a powered wire (GM PIT5677, 21-NA-149)","Internal short to supply in actuator 2","ECM output stage defective"],["MIL on in the first trip","Cam profile switching and cylinder deactivation unavailable","With harness damage, further codes, rough running or no start"],2,3,["P2C08","P2C09","P2C0B","P2C10","P2C19"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C0D:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor C Circuit Bank 1","Position sensor C is the third of the Hall feedback elements on the intake side of bank 1; on GM's L3B it sits in intake actuator 3 and is named intake Hall sensor 3. That engine has four intake and two exhaust profile actuators, so a fourth intake feedback exists beyond the J2012 letters and GM handles it with P30B0 to P30B3.",["Harness rubbed through over the camshaft carrier, wire broken (GM L3B bulletins)","Connector on actuator 3 loose, damaged or corroded","Open circuit inside actuator 3 or its Hall element"],["Check engine light on in the first trip","No lift switching, no cylinder deactivation","Further codes, reduced power or no start if the harness is damaged"],2,3,["P2C05","P2C09","P2C0E","P2C0F","P2C10"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P2C0E:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor C Range/Performance Bank 1","P2C0E is the plausibility test for the feedback of the third intake actuator on bank 1. On the L3B, the ECM classifies each shift by the Hall signal of that actuator: extending when it drops below 55, fully extended under 45, retracted when it rises above 68 again. The code is set when a commanded shift does not produce this pattern, or when activity appears without any command.",["Pin of actuator 3 sticking or responding late","Damaged groove or detent on the cam sleeve served by actuator 3","Old or wrong-grade oil slowing the pin"],["MIL comes on immediately","Lift switching suspended, engine runs on one profile","Occasional ticking or uneven running if a sleeve sits halfway"],2,3,["P2C06","P2C0A","P2C0D","P2C0F","P2C10"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2C0F:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor C Circuit Low Bank 1","With P2C0F the ECM sees the position sensor C circuit of bank 1, the Hall feedback in the third intake actuator, connected to ground. In GM's L3B tables the test runs while the output is commanded on and looks for a signal-to-ground resistance not above 0.5 ohm; after 4 failures in 5 samples at more than 11 V the code is stored as Type A and the MIL lights at once (19OBDG03D;",["Sensor C line pinched or chafed against ground","Internal ground short in actuator 3","Contaminated or damaged connector pins"],["Check engine light comes on during the first drive","Engine no longer switches cam profile or deactivates cylinders"],2,3,["P2C07","P2C0B","P2C0D","P2C0E","P2C10"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C10:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor C Circuit High Bank 1","P2C10 completes the sensor C group for the bank 1 intake camshaft: the feedback line of the third profile actuator is shorted to voltage. GM's L3B logic switches the output off and checks the line against controller power; 0.5 ohm or less in 4 of 5 samples, with supply above 11 V, sets a Type A code and the MIL straight away (19OBDG03D, 25OBDG03B).",["Harness wear at the camshaft carrier cover shorting to a live wire (GM bulletins)","Actuator 3 shorted internally to supply","ECM output stage faulty"],["MIL on immediately","No lift change and no cylinder deactivation","With harness damage, possibly stalling or no start"],2,3,["P2C08","P2C0C","P2C0D","P2C0E","P2C0F"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C11:["Reductant Pump A Current Too Low","P2C11 watches the electric motor of the DEF (AdBlue) pump from the other side than P214E: its driver output carries less current than a working motor should draw, which points to an open winding, a poor plug contact or a motor spinning freely or not at all.",["DEF pump motor with open winding or worn brushes/electronics (pump module in the tank)","Loose, corroded or spread terminals at the pump connector","Open or high-resistance control or low-reference wire between control module and pump","Faulty output stage in the DEF control module"],["MIL and exhaust fluid system warning in the instrument cluster","No DEF consumption, higher NOx emissions","Speed or restart limitation if the fault persists (inducement)"],3,3,["P214E","P208A","P208B","P208C","P208D","P20E8"],"זרם משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2C12:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Bank 1","Camshaft B is the exhaust camshaft in J2012 terms, and P2C12 reports an open circuit in the feedback of its first profile actuator on bank 1. GM's 2.7 L turbo L3B (Silverado and Sierra 1500 from model year 2019) is the documented user: its tables call this element exhaust Hall sensor 1. With the driver energised, the ECM flags a break once the signal-to-ground impedance reaches 200 kilohms or more;",["Engine harness worn through where it crosses the camshaft carrier cover (GM PIT5677, 21-NA-149)","Connector on exhaust actuator 1 not latched or corroded","Open Hall element inside the exhaust actuator"],["Check engine light from the first trip","Exhaust cam profile no longer switched, fuel economy mode unavailable","With harness damage, several other engine codes at the same time"],2,3,["P2C13","P2C14","P2C15","P2C16","P2C05","P002A"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P2C13:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor A Range/Performance Bank 1","P2C13 is the rationality test for the first exhaust profile actuator's feedback on bank 1, so the wiring is not in question. GM's L3B tracks every exhaust shift through exhaust Hall sensor 1: the reading must drop below 55 as the pin starts to fire, below 45 when it is fully out and climb above 68 once the pin is home again.",["Pin of exhaust actuator 1 slow or sticking (sludge, overdue oil change, wrong oil grade)","Worn shift groove or weak detent on the exhaust cam sleeve","Hall element in actuator 1 delivering drifting levels"],["Warning lamp on at once","Exhaust lift locked on one profile, cylinder deactivation inactive","Occasional clicking from the top of the engine"],2,3,["P2C12","P2C14","P2C15","P2C17","P2C06","P005A"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2C14:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit Low Bank 1","With P2C14 the ECM reports that the line of exhaust position sensor A on bank 1 is grounded. GM applies the check on the L3B 2.7 L while the driver is commanded on: a signal-to-ground impedance of 0.5 ohm or below, seen in four of five samples with the key in crank or run and more than 11 V, sets Type A with immediate MIL; the 2025 table 25OBDG03B adds a general enable flag but keeps the limit (19OBDG03D).",["Signal wire of exhaust sensor A rubbed bare against the head or a bracket","Internal short to ground in exhaust actuator 1","Engine oil wicked into the actuator plug"],["MIL on immediately","No exhaust lift change, slightly higher consumption under light load"],2,3,["P2C12","P2C13","P2C15","P2C18","P2C07","P002B"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C15:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor A Circuit High Bank 1","P2C15 stands for a short to voltage on the exhaust position sensor A circuit, bank 1, i.e. the Hall feedback of GM's first exhaust actuator on the L3B four. This test runs with the output switched off: if a resistance of 0.5 ohm or less to controller power remains on the line, four failed reports in five at more than 11 V produce a Type A code, MIL at once (19OBDG03D, 25OBDG03B).",["Chafed harness letting the sensor line touch a supply wire (GM PIT5677, 21-NA-149)","Short to supply inside exhaust actuator 1","Defective output stage in the ECM"],["MIL lit straight away","Exhaust cam profile stays fixed","Together with harness damage, blown fuses, no start or reduced power possible"],2,3,["P2C12","P2C13","P2C14","P2C19","P2C08","P002C"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C16:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Bank 1","P2C16 is the open-circuit fault of position sensor B on the bank 1 exhaust camshaft. On GM's L3B this is exhaust Hall sensor 2, the second and last exhaust feedback: GM's tables list four exhaust pin drivers (control codes P002A, P2B39, P03F1, P3099) but only two exhaust Hall elements, which matches the two exhaust profile actuators described by GM TechLink.",["Plug on exhaust actuator 2 pulled off or not locked after engine work","Wire broken where the harness rubs at the camshaft carrier (GM L3B bulletins)","Open circuit in the Hall element of actuator 2"],["Check engine light in the first trip","Exhaust lift switching and economy modes blocked"],2,3,["P2C12","P2C17","P2C18","P2C19","P2C09","P2B39"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P2C17:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor B Range/Performance Bank 1","P2C17 flags implausible feedback from exhaust Hall sensor 2, the position sensor of the second exhaust profile actuator on bank 1 of GM's L3B. The electrical circuit tests pass, yet the shift pattern is wrong: after a command GM expects the reading to pass below 55 (pin extending), below 45 (pin fully out) and back above 68 (pin retracted).",["Pin of exhaust actuator 2 binding because of deposits or degraded oil","Exhaust cam sleeve not snapping into its detent, worn groove","Low or aerated engine oil slowing the shift"],["Warning lamp on without delay","Engine runs on a fixed exhaust profile, no cylinder deactivation","Possibly a light tapping noise from the valve train"],2,3,["P2C13","P2C16","P2C18","P2C19","P2C0A","P2B51"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2C18:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Low Bank 1","A ground short in the position sensor B line on the bank 1 exhaust side sets P2C18. On GM's L3B this is the feedback wire of exhaust actuator 2. GM's table phrases it as a fault of the sensor's solenoid driver: with the output commanded on, a signal-to-ground impedance not above 0.5 ohm in four samples out of five, supply over 11 V and ignition in crank or run, stores Type A and switches on the MIL (19OBDG03D,…",["Harness insulation damaged at the camshaft carrier cover or under the air cleaner housing","Exhaust actuator 2 shorted internally to ground","Water or oil bridging contacts in the plug"],["MIL comes on in the first trip","Exhaust profile no longer changes, small rise in fuel use"],2,3,["P2C14","P2C16","P2C17","P2C19","P2C0B","P2B3A"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C19:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit High Bank 1","P2C19 closes the sensor B group on the exhaust camshaft of bank 1: the feedback circuit of GM's exhaust Hall sensor 2 is shorted to a voltage source. For the L3B the ECM checks while the output is off; a path of at most 0.5 ohm to controller power, reported four times in five with supply over 11 V, gives a Type A code with the MIL on in the first trip (19OBDG03D, 25OBDG03B).",["Harness chafed at generator bracket or coil spring stud, line touching a live wire (GM 21-NA-149)","Exhaust actuator 2 shorted internally to supply","ECM output stage faulty"],["MIL on in the first drive","Exhaust lift switching disabled","With extensive harness damage, stalling, no crank or blown fuses"],2,3,["P2C15","P2C16","P2C17","P2C18","P2C0C","P2B3B"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C1A:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor C Circuit Bank 1","P2C1A would report an open circuit in a third position feedback on the bank 1 exhaust camshaft. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. GM's L3B, the one engine with publicly documented exhaust feedback codes, has just two exhaust Hall sensors (P2C12 to P2C19), in line with the two exhaust profile actuators that GM TechLink describes; its 2019 and 2025 tables contain no P2C1A.",["Disconnected or corroded plug at the third exhaust actuator","Broken feedback wire in the engine harness","Internal open in the position sensor"],["Engine warning lamp on","Exhaust cam profile switching locked out"],2,3,["P2C1B","P2C1C","P2C1D","P2C16","P2C0D","P03F1"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P2C1B:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor C Range/Performance Bank 1","Range/Performance for exhaust position sensor C, bank 1: the signal is electrically fine but does not match the commanded pin movement of a third exhaust profile actuator. There is no public manufacturer documentation for P2C1B. The comparable test on GM's L3B (P2C13, P2C17) watches three Hall states per shift and also catches pin activity without a command;",["Actuator pin sticking or reacting too slowly","Sludge or wrong oil viscosity in the valve train","Position sensor reporting implausible levels"],["Warning lamp on","Exhaust lift held on one profile, possibly ticking from the head"],2,3,["P2C1A","P2C1C","P2C1D","P2C17","P2C0E","P03F4"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2C1C:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor C Circuit Low Bank 1","P2C1C is reserved for a circuit-low fault, typically a short to ground, in the feedback of exhaust position sensor C on bank 1. It is not used in any public manufacturer documentation. GM's L3B tables show how its siblings work: P2C14 and P2C18 compare the line against ground with the driver on and declare a short at 0.5 ohm or less in four of five samples.",["Sensor C wire chafed through to ground","Shorted actuator or position sensor","Moisture in the actuator connector"],["MIL on","No change of exhaust cam profile"],2,3,["P2C1A","P2C1B","P2C1D","P2C18","P2C0F","P03F2"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C1D:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator Position Sensor C Circuit High Bank 1","P2C1D, the circuit-high code for exhaust position sensor C on bank 1, covers a feedback line pulled towards supply voltage, usually by a short to power. No carmaker publishes a use for it. On GM's L3B the matching codes P2C15 and P2C19 are evaluated with the output off, a short being declared at a resistance up to 0.5 ohm against the controller supply;",["Sensor C line rubbing against a powered wire","Internal short to supply in the actuator","Faulty driver stage in the ECM"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust lift switching suspended"],2,3,["P2C1A","P2C1B","P2C1C","P2C19","P2C10","P03F3"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2C1E:["Cold Start Fuel Pressure Regulator A Performance","Direct-injection petrol engines often run a catalyst-heating mode after a cold start, with split injections that need tightly held rail pressure. P2C1E says regulator A, which meters the high-pressure pump, ran out of authority in that phase.",["Worn high-pressure pump that needs full stroke to reach the target","Insufficient feed pressure from the in-tank pump or a clogged filter","Sticking quantity control valve on the high-pressure pump","Worn pump drive cam or follower reducing effective stroke"],["MIL after two cold starts with the fault","Rough idle or hesitation in the first minute after a cold start","Often no noticeable symptom once warm"],2,1,["P2C1F","P2C20","P0089","P228C","P228D","P053F"],"וסת לחץ דלק התנעה קרה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C1F:["Cold Start Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too Low","P2C1F is the underpressure half of GM's cold-start fuel pressure check on direct-injection petrol engines: while the catalyst is being heated, measured rail pressure lags the target by more than a calibrated margin. Table 25OBDG03B uses a 3 MPa gap for desired pressures from 4 MPa up (2 MPa at 3 MPa), the same map as P228C; 10 s of failures within 12.5 s set the code as Type A, so the MIL lights after one trip.",["High-pressure pump with worn plunger or sticking control valve delivering too little","Low feed pressure from in-tank pump, filter or pressure regulator","Leaking or sticking injector bleeding off rail pressure","Rail pressure sensor reading too low"],["MIL after a single faulty cold start","Long cranking, rough running or stalling when cold","Reduced power possible if pressure stays low"],2,3,["P2C1E","P2C20","P228C","P228D","P0087","P053F"],""],P2C20:["Cold Start Fuel Pressure Regulator A Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too High","P2C20 mirrors P2C1F: during catalyst heating after a cold start the rail pressure overshoots its setpoint because the high-pressure pump supplies more fuel than requested or cannot be throttled back. On GM direct-injection petrol engines the measured pressure must exceed the target by 3 MPa or more, on the map it shares with P228D, for 10 s within 12.5 s (25OBDG03B; in 19OBDG03D only 2 MPa from 20 MPa desired);",["Quantity control valve on the high-pressure pump stuck in the delivering position","Wiring or connector fault in the control valve drive circuit","Rail pressure sensor drifting so the controller overshoots","Engine control software that needs an update"],["MIL after one faulty cold start","Harsh, loud cold idle or ticking injectors","Possible reduced power or rich running smell"],2,3,["P2C1E","P2C1F","P228D","P228C","P0088"],""],P2C21:["Engine Oil Temperature Sensor A/B Correlation","Engines with two oil temperature sensors can check them against each other; P2C21 means sensors A and B disagree although each signal is electrically valid. GM runs up to three tests in its 2019 and 2025 tables (19OBDG03D, 25OBDG03B): after a cold soak (engine off over 540 s or 2,100 s) oil, coolant and intake air must start within 16 °C of each other;",["One oil temperature sensor drifting or stuck within its range","Corroded or loose contacts adding resistance on one sensor","Low oil level leaving one sensor partly uncovered","Block or oil heater use skewing the cold-start comparison"],["MIL after two trips","Oil life or oil temperature display may be wrong","Usually no change in driveability"],2,1,["P0196","P01BA","P0195","P01B9","P0197","P01BB"],"חיישן טמפרטורת שמן מנוע‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2C22:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit","Full hybrids with exhaust heat recovery pass hot exhaust through a coolant heat exchanger after a cold start and divert it around the exchanger with flap A once enough heat has been gathered. A sensor in the flap actuator reports the flap angle to the engine module. P2C22 is the general electrical fault of that feedback: the signal is missing or cannot be read. Ford uses it on its full hybrids.",["Water intrusion into the heat exchanger or its actuator (Ford Maverick hybrid)","Failed bypass valve actuator with integrated position sensor","Corroded or loose connector at the actuator under the vehicle","Harness near the exhaust chafed or heat-damaged"],["Check engine light","Slower engine warm-up and weaker cabin heating in cold weather","Engine of the hybrid runs longer before it may shut off"],3,1,["P2C23","P2C24","P2C25","P237C","P237F","P25D6"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2C23:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Performance","P2C23 means the flap position reported for exhaust heat exchanger bypass valve A is electrically valid but does not make sense – for example it disagrees with the command or with how the coolant behind the exchanger warms up. A Ford patent shows that such plausibility can be judged from temperatures.",["Water or corrosion in the connectors of exhaust coolant temperature sensors 3/4 (Ford)","Outdated PCM calibration (early 2021 F-150 PowerBoost)","Worn, sticking or frozen bypass actuator","Flap or linkage in the heat exchanger binding"],["Check engine light, often after frost","No noticeable change in driving","Heater warms up more slowly"],2,1,["P2C22","P2C24","P2C25","P237F","P25D6","P237C"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C24:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit Low","P2C24 is stored when the position signal of exhaust heat exchanger bypass flap A drops below its permitted band. Typical reasons are a signal wire shorted to ground, an open sensor supply or an actuator whose sensor has failed low. CARB requires engine modules to check such inputs for readings outside their range and to keep separate codes for low, high and open where feasible.",["Position signal wire shorted to ground near the exhaust","Open or missing 5 V supply to the position sensor","Position sensor inside the actuator failed low","Water in the actuator connector"],["Check engine light","Heat recovery switched off, slower warm-up"],2,1,["P2C22","P2C23","P2C25","P237D"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2C25:["Exhaust Heat Exchanger Exhaust Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit High","P2C25 is the counterpart of P2C24: the feedback from the position sensor of exhaust heat exchanger bypass flap A sits above the highest value a working sensor can deliver. This usually points to a signal line touching a voltage source, an interrupted sensor ground or an internal sensor fault that pulls the output toward the reference.",["Position signal wire shorted to a voltage source","Open ground circuit of the position sensor","Position sensor in the actuator failed high"],["Check engine light","Cabin heater slow to warm up in winter"],2,1,["P2C22","P2C23","P2C24","P237E"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף פליטת מחליף חום פליטה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2C26:["Fuel Injector Group B Supply Sense Circuit","Many engines feed their injectors in groups from a switched supply, for example through an injector relay or a high-side driver. A separate sense line lets the engine module read back whether voltage really arrives at group B. P2C26 is the general fault of that read-back: the sensed value is missing, erratic or not consistent with the commanded supply state.",["Open or high-resistance sense wire between injector supply and module","Injector relay or its socket making poor contact","Corroded connector in the injector supply harness","Faulty sense input inside the engine control module"],["Check engine light","Possible misfire or rough running on the cylinders of group B","Hard starting if the group is switched off"],2,3,["P2C27","P2C28","P2149","P2150","P2151","P0685"],"אספקת קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ B — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P2C27:["Fuel Injector Group B Supply Sense Circuit Low","P2C27 reports that the voltage read back on the supply sense line of injector group B is too low while the module expects the group to be powered. In practice the feed never reaches the injectors – a blown fuse, a relay that does not close, a broken supply wire or a grounded feed – or only the sense wire itself is grounded. In the first case the cylinders of group B receive no fuel and misfire or stay dead;",["Blown fuse in the injector group B supply","Injector relay not closing or burnt contacts","Supply or sense wire shorted to ground","Internally shorted injector pulling the group supply down"],["Check engine light","Misfire on several cylinders, rough idle","Clearly reduced power or engine will not start"],2,3,["P2C26","P2C28","P2150","P2149","P0300"],"אספקת קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P2C28:["Fuel Injector Group B Supply Sense Circuit High","P2C28 is set when the sense line of the injector group B supply shows more voltage than allowed – either above the upper limit while the group is switched on, or voltage present while the module has switched the group off. Common reasons are a welded injector relay, a supply wire chafed against another powered circuit, or a sense wire shorted to battery voltage.",["Injector relay contacts stuck closed","Sense or supply wire shorted to battery voltage","Excessive system voltage from the charging system","Internal fault of the supply switch in the engine control module"],["Check engine light","Often no noticeable change in running","Battery drain if the relay stays closed after switch-off"],2,1,["P2C26","P2C27","P2151","P2149","P0687"],"אספקת קבוצת מזרק דלק‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P2C29:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve B Stuck","Bypass valve B is the compressor recirculation valve of the second charger – the later one in series layouts, the bank 2 unit on parallel twin-turbo engines. It is not the wastegate. P2C29 means a position-controlled valve no longer follows its target and stays where it is. No manufacturer documents P2C29 publicly.",["Oil or carbon deposits binding the valve flap or piston","Worn gears or motor in the electric actuator","Bent shaft or damaged housing of the valve"],["Check engine light","Less boost and power","Fluttering compressor noise when lifting off"],3,3,["P23AA","P00C4","P2C2A","P2C2D","P2CD5","P00C0"],"שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ B — תקוע"],P2C2A:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve B Position Sensor Circuit/Open","P2C2A covers an open or otherwise unreadable position feedback from compressor bypass valve B, the electrically positioned recirculation valve of the second charger. Without a valid feedback the engine module cannot confirm how far the valve has opened, which an Achates Power patent names as the reason such sensors are monitored. No manufacturer documents P2C2A publicly.",["Unplugged, loose or corroded connector at valve B","Broken signal, reference or ground wire of the sensor","Internal open in the position sensor of the actuator"],["Check engine light","Boost limited, less power"],2,3,["P2C2B","P2C2C","P2C29","P2BBB","U066B","P00C0"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2C2B:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve B Position Sensor Circuit Low","With P2C2B the position signal of compressor bypass valve B lies below the lowest value a healthy sensor delivers. Likely reasons are a signal wire grounded against the engine, an open 5 V reference or a sensor that has failed low. For valve B no public manufacturer data exist.",["Signal wire of the position sensor shorted to ground","Missing 5 V reference at the sensor","Position sensor in the valve actuator failed low"],["Check engine light","Reduced boost pressure"],2,3,["P2C2A","P2C2C","P2BBC","P2C29"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2C2C:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve B Position Sensor Circuit High","P2C2C flags a position signal from compressor bypass valve B that rises above the plausible top of its range, close to the sensor reference. A signal line touching 5 V or battery voltage, a broken ground wire or a defect inside the sensor are the typical findings. No manufacturer publishes P2C2C.",["Signal wire shorted to reference or battery voltage","Open ground of the position sensor","Position sensor failed high"],["Check engine light","Boost limited by the engine module"],2,3,["P2C2A","P2C2B","P2BBD","P2C29"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2C2D:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve B Position Exceeded Learning Limit","Electrically positioned compressor bypass valves have their end stops relearned regularly so that the sensor reading can be converted into a true opening. P2C2D means that for valve B, belonging to the second charger, a learned stop came out beyond the allowed window. No manufacturer documents the B-side code.",["Carbon or oil deposits preventing the valve from reaching its stop","Worn actuator gear or loose sensor magnet","Valve replaced without relearn or with incorrect part"],["Check engine light after a key-off","Boost control less precise, possible surge noise"],3,3,["P2BBE","P2C29","P2C2A","P2C2B","P2C2C"],""],P2C2E:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve B Supply Voltage Low","P2C2E concerns the power stage of compressor bypass valve B, not its position signal. Such valves are moved by a small DC motor driven through an H-bridge, and the bridge reports when its own supply sags below a safe level. No manufacturer documents the B-side code publicly.",["Weak battery or voltage drop on the module feed","Poor ground or corroded relay contacts in the supply","Internal fault of the H-bridge driver"],["Check engine light","Valve no longer responds, boost reduced","Often accompanied by other low-voltage codes"],2,3,["P2BBF","P2C2F","P00C0","P00C1"],"אספקת שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ B — מתח נמוך"],P2C2F:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve B Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P2C2F is stored when the output stage driving compressor bypass valve B signals excessive current or overheating. The motor driver protects itself by limiting current and finally switching off, and reports this to the engine module. No manufacturer documents P2C2F;",["Jammed valve forcing the motor to stall against its stop","Shorted winding in the valve actuator motor","Motor leads shorted to each other or to ground","Overheated or faulty driver inside the engine module"],["Check engine light","Valve stops responding, boost reduced"],2,3,["P2BC0","P2C2E","P00D8","P2C29","P00C4"],"שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ B — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר"],P2C30:["Ignition Coil Primary Circuit Fuse A","On engines whose ignition coils are fed through more than one fuse, the module checks each fuse so that it notices when a whole group of coils loses power. P2C30 points to fuse A. A GM patent explains the reasoning: coils and injectors sit on separate circuits, so after a fuse blows fuel would still be injected into cylinders without spark;",["Ignition system control module software (Stellantis 3.0L Hurricane)","Fuse A blown by a shorted ignition coil or supply wire","Loose or corroded fuse terminal"],["Check engine light","Misfire on several cylinders, hesitation","Reduced power while cylinders are shut off"],2,3,["P2C31","P0300","P0351","P0350","P0420"],"נתיך מעגל ראשי סליל הצתה‏ A"],P2C31:["Ignition Coil Primary Circuit Fuse B","P2C31 is the second of two fuse checks in the coil primary supply: the fuse B group of coils has lost voltage, or the module believes so. GM's patent on this monitor counts how often the current through the fuse falls below a threshold within a set number of samples before it declares the fuse open, then flags a service warning and stops fuel to the unfired cylinders.",["Ignition system control module calibration (Stellantis 3.0L Hurricane)","Shorted ignition coil in group B blowing the fuse","Chafed coil feed wire shorting to ground"],["Check engine light","Engine misfires or hesitates","Catalyst codes may follow"],2,3,["P2C30","P0300","P0354","P0350","P0430"],"נתיך מעגל ראשי סליל הצתה‏ B"],P2C32:["Crankcase Pressure Sensor B Circuit","A crankcase pressure sensor tells the engine module how the pressure in the crankcase ventilation compares with ambient, mainly so it can detect a disconnected or leaking breather line. P2C32 is the general circuit fault of sensor B: its signal is missing or cannot be decoded at all, without saying high or low. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly.",["Unplugged, loose or corroded sensor connector","Open or chafed wire between sensor and engine module","Sensor electronics failed","Engine module input or software fault"],["MIL on","Crankcase ventilation leak check not available","Usually no change in driveability"],2,1,["P2C33","P2C34","P2C35","P2C36","P051A","U060E","P04DB"],"חיישן לחץ בית גל הארכובה‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2C33:["Crankcase Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2C33 means crankcase pressure sensor B delivers a signal inside its electrical limits that the engine module finds implausible, such as an offset from ambient pressure with the engine stopped or values a running engine cannot produce. Two bulletin families name it.",["Engine control software needing an update (Alfa Romeo and Maserati V6/V8)","Sensor offset or drift, partly due to moisture or ice in the port","Faulty blow-by (PCV) valve producing abnormal crankcase pressure","Harness or pin resistance shifting the signal"],["MIL on, often together with other PCM codes","Limp-in mode possible on affected Alfa Romeo models","Otherwise usually no driveability change"],2,3,["P2C32","P2C34","P2C35","P2C36","P051B","P2C91","P04DB"],"חיישן לחץ בית גל הארכובה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2C34:["Crankcase Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","Circuit Low means the voltage from crankcase pressure sensor B stays under the lowest value the sensor can deliver, typically because the 5 V reference is missing, the signal wire is shorted to ground or the sensor itself has failed. Maserati's bulletin MAS002969/A for MY21 Quattroporte, Ghibli and Levante with the F160 V6 or F154 V8 lists P2C34 next to the sensor-A codes P051B–P051D.",["5 V reference open or shorted to ground","Signal wire shorted to ground or chafed insulation","Crankcase pressure sensor B internally failed","Bent or corroded pins at sensor or ECM"],["MIL on","Other sensors on the same 5 V supply may report faults too","Usually no driveability change"],2,1,["P2C32","P2C33","P2C35","P2C36","P051C"],"חיישן לחץ בית גל הארכובה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2C35:["Crankcase Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","P2C35 is set when the signal of crankcase pressure sensor B sits above the highest voltage the sensor can legitimately produce. That usually means an interrupted signal wire pulled up inside the module, a broken sensor ground, or a short from the signal to the 5 V supply or to battery voltage.",["Open signal wire or unplugged connector","Missing sensor ground (low reference)","Signal shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Faulty sensor or outdated engine control software"],["MIL on","Crankcase ventilation monitor not completed","Usually no driveability change"],2,1,["P2C32","P2C33","P2C34","P2C36","P051D"],"חיישן לחץ בית גל הארכובה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2C36:["Crankcase Pressure Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2C36 covers a crankcase pressure sensor B signal that drops out briefly or jumps faster than real crankcase pressure can change, while staying mostly inside its electrical range. That pattern points to a contact that opens for moments, a wire chafing on the engine, moisture in the plug or a sensor failing internally.",["Loose or fretting contacts at the sensor or an intermediate connector","Wire rubbing on engine parts and shorting briefly","Moisture or oil in the connector","Sensor with intermittent internal fault"],["MIL that may come and go","Erratic crankcase pressure value in live data","Usually no driveability change"],2,1,["P2C32","P2C33","P2C34","P2C35","P051E"],"חיישן לחץ בית גל הארכובה‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2C37:["Cold Start Engine Coolant Pump Performance","Engines with a switchable or electric main coolant pump often keep the coolant still, or nearly so, right after a cold start so the cylinder head and catalyst warm up sooner. P2C37 reports that the pump did not behave as commanded during this cold-start phase, for example running when it should rest or failing to start when flow is requested.",["Switchable pump stuck engaged or disengaged (clutch, shroud or valve actuator)","Electric coolant pump with failing motor or electronics","Air in the system or low coolant level","Coolant or head temperature sensor reading wrong and misleading the check"],["MIL on","Slow warm-up and weak cabin heat, or rising temperature when the pump stays off","Overheating warning possible in severe cases"],3,1,["P2DE9","P2E82","P26CB","P2B85","P050C"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע התנעה קרה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C38:["Cylinder Head Temperature Sensor B Circuit","A cylinder head temperature sensor is an NTC thermistor seated in the head metal that tells the module how hot the engine really is, even without coolant. P2C38 is the general circuit fault of a second such sensor, B: the signal is open, shorted or otherwise unusable, without separating low from high (P2C3A/P2C3B do that, P2C39 judges plausibility).",["PCM software causing false faults (Ford 2025 Explorer/Aviator, TSB 24-2393)","Loose or corroded connector at the head sensor","Failed head temperature sensor B","Heat-damaged or chafed wiring near the cylinder head"],["MIL and engine over-temperature warning","Fail-safe cooling mode with reduced power possible","Temperature warning even though coolant level and fan are fine"],2,3,["P2C39","P2C3A","P2C3B","P2C3C","P2C3D","P017A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ראש מנוע‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2C39:["Cylinder Head Temperature Sensor B Range/Performance","P2C39 flags a second cylinder head temperature sensor, B, whose voltage is electrically valid but whose reading does not fit the engine's state, for instance a value that jumps, lags or disagrees with other temperature inputs.",["PCM calibration misjudging sensor B (Ford EcoBoost bulletins, cured by reprogramming)","Sensor B drifted or responding slowly","Sensor not seated properly in the head or corroded terminals","Genuine local overheating from low coolant or trapped air"],["Engine over-temperature warning although the gauge and coolant level look normal","Check engine light, often together with P1299 or P1285","Reduced power while the fail-safe cooling strategy is active"],2,3,["P2C38","P2C3A","P2C3B","P2C3C","P2C3D","P017B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ראש מנוע‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C3A:["Cylinder Head Temperature Sensor B Circuit Low","P2C3A reports that the signal of cylinder head temperature sensor B sits below the lowest voltage the module accepts. Because these sensors are NTC thermistors, a very low voltage would stand for an impossibly hot head, so the usual reasons are a signal wire shorted to ground, water inside the plug or a sensor with an internal short. No manufacturer publicly documents this code.",["Signal wire of sensor B chafed through to ground","Moisture or coolant in the sensor connector","Internal short in the thermistor of sensor B"],["Overheat warning or very high head temperature in live data on a cold engine","Cooling fans running at full speed without reason","Check engine light, possibly reduced engine power"],2,3,["P2C38","P2C3B","P2C39","P2C3C","P017C"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ראש מנוע‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2C3B:["Cylinder Head Temperature Sensor B Circuit High","With P2C3B the voltage from cylinder head temperature sensor B stays above the valid ceiling, which the module would have to read as a head far colder than any real engine. An interrupted signal wire, a lost sensor ground, a terminal that has backed out of the plug or a thermistor cracked by heat cycling are the typical finds. No manufacturer publicly documents the code.",["Open signal wire or terminal pushed out of the connector","Sensor return (ground) circuit open or high resistance","Thermistor of sensor B broken internally"],["Live data shows head temperature B at the lowest possible value","Check engine light","Fans run more often, idle and warm-up behaviour unusual"],2,1,["P2C38","P2C3A","P2C39","P2C3C","P017D"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ראש מנוע‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2C3C:["Cylinder Head Temperature Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2C3C is stored when the head temperature signal of sensor B drops out briefly or jumps in steps that no mass of hot metal could follow, while the samples on their own may still lie within the valid window. Loose terminals, a wire that touches ground only over bumps or with engine movement, corrosion in the plug and a cracked thermistor are the usual culprits. No manufacturer publicly documents P2C3C;",["Loose or spread terminal in the sensor B connector","Harness rubbing on engine parts and shorting only at times","Corrosion in the plug","Cracked sensor element"],["Check engine light that comes and goes","Jumping head temperature B in live data","Occasional fan runs or brief warnings without real overheating"],2,1,["P2C38","P2C3A","P2C3B","P2C39","P017E"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ראש מנוע‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2C3D:["Cylinder Head Temperature Sensor A/B Correlation","An engine with two head temperature sensors can check one against the other: after a long soak both should read close to each other and to coolant temperature, and while running their gap should stay inside an expected band. P2C3D means sensors A and B disagree beyond that limit although neither circuit shows a fault. No manufacturer publicly documents the code or its thresholds.",["One of the two sensors has drifted out of tolerance","Contact resistance in one sensor circuit shifting its reading","Engine control software judging the pair too tightly","Real temperature difference from air pocket or poor flow in one head area"],["Check engine light without driveability complaints","Clearly different values for head temperature A and B after a cold start"],2,1,["P017B","P2C39","P2C38","P017A","P0116"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ראש מנוע‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2C3E:["Fan 4 Control Circuit","P2C3E reports a fault on the control circuit of a fourth fan output: the driver in the engine or fan control module sees an open line, a missing load or an error it cannot sort into low or high. What counts as fan 4 is up to the maker.",["Broken wire or loose connector in the fan 4 control line","Fan 4 relay coil open or relay missing","Blown fuse feeding the relay or fan module","Output driver in the control module defective"],["One fan or fan stage does not run when commanded","Rising temperature at idle or in traffic, weaker A/C at standstill","Check engine light"],2,3,["P2C3F","P2C40","P2C42","U067D","P0482","P0480"],"מאוורר‏ 4 — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],P2C3F:["Fan 4 Control Circuit Low","With P2C3F the module senses the control line of fan output 4 at too low a level, which in practice means a short to ground or, with a driver that switches to ground, a line held there by a fault downstream.",["Fan 4 control wire chafed through to body or engine ground","Shorted relay coil or fan module input","Water in the fan connector near the radiator"],["Fan 4 runs constantly or not at all","Blown fan fuse","Check engine light"],2,3,["P2C3E","P2C40","P2C42","P0695","P0691"],"מאוורר‏ 4 — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2C40:["Fan 4 Control Circuit High","P2C40 states that fan control output 4 is held at too high a level: the line has contact with battery voltage, or the driver cannot pull it down when it should. In Saab's 2011 9-5 the counterpart relay codes P0692, P0694 and P0696 stand for a relay control wire shorted to a voltage source, and the manual adds that a stage stuck on can also occur without any stored code. No manufacturer publicly documents P2C40.",["Fan 4 control wire in contact with a battery-voltage circuit","Relay or fan module input failed internally","Moisture bridging pins in the connector"],["Fan 4 runs constantly, sometimes after switch-off","Discharged 12 V battery after standing","Check engine light"],2,1,["P2C3E","P2C3F","P2C42","P0696","P0692"],"מאוורר‏ 4 — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2C41:["Fan 3 Performance/Stuck Off","P2C41 judges the outcome rather than the wiring: fan 3 is commanded on and its circuit checks out (otherwise P0482, P0695 or P0696 would appear), yet the controller sees little or no response, usually through speed feedback from a fan module or a missing current draw. No manufacturer publicly documents this code.",["Fan blades blocked by dirt, stones or leaves","Worn or seized fan motor, corrosion from moisture","Fan control module does not drive the motor","Weak power or ground supply to the fan"],["Engine temperature climbs in traffic or under heavy load","Weak air conditioning at standstill","Warning lamp or fan failure message"],2,3,["P0482","P0695","P0696","P2CBB","P2CBC","U067C","P2C42"],"מאוורר‏ 3 — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2C42:["Fan 4 Performance/Stuck Off","P2C42 reports that the fourth fan output does not deliver what is asked of it: the fan stays still or reaches far too little speed while its control line shows no electrical fault (those would be P2C3E to P2C40). No manufacturer publicly documents P2C42.",["Fan jammed by debris or a damaged shroud","Worn bearings or corroded motor","Integrated fan electronics or fan module failed"],["Temperature warning or reduced power under high load","Fan 4 does not turn when activated with a scan tool","Grinding noise before the fan stops"],2,3,["P2C3E","P2C3F","P2C40","P2C41","U067D","P2B31"],"מאוורר‏ 4 — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2C43:["Battery Isolation/Voltage Stabilization Control Circuit","Some vehicles split their 12 V system with a switch so that a heavy starter load, typically an automatic restart, cannot pull the supply of control units and displays down. A Ford patent on start-stop cars puts that dip at roughly 5 to 7 V without such separation.",["Open control wire or loose connector at the isolator","Isolator relay coil or electronic switch failed","Poor ground connection of the isolator circuit","Output driver in the control module defective"],["Warning lamp or powertrain fault indicator on","Automatic stop-start no longer stops the engine","Radio or displays may reboot during engine starts"],2,2,["P2C44","P2C45","P2C46","P2C47","U061E","P25FF"],""],P2C44:["Battery Isolation/Voltage Stabilization Control Circuit Performance","P2C44 means the isolation or voltage stabilization stage is wired and commanded, yet its behaviour does not match what the module expects. Ford is the one maker with published cases: 2021–2022 F-150 trucks with the 3.5 L PowerBoost hybrid and 10R80 MHT gearbox carry a second 12 V battery that an auxiliary battery isolator separates from the main battery.",["Auxiliary battery isolator faulty (Ford replaces it per bulletin 23-2031)","Poor ground in the isolator circuit (Ford GD132, G102, C146, C1989C)","Outdated PCM software","Weak or failing auxiliary 12 V battery"],["Wrench (powertrain malfunction) indicator on","U061E may be stored alongside","Electrical glitches during engine pull-up"],2,2,["P2C43","P2C45","P2C46","P2C47","U061E","U041A"],""],P2C45:["Battery Isolation/Voltage Stabilization Control Circuit Low","P2C45 is stored when the line that commands the battery isolation or voltage stabilization switch reads lower than its commanded state allows, the classic picture of a short to ground or, with a high-side driver, an open coil pulling the sense voltage down. The switch exists so that the starter can draw its peak current from one battery while sensitive loads stay on a separate, stable supply;",["Control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Corroded or water-damaged connector near the battery","Isolator relay coil shorted internally"],["Fault indicator on","Stop-start function unavailable","Possible blown fuse in the control circuit"],2,2,["P2C43","P2C44","P2C46","P2C47","U061E"],""],P2C46:["Battery Isolation/Voltage Stabilization Control Circuit High","P2C46 is the opposite of P2C45: the control line of the battery isolation or voltage stabilization switch sits higher than expected, which points to a short to battery voltage, or, on a low-side driven relay, to an open circuit that leaves the sense input floating high.",["Control wire shorted to battery positive","Open circuit with low-side driver (input pulled high)","Isolator internally defective","Control module input or driver fault"],["Fault indicator on","Stop-start disabled","Screens or radio may reset when the engine restarts"],2,2,["P2C43","P2C44","P2C45","P2C47","U061E"],""],P2C47:["Battery Isolation/Voltage Stabilization Control Circuit Intermittent","With P2C47 the module saw the command line of the isolation or stabilization stage drop out and come back, rather than stay permanently open or shorted. Loose terminals, a cracked solder joint in the isolator or a ground strap that only loses contact when the engine rocks on a restart are typical, and the fault often sets only while driving or on bumpy roads.",["Loose or spread terminal in the isolator connector","Ground strap or ground point with intermittent contact","Cracked solder joint inside the isolator"],["Fault indicator comes and goes","Stop-start works only sometimes","Readiness monitors may stay incomplete"],2,2,["P2C43","P2C44","P2C45","P2C46","U061E"],""],P2C48:["Coolant Pump C Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P2C48 is a performance check on coolant pump C: the pump is driven, but what it draws or delivers does not match the request. GM uses it in its diesel tables, where pump C is the electric pump of the low-temperature loop: 20OBDG04 estimates the phase current expected at the actual pump speed and flags an error above 4 A for more than 5 s (5 failures in 8 samples), 25OBDG04A above 1 A with the pump over 2,800 rpm (10…",["Low coolant or air in the low-temperature loop, e.g. from a chafed hose (GM 21-NA-265)","Worn, sluggish or partly blocked pump","Fault in the pump's integrated motor electronics","Weak supply from the powertrain relay or poor ground"],["Check engine light after two trips","Coolant leak under the vehicle","Higher intake air or fuel temperature, possibly reduced power"],2,3,["P2BA0","P26F4","P26F8","P26FA","P2C49","P2601"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2C49:["Coolant Pump D Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P2C49 is the functional check of coolant pump D: the command arrives and the control line is intact, but the pump does not run or does not reach the effect the module expects. No manufacturer publicly documents P2C49. GM shows the method on pump C with P2C48: its diesel tables derive an expected phase current from the measured pump speed and set a type B fault once the difference persists for about 5 seconds.",["Air in the loop or low coolant after a leak or repair","Seized or worn pump D","High resistance in supply, ground or control wiring","Control module software judging the pump wrongly"],["Check engine light","Higher temperature in the circuit served by pump D","Possible power reduction to protect components"],2,3,["P2B66","P2B6A","P2B6C","P2BA1","P2C48","P261B"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור‏ D — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2C4A:["Clutch Actuator Position Sensor Circuit","The clutch actuator position sensor reports how far the release mechanism of an automated or partly automated clutch has travelled, taken at the slave cylinder or inside the actuator rather than at the pedal. Typical designs are Hall sensors reading a magnet on the clutch piston. P2C4A is the general circuit fault of this sensor.",["Damaged or corroded sensor connector near the gearbox","Open supply, signal or ground wire","Position sensor on slave cylinder or actuator failed","Control module fault (Ford internal check P166F)"],["Stop-start or stop-in-gear disabled","Warning lamp or message","Automated clutch may refuse to engage or drive off"],3,3,["P2C4B","P2C4C","P2C4D","P2C4E","P2C4F","P0805"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצמד — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2C4B:["Clutch Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2C4B flags a clutch actuator position signal that is electrically valid but does not fit the situation, for example a reading that does not move when the actuator is commanded, or end stops that lie outside the learned window.",["Air or leakage in the clutch hydraulics","Sensor drift or loose sensor mounting","Clutch end positions not relearned after service","Clutch wear moving the engagement point out of range"],["Harsh or slipping clutch engagement","Stop-start disabled","Warning message about the gearbox or clutch"],3,3,["P2C4A","P2C4C","P2C4D","P2C4E","P2C50","P0806"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצמד — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2C4C:["Clutch Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Low","P2C4C means the signal of the clutch actuator position sensor has fallen below its valid band. Ford documents it in its gasoline OBD summaries for 2020–2023 and 2024 under Clutch Actuation Position: the check runs continuously and needs less than one second to register the fault, and in the 2024 version it is reported as base code P2C4A with failure type 11.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","5 V reference supply missing or shorted","Position sensor failed internally"],["Stop-start or stop-in-gear unavailable","Warning lamp or message"],2,3,["P2C4A","P2C4B","P2C4D","P2C4E","P2C50","P08A9"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצמד — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2C4D:["Clutch Actuator Position Sensor Circuit High","P2C4D is set when the clutch actuator position signal rises above its upper limit. Ford lists it beside P2C4C in its 2020–2023 and 2024 gasoline OBD summaries: continuous monitoring, under one second to detect, and in 2024 reported as P2C4A with failure type 12. Ford does not state whether the MIL comes on.",["Open sensor ground wire","Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage","Position sensor output stuck high"],["Stop-start or stop-in-gear unavailable","Warning lamp or message"],2,3,["P2C4A","P2C4B","P2C4C","P2C4E","P2C50","P08AA"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצמד — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2C4E:["Clutch Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2C4E covers a clutch actuator position signal that jumps, drops out briefly or changes faster than the mechanism could physically move. The sensor sits in a hot, vibrating spot on the gearbox or at the actuator, so connectors, fretting contacts and chafed wires are the main suspects;",["Fretting or loose contacts in the sensor connector","Wiring chafed against the gearbox housing","Sensor or magnet loose, changing the air gap"],["Intermittent warning message","Jerky or delayed clutch engagement","Stop-start works only sometimes"],2,3,["P2C4A","P2C4B","P2C4C","P2C4D","P0809"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצמד — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2C4F:["Clutch Actuator Performance","P2C4F concerns the actuator itself, the electric motor or electro-hydraulic unit that opens and closes an automated clutch, rather than its position sensor. The code means the actuator does not reach or hold the commanded position within the expected time or effort.",["Actuator motor or gear worn or sticking","Air or leak in the clutch hydraulics","Worn clutch requiring travel beyond the learned range","Low supply voltage to the actuator"],["Difficult or impossible drive-off","Clutch slips or engages harshly","Gearbox warning and limp mode"],3,3,["P2C4A","P2C4B","P2C50","P0810","P2785"],"מפעיל מצמד — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C50:["Clutch Pedal Position Sensor A/Clutch Actuator Position Sensor Correlation","P2C50 compares two views of the same clutch: what the pedal sensor A says the driver is doing and what the sensor at the release side says the clutch is actually doing. In a hydraulic system both move together, so a lasting gap points to a fault in one sensor or in the hydraulics between them.",["Air or leak in the clutch hydraulics between pedal and slave cylinder","Release-side position sensor or slave cylinder faulty","Clutch pedal sensor A drifted or misadjusted","Positions not relearned after clutch or sensor work"],["Stop-start unavailable","Warning lamp or message","Clutch pedal feel may be soft or inconsistent"],3,3,["P2C4A","P2C4B","P08A7","P08A8","P08B9"],""],P2C51:["Fuel Level Sensor A/B Correlation","Saddle tanks have two chambers and therefore two level senders, A and B; the engine module combines both resistances into one fuel level. GM's bulletin PI0926 for the 2011–2013 Equinox and Terrain shows this layout, with each sender reading about 40 Ω when full. P2C51 means the two senders disagree more than the tank design allows.",["Worn resistor track or sticking float on one sender","Jet pump not transferring fuel between the tank halves","Corroded connector adding resistance on one sender","Wrong or misassembled sender after tank work"],["Fuel gauge inaccurate or not reading full after filling","Check engine lamp","Range display jumps"],2,1,["P0461","P2066","P25B2","P0460","P2065"],"חיישן מפלס דלק‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2C52:["Cylinder 1 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Min Limit","Engines with two injectors per cylinder call the second one injector B; with port plus direct injection that is usually one of the two sets, but which one is the maker's choice. For every B injector the engine control learns an offset, a correction for the dead time between the electrical command and the start of real fuel flow.",["Injector B of cylinder 1 leaking at the seat and adding fuel after closing","Replacement injector of a different flow rating or not matched to the engine software","Learned values or engine software not up to date (Volvo pairs an update with an adaptation reset for the related Max codes)","Supply pressure on this injector set higher than the model assumes (regulator)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Long hot start or rough first seconds, possibly misfire on cylinder 1","Possibly fuel smell or higher consumption"],2,1,["P2C53","P02CC","P02CD","P21CF","P2BF1","P0301"],""],P2C53:["Cylinder 1 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Max Limit","P2C53 is the opposite end of the injector B offset learn on cylinder 1: the engine control has lengthened the command as far as it may, and the cylinder still gets less fuel than requested. Ford patents describe the offset as the time the pintle and the driver circuit need before fuel moves, so a sticky or varnished valve or a weak supply raises it.",["Engine software (Volvo TJ 36016: update, then reset injector adaptations in VIDA)","Varnish or deposits in injector B of cylinder 1, slow opening","Corroded or loose connector, chafed wire or voltage drop at this injector","Air leak at the intake runner of cylinder 1 (only where the learn uses exhaust oxygen)"],["Check engine light","Usually no change in how the car drives","Possibly uneven idle or lean misfire on cylinder 1"],2,1,["P2C52","P02CD","P02CC","P21CF","P2BF0","P0301"],""],P2C54:["Cylinder 2 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Min Limit","P2C54 concerns injector B of cylinder 2 and the lower limit of its learned offset. Reaching the floor means the control had to keep cutting the opening time because the injector delivers too much, typically at the short pulses where dead time dominates. Plausible reasons are a seat that drips after closing, a replacement injector of a different flow class, or a rail pressure higher than the model assumes.",["Injector B of cylinder 2 leaking at the seat and adding fuel after closing","Replacement injector of a different flow rating or not matched to the engine software","Learned values or engine software not up to date (Volvo pairs an update with an adaptation reset for the related Max codes)","Supply pressure on this injector set higher than the model assumes (regulator)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Long hot start or rough first seconds, possibly misfire on cylinder 2","Possibly fuel smell or higher consumption"],2,1,["P2C55","P02CE","P02CF","P21D0","P2BF1","P2BF3","P0302"],""],P2C55:["Cylinder 2 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Max Limit","P2C55 reports that injector B of cylinder 2 needs the maximum offset the engine control allows: even with the longest permitted extension of its pulse it underdelivers. Volvo lists it in Technical Journal 36016 for 2022 model-year cars with engine variants L1 and 06.",["Engine software (Volvo TJ 36016: update, then reset injector adaptations in VIDA)","Varnish or deposits in injector B of cylinder 2, slow opening","Corroded or loose connector, chafed wire or voltage drop at this injector","Air leak at the intake runner of cylinder 2 (only where the learn uses exhaust oxygen)"],["Check engine light","Usually no change in how the car drives","Possibly uneven idle or lean misfire on cylinder 2"],2,1,["P2C54","P02CF","P02CE","P21D0","P2BF0","P2BF2","P0302"],""],P2C56:["Cylinder 3 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Min Limit","P2C56 is set once injector B of cylinder 3 has its learned offset stuck at the minimum. How such a value is learned is shown in Ford patents for engines that combine both injection types: with the lift pump switched off, the port injectors fire one cylinder at a time while the others run on direct injection, and how far the low-pressure rail sags after every pulse shows how much fuel that injector really released.",["Injector B of cylinder 3 leaking at the seat and adding fuel after closing","Replacement injector of a different flow rating or not matched to the engine software","Learned values or engine software not up to date (Volvo pairs an update with an adaptation reset for the related Max codes)","Supply pressure on this injector set higher than the model assumes (regulator)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Long hot start or rough first seconds, possibly misfire on cylinder 3","Possibly fuel smell or higher consumption"],2,1,["P2C57","P02D0","P02D1","P21D1","P2BF1","P2BF3","P0303"],""],P2C57:["Cylinder 3 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Max Limit","P2C57 is the upper-limit counterpart for injector B on cylinder 3. A Ford patent on engines with two injector types explains why each injector needs its own learned offset: it is the time needed to overcome the inertia of the pintle and of the driver circuit, and it shifts with battery voltage and temperature.",["Engine software (Volvo TJ 36016: update, then reset injector adaptations in VIDA)","Varnish or deposits in injector B of cylinder 3, slow opening","Corroded or loose connector, chafed wire or voltage drop at this injector","Air leak at the intake runner of cylinder 3 (only where the learn uses exhaust oxygen)"],["Check engine light","Usually no change in how the car drives","Possibly uneven idle or lean misfire on cylinder 3"],2,1,["P2C56","P02D1","P02D0","P21D1","P2BF0","P2BF2","P0303"],""],P2C58:["Cylinder 4 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Min Limit","P2C58 marks the minimum limit of the injector B offset on cylinder 4. Useful for diagnosis is a look at the A injector of the same cylinder: if P02D2 is stored as well, both valves seem to overdeliver, which points to something both learns share, such as the measurement or the cylinder itself, rather than to one injector.",["Injector B of cylinder 4 leaking at the seat and adding fuel after closing","Replacement injector of a different flow rating or not matched to the engine software","Learned values or engine software not up to date (Volvo pairs an update with an adaptation reset for the related Max codes)","Supply pressure on this injector set higher than the model assumes (regulator)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Long hot start or rough first seconds, possibly misfire on cylinder 4","Possibly fuel smell or higher consumption"],2,1,["P2C59","P02D2","P02D3","P21D2","P2BF1","P2BF3","P0304"],""],P2C59:["Cylinder 4 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Max Limit","P2C59 tells that injector B of cylinder 4 has reached the maximum learned offset, so its delivery falls short even with the longest allowed correction. Volvo's Technical Journal 36016 includes it among four codes, one per cylinder from 1 to 4 and all at the Max limit, on 2022 model-year cars; the first step there is software, not parts.",["Engine software (Volvo TJ 36016: update, then reset injector adaptations in VIDA)","Varnish or deposits in injector B of cylinder 4, slow opening","Corroded or loose connector, chafed wire or voltage drop at this injector","Air leak at the intake runner of cylinder 4 (only where the learn uses exhaust oxygen)"],["Check engine light","Usually no change in how the car drives","Possibly uneven idle or lean misfire on cylinder 4"],2,1,["P2C58","P02D3","P02D2","P21D2","P2BF0","P2BF2","P0304"],""],P2C5A:["Cylinder 5 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Min Limit","P2C5A can only occur on engines with at least five cylinders and indicates that cylinder 5's injector B has had its learned offset pulled down to the lower bound. The control has removed as much opening time as it may, yet the cylinder still gets more fuel than intended from this valve. On V engines with Ford numbering cylinder 5 opens bank 2; GM numbering puts it on bank 1.",["Injector B of cylinder 5 leaking at the seat and adding fuel after closing","Replacement injector of a different flow rating or not matched to the engine software","Old learned values not reset after injector or software work","Supply pressure on this injector set higher than the model assumes (regulator)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Long hot start or rough first seconds, possibly misfire on cylinder 5","Possibly fuel smell or higher consumption"],2,1,["P2C5B","P02D4","P02D5","P21D3","P2BF1","P2BF3","P0305"],""],P2C5B:["Cylinder 5 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Max Limit","P2C5B is the Max limit for injector B on cylinder 5, found on five-, six- and eight-cylinder engines. With two injection systems, one set may stay idle in parts of the map, and fuel left in a resting nozzle can varnish and slow the valve; the learned offset then climbs until it hits the ceiling.",["Varnish or deposits in injector B of cylinder 5, slow opening","Corroded or loose connector, chafed wire or voltage drop at this injector","Old adaptation values left at the limit after a repair or software change","Air leak at the intake runner of cylinder 5 (only where the learn uses exhaust oxygen)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Possibly uneven idle or lean misfire on cylinder 5"],2,1,["P2C5A","P02D5","P02D4","P21D3","P2BF0","P2BF2","P0305"],""],P2C5C:["Cylinder 6 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Min Limit","P2C5C reports that the injector B offset for cylinder 6 has been learned down to its minimum. In practice the most telling check is the learned value itself: a scan tool that shows the offsets of all B injectors makes one outlier obvious.",["Injector B of cylinder 6 leaking at the seat and adding fuel after closing","Replacement injector of a different flow rating or not matched to the engine software","Old learned values not reset after injector or software work","Supply pressure on this injector set higher than the model assumes (regulator)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Long hot start or rough first seconds, possibly misfire on cylinder 6","Possibly fuel smell or higher consumption"],2,1,["P2C5D","P02D6","P02D7","P21D4","P2BF1","P2BF3","P0306"],""],P2C5D:["Cylinder 6 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Max Limit","P2C5D says injector B of cylinder 6 needs the largest learned offset allowed. Because the offset depends on how quickly the driver can energise the coil, electrical causes deserve the first look: a corroded or loose connector, chafed wiring or a supply voltage that sags on that injector lengthen the real opening delay. If a circuit code for the same valve (P21D4) is present, that comes first.",["Varnish or deposits in injector B of cylinder 6, slow opening","Corroded or loose connector, chafed wire or voltage drop at this injector","Old adaptation values left at the limit after a repair or software change","Air leak at the intake runner of cylinder 6 (only where the learn uses exhaust oxygen)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Possibly uneven idle or lean misfire on cylinder 6"],2,1,["P2C5C","P02D7","P02D6","P21D4","P2BF0","P2BF2","P0306"],""],P2C5E:["Cylinder 7 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Min Limit","P2C5E belongs to cylinder 7 and therefore to engines with at least seven cylinders, in practice V8s. It is stored when the learned offset of injector B has been driven to its floor: the valve gives more fuel than the model predicts even at the shortest permitted command.",["Injector B of cylinder 7 leaking at the seat and adding fuel after closing","Replacement injector of a different flow rating or not matched to the engine software","Old learned values not reset after injector or software work","Supply pressure on this injector set higher than the model assumes (regulator)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Long hot start or rough first seconds, possibly misfire on cylinder 7","Possibly fuel smell or higher consumption"],2,1,["P2C5F","P02D8","P02D9","P21D5","P2BF1","P2BF3","P0307"],""],P2C5F:["Cylinder 7 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Max Limit","P2C5F, again a V8 code, flags injector B of cylinder 7 whose learned offset is pinned at its maximum. A point often missed is the learn history: when an injector is replaced or software changes, old adaptation values can sit at the limit until they are cleared. Volvo, for example, insists on resetting the injector adaptations with the engine running after its software update for the related four-cylinder codes.",["Varnish or deposits in injector B of cylinder 7, slow opening","Corroded or loose connector, chafed wire or voltage drop at this injector","Old adaptation values left at the limit after a repair or software change","Air leak at the intake runner of cylinder 7 (only where the learn uses exhaust oxygen)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Possibly uneven idle or lean misfire on cylinder 7"],2,1,["P2C5E","P02D9","P02D8","P21D5","P2BF0","P2BF2","P0307"],""],P2C60:["Cylinder 8 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Min Limit","P2C60 is the minimum-limit code for injector B on cylinder 8, the last cylinder of a V8 and the end of this code series. Its A-side twin P02DA is documented by GM for the L5P diesel and by Land Rover for a 5.0 V8, but the B version has no public manufacturer source at all.",["Injector B of cylinder 8 leaking at the seat and adding fuel after closing","Replacement injector of a different flow rating or not matched to the engine software","Old learned values not reset after injector or software work","Supply pressure on this injector set higher than the model assumes (regulator)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Long hot start or rough first seconds, possibly misfire on cylinder 8","Possibly fuel smell or higher consumption"],2,1,["P2C61","P02DA","P02DB","P21D6","P2BF1","P2BF3","P0308"],""],P2C61:["Cylinder 8 Fuel Injector B Offset Learning At Max Limit","P2C61 closes the series: injector B of cylinder 8 has driven its learned offset into the ceiling, so this valve stays short of fuel despite the longest correction allowed. Because a weak supply pump or low rail pressure would starve every injector of the same set, a Max code on a single cylinder narrows the search to that valve, its wiring or the air path of that cylinder.",["Varnish or deposits in injector B of cylinder 8, slow opening","Corroded or loose connector, chafed wire or voltage drop at this injector","Old adaptation values left at the limit after a repair or software change","Air leak at the intake runner of cylinder 8 (only where the learn uses exhaust oxygen)"],["Check engine light","Often nothing else noticeable","Possibly uneven idle or lean misfire on cylinder 8"],2,1,["P2C60","P02DB","P02DA","P21D6","P2BF0","P2BF2","P0308"],""],P2C62:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit/Open Bank 1 Sensor 3","P2C62 points to an open trim circuit at the third oxygen probe of bank 1. Wide-band probes such as Bosch's LSU 4.9 carry a trimming resistor in the connector on a pin of its own (RT/IA) that sets each probe's characteristic; the engine module reads it to scale the pump current, so with the lead broken the signal still moves but with the wrong gain.",["Trim line broken or terminal pushed back in the probe connector","Moisture or corrosion in the connector of the rear probe","Trimming resistor in the probe connector open (probe replacement)"],["MIL on, usually without noticeable driving change","Catalyst or aftertreatment monitors not completing"],2,1,["P2C63","P2C64","P2C65","P2626","P22B5","P0142"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P2C63:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit Low Bank 1 Sensor 3","P2C63 reports that the oxygen value from the third exhaust sensor of bank 1 has dropped below its physically possible minimum. Despite the trim wording, GM uses it on the 3.0L Duramax diesel for the O2 signal of NOx sensor 3, which sits behind the second catalyst: table 25OBDG04B (2025) fails a reading under -6 percent in 100 of 200 samples on a 25 ms task, with the engine running, supply above 11 V and the sensor…",["Engine harness chafed or shorted (GM 3.0L LM2 - at the generator or the crankcase pressure regulator clamp)","Third exhaust sensor (on GM diesels NOx sensor 3) reporting an implausibly low O2 value","Corroded or loose sensor connector"],["MIL on after two trips","On the GM LM2 often many other codes, rough running or blown fuses when the harness is damaged","Aftertreatment monitors not completing"],2,1,["P2C62","P2C64","P2C65","P23AE","P2627"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P2C64:["O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit High Bank 1 Sensor 3","P2C64 is the high-side partner of P2C63: the oxygen reading attributed to sensor 3 of bank 1 climbs above what the probe can physically deliver. On GM's 3.0L Duramax diesel the value comes from NOx sensor 3 behind the second catalyst, and table 25OBDG04B sets the code once that O2 reading exceeds 29 percent, clearly more than the roughly 21 percent of fresh air, in 100 of 200 samples under the same enable conditions…",["Third exhaust sensor (on GM diesels NOx sensor 3) delivering an implausibly high O2 value","Engine harness chafed or shorted (GM 3.0L LM2, PIT5751C)","Moisture or corrosion in the sensor connector"],["MIL on after two trips","Further NOx sensor or aftertreatment codes stored"],2,1,["P2C62","P2C63","P2C65","P23AF","P2628"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P2C65:["O2 Sensor Out of Range During Deceleration Bank 1 Sensor 3","P2C65 is the overrun plausibility check for the third oxygen sensor of bank 1: with fuel cut on deceleration the exhaust is close to fresh air, so the reading must land inside a known window. GM's 3.0L Duramax runs this test for sensor 1 under P2297, where table 25OBDG04B compares the measured O2 value with an estimate in overrun and flags a gap above 4 or below -3.25 percent (Type B).",["Third exhaust sensor aged or drifting (wrong value in fresh air)","Exhaust leak ahead of sensor 3 distorting the overrun reading","Damaged sensor wiring or chafed engine harness (GM 3.0L LM2)","Leaking injector or model error disturbing the comparison in overrun"],["MIL on, usually without noticeable driving change","Possibly stored together with other sensor 3 or NOx sensor codes"],2,1,["P2C63","P2C64","P232F","P2297","P23AD"],""],P2C66:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump A Underspeed","P2C66 reports that pump A of the electronics cooling loop, which carries heat away from inverter, DC/DC converter and often the on-board charger or drive motor, turns slower than requested. Pumps of this kind report their actual speed, and the controller compares it with the target. No manufacturer publicly documents P2C66.",["Worn bearings or a sluggish impeller","Debris or sludge in the pump or a restricted loop","Low supply voltage from fuse, relay or ground faults","Air pockets after a coolant service"],["Hybrid/EV system warning and check engine light","Reduced drive power or slower charging","Electronics temperature rises faster than usual"],3,3,["P2C67","P2C68","P0CEA","P0CE9","P2E47","U063D"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ A — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2C67:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump A Overspeed","With P2C67 the electronics coolant pump A runs faster than commanded. A centrifugal pump speeds up as soon as it loses load, so air in the loop is the leading suspect, followed by a loose impeller or a faulty speed signal.",["Air in the electronics loop after service or from a leak","Low coolant level in the low-temperature reservoir","Impeller slipping on the shaft or broken","Implausible speed feedback from the pump electronics"],["Coolant or drive system warning in the cluster","Churning or gurgling noise from the pump","Reduced power when electronics temperatures climb"],2,3,["P2C66","P2C68","P2B2A","P0CEA","P2E48","P2E46"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ A — מהירות יתר"],P2C68:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump A Stuck/Stalled","P2C68 means the electronics coolant pump A has power and a command, yet its rotor does not turn or stops. Brushless pumps notice this themselves from a failed start attempt or high current with no rotation and report it to the controller. No manufacturer publicly documents P2C68.",["Seized bearing or impeller in pump A","Foreign matter or sludge blocking the impeller","Burnt winding or failed pump electronics","Coolant frozen due to weak antifreeze"],["Drive system warning, check engine light","Strongly reduced power or charging interrupted","No pump noise when the pump is activated with a scan tool"],3,3,["P2C66","P2C67","P0CE9","P0CEA","P2E49","U063D"],""],P2C69:["Drive Motor A Phase X Current","P2C69 is the general fault for the current in phase X of drive motor A, as the inverter measures it. J2012 places the X, Y and Z series next to the U/V/W codes P0A5D-P0A65 without public explanation; in motor design those letters usually name the second three-phase winding set of a dual-winding machine.",["Phase X current sensor or its supply/signal circuit in the inverter faulty","High-voltage phase lead X loose, burnt or poorly joined at motor or inverter","Internal inverter fault (switching leg or measurement electronics of the X/Y/Z set)","Winding fault in phase X of drive motor A"],["Hybrid or electric drive warning and MIL on","Reduced electric drive power or vehicle not ready to drive","Further phase current or inverter codes stored at the same time"],4,3,["P2C6A","P2C6B","P2C6C","P2C6F","P0A5D","P0A78"],"זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A X"],P2C6A:["Drive Motor A Phase X Current Low","P2C6A means that too little current is seen in phase X of drive motor A while the inverter is driving it, which typically points to an open phase or a dead sensor. No carmaker documents the code publicly.",["Phase X lead or terminal open or high-resistance between inverter and motor","Phase X current sensor reading near zero (sensor or its supply failed)","Switching leg for phase X in the inverter not conducting","Open winding of phase X inside drive motor A"],["Hybrid or drive system warning and MIL on","Noticeably weaker or jerky electric drive, or drive disabled"],4,3,["P2C69","P2C6B","P2C6D","P2C70","P0A5E"],"זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A X — ערך נמוך"],P2C6B:["Drive Motor A Phase X Current High","P2C6B flags an overcurrent in phase X of drive motor A. X, Y and Z name the second three-phase winding set of a dual-winding machine, which a Mitsubishi Electric patent shows with its own inverter bridge and a current sensor per phase. No carmaker documents P2C6B publicly.",["Turn-to-turn or ground short in the phase X winding of drive motor A","IGBT/MOSFET of the X leg in the inverter shorted or failing to turn off","Phase X current sensor reading too high (gain or offset drift)","Chafed or wet phase X lead touching another phase or the housing"],["Hybrid or drive system warning with MIL on","Sudden loss of electric drive, vehicle may not become ready","Isolation fault codes stored at the same time if the winding touches the housing"],4,3,["P2C69","P2C6A","P2C6E","P2C71","P0A5F","P2E1B"],"זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A X — ערך גבוה"],P2C6C:["Drive Motor A Phase Y Current","P2C6C is the umbrella code for the current in phase Y of drive motor A, the middle phase of the second X/Y/Z winding set. No manufacturer documents it publicly. Ford's 2019 hybrid summary explains what such phase current codes collect: the inverter is watched for overcurrent, current sensor faults and current regulation faults, and the result is stored per phase.",["Inverter cannot regulate the phase Y current to its command (control or gate drive fault)","Loose, corroded or overheated phase Y terminal at inverter or motor","Phase Y current reading implausible against the other two phases","Partial winding fault in phase Y of the motor"],["Hybrid or drive warning, MIL on","Reduced electric torque or jerky drive","Vehicle not ready to drive in severe cases"],4,3,["P2C6D","P2C6E","P2C69","P2C6F","P2E1F","P0A60"],"זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Y"],P2C6D:["Drive Motor A Phase Y Current Low","P2C6D is set when phase Y of drive motor A carries too little current while the inverter drives it, the typical signature of an open phase. No manufacturer documents P2C6D publicly. A test of this kind can run at start-up: on its 2019 power-split hybrids Ford checks the phase circuits right after power-up and declares a fault if less than 5 A flows during the 100 ms test.",["Phase Y lead, busbar or terminal open or high-resistance","Y switching leg of the inverter not conducting (switch or gate driver)","Phase Y current sensor or its supply failed, reading near zero","Open phase Y winding inside the motor"],["Hybrid or drive warning and MIL","Noticeably weaker electric drive, vibration or humming under load"],4,3,["P2C6C","P2C6E","P2C6A","P2C70","P0A61","P0C00"],"זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Y — ערך נמוך"],P2C6E:["Drive Motor A Phase Y Current High","P2C6E reports that too much current flows in the Y phase of drive motor A, which sits in the machine's second winding set. No manufacturer documents P2C6E publicly. A Hyundai bulletin shows what usually lies behind a phase overcurrent: on the 2017 Ioniq Hybrid, coolant leaking inside the traction motor set the high codes of phases U, V and W (P0A5F, P0A62, P0A65), often with the isolation fault P0AA6.",["Coolant or moisture inside the motor degrading winding insulation","Short between phase Y and another phase or the stator core","Shorted power switch in the Y leg of the inverter","Phase Y current sensor reading too high"],["Hybrid warning and MIL, often with an isolation fault code","Weak acceleration or electric drive switched off","Electric air conditioning compressor disabled"],4,3,["P2C6C","P2C6D","P2C6B","P2C71","P0A62","P0AA6"],"זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Y — ערך גבוה"],P2C6F:["Drive Motor A Phase Z Current","P2C6F is the general current fault for phase Z, the third phase of the second winding set of drive motor A. No manufacturer documents it publicly. Whether Z is measured at all depends on the design: the Mitsubishi Electric patent fits a sensor to each of X, Y and Z, while a Hyundai patent describes inverters that measure two phase currents and calculate the third, since all three must add up to zero.",["Error in the X or Y current measurement corrupting a calculated Z value","Phase Z terminal or busbar loose, corroded or overheated","Fault in the Z switching leg or its gate driver","Damaged phase Z winding"],["Hybrid or drive system warning with MIL","Reduced electric power, possibly engine-only operation on hybrids","Other X/Y phase codes stored alongside"],4,3,["P2C70","P2C71","P2C69","P2C6C","P2E23","P0A63"],"זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Z"],P2C70:["Drive Motor A Phase Z Current Low","P2C70 means phase Z of drive motor A delivers too little current although the inverter is commanding it. No manufacturer documents P2C70 publicly. GM's missing-phase check for the U/V/W set shows the principle: the 2016 Volt only judges a phase while the rotor angle sits near that phase axis and enough current is requested, and fails it when the peak stays under 9 A, Type A with MIL after one trip.",["Phase Z lead or terminal open or burnt","Phase Z current sensor stuck near zero","Z leg of the inverter not switching","Open phase Z winding in the motor"],["MIL and hybrid or drive warning","Loss of torque and vibration from the motor under load"],4,3,["P2C6F","P2C71","P2C6A","P2C6D","P0A64","P0A5E"],"זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Z — ערך נמוך"],P2C71:["Drive Motor A Phase Z Current High","P2C71 reports overcurrent in phase Z of drive motor A, the last phase of the second winding set. No manufacturer documents P2C71 publicly. Once overcurrent is detected the inverter has to bring the machine into a safe state, and the Mitsubishi Electric patent on dual-winding drives deals with exactly that: when the battery link opens, each winding set is moved in steps from a phase short circuit to all switches off,…",["Shorted power semiconductor in the Z leg","Short in the phase Z winding or lead, to another phase or ground","Phase Z current sensor reading too high or noisy","Inverter control software reacting wrongly to transients"],["Sudden loss of drive power with hybrid or drive warning","MIL on, vehicle may not restart into ready mode"],4,3,["P2C6F","P2C70","P2C6B","P2C6E","P0A65","P0A78"],"זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Z — ערך גבוה"],P2C72:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Cooling System Performance","P2C72 says the coolant loop serving the hybrid or EV power electronics (inverter, DC/DC converter, often the charger) does not cool as expected. CARB requires a functional check of inverter cooling performance where feasible, on top of the circuit checks of pump and sensors. No manufacturer documents P2C72 publicly.",["Low coolant level or leak in the electronics loop","Air trapped in the loop after service","Electronics coolant pump delivering too little flow","Clogged low-temperature radiator or failed cooling fan"],["Hybrid system warning and MIL","Reduced power, no EV mode, especially in heat or under load","Inverter over-temperature codes stored as well"],2,3,["P0A93","P0C31","P2C66","P2C67","P2C68","P0A3C"],"מערכת קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C73:["Active Grille Air Shutter C Stuck On","Some vehicles split the grille opening into several separately driven flaps; shutter C is a third one next to A (usually upper) and B (lower). P2C73 says flap C stays open although the engine module asks it to close – the counterpart of P05FE, which covers a flap that will not move to its target. Nobody publishes P2C73 itself.",["Debris, snow or ice holding the louvres of shutter C open","Actuator motor or gear of shutter C failed in the open position","Linkage or flap frame bent or broken, e.g. after minor front damage","Water ingress and corrosion at the bumper connector of the actuator"],["Engine warning lamp, sometimes a grille shutter or air flap message","Slightly higher fuel consumption at motorway speed","Slower engine and heater warm-up in cold weather"],2,1,["P05FE","P2C74","P2C75","P05A0","P05AF","P2C76"],"תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ C — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2C74:["Active Grille Air Shutter C Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2C74 judges the drive of grille shutter C: the command to the actuator or the feedback it returns does not fit the expected range, so the flap may move sluggishly, erratically or not at all. Hyundai is the documented user.",["Water ingress and corroded pins at the bumper connectors of the flap actuator or sensor","Chafed or broken front bumper harness","Actuator of shutter C faulty or responding too slowly","Flap position sensor of the lower air flap faulty"],["Engine warning lamp and an active air flap warning message","Flap does not move or moves jerkily","Possibly an unrelated low engine oil message at the same time"],2,1,["P05FE","P2C73","P2C75","P05A3","P05B2","P2C77"],"תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2C75:["Active Grille Air Shutter Module C Over Temperature","Smart grille shutter actuators carry their own driver chip and protect it by temperature. P2C75 is that self-protection for shutter C: the module reports its electronics as overheated and stops driving the motor. No manufacturer documents P2C75;",["Flap frozen, jammed or bent so the motor works against a stop","Partly shorted motor winding drawing excess current","Internal fault of the actuator electronics"],["Engine warning lamp, often intermittent","Shutter C stops moving until the module has cooled down"],2,1,["P2C73","P2C74","P05C0","P05C1","P2C78"],"מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ C — חום יתר"],P2C76:["Active Grille Air Shutter D Stuck On","Shutter D would be the fourth individually driven grille flap. P2C76 reports that this flap remains open when the engine module wants it shut. Not a single published document uses a shutter D: GM and Ford stop at A and B, and Hyundai's 2026 Palisade reaches C. The meaning therefore follows the stuck-open codes of the other flaps, P05A0 for A and P2C73 for C.",["Leaves, stones or other debris wedged in the louvres of shutter D","Actuator of shutter D failed while the flap was open","Flap frame or linkage damaged by a front impact"],["Engine warning lamp and possibly a grille shutter message","Longer warm-up and weaker heater output in winter","Marginally higher fuel use"],2,1,["P2C77","P2C78","P2C73","P05A0","P05AF"],"תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ D — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2C77:["Active Grille Air Shutter D Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2C77 flags the drive circuit of a fourth grille shutter D as implausible: the actuator does not respond to its command in the expected way, or the signal it returns lies outside the permitted window. No manufacturer publishes a shutter D, so the code is reserved for designs with four separately powered flaps. Comparable faults on other flaps show where to look.",["Corroded connector or damaged wiring to the actuator of shutter D","Actuator of shutter D faulty, including faulty internal software","Stiff or partly blocked flap slowing the actuator response"],["Engine warning lamp","Shutter D no longer follows commands"],2,1,["P2C76","P2C78","P2C74","P05A3","P05B2"],"תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2C78:["Active Grille Air Shutter Module D Over Temperature","P2C78 is the over-temperature report of the actuator module for a fourth grille shutter D: its driver electronics have exceeded their thermal limit and the output stage has been switched off to protect it.",["Motor stalled against ice or a damaged linkage","Partly shorted actuator coil","Heat soak near the radiator combined with constant repositioning"],["Intermittent engine warning lamp","Shutter D stops moving for a while"],2,1,["P2C76","P2C77","P2C75","P05C0","P05C1"],"מודול תריס אוויר גריל פעיל‏ D — חום יתר"],P2C79:["NOx Adsorber - Sulfur Limit Exceeded","P2C79 says the sulfur load held in the NOx adsorber (lean NOx trap) has reached the limit the engine computer allows. Sulfur from fuel and oil occupies the storage sites more firmly than NOx, so capacity shrinks until a desulfation is run: rich phases with the trap above roughly 550 °C, as a Volkswagen patent explains.",["Desulfation never completes because the trap stays too cool (short trips, idling)","Fuel with high sulfur content (outside EU/US ultra-low-sulfur grades)","Increased oil consumption carrying sulfur-bearing additives into the exhaust","Faulty exhaust temperature or lambda signal that blocks or aborts the rich desulfation phases","Thermally aged trap whose sulfur can no longer be removed"],["Check engine light","Higher fuel consumption from repeated rich regeneration attempts","Occasional rotten-egg smell from the exhaust","Raised NOx emissions, possible failure at an emissions test"],2,1,["P2000","P2001","P21B2","P21B3","P21B4"],""],P2C7A:["SCR NOx Catalyst Efficiency Below Threshold Bank 1 Catalyst 2","P2C7A concerns the second SCR catalyst on bank 1, typically an underfloor brick behind a first SCR stage. GM uses it on its 3.0-litre Duramax diesel: the 2020 table 20OBDG04 compares the efficiency of this catalyst, taken from the NOx sensors ahead of and behind it, with a reference built from the inlet NOx and a calibrated offset.",["ECM software that flags the second SCR falsely (GM 3.0 l diesel bulletins)","Second SCR catalyst aged, poisoned or with reduced ammonia storage","Drifting NOx sensor in front of or behind the second SCR","Poor DEF quality or under-dosing by the reductant injector","Exhaust leak between the sensors that distorts the NOx readings"],["MIL on after one trip","Exhaust fluid or emissions warning in the instrument cluster","Usually no noticeable change in driving behaviour"],3,3,["P20EE","P20EF","P2BA6","P2BA9","P20F4"],""],P2C7B:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Control Performance","The turbine inlet valve opens or blocks an exhaust path to a turbine: in a two-stage system it lets gas bypass the small high-pressure stage, in a sequential layout it brings the second turbo in. GM's patent US8276378B2 shows such a bypass valve run in closed loop with its own position control.",["Valve or shaft stiff from soot and corrosion","Worn electric actuator (motor, gears)","Loose or bent linkage between actuator and valve","Position feedback that misreports the true valve opening"],["Reduced power or hesitation in the boost changeover range","Fluctuating boost pressure","Check engine light, possibly limp mode"],3,3,["P22D2","P22D3","P22D5","P2C7F","P0299"],"בקרת שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C7C:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Supply Circuit Low","P2C7C reports that the voltage feeding the turbine inlet valve actuator is too low. Electric turbo actuators of this kind combine a DC motor, gearing and a position sensor and rely on a stable feed; BorgWarner's patent on such an actuator adds a spring that returns the valve to a default position when power is lost. No manufacturer documents P2C7C publicly.",["Blown fuse or faulty supply relay for the actuator","Corroded or loose pins at the actuator connector","Chafed or broken feed or ground wire near the hot turbo area","Defective supply output in the control module"],["Check engine light","Low boost and reduced power","Further turbo actuator codes stored at the same time"],2,3,["P22CF","P22D0","P22D1","P2C7D","P2B98"],"אספקת שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2C7D:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Motor Driver High Current","P2C7D is set when the output stage driving the turbine inlet valve motor carries more current than permitted. H-bridge chips such as NXP's MC33926 limit motor current and flag overcurrent to the controller, and a Korean patent on electric turbo actuators explains how a DC motor that cannot reach its target draws excess current and is switched off before it burns out. No manufacturer documents P2C7D publicly.",["Valve jammed by soot or corrosion, motor stalls","Shorted windings in the actuator motor","Motor leads chafed and shorted to each other or to ground","Defective H-bridge driver in the control module"],["Sudden loss of boost and power","Check engine light, limp mode","Code returns immediately after clearing when the valve is commanded"],3,3,["P2C7B","P2C7C","P2C7E","P22D1","P2B99"],""],P2C7E:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Motor Driver Overtemperature","P2C7E indicates that the driver circuit for the turbine inlet valve motor has grown too hot. Driver chips monitor their own junction temperature and switch off beyond a limit, as the data sheet of NXP's MC33926 H-bridge shows. No manufacturer documents P2C7E publicly;",["Binding valve that keeps the motor under constant load","Partially shorted motor windings raising current and heat","Actuator electronics overheated by missing heat shield or poor cooling","Defective driver stage reporting overtemperature"],["Loss of boost after a longer drive or under high load","Check engine light, possibly limp mode","Fault may disappear after the engine has cooled down"],3,3,["P2C7D","P2C7B","P2C7C","P2B99"],"דרייבר מנוע שסתום כניסת טורבינת מגדש טורבו — חום יתר"],P2C7F:["Turbocharger Turbine Inlet Valve Position Sensor Exceeded Learning Limit","P2C7F means the turbine inlet valve's position sensor has delivered an end-stop value outside the window the module accepts during its learning routine. Electric turbo valves are periodically driven against their stops and the reading there is stored as a reference; Ford's patent US9243553B2 explains for wastegates why this reference has to be refreshed, since hot linkages change length.",["Carbon deposits preventing the valve from reaching its end stop","Replaced actuator or turbocharger without a completed learn procedure","Bent or worn linkage shifting the end positions","Position sensor or its magnet shifted on the shaft"],["Check engine light","Inconsistent boost during changeover between turbine paths","Reduced power in some engines"],2,3,["P22D5","P22D4","P2C7B","P2B93","P2B97"],""],P2C80:["AIR System Pump Overspeed Bank 1","P2C80 says the secondary air pump on bank 1 is turning faster than it should. Newer designs use a brushless motor whose speed is measured: an FCA patent describes a pump with a Hall sensor and target wheel so the controller can infer the air mass delivered from the revolutions and adjust pump speed.",["Outlet hose detached or split so the pump runs without back-pressure","Damaged impeller or loose coupling between motor and impeller","Faulty speed signal (Hall sensor) or its wiring","Defective control electronics inside the pump"],["Check engine light","Louder or higher-pitched pump noise after a cold start","Secondary air readiness not completed, emissions test may fail"],2,1,["P2C81","P2C82","P2445","P2444","P0411"],"משאבת מערכת האוויר המשני — מהירות יתר (בנק 1)"],P2C81:["AIR System Pump Overtemperature Bank 1","P2C81 reports that the secondary air pump on bank 1 has become too hot. The pump is only meant to run for a short time after a cold start, until the catalyst lights off, as Hella describes; a pump with integrated electronics can sense its own temperature and protect its motor. No manufacturer documents P2C81 publicly, so thresholds are unknown; CARB requires monitoring of secondary air delivery.",["Pump running too long (many short cold starts, relay stuck on)","Clogged intake filter or blocked outlet path","Worn bearings or debris increasing friction","Moisture or condensate inside the pump"],["Check engine light","Pump stops early or does not run on the next cold start","Hot smell or grinding noise from the pump"],2,1,["P2C80","P2C82","P2444","P2445","P0418"],"משאבת מערכת האוויר המשני — חום יתר (בנק 1)"],P2C82:["AIR System Pump Supply Voltage Circuit Bank 1","P2C82 points to a fault in the supply voltage circuit of the bank 1 secondary air pump. Conventional pumps are switched on by a relay; pumps with their own electronics, like the brushless design in an FCA patent, receive a feed and can judge whether the voltage arriving there is plausible. No manufacturer documents P2C82 publicly;",["Blown high-current fuse for the pump","Relay with burnt or sticking contacts","Corroded or loose pump connector","Damaged feed or ground wire to the pump"],["Check engine light","No pump noise for the first minute after a cold start","Secondary air readiness incomplete"],1,1,["P2C80","P2C81","P0418","P2445"],"משאבת מערכת האוויר המשני — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה (בנק 1)"],P2C83:["Cold Start Shift Time Too Short","California requires every part of an emission-reducing cold-start routine to be checked while it is active and its faults to be stored apart from ordinary ones. Many automatics take part in that strategy: a warm-up gearshift mode lets the engine rev further before each upshift so engine and catalyst heat faster, as a ZF patent describes. P2C83 belongs to this family.",["Clutch apply pressure too high while the fluid is cold","Fill or pressure adaptation for cold fluid outside its target, e.g. after a reset or software fault","Transmission fluid temperature signal implausible, so the wrong cold-start values are used","Pressure control solenoid sticking or overshooting"],["Harsh or jerky first upshifts after a cold start","Engine or transmission warning lamp","Shifting returns to normal once the gearbox is warm"],3,3,["P2C84","P0895","P0896","P07FF","P050A","P0711"],""],P2C84:["Cold Start Shift Time Too Long","P2C84 is the opposite verdict to P2C83: a shift observed during the active cold-start phase took longer than its calibrated limit. Cold transmission fluid is thick, so clutches fill slowly and the engine can rev up between gears; a gearbox module normally compensates with temperature-dependent pressure and fill adaptation. When that is not enough, the shift stretches out.",["Transmission fluid level low or wrong fluid specification","Shift valve or solenoid sticking when cold","Worn clutch plates needing more fill volume","Fluid temperature signal faulty, so cold-start shift values are misapplied"],["Slow, slipping upshifts with engine flare after a cold start","Engine or transmission warning lamp","Possible emergency program with a fixed gear"],3,3,["P2C83","P0896","P0895","P07FF","P0711","P0868"],""],P2C85:["Hybrid/EV Battery Voltage External Isolation Fault","P2C85 means the isolation monitor has found a fault-level loss of insulation on the vehicle side of the battery, in cables or components connected through the contactors. Mercedes-Benz uses the code in the battery management system with the text vehicle-side insulation fault.",["Insulation breakdown in the high-voltage A/C compressor","Moisture in the high-voltage PTC heater or its connector","Chafed or crushed high-voltage cable touching the body","Coolant or water inside inverter, motor or charger"],["Red high-voltage or battery warning, do not restart message","Vehicle cannot be restarted after switching off","Electric heater or A/C not working"],4,3,["P2C87","P2C88","P2C86","P0AA6","P0E74","P0DAA"],""],P2C86:["Hybrid/EV Battery Voltage Internal Isolation Warning","P2C86 is an early warning that the insulation inside the traction battery, between cells, busbars or module electronics and the pack housing, is dropping but has not yet reached the fault limit. The full internal fault is P0E74. No manufacturer documents P2C86 publicly. Mercedes-Benz shows the same content under its own code P142900 (warning, insulation inside the battery) on its 2015-2020 plug-in hybrids.",["Coolant leaking inside the battery pack","Condensation or water ingress through a failed pack seal or vent","Damaged cell sensing or busbar insulation inside the pack","Isolation measurement in the battery controller drifting"],["Battery or high-voltage service message, often without immediate limits","Charging may be refused if the value keeps falling"],4,0,["P0E74","P2C87","P2C88","P2C85","P0AA6"],"התרעת בידוד פנימי מתח סוללת מתח גבוה"],P2C87:["Hybrid/EV Battery Voltage External Isolation Warning","P2C87 is the warning stage for weakening insulation outside the battery, on the vehicle-side high-voltage network. Many systems use two limits; Volkswagen's ID.4, for example, shows a yellow lamp below 510 kOhm and a red one below 90 kOhm.",["Moisture or corrosion in an external HV component (compressor, heater, charger)","Insulation fault inside the on-board charger or DC/DC converter","Dirty or wet high-voltage connector"],["Yellow high-voltage or battery warning","Reduced power or no gear engagement on some models","Intermittent, often after rain or washing"],4,2,["P2C85","P2C88","P2C86","P0AA6","P0DAA"],"התרעת בידוד חיצוני מתח סוללת מתח גבוה"],P2C88:["Hybrid/EV Battery Voltage System Isolation Warning","P2C88 is the warning counterpart to P0AA6: the isolation resistance of the high-voltage system as a whole has fallen below a first limit without the monitor yet being able to say whether the battery or the vehicle side is to blame. Mercedes-Benz uses P2C8800 in the battery management system of the 295, 296 and 297 model series;",["Moisture in a high-voltage component that is only switched in at times (heater, compressor)","Gradual insulation aging in cables or connectors","Beginning insulation loss inside the battery pack"],["High-voltage warning message, sometimes towing not allowed notice","Electric heater stays cold if it is the leaking part"],4,2,["P0AA6","P2C85","P2C86","P2C87","P0E74"],"התרעת בידוד מערכת מתח סוללת מתח גבוה"],P2C89:["Hybrid/EV Battery System Precharge Current Too High","Before the main contactors close, the DC link capacitors are charged through a current-limiting path. P2C89 is stored when the current in that phase exceeds its limit, which points to a short or an unexpected load on the high-voltage bus, a precharge resistor that is bypassed, or a measurement error.",["Battery management or DC/DC converter software misjudging the precharge","Short or active load on the high-voltage bus during precharge","Precharge resistor shorted or main contactor closing early","Pack current sensor reading too high"],["MIL and high-voltage system warning at start-up","Electric drive or charging unavailable, engine-only on plug-in hybrids"],4,3,["P0C77","P0C78","P0AE2","P0AE1","P2BE8"],"זרם טעינה מוקדמת מערכת סוללת מתח גבוה — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2C8A:["Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module A Performance","Battery interface control modules are the satellite boards in the traction battery that measure cell voltages and temperatures and report them to the battery energy control module. P2C8A says module A is reachable but not working properly.",["Battery energy control module software or calibration error","Supply dip at the cell monitoring module (12 V battery weak, wake-up issue)","Damaged communication or supply harness inside the battery pack","Failed interface module A board"],["MIL or Service High Voltage message","12 V battery discharging while parked","Many battery communication codes stored at the same time"],4,3,["P2C8B","U01A0","U033A","U04A1"],"מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C8B:["Hybrid/EV Battery Interface Control Module B Performance","P2C8B is the performance fault for the second battery interface control module, B. In GM's Ultium bulletins it never appears alone: PIP6021 applies only if P2C8B is stored together with P2C8A and the module communication codes U3577 to U35AF, and the 2025-26 versions of PIP6081 extend it through U3584 and add U2BAA-U2BB1.",["BECM software anomaly affecting several monitoring modules at once","Weak 12 V battery causing a brownout of the monitoring modules","Connector or harness fault at interface module B","Interface module B itself defective"],["MIL or high-voltage service message","Discharged 12 V battery"],4,3,["P2C8A","U01A1","U033B","U04A2"],"מודול בקרת ממשק סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C8C:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor D Circuit","P2C8C reports a general fault in the circuit of the fourth temperature sensor of a DC/DC converter, after sensors A, B and C (P0C38, P0C3D, P0E58). Where sensor D sits inside the converter is up to each maker.",["Sensor connector or wiring damaged or corroded","Temperature sensor D in the converter defective","Sensor reference or evaluation circuit inside the converter faulty"],["MIL or hybrid system warning","Converter output limited, 12 V charging voltage may drop"],4,3,["P2C8D","P2C8E","P2C8F","P0E58","P0C38","P0C3D","P2CA5"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2C8D:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor D Circuit Range/Performance","P2C8D is the plausibility test of DC/DC converter temperature sensor D: the voltage is electrically valid, but the temperature it implies does not match what the controller expects. Typical cross-checks compare the sensor with its neighbours after a long rest or look for a value that hardly changes while the converter works hard.",["Hybrid control software level (FCA HCP update per 08-037-21)","Sensor D drifting and disagreeing with the other converter sensors","Uneven cooling of the converter, e.g. low coolant or air in the circuit"],["MIL on, with newer FCA software after one faulty drive","Reduced eTorque assist or start-stop availability"],4,3,["P2C8C","P2C8E","P2C8F","P0E59","P0C39","P0C3E"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2C8E:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor D Circuit Low","P2C8E is logged when the voltage from DC/DC converter temperature sensor D drops under the lower limit of its window. Power electronics mostly use NTC thermistors, where a falling voltage means rising temperature; an implausibly low value therefore reads as a converter far hotter than it can be.",["Sensor D signal wire shorted to ground","Thermistor shorted internally","Converter genuinely overheating because of a cooling fault"],["Hybrid or charging system warning","Converter derated right away, less electrical power available"],4,3,["P2C8C","P2C8D","P2C8F","P0E5A","P2CA6"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2C8F:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor D Circuit High","P2C8F stands for a sensor D signal stuck above the upper edge of its permitted range. With a thermistor fed through a pull-up resistor, the voltage climbs towards the reference as soon as the loop is broken, so an unplugged connector, a cracked wire or a corroded pin is the classic finding; a short to a supply voltage gives the same picture. The resulting reading would be a converter colder than any real ambient.",["Connector unplugged or sensor wire broken","Corroded or pushed-back pin at the converter connector","Signal shorted to a supply voltage"],["Hybrid system warning, MIL possible","Electrical power limited as a precaution"],4,3,["P2C8C","P2C8D","P2C8E","P0E5B","P2CA7"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2C90:["Crankcase Ventilation System - Hose A Disconnected","Under California's phase-in (20 % of 2023, 50 % of 2024, all 2025 models) every PCV hose carrying crankcase vapour must be watched for a break as large as its smallest bore, so makers moved from the general P04DB to per-hose codes. P2C90 covers hose A.",["PCV hose A pulled off, cracked or with a broken fitting","Detection software too sensitive (Ford, Toyota/Lexus and Stellantis updates)","PCV valve or make-up-air check valve not sealing","Crankcase pressure sensor or its signal faulty"],["Engine warning lamp, often without any other complaint","Oil mist or oily residue near the disconnected hose","Possibly unstable idle or lean mixture codes"],1,1,["P2C91","P04DB","P04FC","P051B","P04E1"],""],P2C91:["Crankcase Ventilation System - Hose B Disconnected","P2C91 is the second hose-specific PCV disconnection code: crankcase vapour line B is detected as open or broken, separately from line A (P2C90). Which physical hose carries the letter is the maker's choice; the code slot exists so that systems with two monitored lines can name the faulty one. The documented user is Stellantis on the Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio (2021–22) with the 2.9-litre twin-turbo V6.",["Engine control software reporting a disconnection that is not there (Alfa Romeo 2.9 V6)","PCV hose B loose, split or with a broken connector","Crankcase pressure sensor B or its wiring faulty"],["Engine warning lamp","Oil residue or hissing at a crankcase ventilation hose","Possibly rough idle"],1,1,["P2C90","P04DB","P04FC","P2C33","P2C32"],""],P2C92:["Hybrid/EV Battery Contactor Control Supply Circuit/Open","The main contactors of a traction battery are relays whose coils are energised by driver stages in the battery controller, and those drivers take their energy from a dedicated supply feed. P2C92 means this feed is missing or interrupted, for example because of a blown fuse, a broken wire or a feed relay that does not pull in.",["Fuse in the contactor supply feed blown","Supply wire or connector at the battery pack interrupted","Relay or switch feeding the contactor drivers not closing","Battery controller input or driver stage defective"],["Vehicle does not become ready to drive","Charging does not start","Hybrid or EV system warning"],3,3,["P2C93","P2C94","P2C95","P0AA0","P0AA3"],"אספקת בקרת מגען סוללת מתח גבוה — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2C93:["Hybrid/EV Battery Contactor Control Supply Circuit Range/Performance","With P2C93 the supply for the contactor drivers is present but does not behave as it should: it sags when a coil is switched on, ripples, or recovers too slowly before the next contactor in the closing sequence. A high-resistance contact or a weak feed therefore shows up here rather than as an open circuit.",["Corroded or loose contact in the supply feed causing voltage drop","Weak 12 V battery or ground connection sagging under coil load","Contactor coil drawing excessive current or driver stage faulty"],["Several attempts needed before the vehicle is ready","Charging stops unexpectedly","Intermittent hybrid or EV warning"],3,3,["P2C92","P2C94","P2C95","P0AA0","P0AE1"],"אספקת בקרת מגען סוללת מתח גבוה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2C94:["Hybrid/EV Battery Contactor Control Supply Circuit Low","P2C94 says the supply feeding the contactor drivers lies below its lower limit. Ford is the maker that documents it: special service messages 51513 and 51783 (2023) describe 2021–2023 Escape, Corsair, Aviator, Mustang Mach-E, F-150 and Transit plug-in models whose AC charging at level 1 or 2 stops with the MIL on and P2C94 logged in the SOBDM, the on-board charger module.",["On-board charger (SOBDM) software, Ford TSB 23-2399/24-2027","Supply feed pulled down by a weak 12 V battery or poor ground","Partial short or high resistance in the supply wiring"],["AC charging stops while plugged in, MIL on","Charging resumes after unplugging and reconnecting","Vehicle may not become ready to drive"],4,3,["P2C92","P2C93","P2C95","P0ADF","P0E6A"],"אספקת בקרת מגען סוללת מתח גבוה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2C95:["Hybrid/EV Battery Contactor Control Supply Circuit High","P2C95 is the upper-limit counterpart of P2C94: the voltage on the feed for the contactor coil drivers exceeds what the battery controller accepts. An excessive supply is less common than a weak one, but it heats the coils and stresses the driver transistors, and it can mean the measurement is wrong, for instance when the sense line touches a higher potential or the feed regulator inside the controller has failed.",["Supply or sense line shorted to a higher voltage","Supply regulator or measurement in the battery controller faulty","12 V system overvoltage from a faulty DC/DC converter or jump start"],["Hybrid or EV system warning","Vehicle may not become ready or may shut down HV"],3,3,["P2C92","P2C93","P2C94","P0ADC"],"אספקת בקרת מגען סוללת מתח גבוה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2C96:["Hybrid/EV Battery Disable Circuit/Open","Besides commands over the vehicle network, many high-voltage batteries have a separate wired input through which another controller can force the contactors open. The best-known use is the crash signal: in Volkswagen patent US9586481B2 the battery opens its contactor 10–100 ms after a hard-wired crash signal, versus roughly 20–200 ms when the message arrives over CAN, and blocks reclosing until the stored fault has…",["Disable line or its connector at the battery pack interrupted","Sending controller (e.g. crash or airbag module) not driving the line","Connector left unplugged after body or battery repair","Input stage in the battery controller defective"],["Vehicle does not become ready to drive","High-voltage system warning"],4,3,["P2C97","P2C98","P0A0A","P0AA0"],""],P2C97:["Hybrid/EV Battery Disable Circuit Low","P2C97 is set when the high-voltage battery's wired disable input sits below its valid range, typically because the line is chafed through to body ground or the sending module pulls it low permanently. Whether low means shut down depends on the design. Where the line is active-low, a short to ground looks like a constant request to open the contactors, and the battery stays switched off;",["Disable line chafed and shorted to ground","Sending module holding the line low permanently","Water in the connector creating a leakage path to ground"],["High-voltage battery stays switched off, no ready mode","High-voltage system warning"],4,3,["P2C96","P2C98","P0A0A"],""],P2C98:["Hybrid/EV Battery Disable Circuit High","P2C98 flags a battery disable line whose level is above the permitted range, usually through a short to 12 V or a sender that drives the line too high. Unlike the low case, the risk here can be hidden: if a high level means all clear, a stuck-high line would no longer pass on a real shutdown request.",["Disable line shorted to 12 V supply","Sending module driving the line above the valid level","Input stage in the battery controller misreading the level"],["High-voltage system warning, often without noticeable driving fault","Ready mode may be blocked after the next restart, depending on maker"],4,3,["P2C96","P2C97","P0A0A","P0AA1"],""],P2C99:["Throttle Actuator A Control Exceeded Learning Limit","An electronic throttle relies on learned values: the closed-stop position of its sensors and, in many systems, a correction that widens the commanded opening as carbon narrows the bore. P2C99 says a learned value for throttle A has run into its permitted limit, so the module can no longer compensate. No manufacturer publishes P2C99.",["Heavy carbon deposits in the throttle bore needing more correction than allowed","Throttle body cleaned or replaced without resetting and relearning the adaptation","Worn throttle shaft, plate or end stop shifting the closed position","Throttle position sensor drifting"],["Engine warning lamp, possibly an electronic throttle warning","Idle speed too high, too low or hunting","Reduced power in a throttle emergency mode"],2,3,["P2C9A","P2176","P2119","P0638","P2111"],""],P2C9A:["Throttle Actuator B Control Exceeded Learning Limit","Throttle B exists only on engines with two electronically driven throttle bodies, usually one per cylinder bank on large V engines. P2C9A means a learned value of that second throttle – its closed-stop reference or the airflow correction stored for it – has reached the edge of the allowed range.",["Carbon deposits in throttle body B only","Throttle body B replaced or cleaned without relearn","Throttle plate B sticking or its return spring weak","Position sensor of throttle B drifting"],["Engine warning lamp","Uneven or hunting idle","Reduced power if the throttle is restricted"],2,3,["P2C99","P218A","P0639","P211A","P211B"],""],P2C9B:["Cold Start Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate Actuator A Range/Performance","P2C9B checks wastegate A while the engine runs its catalyst warm-up strategy after a cold start, when the wastegate is commanded open so hot exhaust reaches the catalyst rather than the turbine. GM uses the code on the 2.7-litre L3B (table 19OBDG03D): it fails if the position error stays above 20 % for over 1 s, the actuator current above 1 A or the duty cycle above 40 %, judged on 25 of 30 samples at 100 ms;",["Wastegate flap or linkage stiff from corrosion or deposits, worst when cold","Electric wastegate actuator with worn motor or gears","Actuator position feedback incorrect","Poor contact at the actuator connector or wiring"],["Check engine light shortly after a cold start","Rattle or noise from the wastegate area when cold","Often no noticeable change in performance"],2,1,["P2C9C","P2B81","P2B93","P050E","P0299"],"מפעיל שסתום Wastegate של המגדש התנעה קרה‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C9C:["Cold Start Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate Actuator B Range/Performance","P2C9C is the counterpart of P2C9B for wastegate B and only exists on engines with two turbochargers: GM's tables define turbo A as the first in a series layout or the bank 1 unit in a parallel one, so B is the second or the bank 2 charger. GM's 4.2-litre twin-turbo V8 (table 19OBDG07, test group KGMXV04.2088) watches the bank 2 turbine bypass valve during the cold-start rapid heat-up mode;",["Bank 2 wastegate flap or linkage stiff from corrosion or deposits","Worn or weak wastegate actuator B","Wiring or connector fault at actuator B"],["Check engine light shortly after a cold start","Uneven boost between banks later in the drive","Often no noticeable change during the cold start"],2,1,["P2C9B","P2B82","P2B94","P050E"],"מפעיל שסתום Wastegate של המגדש התנעה קרה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2C9D:["Fuel Pressure Regulator C Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too High","P2C9D reports that the fuel pressure in the section governed by regulator C stays above its target although that regulator is already reducing delivery as far as it can. A third regulator letter is only needed where an engine has several pressure control elements, for instance two high-pressure pumps or separate rail circuits. No manufacturer documents P2C9D publicly.",["Quantity control valve of circuit C sticking in the delivery position","Rail pressure sensor of that circuit reading too high","Wiring or connector fault keeping the valve from being switched","Outdated engine control calibration"],["MIL on, often after a single trip","Harsh or noisy idle, especially when cold","Reduced engine power"],3,3,["P2C9E","P2C9F","P2C00","P228D","P229B","P0088"],""],P2C9E:["Fuel Pressure Regulator C Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too Low","P2C9E is the underpressure counterpart of P2C9D: the circuit run by regulator C cannot reach its pressure target even with the regulator already asking for full delivery. No manufacturer publishes a definition of P2C9E, so the detail comes from analogous codes.",["Worn high-pressure pump of circuit C","Low feed pressure from the tank pump or a clogged fuel filter","Quantity control valve stuck closed or open circuit to it","Leaking injector or rail connection"],["MIL on","Hesitation or stumbling under load","Extended cranking before the engine starts","Power limitation"],3,3,["P2C9D","P2CA0","P2C00","P228C","P229A","P0087"],""],P2C9F:["Fuel Pressure Regulator D Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too High","P2C9F concerns regulator D, which GM uses for the second quantity control valve of a twin high-pressure system. GM's 2023 and 2024 tables 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 carry it in an ECM section that also lists the bank 2 rail sensor codes of bulletin 24-NA-106 for the 5.5 L LT6 Corvette.",["Second quantity control valve (bank 2) not regulating correctly","Water intrusion or fault in the bank 2 fuel harness connector (GM LT6)","Bank 2 rail pressure sensor reading implausibly","Very low tank level causing pressure dropouts"],["MIL on after one trip","Rough running or reduced power","Further fuel pressure or bank 2 injector codes stored"],3,3,["P2CA0","P2C9D","P2C01","P228D","P228C","P0088"],""],P2CA0:["Fuel Pressure Regulator D Exceeded Control Limits - Pressure Too Low","P2CA0 is the low-pressure verdict for regulator D. GM bulletin 24-NA-106 names it as a bank 2 low-pressure fault on the 2023–24 Corvette with the 5.5 L LT6 and links it, together with P228C, P01BF, P312B and several injector high-side codes, to an incorrect twelve-pin inline plug with an unsealed cavity that admits water to the bank 2 injector wiring;",["Incorrect 12-way in-line connector admitting water to the bank 2 harness (GM 24-NA-106)","Weak bank 2 high-pressure pump or its quantity valve stuck","Bank 2 rail pressure sensor faulty","Insufficient feed pressure from the tank pump"],["MIL on after one trip","Stumbling or misfire-like running","Several bank 2 injector or rail sensor codes at the same time"],3,3,["P2C9F","P2C9E","P2C01","P228C","P01BF","P0087"],""],P2CA1:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump Sense Circuit High","Some electric pumps in a water-cooled charge air cooler loop report back to the engine computer on a dedicated sense or feedback wire, kept apart from the line commanding them. P2CA1 means the level on that return wire stays above its plausible band.",["Feedback wire chafed through and touching a battery or ignition feed","Broken feedback wire or backed-out pin, input floats to its high level","Pump electronics no longer pulling the feedback line down","Damaged input stage in the engine control module"],["MIL on","Reduced power or boost under load, especially in hot weather","Pump fault messages from the pump no longer reach the controller"],2,3,["P2CA2","P2CA3","P023A","P026E","U05AA"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר) — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P2CA2:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump Sense Circuit Low","P2CA2 is set when the return wire from the intercooler pump sits below its valid range for longer than allowed. Insulation worn through against the body, water in the plug, or pump electronics that keep pulling the line down are the usual suspects.",["Feedback wire chafed against body or engine ground","Pump electronics holding the line low because of an internal fault","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the pump connector"],["MIL on","Engine power limited when charge air temperature rises","Code may appear together with pump speed or performance codes"],2,3,["P2CA1","P2CA3","P023B","P026E","U05AA"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר) — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P2CA3:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump Sense Circuit Performance","With P2CA3 the feedback signal from the intercooler pump is electrically inside its limits but does not fit what the controller expects: a reported speed or status that contradicts the command, a pulse pattern it cannot decode, or a reply that changes although the request stayed constant.",["Loose or corroded terminal distorting the feedback signal","Pump circuit board sending erratic or implausible feedback","Interference from ignition or alternator on a poorly routed wire","Pump or engine module software not matching each other"],["MIL on, sometimes only intermittently","Power reduction on long climbs or in hot weather"],2,3,["P2CA1","P2CA2","P026E","P2CB0","U05AA"],"חישת משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר) — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2CA4:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor Signals Swapped A/B","P2CA4 means the engine module believes the readings of particulate filter pressure sensors A and B arrive on each other's inputs, typically because connectors, sensors or sensing hoses were interchanged during service. Such a mix-up yields values that look electrically sound but invert the pressure picture across the filter. No manufacturer documents P2CA4 publicly.",["Sensing hoses of sensors A and B fitted to the wrong ports","Electrical connectors of the two sensors interchanged after service","Replacement sensor with different pin assignment or range","Crossed wires after a harness repair"],["MIL on, usually right after work on the exhaust or sensors","Regeneration too frequent or not taking place","Implausible filter pressure values in live data"],2,1,["P246D","P2452","P2453","P245E","P245F","P2CE5"],""],P2CA5:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor E Circuit","P2CA5 is the general circuit fault of the fifth temperature sensor in a DC/DC converter, the one carrying letter E. Converters measure several hot spots because each part heats differently: a Hyundai patent for a hybrid high-side converter places separate sensors on the inductor and on both IGBT switches, high side and low side, and changes the switching frequency when their readings drift apart.",["Loose, corroded or pushed-out terminal at the converter connector","Temperature sensor E inside the converter failed","Evaluation circuit of the converter control board faulty"],["Hybrid or electrical system warning and MIL on","DC/DC converter output limited, 12 V battery discharges"],4,3,["P2CA6","P2CA7","P2CA8","P2CA9","P2C8C","P0E58"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ E — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2CA6:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor E Circuit Low","P2CA6 is logged when the voltage of DC/DC converter temperature sensor E sits below the lower edge of its window. Converter sensors are usually thermistors whose resistance falls as they warm, so a signal that collapses towards zero would mean a converter hotter than physically plausible. A chafed signal wire touching ground or an internally shorted thermistor is the normal explanation;",["Signal wire of sensor E chafed through and shorted to ground","Thermistor of sensor E shorted internally","Actual severe overheating of the converter, e.g. coolant loss"],["MIL and hybrid or charging warning on","Converter switched off or strongly limited immediately after start","Low 12 V voltage message on longer drives"],4,3,["P2CA5","P2CA7","P2CA8","P2CAA","P2C8E","P0E5A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ E — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2CA7:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor E Circuit High","P2CA7 means the signal of DC/DC converter temperature sensor E is stuck above its upper limit. In a thermistor input fed through a pull-up resistor, an interrupted loop lets the voltage rise to the reference, so a pin pushed out of the connector, a broken conductor or a short to a supply line gives this result. The implied reading would be colder than any real surroundings. No manufacturer documents P2CA7 publicly;",["Open circuit in the sensor E signal or return line, e.g. pushed-out pin","Signal line shorted to a supply voltage","Thermistor of sensor E broken (open)"],["MIL and hybrid or charging warning on","Implausibly cold converter temperature in live data","Reduced converter output, 12 V battery charge drops"],4,3,["P2CA5","P2CA6","P2CA8","P2CAB","P2C8F","P0E5B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ E — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2CA8:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor E Circuit Range/Performance","P2CA8 covers sensor E of the DC/DC converter when its voltage is electrically fine but the temperature it reports does not make sense. Typical plausibility tests compare all converter sensors after a long soak, when they should agree, or check whether a reading moves at all while the converter is under heavy load.",["Sensor E drifting away from the other converter sensors","Sensor E has lost thermal contact with the part it measures","Outdated converter or hybrid control software with too tight limits","Contact resistance in the connector shifting the signal"],["MIL on, possibly after a single drive","Converter temperature in live data not following load or ambient"],4,3,["P2CA5","P2CA6","P2CA7","P2CAC","P2C8D","P0E59"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ E — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2CA9:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor F Circuit","P2CA9 is the general fault code for the circuit of the sixth DC/DC converter temperature sensor, letter F. Which component this sensor watches is left to the manufacturer. No manufacturer documents P2CA9 publicly; the converter sensors visible in bulletins end at D (Ram 1500 eTorque, FCA 08-037-21).",["Damaged harness or poor contact in the sensor F circuit","Temperature sensor F inside the converter failed","Input stage on the converter control board faulty"],["MIL and hybrid system warning on","Converter output limited, 12 V voltage may sag"],4,3,["P2CAA","P2CAB","P2CAC","P2CA5","P2C8C","P0E58"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ F — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2CAA:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor F Circuit Low","P2CAA reports that the input for DC/DC converter temperature sensor F reads too low. With the usual thermistor circuit this corresponds to an impossibly hot reading, so the controller suspects the signal path before the hardware: a ground short in the harness, moisture in the connector or a thermistor that failed short.",["Sensor F signal shorted to ground in the harness","Moisture or contamination in the converter connector","Thermistor of sensor F failed short"],["MIL and hybrid or charging warning on","Very high converter temperature shown even with a cold vehicle","Converter limited or switched off"],4,3,["P2CA9","P2CAB","P2CAC","P2CA6","P2C8E","P0E5A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ F — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2CAB:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor F Circuit High","P2CAB is set when DC/DC converter temperature sensor F delivers a voltage above the top of its valid band. For a thermistor input this is the typical signature of an open circuit, since the pull-up drags the line to reference voltage, or of a short to a higher voltage. The resulting value would be colder than the surroundings, which a working converter can never be. No manufacturer documents P2CAB publicly;",["Converter connector not latched or terminals spread","Broken signal or return wire of sensor F","Signal line shorted to a higher voltage"],["MIL and hybrid system warning on","Converter temperature shown far below ambient","Reduced 12 V supply from the converter"],4,3,["P2CA9","P2CAA","P2CAC","P2CA7","P2C8F","P0E5B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ F — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2CAC:["DC/DC Converter Temperature Sensor F Circuit Range/Performance","P2CAC flags DC/DC converter temperature sensor F as implausible although its signal is electrically valid. With six sensors in one converter the controller has plenty of reference values: after a cold soak all should read close to ambient, and during operation sensor F should rise and fall in step with the load on the part it watches.",["Sensor F detached from its heat sink or measuring point","Sensor F drifting against the other converter sensors","Outdated converter or hybrid control software","Uneven cooling of the converter, e.g. air in the coolant circuit"],["MIL on, sometimes after a single drive","Sensor F reading out of line with the other converter temperatures"],4,3,["P2CA9","P2CAA","P2CAB","P2CA8","P2C8D","P0E59"],"חיישן טמפרטורת ממיר DC/DC‏ F — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2CAD:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump B Control Circuit/Open","Where a charge air cooling loop has a second electric pump, it carries the letter B. P2CAD reports that the control line to that pump is open, so the driver stage in the engine computer sees no load. No manufacturer documents a pump B or this code publicly.",["Pump B connector loose, unplugged or corroded","Broken control wire between engine module and pump B","Open motor winding or internal board fault in pump B"],["MIL on, often after the first trip","Pump B silent; charge air temperature rises under load","Reduced engine power"],2,3,["P2CAE","P2CAF","P023A","P2CB0","U01BC"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2CAE:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump B Control Circuit Low","P2CAE concerns the second electric pump of a charge air cooling loop: its control line is held at ground potential where the driver expects a higher level. No manufacturer documents pump B publicly.",["Control wire of pump B rubbed through to ground","Water or corrosion in the pump B connector","Internal short in the electronics of pump B"],["MIL on","Pump B runs continuously or stays in a fallback mode","Possible power reduction when the charge air gets hot"],2,3,["P2CAD","P2CAF","P023B","P2CB0"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2CAF:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump B Control Circuit High","P2CAF says the control line of charge air cooler pump B is tied to supply voltage, so the engine computer cannot pull it down when it switches the pump on. As with the rest of the pump B series, no manufacturer documents the code publicly.",["Control wire of pump B pinched against a 12 V feed","Moisture bridging supply and control pins at the pump","Shorted electronics inside pump B"],["MIL on after the first faulty trip","Pump B does not start when commanded","Reduced power at high load"],2,3,["P2CAD","P2CAE","P023C","P2CB4"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2CB0:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump B Performance","P2CB0 flags that charge air cooler pump B is electrically in order but does not work the way its operating data say it should. No manufacturer documents the code publicly. GM shows how the same check runs on pump A (P026E) in its 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B: the motor phase current expected for the measured pump speed is compared with the actual current, and an error above 5 A for more than 5 s, with the pump above…",["Low coolant level or air pockets in the charge air cooler loop","Worn bearing or damaged impeller in pump B","Kinked hose, clogged cooler or debris restricting flow"],["MIL on","Charge air temperature higher than normal, power reduced","Unusual whining or rattling from the pump"],2,3,["P026E","P2CB1","P2CB2","P2CB3","P2CAD"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2CB1:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump B Overspeed/Air In System","P2CB1 means pump B in the charge air cooling loop turns faster than it should. An electric pump loses its hydraulic load when the impeller churns air instead of coolant, so overspeed is mostly a symptom of a low level or poor bleeding. No manufacturer documents P2CB1 publicly.",["Air trapped in the loop after service or incomplete bleeding","Low coolant from a leak in the charge air cooler circuit","Impeller loose or broken on the shaft of pump B"],["MIL on after two trips","Gurgling or a high-pitched pump noise","Low coolant warning or falling expansion tank level"],2,3,["P2B83","P2CB2","P2CB0","P2CB5","U01BC"],""],P2CB2:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump B Underspeed","With P2CB2 the speed reported by charge air cooler pump B stays below what it should reach. The motor is braked mechanically or gets too little power: a dragging bearing, debris or sludge at the impeller, a weak supply or a high-resistance connector. No manufacturer documents P2CB2 publicly.",["Dragging bearing or sludge slowing the rotor of pump B","Water or corrosion in the pump connector raising resistance","Low supply voltage from a poor ground or weak battery"],["MIL on after two trips","Charge air runs hot, engine power reduced under load"],2,3,["P2B84","P2CB1","P2CB3","P2CB0","P2CB4"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2CB3:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump B Stuck/Stalled","P2CB3 is reported when charge air cooler pump B receives power and a command but its rotor does not turn. The pump's own electronics usually detect this from current flowing without rotation and pass the result to the engine module. No manufacturer documents P2CB3 publicly.",["Rotor stuck after a long period without use","Debris or deposits jamming the impeller of pump B","Burnt winding or failed drive electronics in the pump","Coolant frozen because of insufficient antifreeze"],["MIL on, often with a reduced-power message","No flow in the second branch of the charge air cooling loop"],2,3,["P2BC1","P2CB2","P2CB4","P2CB5","P2B63"],""],P2CB4:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump B Supply Voltage Circuit","P2CB4 concerns the power feed of charge air cooler pump B rather than its command line: the pump finds its supply missing or outside the window in which it can run. No manufacturer documents P2CB4 publicly. Ford's 2024 gasoline OBD summary contains the same fault type, 1C (supply out of range), for auxiliary coolant pump B (P2B62); it is monitored all the time from 11 V battery voltage and logged after 5 s.",["Blown fuse or faulty relay in the pump B feed","Corroded or loose ground connection of the pump","Moisture or corrosion at the supply pins of the connector","Weak battery or charging fault pulling the voltage down"],["MIL on","Pump B silent, charge air temperature climbs","Other supply-related codes may be stored at the same time"],1,3,["P2BC2","P2CB3","P2CB5","P2B62","U01BC"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2CB5:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump B Control Module Overtemperature","P2CB5 is raised by the electronics inside charge air cooler pump B when their temperature exceeds the limit; the pump then throttles back or stops to protect itself. No manufacturer documents P2CB5 publicly. Ford's 2024 gasoline OBD summary lists the same fault type, 98 (system over temperature), for its auxiliary coolant pump B (P2B64), monitored continuously from 11 V.",["Pump running dry or partly in air because of low coolant","Stiff impeller making the motor draw more current","Pump mounted close to hot exhaust or turbo parts","Ageing power stage in the pump electronics"],["MIL on","Pump B slows down or switches off, charge air gets warmer","Reduced power in hot weather or on long climbs"],2,3,["P2BC3","P2CB1","P2CB3","P2CB4","P2B64"],"מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — חום יתר"],P2CB6:["Turbocharger/Supercharger B Boost System Performance","P2CB6 rates the boost control loop of charger B as a whole: the pressure produced by the second turbocharger or supercharger strays too far, upward or downward, from what the engine module requests in steady closed-loop operation. It is the B counterpart of P2263 and only applies to engines with two separately controlled chargers. No manufacturer documents P2CB6 publicly.",["Leak in the charge air path of charger B","Sticking wastegate or variable vanes of charger B","Restriction in the exhaust upstream or downstream of turbine B","Boost pressure sensor B reading inaccurately"],["MIL on","Uneven or reduced power under load","Hissing or whistling from the charge air system"],2,3,["P2263","P2CB7","P2CB8","P02CA","P02CB","P0239"],"מערכת לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2CB7:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Pressure B Not Detected - Mechanical","P2CB7 states that charger B delivers practically no boost although the operating point calls for it, and that the reason is likely mechanical rather than electrical: the pressure measured after the second compressor hardly rises above ambient. It mirrors P2262 for charger A and is relevant only to engines with two separately monitored boost paths. No manufacturer documents P2CB7 publicly.",["Intake or charge air hose of charger B detached or split","Wastegate or bypass of charger B stuck open","Damaged or seized turbocharger B","Actuator linkage or vacuum supply to charger B failed"],["Clearly flat acceleration","MIL on, power limited","Unusual hissing or no turbo sound"],2,3,["P2262","P2CB6","P2CB8","P02CB","P0239"],""],P2CB8:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Pressure B Too High - Mechanical","P2CB8 reports that the second charger, B, produces more boost than the engine module allows, and attributes this to a mechanical cause such as a wastegate or bypass of charger B that no longer opens, a seized actuator rod or sooted variable vanes stuck in the closed position. It is the B twin of P226B. No manufacturer documents P2CB8 publicly.",["Wastegate of charger B stuck closed","Variable turbine vanes of charger B sooted and sticking","Seized actuator rod or linkage on charger B","Boost pressure sensor B reading too high"],["Sudden power cut under full load","MIL on","Surging or jerky boost build-up"],2,3,["P226B","P2CB6","P2CB7","P02CA","P0239"],""],P2CB9:["Fan 2 Underspeed","P2CB9 means the second electric cooling fan reports a lower speed than its command calls for, while communication and wiring are judged sound. GM uses it in two ways. In tables 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07 the fan must stay below a speed-dependent floor of up to 3550 rpm for 20 s once it has been commanded above 7.65 % for more than 5 s.",["Fan blades slowed by debris, leaves, snow or ice","Fan 2 motor or its integrated electronics worn or faulty","Blown fuse, weak supply or poor ground at the fan","Sporadic entry without fault found (GM investigated without a fix)"],["Check engine light after two trips","Coolant temperature rises at idle or when towing","Weaker air conditioning at standstill"],2,1,["P2CBA","P0494","P2CBB","U0633","P2B31","P2B32"],"מאוורר‏ 2 — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2CBA:["Fan 2 Overspeed","With P2CBA the controller finds fan 2 spinning clearly faster than its own estimate of what the current command should produce. GM documents the check in tables 23OBDG07 and 24OBDG07: the reported speed minus the estimated speed must exceed a margin of 1400 to 4050 rpm, depending on the operating point, for 20 s with more than 9.5 V on board, and the lamp follows on the second trip.",["Fan blade broken or partly missing, less load on the motor","Fan electronics drive the motor harder than commanded","Implausible speed feedback from the fan module","Shroud damaged or detached so the rotor runs free"],["Check engine light after two trips","Unusually loud or vibrating fan noise","Fan runs at high speed even with a cool engine"],2,1,["P2CB9","P0495","P2CBC","U0633","P2B32"],"מאוורר‏ 2 — מהירות יתר"],P2CBB:["Fan 3 Underspeed","P2CBB concerns vehicles with three electric radiator fans: the third one turns slower than modelled for its command. GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B describes the check for a LIN-controlled fan 3. The controller converts the request into an expected speed, allows for start-up and ramp delays and for supply voltage, and compares the reported speed with a lower limit;",["Fan 3 slowed by debris, ice or a distorted shroud","Fan 3 motor bearings or integrated controller worn","Voltage drop on the fan 3 power feed or ground"],["Check engine light after two trips","Engine runs warmer under high load or in heat","Reduced A/C cooling at low speed"],3,1,["P2CBC","P2CB9","U067C","P2C41","P0494"],"מאוורר‏ 3 — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2CBC:["Fan 3 Overspeed","P2CBC is the counterpart to P2CBB: the third cooling fan turns noticeably faster than the controller expects for the present request. No manufacturer publicly documents this code. The closest published logic is GM's: table 23OBDG07 flags fan 2 overspeed as P2CBA when the reported speed exceeds the estimate by 1400 to 4050 rpm for 20 s, and treats fan 3 the same way under its own code P14D8 with a margin of 1300 to…",["Fan 3 blade broken or rotor unbalanced","Fan 3 electronics ignore the speed command","Wrong speed value reported by the fan module"],["Check engine light, depending on the maker","Loud or rough fan noise"],3,1,["P2CBB","P2CBA","U067C","P0495","P2C41"],"מאוורר‏ 3 — מהירות יתר"],P2CBD:["PCV Heater B Control Circuit/Open","Some engines heat the crankcase ventilation path so that moisture and oil carried by blow-by gas cannot freeze and block it; engines with two such paths, for example a PCV line and a separate make-up air line feeding the turbo intake, may carry a second heater, B. P2CBD reports that the control circuit of heater B is open, so the element never receives current. No manufacturer documents P2CBD publicly.",["Heating element B burnt out","Corroded or loose connector at heater B","Broken control or supply wire","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["MIL on (depending on manufacturer) or code stored only","No noticeable effect in mild weather","In hard frost, iced ventilation path with oil leaks or rough idle"],1,1,["P2CBE","P2CBF","P2CC0","P053A"],"גוף חימום PCV‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2CBE:["PCV Heater B Control Circuit High","P2CBE says the switched control line of PCV heater B carries too high a voltage, usually because it touches battery positive. Since the module normally completes the heater circuit by pulling this line to ground, a short to supply means the output can no longer switch the element on, or the driver shuts down to protect itself, so heater B stays cold. No manufacturer documents P2CBE publicly.",["Control wire chafed through and touching battery voltage","Moisture bridging pins in the heater B connector","Internal short in heating element B","Damaged output stage in the engine control module"],["Code stored, MIL depending on manufacturer","Heater B inactive, risk of an iced ventilation path in frost"],2,1,["P2CBD","P2CBF","P2CC0","P053C"],"גוף חימום PCV‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2CBF:["PCV Heater B Control Circuit Low","P2CBF is set when the control line of PCV heater B sits at ground potential at a moment the module expects a voltage on it. On the usual low-side layout, with supply fed directly to the heater and the module providing the ground, a short to ground on that line turns heater B on permanently regardless of command.",["Control wire pinched or chafed to engine ground","Damaged connector at heater B","Output stage in the engine module shorted internally"],["Code stored, MIL depending on manufacturer","Heater B constantly on, slightly higher electrical load","Usually no driveability complaint"],2,1,["P2CBD","P2CBE","P2CC0","P053B"],"גוף חימום PCV‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2CC0:["PCV Heater B Performance","P2CC0 covers PCV heater B when its wiring passes the electrical tests but the heater does not behave as expected: current outside the plausible window, an overheated output stage, or no sign of the commanded warming. It complements the circuit codes P2CBD to P2CBF, which only detect opens and shorts. No manufacturer documents P2CC0 publicly, and the A-side code P053D is not published either;",["Heating element B with drifted resistance","High-resistance contact in connector or supply","Output stage overheating in the engine control module"],["Code stored, MIL depending on manufacturer","Possible icing of the ventilation line in frost"],2,1,["P2CBD","P2CBE","P2CBF","P053D","P052E"],"גוף חימום PCV‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2CC1:["Generator Voltage Sense Circuit B","P2CC1 is the general fault of a second sense line through which the engine controller reads the actual charging voltage. In the charging system, generator means the alternator; a sense input taps the voltage at the rectifier or battery without load current, so wiring losses do not distort it.",["Sense wire B, its fuse or connector open or corroded","Second alternator or its regulator faulty","Sense input in the engine control module faulty"],["Battery or charging warning lamp on","Charging voltage regulated to a fixed or unsuitable value"],2,0,["P2CC2","P2CC3","P2CC4","P063A","P0562","P0563"],"מעגל חישת מתח גנרטור‏ B"],P2CC2:["Generator Voltage Sense Circuit B Range/Performance","P2CC2 means the voltage arriving on generator sense circuit B is within electrical limits but does not agree with what the controller expects, such as the battery voltage measured elsewhere, the commanded set point or the reading of sense circuit A. The usual cause is a voltage drop: corroded ring terminals, a loose ground strap or a damaged fusible link make the sensed value lag behind reality.",["Voltage drop from corroded terminals, loose ground strap or damaged fusible link","Alternator B delivering too little or unstable output","Battery with high internal resistance distorting the comparison"],["Charging warning lamp on or flickering","Battery not fully charged or charging voltage fluctuating"],2,0,["P2CC1","P2CC3","P2CC4","P063B","P0562","P0563"],"מעגל חישת מתח גנרטור‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2CC3:["Generator Voltage Sense Circuit B Low","P2CC3 is stored when generator sense circuit B reports a voltage below its lower limit, in practice often close to zero. Typical causes are an open sense lead, a blown fuse in it or a short to ground; on Chrysler alternators, according to Remy, an internal 2.4 kΩ resistor shields the sense terminal against such a ground fault.",["Sense wire B broken or its fuse blown","Sense wire B chafed and shorted to ground","Corroded sense terminal at the alternator or module"],["Charging warning lamp on","Charging voltage too high or held at a fixed value","Overcharged battery, bright lights"],2,0,["P2CC1","P2CC2","P2CC4","P063C","P0562","P0563"],"מעגל חישת מתח גנרטור‏ B — ערך נמוך"],P2CC4:["Generator Voltage Sense Circuit B High","P2CC4 indicates that generator sense circuit B reads above its upper limit. Either the line is shorted to a higher voltage, or the voltage at the measuring point really is excessive, for example because the regulator keeps the field fully energised; Remy warns that a full-field alternator can quickly push the system above 16 V.",["Regulator of alternator B stuck in full field, real overvoltage","Sense wire B shorted to a higher-voltage line","Sense input of the engine control module faulty"],["Charging warning lamp on","Very high system voltage, bulbs failing early","Battery gassing or smelling"],2,0,["P2CC1","P2CC2","P2CC3","P063D","P0563"],"מעגל חישת מתח גנרטור‏ B — ערך גבוה"],P2CC5:["Generator Inverter Power Supply B Circuit/Open","P2CC5 concerns supply B inside the inverter that drives a hybrid's generator (motor-generator), typically a low-voltage rail feeding the gate drivers of the power transistors. Which supply gets the letter B is defined by the manufacturer; a second inverter channel or second generator would also fit. The code covers a missing supply or an interrupted feed. No manufacturer documents P2CC5 publicly.",["Supply B for the gate drivers failed inside the inverter","12 V feed, fuse or connector of the inverter interrupted","Poor ground connection of the inverter control electronics"],["Hybrid system warning light and MIL on","Generator out of operation, vehicle may not become ready to drive"],4,3,["P2CC6","P2CC7","P0E0F","P0C0B"],"אספקת מתח אינוורטר גנרטור‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2CC6:["Generator Inverter Power Supply B Circuit Low","P2CC6 means supply B of the generator inverter is present but below its permitted level. A weak gate driver feed is dangerous for the power stage: transistors that are not driven fully on run in a lossy partial state and heat up quickly, so the inverter typically blocks the generator. No manufacturer documents P2CC6 publicly.",["Internal regulator of supply B delivering too little voltage","Low 12 V input to the inverter, e.g. weak auxiliary battery","Corroded ground or connector of the inverter"],["Hybrid system warning light and MIL on","Generator limited or switched off, reduced hybrid performance"],4,3,["P2CC5","P2CC7","P0E10","P0BCE","P0BCF"],"אספקת מתח אינוורטר גנרטור‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2CC7:["Generator Inverter Power Supply B Circuit High","P2CC7 is set when supply B of the generator inverter exceeds its upper limit. Gate inputs of IGBTs tolerate only a limited voltage, so overvoltage on the driver rail puts the switches at risk and the inverter is normally shut down.",["Regulator of supply B inside the inverter faulty","Short between two internal supply rails","Overvoltage in the 12 V system from a DC/DC converter fault"],["Hybrid system warning light and MIL on","Generator blocked, battery no longer charged while driving"],4,3,["P2CC5","P2CC6","P0E11"],"אספקת מתח אינוורטר גנרטור‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2CC8:["Coolant Pump Speed Sensor Circuit","Some engines measure how fast a coolant pump turns with a dedicated speed sensor, for instance on a pump that can be engaged and released or on an electric pump read back by the controller. P2CC8 is the general fault of that sensor's circuit: the signal is absent or cannot be used, without the controller deciding whether it is too low or too high. No manufacturer documents P2CC8 publicly.",["Failed speed sensor delivering no usable signal","Damaged wiring or loose connector at the sensor","Missing reference voltage or ground for the sensor"],["MIL on","Coolant pump held in a default state, warm-up may change"],2,1,["P2CC9","P2CCA","P2CCB","P2B85","P26CE"],"חיישן מהירות משאבת נוזל קירור — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2CC9:["Coolant Pump Speed Sensor Range/Performance","P2CC9 means the coolant pump speed sensor delivers a clean electrical signal whose value does not make sense. The controller compares it with what the pump should be doing: a belt-driven pump has to follow engine speed in a fixed ratio once engaged, an electric pump should match its commanded speed.",["Slipping belt or clutch, so the pump turns slower than expected","Sensor loose, wrong air gap or damaged trigger wheel","Sensor electronics drifting or dropping pulses"],["MIL on after repeated detection","Engine may run warmer than usual or take longer to warm up"],2,1,["P2CC8","P2CCA","P2CCB","P2B85","P26CB"],"חיישן מהירות משאבת נוזל קירור — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2CCA:["Coolant Pump Speed Sensor Circuit Low","P2CCA is stored when the signal line of the coolant pump speed sensor remains below its lower limit, so no pulses or levels above the threshold arrive. Most often the signal wire is shorted to ground, the sensor has lost its supply voltage and therefore cannot switch, or its output stage has failed in the off state. No manufacturer documents P2CCA publicly.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","Sensor supply voltage missing because of an open feed","Sensor output stage failed in the low state"],["MIL on","Pump speed reads zero in live data although the engine runs"],2,1,["P2CC8","P2CC9","P2CCB","P2B85"],"חיישן מהירות משאבת נוזל קירור — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2CCB:["Coolant Pump Speed Sensor Circuit High","P2CCB covers the upper end of the coolant pump speed sensor signal: the input stays above its permitted maximum. On sensors with an open-collector output and a pull-up resistor in the controller, an interrupted signal wire or a sensor that has lost its ground leaves the line resting high, so the open case often lands here rather than under P2CCA.",["Open signal wire, input pulled up by the controller","Lost ground connection at the sensor","Signal wire shorted to a voltage feed"],["MIL on","Pump speed missing or stuck at an implausible value in live data"],2,1,["P2CC8","P2CC9","P2CCA","P26CE"],"חיישן מהירות משאבת נוזל קירור — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2CCC:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack G Deterioration","P2CCC continues the state-of-health series for sectioned traction batteries in the P2 block: after A (P0A7F) and B to F (P0EDD to P0EE1), section G is the seventh. The controller has concluded that this part of the pack has lost too much usable capacity or power. Audi uses the code on the Q5 PHEV as P2CCC00 for battery group 7 in hybrid battery management unit 008C.",["Battery module of group 7 lost capacity or power","Single weak cell block dragging the section down","State-of-health estimate of the battery controller wrong"],["Yellow engine warning lamp on","Displayed electric range too low","Electric driving mode unavailable or ends early"],4,3,["P2CCD","P0EE1","P0A7F","P0BBD","P2CCE"],""],P2CCD:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack H Deterioration","P2CCD reports that section H, the eighth subdivision of a traction battery, has aged past the limit its controller accepts. In practice this code only exists on large packs that the battery management splits into at least eight separately judged groups.",["Battery module of group 8 worn out","Module aged faster due to heat or uneven cooling","Faulty state-of-health judgement by the battery controller"],["MIL on","Shorter electric range","Less power in electric mode"],4,3,["P2CCC","P2CCE","P0A7F","P0EE1","P0BBD"],""],P2CCE:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack I Deterioration","P2CCE is reserved for the ninth section, I, of a traction battery whose controller rates the health of each section on its own. The fault is a capacity or power verdict, not an electrical one: section I no longer delivers what a healthy unit should. No manufacturer publicly documents P2CCE. The nearest published use is Audi's Q5 PHEV, which splits its pack into eight groups and therefore stops at P2CCD for group 8;",["Module or cell group of section I aged beyond its limit","Uneven pack temperature stressing this section","Misjudged state of health in the battery controller"],["MIL or hybrid system warning on","Shorter electric range"],4,3,["P2CCD","P2CCF","P2CCC","P0A7F"],""],P2CCF:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack J Deterioration","P2CCF belongs to the deterioration series that rates each section of a divided traction battery on its own; J is the tenth section after A (P0A7F), B to F (P0EDD–P0EE1) and G to I (P2CCC–P2CCE). It is not an electrical fault: the controller has decided that the modules of section J have given up more usable capacity or power than allowed. No manufacturer publicly documents P2CCF.",["Modules of section J worn beyond the accepted capacity or power limit","Section J repeatedly ran hotter than the rest of the pack","Health estimate of the battery controller wrong after software or sensor issue"],["MIL or hybrid system warning on","Electric range noticeably shorter","Less power available in electric driving"],4,3,["P2CCE","P2CD0","P2D4E","P0A7F"],""],P2CD0:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack K Deterioration","With P2CD0 the battery controller reports that section K, the eleventh separately judged part of the high-voltage battery, has exceeded its ageing limit. Such a verdict normally rests on comparing what this section stores and delivers with its neighbours over many charge cycles, so it rarely appears suddenly after one event. No manufacturer publishes P2CD0;",["Cells of section K lost capacity faster than the other sections","Internal resistance of section K increased, limiting power","Uneven coolant flow leaving section K warmer over years"],["Warning lamp for engine or hybrid system","Shorter range on a full charge","Weaker acceleration on battery power"],4,3,["P2CCF","P2CD1","P2D4F","P0A7F"],""],P2CD1:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack L Deterioration","P2CD1 marks section L, the twelfth subdivision of the high-voltage pack, as worn: its usable capacity or power capability has fallen below what the controller accepts. The code only makes sense for packs whose management tracks twelve or more groups individually; no carmaker documents it publicly, and the largest published series, Audi's Q5 PHEV, ends with group 8.",["Section L has reached the end of its usable life","One weak cell block pulling the whole section down","Faulty voltage sensing making section L look weaker than it is"],["MIL illuminated","Battery charge falls faster than usual"],4,3,["P2CD0","P2CD2","P2D50","P0BBD"],""],P2CD2:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack M Deterioration","P2CD2 flags section M, the thirteenth part of a sectioned high-voltage battery, as degraded in capacity or power. Unlike sections J to L, M has no matching over-temperature code in the available code lists, so the thermal history of this section has to be read from general pack temperature data. No manufacturer publicly documents P2CD2, and no published battery is divided into thirteen individually rated groups;",["Section M degraded by age and charge cycles","Long standstill at low charge damaged cells of section M","Cell balancing of section M no longer working"],["Hybrid or engine warning lamp on","Reduced electric-only range","Sluggish response in electric mode"],4,3,["P2CD1","P2CD3","P0A7F","P0BBD"],""],P2CD3:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack N Deterioration","P2CD3 closes the lettered deterioration series: N is the fourteenth section of a drive battery whose management assesses each section's condition separately. When it sets, section N can no longer hold or release the energy expected of it, even though wiring and sensors may be intact. No manufacturer documents P2CD3 publicly, and no published battery reaches fourteen individually rated groups;",["Cells in section N aged beyond the acceptance limit","Earlier replaced neighbour modules leave section N as the weak link","Battery controller misjudges section N after a reset or update"],["MIL or hybrid warning","Electric range clearly reduced","Drive power limited at times"],4,3,["P2CD2","P2CCF","P0A7F","P0BBD"],""],P2CD4:["A/C Refrigerant Pressure Sensor A/B Correlation","P2CD4 is a plausibility check between two refrigerant pressure sensors that serve one A/C or heat pump circuit: the module flags it when the pair disagrees beyond what the system allows, even though each sensor is electrically fine. Bentley documents the code as P2CD400 in the thermal management ECU (address 00C5) of 2025 Continental GT and GTC models as well as the Flying Spur;",["Thermal management software misjudging the sensor comparison (Bentley 2025 campaign)","One pressure sensor drifting or failing internally while still in range","Contact resistance at one sensor connector shifting its signal"],["A/C cools weakly or the compressor is limited","Code stored in the thermal management or climate module"],2,0,["P0530","P0531","P2515","P2516","P0534"],"חיישן לחץ גז מזגן‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2CD5:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve C Stuck","Bypass valve C is a third compressor recirculation valve, which only exists on layouts with three charging paths or stages; on lift-off it routes boosted air back to the compressor inlet so the compressor does not surge. It is not the wastegate. P2CD5 says the valve no longer moves when commanded and stays in one position. No manufacturer documents P2CD5 publicly.",["Valve or piston seized by oil and soot deposits from the crankcase breather","Electric actuator or diaphragm of the valve worn or failed","Missing vacuum or control signal on a pneumatically operated valve","Position feedback reports movement wrongly although the valve works"],["Fluttering or surging noise from the intake when lifting off the throttle","Boost builds slowly or stays low when the valve is stuck open","Warning lamp on and engine power limited"],3,3,["P2C29","P25F8","P25FC","P23AA","P00C4","P0033"],"שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ C — תקוע"],P2CD6:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor D Circuit","A fourth boost pressure sensor, D, is only needed where charge pressure is read at four points, for example on twin-turbo engines with two stages per bank or on combinations of supercharger, turbocharger and electric compressor. Which tap gets the letter is up to the manufacturer. P2CD6 is the umbrella fault for this sensor's circuit when the module does not or cannot separate low, high and implausible readings;",["Corroded or loose connector, chafed wire at sensor D","Boost sensor D internally faulty","5 V reference or sensor ground interrupted","Input stage of the engine control module faulty"],["Warning lamp on","Reduced boost and noticeably less power","Other sensor codes at the same time if a shared 5 V supply is affected"],2,3,["P2CD7","P2CD8","P2CD9","P25F2","P0235","P0239"],"חיישן לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2CD7:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor D Circuit Range/Performance","With P2CD7 the boost sensor D signal is electrically valid but does not fit the other pressure readings or the engine's air model. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; the checks used for sensor A show what it would cover.",["Sensor D drifted or contaminated with oil","Leaking seal or blocked port at the sensor's measuring point","Charge air leak in the section monitored by sensor D","Sensor with the wrong pressure range fitted"],["Warning lamp on","Boost limited, weaker acceleration","Scan tool shows sensor D value differing from barometric pressure with the engine off"],2,3,["P2CD6","P2CD8","P2CD9","P25F3","P0236","P0240"],"חיישן לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2CD8:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor D Circuit Low","P2CD8 is stored when the voltage from boost sensor D falls below the lowest value a healthy sensor can output. Since these sensors rise in voltage as pressure rises, a reading near zero almost always points to the electrics: signal shorted to ground, an interrupted 5 V supply, or a broken signal wire that the module pulls low. No manufacturer publishes limits for sensor D.",["Signal wire of sensor D shorted to ground","5 V reference to the sensor open or shorted","Sensor D internally failed with output stuck low"],["Warning lamp on","Only base boost available, clear loss of power","Live data shows sensor D at or near minimum pressure even under load"],2,3,["P2CD6","P2CD7","P2CD9","P25F4","P0237","P0241"],"חיישן לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2CD9:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Sensor D Circuit High","P2CD9 reports a boost sensor D voltage above the highest valid level. A signal pinned near the reference rarely reflects real overboost; more often the signal wire touches 5 V or battery voltage, the sensor ground is open, or a broken signal line floats up through a pull-up inside the module. No carmaker publishes a sensor D limit.",["Sensor ground open or high resistance at the connector","Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Sensor D internally failed with output stuck high"],["Warning lamp on","Engine runs on base boost only with reduced power","Live data shows sensor D at maximum even at idle"],2,3,["P2CD6","P2CD7","P2CD8","P25F5","P0238","P0242"],"חיישן לחץ גדישה מגדש‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2CDA:["Alternative Fuel Tank A Vacuum Insulation Deteriorated","P2CDA concerns cryogenic fuel storage, in practice liquefied natural gas (LNG) and possibly liquid hydrogen, kept in a double-walled tank whose gap is evacuated. Once that vacuum softens, heat leaks in, the liquid boils faster and pressure climbs until the relief valve vents gas.",["Vacuum between inner and outer tank wall lost through a leaking weld, fitting or seal","Gradual vacuum decay from outgassing over years of service, tank due for pump-down","Dent or impact damage to the outer shell breaching the insulation space","Pressure rise from another cause (economizer, pressure regulator, sensor) misread as insulation loss"],["Tank pressure rises quickly while the vehicle stands, relief valve vents gas","Frost or condensation on the outer tank shell","Fuel loss and shorter standing time after refuelling"],4,0,["P019E","P019F","P01AA","P2BB2","P224C"],""],P2CDB:["Cold Start Cylinder 1 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P2CDB is part of the monitoring of cold start emission strategies: some engines shut off cylinders or hold intake valves closed right after a cold start to heat the catalyst faster, and CARB requires the commanded elements of such a strategy to be checked while it is active.",["Latch pin of the switchable rocker or lifter on cylinder 1 sticking, often from contaminated oil","Wrong oil grade or low oil level slowing the switching while the oil is still cold","Cylinder 1 control solenoid responding sluggishly at low temperature","Engine control software misjudging the cold start test, cured by an update"],["Check engine lamp after a cold start","Rough running in the first minutes after starting a cold engine","Misfire code for cylinder 1 stored alongside"],3,1,["P2CDC","P3402","P3401","P3498","P0301","P050D"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 1 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2CDC:["Cold Start Cylinder 2 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","With P2CDC the control unit reports that cylinder 2 did not take the valve state that the cold start routine asked for. Timing matters here: in a Ford patent on electrically latched rockers, intake deactivation is wanted at engine start, yet the cam of cylinder 2 sits on its lobe, so its latch pin cannot move at first. That is normal;",["Latch pin on cylinder 2 seized by dirt or varnish in the oil","Hydraulic lash adjuster pumped up so the rocker stays loaded on base circle","Weak cylinder 2 solenoid or high resistance in its connector","Worn cam lobe or collapsed lifter on cylinder 2"],["Uneven idle while the engine warms up","Warning lamp, sometimes with a cylinder 2 misfire code","Engine control may suspend the cold start strategy"],3,1,["P2CDB","P2CDD","P3410","P3409","P3499","P0302"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 2 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2CDD:["Cold Start Cylinder 3 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P2CDD flags cylinder 3 when its deactivation or intake valve control misbehaves during the cold start phase. No maker documents this code publicly, so the closest evidence comes from neighbouring checks.",["Cylinder 3 valves keep opening because the switching element does not unlock","Insufficient oil pressure or flow to the switching gallery right after a cold start","Cylinder 3 control solenoid sticking or leaking internally","Manifold pressure signal biased, so a sealed cylinder looks like it still breathes"],["Malfunction lamp, typically after repeated cold starts","Vibration or rough idle shortly after a cold start","Engine takes longer to settle into normal running"],3,1,["P2CDC","P2CDE","P3418","P349A","P0303"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 3 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2CDE:["Cold Start Cylinder 4 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","On a four-cylinder engine cylinder 4 is the last one in the count; P2CDE reports that cylinder 4 did not follow the cold start valve command. Engines may do two different things during a cold start. A Delphi patent closes the intake and exhaust valves of selected cylinders after start-up and reopens them once the converter is hot enough to work, around 350 °C.",["Switchable rocker or lifter on cylinder 4 not changing state","Cylinder 4 solenoid drawing too little current due to corroded terminals","Aged or overdue engine oil impairing the hydraulic switching when cold","Implausible coolant or oil temperature signal triggering the cold start strategy wrongly"],["Harsher cranking or start-up shake","Rough first minute after a cold start","Check engine lamp"],3,1,["P2CDD","P2CDF","P3426","P349B","P0304"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 4 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2CDF:["Cold Start Cylinder 5 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P2CDF only occurs on engines with at least five cylinders, mostly V6 and V8 units, and says cylinder 5 did not respond correctly to the cold start deactivation or intake valve command. The Delphi patent behind this idea chooses cylinders that sit farthest from the converter along the exhaust, so less heat is lost in the manifold; in its V8 tests the exhaust ran at least 75 °C hotter at equal load.",["Deactivation lifter or rocker on cylinder 5 failing to lock or unlock","Restricted oil gallery or screen feeding the switching elements of that bank","Faulty cylinder 5 control valve in the valve lifter oil manifold","Calibration issue in the engine control module"],["Lamp on after cold starts, sometimes with a cylinder 5 misfire code","Ticking or tapping valve noise when cold","Rough idle until the engine is warm"],3,1,["P2CDE","P2CE0","P3434","P349C","P0305"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 5 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2CE0:["Cold Start Cylinder 6 Deactivation/Intake Valve Control Performance","P2CE0 closes this series of cold start codes; numbering ends at cylinder 6 although many deactivation engines have eight cylinders. It indicates that cylinder 6 did not reach the valve state demanded during the cold start routine. No manufacturer documents P2CE0 publicly.",["Deactivating lifter or rocker on cylinder 6 not switching","Engine control software that misjudges or mis-times the cold start switching, fixed by reprogramming","Low or delayed oil pressure after a cold start","Cylinder 6 control solenoid or its wiring degraded"],["Rough idle or misfire while warming up","Check engine lamp, often with a cylinder 6 misfire code","Cylinder deactivation may stay disabled afterwards"],3,1,["P2CDF","P3442","P3441","P349D","P0306","P3400"],"בקרת שסתום יניקה/השבתת צילינדר צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 6 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2CE1:["Intake Air Heater C Circuit/Open","P2CE1 reports an interrupted circuit at intake air heater C, part of the grid-type pre-heat system a diesel uses to warm the incoming air for cold starts. Volvo and Mack use exactly this code on heavy trucks: their 2019 solution K53338075 for 11, 13 and 16 litre engines, including Mack MP7, MP8 and MP10, from US10+OBD13 onwards lists P2CE1-13, the suffix marking an open circuit, among the pre-heat relay codes.",["Damaged supply power cable between relay and heater, not always visible on an ohmmeter","Pre-heat relay contacts or output burnt open","Poor terminal tension at the heating element or relay plug","Heating element C itself burnt through"],["Hard starting and long cranking in cold weather","White smoke after a cold start","Engine warning lamp"],2,1,["P2CE2","P2CE3","P2CE4","P0543","P2605","P0540"],"גוף חימום אוויר יניקה‏ C — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2CE2:["Intake Air Heater C Circuit Range/Performance","P2CE2 is the plausibility test for intake air heater C: the circuit is neither open nor shorted, but current draw, voltage drop or heating effect do not fit the command. Under the heavy-duty OBD rules a glow plug or intake air heater must react properly to commands and its circuit must show plausible current and voltage drop. No manufacturer documents P2CE2 publicly.",["Extra resistance from corroded terminals or a worn supply cable lowering heater current","Pre-heat relay switching with excessive voltage drop","Heating element C aged, drawing current outside the expected window","Weak batteries or poor main ground distorting the current and voltage reading"],["Longer cranking on cold mornings","White smoke and rough running until warm","Warning lamp without an open or short code for heater C"],2,1,["P2CE1","P2CE3","P2CE4","P2604","P2606","P2609"],"גוף חימום אוויר יניקה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2CE3:["Intake Air Heater C Circuit Low","P2CE3 means the signal in the circuit of intake air heater C reads too low, as with the control or feedback line shorted to ground or a relay output pulled down. Volvo uses it with the suffix -11, which in the failure type scheme denotes a ground short.",["Control or feedback wire of heater C chafed through to ground","Pre-heat relay with an internal fault pulling its output low","Outdated engine management software, addressed by a Volvo update","Moisture or corrosion in the relay connector creating a path to ground"],["Pre-heat not working, hard cold starts","White smoke after starting in cold weather","Fault lamp on the dash"],2,1,["P2CE1","P2CE2","P2CE4","P0541","P2607"],"גוף חימום אוויר יניקה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2CE4:["Intake Air Heater C Circuit High","P2CE4 is stored when heater C's circuit shows an excessive signal, typically a short to battery voltage on the control line or a relay that remains switched on. Volvo and Mack document it as P2CE4-12, the suffix standing for a short to battery.",["Pre-heat relay contacts welded or stuck closed","Control line of heater C shorted to a battery-voltage wire","Faulty supply power cable or loose bracket mounting affecting the circuit","Engine control module output stage for the relay faulty"],["Batteries drained after the truck has been parked","Hot or discoloured cable near the heater","Warning lamp and possibly hard starting if the heater no longer switches"],2,1,["P2CE1","P2CE2","P2CE3","P0542","P2608"],"גוף חימום אוויר יניקה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2CE5:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor C Circuit","Two manufacturers use P2CE5, with different meanings. In GM's 2025 diesel tables 25OBDG04A and 25OBDG04B, sensor C is the downstream relative pressure sensor that reads gauge pressure behind the particulate filter.",["Sensor C zero point drifted (offset at standstill too large)","Condensate or soot in the sensing hose holding pressure","Damaged connector or wiring of a digital sensor C","Sensor C internally faulty"],["Warning lamp on, usually after two trips on GM diesels","Particulate filter regeneration may run less accurately or more often","Usually no noticeable change in driving"],2,1,["P2CE6","P2CE7","P2CE8","P2CE9","U0696","P2CEA","P2452"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2CE6:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P2CE6 marks a sensor C reading that is electrically valid but physically wrong. GM's 2025 diesel tables use it for a frozen downstream relative pressure signal: during transients, with engine speed changing faster than 150 rpm/s and fuel and airflow also changing quickly, the signal must move; too little variation (25OBDG04B: 0.14 % or less in 40 of 50 samples) sets a two-trip Type B code.",["Sensing hose to sensor C kinked, blocked or disconnected","Condensate or frozen water in the sensing line","Sensor C drifted or sluggish","Exhaust leak near the measuring point"],["Warning lamp on","Particulate filter regenerations triggered too early or too late","Filter monitoring (missing substrate test) cannot complete"],2,1,["P2CE5","P2CE7","P2CE8","P2CE9","P2CEB","P2453","P245F","P226D"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2CE7:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor C Circuit Low","P2CE7 means the raw signal of filter pressure sensor C has dropped below its electrical floor, the typical picture of a signal wire shorted to ground or a lost 5 V supply. GM's 2025 diesel tables, where C is the relative pressure sensor behind the particulate filter, set it when the raw value is under 0.02 % in 158 of 200 samples taken every 12.5 ms with the ignition in range and the engine not cranking;",["Signal wire of sensor C shorted to ground, often from heat damage near the exhaust","5 V supply to the sensor interrupted","Sensor C internally failed with output stuck low"],["Warning lamp on","Live data shows sensor C at minimum regardless of engine load","Regeneration planning relies on a soot model only"],2,1,["P2CE5","P2CE6","P2CE8","P2CE9","P2CEC","P2454","P2460"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2CE8:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor C Circuit High","P2CE8 is the high-side electrical fault of filter pressure sensor C: its output sits above the range a working sensor can produce. GM's 2025 diesel tables aim this test at a broken line or a battery-voltage short and set the code when the raw signal of the downstream relative pressure sensor exceeds 99.80 % in 158 of 200 samples (12.5 ms task), Type B with two trips.",["Sensor ground or signal wire open","Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Sensor C internally failed with output stuck high"],["Warning lamp on","Live data shows sensor C at maximum even at idle","Regeneration requests may become more frequent"],2,1,["P2CE5","P2CE6","P2CE7","P2CE9","P2CED","P2455","P2461"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2CE9:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor C Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2CE9 catches a sensor C signal that jumps rather than drifts. GM's 2025 diesel tables call this a quick change check: when two consecutive raw samples of the downstream relative pressure sensor differ by more than 20 %, the sample counts as failed, and 99 failures in 200 samples set a Type B code.",["Loose or corroded terminal in the sensor C connector","Harness rubbing through on a bracket or exhaust part","Water entering the connector intermittently","Intermittent internal fault of the sensor"],["Warning lamp on, sometimes after rough roads or rain","Pressure value jumps in live data","Fault may disappear and return"],2,1,["P2CE5","P2CE6","P2CE7","P2CE8","P2CEE","P2456","P2462"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ C — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2CEA:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor D Circuit","Sensor D is the fourth slot for particulate filter pressure and only appears in Ford's 2024–25 petrol OBD summary, which watches a filter on each bank (missing substrate codes P226D and P226E); Ford does not say publicly which letter belongs to which filter or tap.",["Damaged or corroded connector at sensor D","Harness to sensor D damaged by exhaust heat","Sensor D internally faulty"],["Warning lamp on","Particulate filter monitoring for one bank incomplete","Usually no change in driveability"],2,1,["P2CEB","P2CEC","P2CED","P2CEE","U0697","P2CE5","P226E"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2CEB:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor D Circuit Range/Performance","P2CEB says sensor D reports a pressure that is electrically fine but does not match what the exhaust flow should produce. Ford is the only maker found using it, in its 2024–25 petrol summary for engines with a gasoline particulate filter per bank.",["Sensing hose to sensor D cracked, kinked or disconnected","Condensate in the sensing line after short trips","Sensor D drifted or responding slowly"],["Warning lamp on","Missing substrate test for that bank cannot be completed","Usually no noticeable change while driving"],2,1,["P2CEA","P2CEC","P2CED","P2CEE","P2CE6","P245F","P226E"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2CEC:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor D Circuit Low","P2CEC is set when an analog filter pressure sensor D delivers less voltage than it can in normal service. In Ford's 2024–25 petrol summary, the only public source using sensor D, the limit is 0.3 V for 5 s, checked continuously alongside the A, B and C sensors of the gasoline particulate filters.",["Signal wire of sensor D shorted to ground","5 V reference to sensor D open or pulled down","Sensor D failed with output stuck low"],["Warning lamp on","Live data shows sensor D at minimum","Further 5 V sensor codes if the shared supply is affected"],2,1,["P2CEA","P2CEB","P2CED","P2CEE","P2CE7","P2460"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2CED:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor D Circuit High","With P2CED the analog output of filter pressure sensor D lies above its usable top end. Ford's gasoline OBD document for 2024–25, with filters on both banks and up to four pressure sensors, sets the code above 4.73 V lasting 5 s. That usually traces back to an open sensor ground, a signal line touching the 5 V reference or battery voltage, or an open signal wire on an input with a pull-up.",["Sensor ground open or high resistance","Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Sensor D failed with output stuck high"],["Warning lamp on","Live data shows sensor D at maximum with the engine at idle","Filter monitoring for that bank incomplete"],2,1,["P2CEA","P2CEB","P2CEC","P2CEE","P2CE8","P2461"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2CEE:["Particulate Filter Pressure Sensor D Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2CEE stands for brief dropouts or jumps in the sensor D signal that do not last long enough for the low or high codes. Ford's 2024–25 petrol summary includes it in the continuous analog check of its gasoline particulate filter sensors, about 5 s to register, with no separate threshold given.",["Loose or corroded terminal in the sensor D connector","PCM software setting the code falsely (Ford bulletin 20-2257, F-150 2.7L)","Harness to sensor D chafed or intermittently shorted","Intermittent internal fault of sensor D"],["Warning lamp on, sometimes only now and then","Pressure value of sensor D jumps in live data","Possibly stored together with other, unrelated codes after a software issue"],2,1,["P2CEA","P2CEB","P2CEC","P2CED","P2CE9","P2462"],"חיישן לחץ מסנן חלקיקים‏ D — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2CEF:["Auxiliary Thermostat A Stuck Open","P2CEF concerns a second thermostat that regulates its own part of the cooling system; stuck open means coolant passes through it before the intended temperature, so that circuit warms too slowly or stays too cool.",["Debris in the coolant holding the thermostat valve off its seat","Worn or leaking wax element, piston no longer returns","Earlier thermostat version superseded by the maker (Mercedes M139)"],["Engine warning lamp","Low coolant temperature warning or slow warm-up","Weaker cabin heating in cold weather"],2,1,["P2CF0","P2CF1","P0128","P026F"],"תרמוסטט עזר‏ A — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2CF0:["Auxiliary Thermostat A Stuck Closed","P2CF0 is the closed-side counterpart of P2CEF: auxiliary thermostat A fails to open, so the circuit it governs gets too little flow and its temperature climbs past the regulating point while other parts of the engine may look normal. No manufacturer documents P2CF0 publicly.",["Wax element lost its charge, thermostat no longer opens","Piston jammed by deposits or debris","Air pocket around the element after a coolant service, so it never sees hot coolant"],["Engine warning lamp","High temperature in one cooling circuit or an overheating warning","Possible power reduction to protect the engine"],2,3,["P2CEF","P2CF2","P0217","P026F"],"תרמוסטט עזר‏ A — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2CF1:["Auxiliary Thermostat B Stuck Open","P2CF1 covers a further auxiliary thermostat, labelled B, that stays open, so its loop loses its warm-up phase and runs below the intended temperature. Which loop B controls is the maker's choice: engines with split cooling may regulate head, block, oil or heater flow with separate thermostats, each needing its own temperature sensor for diagnosis.",["Valve held open by debris or a weak return spring","Worn wax element that no longer retracts fully","Temperature sensor of that loop reading too low and faking the fault"],["Engine warning lamp","Slow warm-up and higher fuel use in cold weather","Weaker cabin heating"],2,1,["P2CF2","P2CEF","P0128","P026F"],"תרמוסטט עזר‏ B — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2CF2:["Auxiliary Thermostat B Stuck Closed","P2CF2 is logged when auxiliary thermostat B does not open: the temperature in its loop keeps rising beyond the opening point while the controller expects it to level off. The loop assigned to B differs by maker, so the actual consequence can be an overheating cylinder head, hot engine oil or, if B guards a smaller branch, merely a local hot spot that the main gauge does not show.",["Leaking wax charge, thermostat stays shut","Piston seized by corrosion or deposits","Temperature sensor of that loop reading too high"],["Engine warning lamp","Overheating warning or high oil temperature","Reduced power to protect the engine"],2,3,["P2CF1","P2CF0","P0217","P026F"],"תרמוסטט עזר‏ B — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2CF3:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Pump A Underspeed","P2CF3 is set when battery coolant pump A turns more slowly than the controller commands, although it is powered and not fully blocked. Typical reasons are a sluggish bearing, deposits on the impeller, low supply voltage or a pump motor that has lost strength; a faulty speed signal can produce the same picture.",["Worn bearing or deposits slowing the pump","Battery controller software misreading pump speed (Ford 2020 hybrids)","Voltage drop on the pump feed or ground under load","Implausible speed feedback from the pump electronics"],["MIL or hybrid system warning","Battery temperature higher than usual","Reduced drive or charging power"],2,3,["P2B29","P0CFF","P0C4A","P2B28","P2CF7"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2CF4:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Pump B Supply Voltage Circuit","P2CF4 is about the power feed of the second battery coolant pump, B: the pump or its control unit sees a supply voltage outside the permitted window, or none at all. Unlike the control-circuit codes P0E1A to P0E1C, which watch the command line, this code looks at the line that actually powers the motor, typically a fused 12 V feed plus ground.",["Blown fuse or faulty relay in the pump B feed","Corroded connector or poor ground on the pump B supply","Weak 12 V battery or DC/DC output dragging the supply down","Internal fault in the pump electronics misreading the supply"],["MIL or hybrid warning on","Pump B silent when commanded","Charging or drive power limited when the battery warms up"],2,3,["P0E1A","P0E1E","P2CF5","P0C4B","U0695"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2CF5:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Pump B Stuck/Stalled","P2CF5 means battery coolant pump B does not turn at all although it is commanded and powered: the rotor is blocked, or the pump electronics has given up after failed start attempts. A seized bearing, debris or deposits after coolant work, a failed motor winding or frozen coolant in a weak mixture are the usual suspects. Ford's 2024 summary lists the corresponding pump fault type as actuator stuck (71).",["Pump B rotor or bearing seized","Debris or deposits jamming the impeller after coolant work","Pump motor or its electronics failed","Coolant frozen due to insufficient antifreeze"],["Warning lamp for hybrid system or engine","Charging slower or interrupted","Power reduced as battery temperature rises"],2,3,["P2CF7","P2CF6","P0CFF","P0E1D"],""],P2CF6:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Pump B Overspeed/Air in System","P2CF6 reports that battery coolant pump B spins above its commanded speed. Once a centrifugal pump loses its load it accelerates, so the most common explanation is air or a low level in the loop, which the title names directly.",["Air left in the battery loop after service or poor bleeding","Leak at a battery coolant tube or joint lowering the level","Impeller slipping on the shaft or broken","False speed feedback from the pump electronics"],["Gurgling or whining from the pump area","Coolant level in the battery reservoir drops","MIL or hybrid warning, sometimes without other effect"],2,3,["P2CF7","P2CF5","P2B29","P0E1D"],""],P2CF7:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Pump B Underspeed","P2CF7 is the underspeed fault of battery coolant pump B: the pump turns, but clearly below the commanded speed for longer than the controller tolerates. Compared with the stall code P2CF5 the rotor is still moving, so friction, a partly obstructed impeller, coolant that is too viscous in the cold or a sagging supply are likelier than a dead motor.",["Worn bearing or deposits slowing pump B","Supply voltage of pump B dropping under load","Wrong or aged coolant too viscous at low temperature","Battery controller software misjudging pump speed"],["MIL or hybrid system warning","Battery runs warmer than normal"],2,3,["P2CF6","P2CF5","P2CF3","P2CF4"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2CF8:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve D Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P2CF8 is raised by the driver of coolant bypass valve D when it measures excessive current or overheats and protects itself. No manufacturer documents P2CF8 publicly, and the meaning of D varies: Ford's 2020–2025 gasoline summaries define valve D as the cabin heating valve and report only the smart driver's circuit fault P26BD, plus P26BF from 2024, while GM's 2019 and 2025 tables use the D stuck codes P26C0/P26C2…",["Valve stiff or seized, so the motor or solenoid draws excess current","Shorted winding in the valve actuator","Valve wires partly shorted to ground or to each other","Overheated or faulty output stage in the control module"],["Engine warning lamp","Cabin heat weak or not adjustable (heater valve)","Engine warms up abnormally if the valve sits in the engine loop"],2,3,["P26BD","P26BE","P26BF","P26C1","P23C6"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ D — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה"],P2CF9:["Belt Integrated Starter Generator Belt Tensioner Control Circuit/Open","P2CF9 applies to belt starter-generator systems whose belt tensioner is moved by an actuator rather than by a spring alone. Patents describe the idea: Ford raises belt tension for engine starts and boost and lowers it while charging (US 9,297,445, with an actuator that falls back to high tension when unpowered); a Hyundai/Kia patent uses a solenoid with three tension stages (US 10,648,544);",["Broken wire or loose connector in the tensioner drive circuit","Open coil or motor winding in the tensioner actuator","Output stage in the controlling module failed"],["Belt squeal or slip during automatic restarts","Stop-start or electric assist disabled","MIL or system warning on"],2,1,["P2CFA","P2CFB","P2BA3","P0A1E"],""],P2CFA:["Belt Integrated Starter Generator Belt Tensioner Control Circuit Low","P2CFA is logged when the control line of an electrically adjusted BISG belt tensioner reads too low, typically a ground short or a driver that holds the line down permanently. The tensioner's reaction varies with the design: Ford's patent US 9,297,445 describes an actuator that defaults to high belt tension when power is lost, which protects starts but costs efficiency, while a solenoid unit like the one in…",["Tensioner control wire chafed through to ground","Internal short in the tensioner actuator","Water or corrosion bridging pins at the actuator plug"],["Stop-start no longer active","Belt noise at start or under load","Warning lamp on"],2,1,["P2CF9","P2CFB","P2BA3"],""],P2CFB:["Belt Integrated Starter Generator Belt Tensioner Control Circuit High","P2CFB mirrors P2CFA on the high side: the tensioner control circuit of a belt integrated starter generator shows a voltage above the expected range, usually from a wire touching a battery-voltage feed or a driver stage that cannot switch off. The actuator may then be held in one position permanently.",["Control wire shorted to a supply voltage","Output stage in the module unable to switch off","Actuator electronics reporting an implausibly high level"],["Belt slip or squeal at engine start","Faster belt wear or bearing noise","MIL on, stop-start or assist unavailable"],2,1,["P2CF9","P2CFA","P2BA3"],""],P2CFC:["A/C Clutch Control Circuit","P2CFC is the general fault of the output that powers the compressor clutch coil directly, unlike P0645, which covers a clutch relay. Ford is the documented user and runs it in a body module, not the PCM. Special service messages 50811 and 51380 list P2CFC, often with P0645 and P2CFD, in the HVAC module of 2020–2023 Explorer and Aviator;",["Spread or pushed-out terminals at the body control module connector","Open or burnt clutch field coil","Damaged wire or connector between module and compressor","Faulty clutch output in the controlling module"],["A/C blows only warm air","Compressor clutch does not engage","Code stored in the HVAC or body control module, usually without engine lamp"],2,0,["P2CFD","P2CFE","P2CFF","P0645"],"מצמד מזגן — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],P2CFD:["A/C Clutch Control Circuit Low","P2CFD means the voltage on the clutch coil output reads lower than the module expects for the commanded state, most often because the line or the coil is grounded. With a high-side driver that short pulls the feed down, so the clutch cannot engage and the driver may protect itself; on a low-side design a grounded line would hold the clutch in instead.",["Clutch feed wire chafed through and touching ground","Damaged terminals at the body control module (Ford SSM 50811/51380)","Clutch coil shorted internally to its housing"],["No cooling, compressor clutch stays disengaged","Possibly blown fuse in the clutch feed"],2,0,["P2CFC","P2CFE","P2CFF","P0646"],"מצמד מזגן — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2CFE:["A/C Clutch Control Circuit High","P2CFE reports a clutch coil output that sits higher than it should, typically because the line touches a battery feed. Then the clutch may stay energized after the module switches off, so the compressor keeps running and can ice the evaporator; a low-side driver instead shuts down and the clutch never engages. No manufacturer documents P2CFE publicly.",["Clutch control wire shorted to a battery-powered circuit","Output stage in the module stuck switched on","Moisture bridging pins in the compressor or module connector"],["Compressor runs even with A/C switched off","Iced evaporator, weak airflow after a while","Alternatively no cooling at all if the driver shuts down"],2,0,["P2CFC","P2CFD","P2CFF","P0647"],"מצמד מזגן — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2CFF:["A/C Clutch Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P2CFF does not come from a voltage comparison but from the protective logic of the clutch output itself. Modern smart switches limit their current and switch off once the junction gets too hot; the TI TPS1HB16-Q1, a typical automotive high-side switch, shuts down from 150 °C and retries within milliseconds, and the module logs this as overcurrent or overtemperature.",["Clutch field coil with shorted turns drawing too much current","Feed wire partly shorted to ground","Output stage overheating from poor module cooling or an internal fault"],["Cooling cuts in and out","Compressor clutch disengages under load or after warm-up"],2,0,["P2CFC","P2CFD","P2CFE","P0645"],"מצמד מזגן — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה"],P2D00:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump A Stuck/Stalled","P2D00 reports that coolant pump A of the motor electronics loop, which cools the inverter and drive-motor electronics, does not rotate although commanded. It opens its own series P2D00–P2D0E (stuck, overspeed/air, underspeed, supply voltage and module overtemperature for pumps A to C) and should not be confused with the Hybrid/EV electronics pump codes P2C66–P2C68.",["Pump rotor or bearing seized","Battery or powertrain controller software misreading the pump (Ford 2020 hybrids)","Debris jamming the impeller after coolant work","Pump motor or integrated electronics failed"],["MIL on","Reduced drive power when the inverter gets hot","Hybrid system warning message"],2,3,["P2D01","P2D02","P2D03","P2D04","P0C73","P2D05"],""],P2D01:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump A Overspeed/Air in System","P2D01 is logged when the first electric pump of the motor electronics loop, which carries heat away from the inverter and drive-motor electronics, spins faster than commanded. A centrifugal pump that suddenly has nothing to push races, so the title points straight at air or a low coolant level.",["Low coolant level or trapped air in the motor electronics loop, for example after service work","Monitoring strategy in the control software (Ford 2020 hybrids, cured by reprogramming)","External leak at hoses, connectors or the pump housing that keeps drawing in air","Loose impeller or false speed feedback from the pump electronics"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Coolant level in the degas bottle at or below minimum","Gurgling or whining from the electric pump","Reduced drive power when the inverter runs hot"],2,3,["P2D00","P2D02","P2D03","P2D04","P2D06","P2D0B","P0C73"],""],P2D02:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump A Underspeed","With P2D02 the controller sees pump A of the motor electronics cooling loop turning, but clearly below its target speed for longer than allowed. The rotor is not locked, which separates it from P2D00; a stiff bearing, deposits on the impeller, cold and thick coolant or a supply that sags under load are therefore more likely than a dead motor.",["Stiff bearing or deposits on the impeller of pump A","Control software strategy (Ford 2020 hybrids, fixed by reprogramming)","Voltage drop on the pump feed or ground under load","Wrong, contaminated or aged coolant raising viscosity at low temperature"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Higher inverter or motor electronics temperatures in live data","Power limitation under sustained load"],2,3,["P2D00","P2D01","P2D03","P2D07","P2D0C","P0C73"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ A — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2D03:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump A Supply Voltage Circuit","P2D03 concerns the power feed of motor electronics coolant pump A rather than its command line: the pump, or the module reading its status, finds the supply outside its allowed window or missing. That points to a blown fuse, a corroded connector, a weak ground or a 12 V system that drops too low. The command-side faults of the same pump are P0A05 to P0A07;",["Corroded connector, loose terminal or poor ground at pump A","Blown fuse or faulty relay in the pump feed","Weak 12 V battery or DC/DC converter output too low","Software strategy on 2020 Ford hybrids, cured by reprogramming"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Pump A runs intermittently or not at all","Further low-voltage codes in other modules"],2,3,["P2D00","P2D01","P2D04","P2D08","P2D0D","P0A05"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ A — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2D04:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump A Control Module Overtemperature","P2D04 refers to the small electronics built into coolant pump A of the motor electronics loop: its own temperature has exceeded the limit, and the pump usually reports this before cutting back or switching off to protect itself. Heat builds up when the pump works hard against a restriction, runs dry, sits close to a hot component or has an internal electrical fault.",["Pump running dry or with too little coolant, so it loses its own cooling","Blocked or kinked line forcing the pump to work at high load","Internal fault in the pump control electronics","Software strategy on 2020 Ford hybrids, cured by reprogramming"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, sometimes only after longer drives or in hot weather","Pump stops temporarily and restarts after cooling down","Inverter overtemperature warning or reduced power"],2,3,["P2D00","P2D03","P2D09","P2D0E","P0C73","P0A3C"],"מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ A — חום יתר"],P2D05:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump B Stuck/Stalled","P2D05 opens the pump B block of the motor electronics series: the second electric pump in the loop that cools inverters and drive-motor electronics is commanded and supplied, yet its rotor does not move. Where a vehicle has two electric drive units, B may be the pump serving the second inverter. A seized bearing, debris after a coolant change, a burnt winding or coolant that froze in a weak mixture can lock it.",["Seized bearing or blocked rotor in pump B","Debris or deposits in the loop after repairs or coolant change","Failed motor winding or pump electronics unable to start the motor","Coolant frozen because the antifreeze ratio is too low"],["Malfunction or hybrid system warning lamp on","No pump noise or vibration when the pump should run","Rising temperature of the second inverter, power limited"],2,3,["P2D06","P2D07","P2D00","P2D0A","P0C74"],""],P2D06:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump B Overspeed/Air in System","P2D06 says pump B of the motor electronics loop turns above its commanded speed, the classic sign of a pump that has lost its coolant column to air or a falling level. Ford documents a real case: customer satisfaction programme 23B09 covered 72 F-150 Lightning trucks of model years 2022–2023, built between 28 and 30 September 2022, whose high-voltage battery coolant tubes were made of the wrong material.",["Coolant leak anywhere in the shared loop, such as faulty battery coolant tubes (Ford 23B09)","Air left in the loop after filling without the prescribed bleeding procedure","Impeller slipping on the shaft or implausible speed feedback"],["Often none apart from the stored code","Falling level in the degas bottle or traces of coolant","Inverter overtemperature warning and reduced acceleration if the loss continues"],2,3,["P2D05","P2D07","P2D01","P2D0B","P2B29","P0A3C"],""],P2D07:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump B Underspeed","P2D07 is the underspeed report for the second motor electronics pump: B is moving, so it is not stalled as in P2D05, yet its actual speed stays well short of the request for too long. Friction in a worn bearing, a partly obstructed impeller, a pump motor that has lost strength or a supply that drops when the pump draws current are the usual chain of suspects. No manufacturer publicly documents P2D07.",["Worn bearing or friction inside pump B","Impeller partly obstructed by deposits or debris","High resistance in feed or ground causing the voltage to sag under load","Pump motor or its electronics losing performance with age"],["Warning lamp on","Pump B speed in live data clearly below the target value","Power limitation during long climbs or towing"],2,3,["P2D05","P2D06","P2D02","P2D0C","P0C74"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2D08:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump B Supply Voltage Circuit","P2D08 watches the line that actually powers motor electronics coolant pump B, typically a fused 12 V feed plus ground: the voltage there is too low, too high or absent. The control-line faults of the same pump have their own codes, P0B38 to P0B3A, so P2D08 sends the search to fuses, relays, splices and the ground point rather than to the signal wire.",["Corroded connector, loose terminal or poor ground at pump B","Blown fuse or faulty relay in the pump B feed","Weak 12 V battery or DC/DC converter delivering too little voltage","Chafed supply wire with intermittent contact"],["Warning lamp on","Pump B works only intermittently","Additional voltage codes in neighbouring modules"],2,3,["P2D09","P2D05","P2D03","P2D0D","P0B38"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2D09:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump B Control Module Overtemperature","P2D09 is raised when the controller inside motor electronics coolant pump B reports that it has become too hot. The pump's own electronics are cooled by the fluid it moves, so the code often follows dry running, a blocked line that makes the motor draw high current, or a mounting spot exposed to heat; an internal defect in the pump board is the other possibility. No manufacturer publicly documents P2D09.",["Low coolant or air, so pump B electronics lose their cooling","Restricted line or clogged component raising pump load and current","Internal defect of the pump B control board"],["Code appears mainly in hot weather or under sustained load","Pump B switches off temporarily","Warning lamp and reduced power"],2,3,["P2D08","P2D05","P2D04","P2D0E","P0C74"],"מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — חום יתר"],P2D0A:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump C Stuck/Stalled","P2D0A starts the five codes for pump C, a third electric pump that some layouts add to the motor electronics loop, for example for a further drive unit or a separate charger and DC/DC branch. The code means pump C is driven and powered but its rotor stays still. Seized bearings, foreign bodies in the impeller and burnt windings are the usual mechanical and electrical reasons.",["Seized bearing or blocked rotor in pump C","Foreign bodies or deposits jamming the impeller","Burnt motor winding or failed start electronics in the pump"],["Warning lamp on","Pump C silent while commanded on","Rising temperature in the branch cooled by pump C and reduced power"],2,3,["P2D0B","P2D0C","P2D00","P2D05","P2BD7"],""],P2D0B:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump C Overspeed/Air in System","P2D0B is stored when pump C of the motor electronics loop reaches a speed above the commanded value. Since a pump with air around its impeller loses load and accelerates, the code is first of all a hint at a low level, a leak or incomplete bleeding; a third pump in a branch that sits high in the vehicle is especially prone to trapping air. No manufacturer publicly documents P2D0B.",["Air trapped in the pump C branch after incomplete bleeding","Coolant loss through a leak in the loop","Loose impeller or false speed signal from the pump"],["Warning lamp on, sometimes without other effects","Coolant level below minimum or visible leak traces","Gurgling noise from the pump area"],2,3,["P2D0A","P2D0C","P2D01","P2D06","P2BD7"],""],P2D0C:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump C Underspeed","P2D0C tells you that pump C, the third pump of the motor electronics loop, is turning too slowly for longer than its controller accepts. Compared with P2D0A the rotor is free, and compared with P2D0B the problem is lack of speed, not lack of load: think of a dragging bearing, a partly clogged impeller or filter screen, or a feed that cannot hold its voltage while the motor draws current.",["Dragging bearing or internal friction in pump C","Partly clogged impeller or screen in the pump C branch","Voltage drop on feed or ground of pump C under load"],["Warning lamp on","Pump C speed below target in live data","Higher component temperatures and power limits under load"],2,3,["P2D0A","P2D0B","P2D02","P2D07","P2BD7"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2D0D:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump C Supply Voltage Circuit","P2D0D flags the supply side of motor electronics coolant pump C: the voltage on its power feed is outside the permitted window or missing. Its counterparts on the command line are P2BD4 (open), P2BD5 (low) and P2BD6 (high), so a technician who sees P2D0D alone should check the fuse, relay, power splice and ground of pump C before touching the signal wire. No manufacturer publicly documents P2D0D.",["Poor ground or corroded supply terminal at pump C","Blown fuse or faulty relay in the pump C feed","Weak 12 V battery or low DC/DC converter output"],["Warning lamp on","Pump C runs intermittently or not at all","Other voltage-related codes stored at the same time"],2,3,["P2D0E","P2BD4","P2BD5","P2D03","P2D08"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2D0E:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump C Control Module Overtemperature","P2D0E closes the motor electronics pump series: the control electronics integrated in pump C have reported an internal temperature above their limit. Smart pumps protect themselves by derating or switching off, and the module storing the code learns of it through the pump's status feedback.",["Pump C running with too little coolant or air","Blocked branch raising pump load and electronics temperature","Defective control board inside pump C"],["Code sets mainly in heat or after long high-load operation","Pump C switches off and restarts after cooling","Warning lamp and reduced power"],2,3,["P2D0D","P2D0A","P2D04","P2D09","P2BD6"],"מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C — חום יתר"],P2D0F:["Engine Pre-Ignition Above Threshold","Pre-ignition means the charge ignites by itself ahead of the spark, mostly at low engine speed and high load in small turbocharged direct-injection engines. Ford patents describe how such events are found: the knock sensor signal is judged in an early crank angle window against a higher limit than ordinary knock, and a counter per cylinder keeps the history.",["Fuel with too low an octane rating or poor quality","Oil droplets in the chamber, unsuitable oil or oil diluted by fuel","Glowing carbon deposits on pistons or valves","Spark plugs with too hot a heat range or worn electrodes","Engine control calibration that needs a manufacturer update"],["Check engine light, often after hard acceleration from low speed","Sharp knocking or a single loud bang under load","Rough running or misfire if a piston has already been damaged","Rising oil consumption after repeated events"],2,3,["P2D10","P0324","P0325","P0300"],""],P2D10:["Engine Pre-Ignition Above Threshold - Forced Limited Power","P2D10 is the escalated form of P2D0F: pre-ignition events have exceeded the threshold, and the engine computer now restricts power to protect pistons and rings. A Ford patent gives an idea of the scale, cutting engine load by about 10 percent after three detected events while also capping boost and enriching the mixture.",["Repeated pre-ignition from low-octane or contaminated fuel","Engine software fault, known on VW 1.5 L turbo together with P0196","Oil droplets, wrong oil grade or fuel-diluted oil in the cylinder","Piston or ring damage that already keeps causing hot spots"],["Noticeably reduced power, often with a warning message","Check engine or EPC light on","Knocking noises under load before the limit kicks in"],2,3,["P2D0F","P0196","P0324","P0300"],""],P2D11:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve A Position Not Learned","Electrically driven exhaust flaps need their end stops taught to the control unit, so that commanded and actual angles line up. P2D11 says this adaptation is missing or invalid for valve A, as after a new actuator, a new muffler, a reflashed ECM or a flat battery. Maserati lists P2D11 together with its own P1217 on the Grecale 2.0 L4 mild hybrid, where owners see the MIL and hear abnormal exhaust noise.",["Learn procedure not run after actuator, silencer or ECM work","Learned values lost after a flat or disconnected battery","Corroded or binding flap that cannot reach its end stops","Control software that rejects the learn result"],["Check engine light","Unusual exhaust noise, rattling or a flap hunting for position","Exhaust sound modes no longer change"],2,1,["P2D12","P2D1B","P26C5","P26FE","P2BF5"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ A — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2D12:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve B Position Not Learned","P2D12 is the counterpart of P2D11 for the second flap or bank 2: the stored end positions of exhaust valve B are missing or were rejected. No manufacturer documents P2D12 publicly. The closest public logic sits in GM's 23OBDG07 table, which decides from the PWM feedback of exhaust valve 2 whether its end stops have been learned, over 4 seconds with more than 9 V on board, as a two-trip fault under its own code…",["Alignment or learn run for valve B skipped after repair","Adaptation erased by a discharged or disconnected battery","Actuator mounted out of position or flap shaft binding","Outdated engine software that makes the learn fail"],["MIL on, sometimes with an exhaust mode not available message","Flap B noisy or searching for position","No audible change between sound modes on one side"],2,1,["P2D11","P2D1B","P2BF8","P2BFB","P2BFD"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ B — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2D13:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve C Control Circuit/Open","P2D13 tells that the drive circuit of a third exhaust flap, valve C, is open or cannot be evaluated. Such a valve only exists on layouts with more than two controlled flaps, for instance a separate bypass in the rear silencer next to one flap per bank. No manufacturer publishes P2D13 or any other valve C code. Ford's 2020-2024 OBD summaries know only valve A on bank 1 and valve B on bank 2;",["Actuator connector unplugged or loose after exhaust work","Broken control wire near the hot exhaust or at a bracket","Internal open in the valve C actuator","Failed output stage in the control module"],["Check engine light","Flap C stays in its rest position, exhaust sound does not change","Message that an exhaust or drive mode is unavailable"],2,1,["P2D14","P2D15","P2D16","P26C5","P2BF8"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2D14:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve C Control Circuit Low","With P2D14 the drive wire of flap C is dragged toward ground when the driver expects a higher level. Chafed insulation touching the body or the exhaust, a crushed harness after the car was jacked up, or a shorted actuator winding are the classic reasons. No manufacturer documents P2D14.",["Control wire chafed through and touching ground","Shorted winding or electronics in the valve C actuator","Water or salt bridging pins in the connector"],["MIL on","Flap C does not move or stays at its default angle","Exhaust louder or quieter than the selected mode"],2,1,["P2D13","P2D15","P2D16","P26C6","P2BF9"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2D15:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve C Control Circuit High","P2D15 is set when the drive wire of flap C carries too high a level, so the output stage cannot pull it down as commanded. Either the wire touches something live, or the electronics inside the actuator push voltage back onto it. No manufacturer publishes P2D15.",["Control wire shorted to a voltage-carrying circuit","Defective electronics in the valve C actuator feeding voltage back","Output stage in the control module stuck high"],["Check engine light","Flap C open or moving without being commanded","Exhaust sound modes unavailable"],2,1,["P2D13","P2D14","P2D16","P26C7","P2BFA"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2D16:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve C Control Performance","P2D16 covers the case where flap C passes every wiring test but still fails to follow its command: it moves too slowly, stops short of the target or drifts away from it. No manufacturer documents valve C codes publicly. Ford's handling of its A and B flaps shows the idea. The actuator electronics flag a jammed flap through the PWM return line, and a plausibility test sets the measured against the requested angle.",["Flap shaft seized by soot or corrosion","Worn or overheated actuator motor or gearbox","Silencer or actuator bracket misaligned after exhaust work","Actuator not aligned after replacement"],["MIL on, possibly with an exhaust mode warning","Rattle or buzzing from the flap area","Exhaust sound no longer matches the selected mode"],2,1,["P2D13","P2D14","P2D15","P2D18","P26FE","P2BFB"],"בקרת שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D17:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve C Position Circuit","P2D17 is the catch-all fault for the return signal by which actuator C reports its angle to the engine computer. The signal is missing or unusable, yet it does not fit the clear low or high pattern of P2D19 and P2D1A. The code can only appear where a third flap with its own position output exists. No manufacturer documents P2D17.",["Corroded or loose connector on actuator C","Damaged feedback or ground wire near the exhaust","Failed position sensor inside the actuator"],["Check engine light","Flap C held in a default position by the control unit","Sound modes partly unavailable"],2,1,["P2D18","P2D19","P2D1A","P2D13","P2BFC"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2D18:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve C Position Circuit Range/Performance","With P2D18 the position signal of flap C is electrically sound, but its value makes no sense: the reported angle lags or contradicts the command, the end points have wandered off the stored values, or the reading creeps while the flap is idle. No manufacturer publishes P2D18.",["Actuator or silencer shifted so the end points no longer match","Worn or drifting position sensor in the actuator","Pinched or chafed wiring causing an unsteady signal","Learned values no longer valid after parts were replaced"],["MIL on after a drive cycle","Exhaust note changes at the wrong moment or flap C hunts","Drive or exhaust mode reported unavailable"],2,1,["P2D17","P2D19","P2D1A","P2D16","P2D1B","P2BFD"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2D19:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve C Position Circuit Low","P2D19 is stored when the angle feedback from actuator C drops beneath the bottom of its permitted band. With an analog sensor the line then reads close to zero volts, mostly through a ground short or a lost 5 V supply; with a PWM return the duty cycle hangs close to zero. No manufacturer documents P2D19.",["Feedback wire shorted to ground","Missing sensor supply voltage or open supply wire","Position sensor in actuator C failed low","Faulty evaluation logic in the engine software"],["Check engine light","Flap C no longer adjusted, default position held","Possible power reduction on engines that tie the flap to cylinder deactivation"],2,3,["P2D17","P2D18","P2D1A","P2BF6","P2BFE"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2D1A:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve C Position Circuit High","P2D1A flags an angle feedback from actuator C that sits above the top of its permitted band: an analog line close to the supply level, or a PWM return hanging near full duty. Typical reasons are a broken sensor ground, a feedback wire chafed against a live conductor, or water creeping between the connector contacts.",["Open or corroded sensor ground","Feedback wire touching a voltage-carrying wire","Moisture or road salt in the actuator connector","Position sensor in actuator C failed high"],["MIL on","Control unit ignores flap C feedback and stops adjusting it","Exhaust sound stuck in one mode"],2,1,["P2D17","P2D18","P2D19","P2BF7","P2BFF"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2D1B:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve C Position Not Learned","P2D1B closes the valve C series: the control unit holds no valid end stop values for the third exhaust flap, so it cannot translate its position feedback into a reliable angle. No manufacturer documents P2D1B publicly, and so far even the A and B versions P2D11 and P2D12 are rare in published material.",["Learn run for flap C not completed after installation or repair","Learned end stops lost after battery disconnection","Flap blocked or binding so the learn run aborts","Engine software that needs an update before the learn succeeds"],["Check engine light shortly after exhaust or battery work","Flap C hunting, buzzing or rattling","Sound modes do not switch as expected"],2,1,["P2D11","P2D12","P2D16","P2D18"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ C — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2D1C:["Cold Start EGR A/B Ratio Performance","P2D1C belongs to engines with two exhaust gas recirculation paths, A and B, whose share of the total recirculated flow is scheduled differently right after a cold start. The code says that during the cold start strategy the split between both paths did not follow its target.",["EGR valve A or B sooted or sluggish, so it cannot reach its cold start position","Restricted EGR cooler or leaking pipe in one of the two loops","Faulty pressure, temperature or position signal used to estimate the flows","Engine control software that misjudges the split in cold weather"],["Check engine light after cold starts, often without noticeable driveability change","Rough or smoky running in the first minutes after starting","Further EGR flow codes such as P0401 or P049B stored alongside"],3,1,["P04DD","P04DE","P0401","P049B","P0400","P049D"],"יחס EGR התנעה קרה‏ A/B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D1D:["Reductant System Leak Detected - Small Leak","P2D1D reports that the pressurised DEF (AdBlue) circuit between pump, line and dosing valve loses fluid slowly, too little to collapse pressure but enough to be measurable. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. A supplier patent from Plastic Omnium shows how such leaks are found: with dosing at zero the pump should idle near 1,500 rpm at 5 bar, and a speed above 1,750 rpm raises suspicion;",["Seeping quick connector or damaged O-ring on the DEF pressure line","Worn seal or gasket at the DEF dosing valve on the exhaust pipe","Hairline crack in the DEF line, often after freezing or chafing","Pump module leaking internally or at its housing seal"],["Check engine light, usually with an exhaust service message","White crystalline deposits at line fittings or the dosing valve","DEF consumption noticeably higher than usual"],2,3,["P2D1E","P202D","P20E8","P2D1F","P2BA8"],""],P2D1E:["Reductant System Leak Detected - Large Leak","P2D1E is the severe form of the DEF leak verdict: the pump cannot build or hold working pressure because fluid escapes freely, for example from a split or disconnected line. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["DEF line pulled off or connector not latched after service","DEF line split by ice expansion or road debris","Cracked dosing valve body or blown seal at the exhaust","Cracked pump module housing in the tank unit"],["Check engine light and DEF system warning soon after start","Puddle or wet trail of DEF under the vehicle","Countdown to restricted speed or no restart"],2,3,["P2D1D","P202D","P20E8","P2BA8","P2BAA"],""],P2D1F:["Reductant System Flow - Restricted","P2D1F means DEF still moves, but less than the dosing command implies, typically because a filter, line or dosing valve tip is partly clogged. Stellantis lists it on 2025–2026 Ram 2500 to 5500 heavy-duty trucks together with P208B, P218F and P20E8 and advises a bucket test before replacing the doser: with doser fitted, pressure should hold 80–94 psi for over 6 minutes; with doser removed, 55–75 psi for over 30 s.",["Urea crystals partly blocking the dosing valve nozzle","Clogged DEF pump filter or suction strainer","Kinked or pinched DEF line after body or exhaust work","Contaminated or aged DEF leaving deposits"],["Check engine light with exhaust fluid service message","Code returns intermittently, often without a lasting fault","Possible NOx efficiency code if dosing stays low"],2,3,["P2D20","P218F","P208B","P20E8","P2BAA"],""],P2D20:["Reductant System Flow - Blocked","P2D20 is the hard verdict after P2D1F: no measurable DEF passes, so the pump keeps pressure but nothing reaches the exhaust. A public manufacturer description of P2D20 does not exist; GM's 2025 diesel tables flag the matching symptom under P20E9 when DEF pressure stays more than 63 kPa above its setpoint for 4 s during closed loop control (Type A).",["Dosing valve stuck closed or nozzle fully crystallised","Frozen DEF in line or valve due to a failed line heater","Crushed or fully kinked DEF line","Pump filter completely blocked by deposits"],["Check engine light and DEF warning, often in frost","Countdown to speed limitation or start inhibit","Follow-up NOx efficiency codes"],2,3,["P2D1F","P20E9","P218F","P208E","P2BA8"],""],P2D21:["Turbocharger Interstage Pressure Sensor A Circuit","Engines with two turbochargers in series can measure the pressure between the low-pressure and the high-pressure compressor. GM's patent on two-stage boost control uses this mid-stage value to split the pressure ratio between both stages and to steer the low-pressure wastegate; Cummins describes the same sensor between the stages and the intercooler.",["Loose, corroded or oil-soaked sensor connector","Chafed or heat-damaged harness near the turbochargers","Failed interstage pressure sensor","Shared 5 V sensor supply faulty"],["Check engine light","Reduced power, boost held to a safe value","Sluggish response while accelerating"],2,3,["P2D22","P2D23","P2D24","P2D25","P0239"],""],P2D22:["Turbocharger Interstage Pressure Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","P2D22 flags an interstage pressure reading that is electrically valid but implausible, for instance offset, stuck or out of step with the other pressures. No manufacturer documents a detection rule. A Cummins patent on a two-stage engine shows what plausible means: with the compressor bypass valve open, interstage and charge pressure should be almost the same, about 102 kPa at 600 rpm and 119 kPa at 2,000 rpm;",["Sensor element drifted or offset","Sensor port clogged with oil or soot deposits","Leak in the duct or intercooler between the stages","Stage bypass valve stuck, giving pressures the model does not expect"],["Check engine light","Uneven boost build-up or reduced power","Possible boost deviation codes alongside"],2,3,["P2D21","P2D23","P2D24","P2D25","P0240","P2263"],""],P2D23:["Turbocharger Interstage Pressure Sensor A Circuit Low","P2D23 says the interstage pressure signal sits below the lowest voltage a working sensor can produce. Typical causes are a signal wire shorted to ground, a lost 5 V supply or an internal sensor short. No public table gives a threshold for this sensor; for comparison, Ford's 2023 diesels treat a DEF pressure sensor below 0.2 V as circuit low.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","5 V reference open or pulled down by another sensor","Sensor shorted internally"],["Check engine light","Boost limited, noticeably less power","Further codes if the shared sensor supply is affected"],2,3,["P2D24","P2D21","P2D22","P2D25","P0241"],""],P2D24:["Turbocharger Interstage Pressure Sensor A Circuit High","P2D24 is the opposite case to P2D23: the interstage pressure signal is pinned near or above the top of its range. On a three-wire sensor this usually points to an open ground, a signal wire touching the 5 V reference or battery voltage, or an open signal line pulled up inside the controller. Ford's 2023 diesels, as a comparable pressure sensor example, set circuit high above 4.85 V.",["Open sensor ground or corroded ground pin","Open signal wire pulled up by the controller","Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Sensor electronics failed high"],["Check engine light","Power reduced, boost held back","Interstage pressure reads high even with the engine off"],2,3,["P2D23","P2D21","P2D22","P2D25","P0242"],""],P2D25:["Turbocharger Interstage Pressure Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2D25 is set when the interstage pressure signal jumps or drops out faster than any real pressure between two turbo stages could change, typically through brief interruptions in the circuit. No manufacturer documents the code or its rate limit publicly.",["Loose or spread terminal in the sensor plug","Heat-cracked insulation causing brief shorts","Moisture or oil in the connector","Sensor with intermittent internal contact"],["Check engine light that comes and goes","Surging or hunting boost","Brief power loss over bumps"],2,3,["P2D21","P2D22","P2D23","P2D24","P025F"],""],P2D26:["Coolant Pump E Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P2D26 belongs to the general auxiliary coolant pumps, not to the motor electronics family above: pump E is the fifth electric pump of a vehicle, and its assignment (low-temperature loop, charge air cooler, turbo or component cooling) depends entirely on the manufacturer. The code says the control circuit is intact but the pump does not run or does not deliver the expected effect.",["Pump E seized or mechanically worn so it does not reach its target","Air or low coolant in the loop served by pump E","High resistance in connector, feed or ground of pump E","Control module software requiring an update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Higher temperature in the circuit cooled by pump E","Possible reduced power, depending on what pump E cools"],2,3,["P2D27","P2DF4","P2DF8","P2DF9","P2C48","P2C49"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור‏ E — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2D27:["Coolant Pump F Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P2D27 is the functional check for coolant pump F, the sixth auxiliary pump in the lettering scheme and thus only relevant on vehicles with very many electric pumps, typically plug-in hybrids, electric vehicles or heavy diesels with several separate loops. The control line answers, yet the pump stays off or falls short of what the module expects from speed, current or temperature response.",["Pump F blocked or worn so it runs too weakly","Air pocket or low coolant in the circuit of pump F","Corroded connector or high resistance in the pump F supply"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Overtemperature in the component or loop served by pump F","Power limitation if the cooled component protects itself"],2,3,["P2D26","P2C48","P2C49","P2DF9","P2601"],"מעגל בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור‏ F — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2D28:["Cold Start Propulsion Torque Performance","P2D28 concerns the torque side of a cold start strategy. To heat the catalyst, the engine control asks for a torque reserve: spark is retarded and airflow raised so the wheels still get the requested torque while extra heat goes into the exhaust. A GM patent describes this, with a heat estimate turned into a reserve request that enters the propulsion torque calculation.",["Engine control software with a monitor that sets the code without a real fault","Throttle, intake leak or airflow error, so retarded spark cannot be balanced by more air","Misfires or weak ignition while spark is heavily retarded","Implausible temperature or speed input to the torque model"],["Check engine light shortly after a cold start","Hesitant or uneven pull while the engine is still cold","Often no noticeable symptom when the cause is software"],2,1,["P032F","P050A","P050B","P050E","P050D"],""],P2D29:["A/C Compressor Motor Stalled","Hybrids and electric vehicles drive the A/C compressor with its own high-voltage motor and inverter. P2D29 reports that this motor is commanded to turn but does not rotate. No manufacturer documents P2D29 publicly.",["Mechanically seized compressor, often after oil loss or refrigerant leak","Fault in the compressor's integrated inverter or phase output","Restart against high head pressure or overcharged system","High-voltage supply to the compressor interrupted or weak"],["Air conditioning blows warm air","Warning about reduced battery cooling or charging power","Compressor phase current or overload codes stored alongside"],4,3,["P2D44","P0EC5","P0D6F","P0D7A","U016B","P26FD"],""],P2D2A:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor A/B Correlation","Some drives measure the coolant of the inverter and power electronics loop at two points. After a long rest both should read nearly the same, so P2D2A records that sensors A and B disagree by more than the allowed margin; the code does not say which one is wrong. No manufacturer documents P2D2A publicly.",["One of the two sensors has drifted","Added resistance in a connector or wire shifting one reading","Air pocket at one sensor after coolant service","Replacement sensor with a different characteristic"],["Hybrid or EV system warning","Electronics coolant pump runs more often or at full speed","Possible power reduction to protect the inverter"],2,3,["P0CEF","P2B21","P0CEE","P2B20","P2D2B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2D2B:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor A/B Correlation","Liquid-cooled traction batteries often have coolant sensors at pack inlet and outlet. When the pack has rested long enough, sensors A and B should agree; P2D2B records a gap beyond the limit without naming the faulty one. No manufacturer documents P2D2B publicly.",["One pack coolant sensor has drifted","Corroded or loose connector at a sensor","Air trapped in the battery coolant loop after service","Faulty measuring input in the battery control module"],["Hybrid or EV battery warning","Reduced charging power or range","Battery heater or chiller running unexpectedly"],2,3,["P0C43","P0CD6","P0C42","P0CD5","P0ECA","P2D2A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2D2C:["Engine Coolant Temperature Measurement System - Multiple Sensor Correlation","Engines with split or map-controlled cooling carry several coolant sensors, for example at head, block, inlet, outlet, radiator and heater core. After a cold soak all should read alike; P2D2C reports that the set as a whole disagrees and the module cannot single out one sensor. No manufacturer documents P2D2C publicly.",["One coolant sensor in the set has drifted","Uneven soak, e.g. block heater or short stop, misread as a fault","Low coolant or air leaving one sensor dry","Corroded terminal shifting one reading"],["Check engine light","Temperature gauge or fan behaviour unusual","Rough cold running or higher fuel use when warming up"],2,1,["P0116","P011A","P2183","P00B6","P011B","P012F"],""],P2D2D:["Cold Start Intake Manifold Runner Performance Bank 1","P2D2D reports that the intake manifold runner or swirl flaps of bank 1 did not reach the position the cold start strategy asked for. Many engines hold these flaps in a special setting after a cold start to stir the charge and stabilise combustion while the catalyst warms up.",["Engine control software that judges the cold start flap check too strictly","Flap shaft or runner coated with soot and oil deposits, stiff when cold","Worn actuator or loose linkage on bank 1","Position sensor signal or wiring fault"],["Check engine light, usually without a noticeable driving change","Slightly rougher idle in the first minutes after a cold start","P2D2E or P200A may be stored too"],2,1,["P2D2E","P200A","P2004","P2008","P2015"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה התנעה קרה — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2D2E:["Cold Start Intake Manifold Runner Performance Bank 2","P2D2E is the bank 2 version of the cold start runner check, so it only appears on V or boxer engines whose second cylinder row has its own flaps or actuator. The module compares the position commanded for the cold start phase with the feedback from that bank and flags a flap that stays short of target.",["Engine control software, especially when P2D2D is stored at the same time","Deposits making the bank 2 flap shaft stiff in the cold","Bank 2 actuator, linkage or connector worn or corroded"],["Check engine light, often with no other complaint","Uneven idle shortly after a cold start","P2D2D or P200B may appear alongside"],2,1,["P2D2D","P200B","P2005","P2009","P2016"],"מובילי סעפת יניקה התנעה קרה — ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P2D2F:["Cold Start Turbocharger/Supercharger A Underboost","P2D2F means boost from turbocharger or supercharger A stayed below its target during the cold start strategy; P0299 is the same complaint in normal operation. CARB counts electronic wastegate position on petrol engines and variable turbine geometry on diesels among the features that must follow their cold start command. Stellantis uses the code on the 3.0 l EcoDiesel.",["Leak in charge air pipes, intercooler or intake manifold","Intake manifold damaged by combustion after an internal EGR cooler crack (FCA EcoDiesel recalls)","Variable turbine vanes or wastegate sticking in the cold","Engine control software that needs an update"],["Weak pulling power shortly after a cold start","Check engine light, sometimes together with P0299","Hissing noise under load if the charge air path leaks"],2,3,["P2D30","P0299","P0234","P2C9B","P2563"],""],P2D30:["Cold Start Turbocharger/Supercharger A Overboost","P2D30 is the opposite of P2D2F: during the cold start strategy, boost from turbocharger or supercharger A rose above the permitted value. Outside that phase P0234 covers it. CARB lists electronic wastegate position as a cold start feature that has to follow its command, so a gate that stays shut when the strategy wants it open is the classic trigger. No manufacturer documents P2D30 publicly.",["Wastegate flap or linkage stuck closed or stiff in the cold","Wastegate regulator solenoid blocked by frozen moisture or oil deposits","Electric wastegate actuator or its position feedback faulty","Boost pressure sensor reading too high"],["Sudden power reduction shortly after starting in the cold","Check engine light, sometimes with P0234 or a wastegate code","Unusually strong surge of power while the engine is cold"],2,3,["P2D2F","P0234","P2C9B","P2B81","P0299"],""],P2D31:["Intake Manifold Tuning Valve Exceeded Learning Limit Bank 1","An intake manifold tuning valve switches the effective volume or length of the intake to use pressure waves for more cylinder filling. Electrically positioned versions learn the feedback value at their end stop, and P2D31 says that learned value lies outside its tolerance band.",["Worn end stop or deposits changing the closed position of the valve","Bent valve plate or shaft after mechanical stress","Position sensor inside the actuator drifting","Actuator replaced without completing the relearn"],["Check engine light","Less torque in some engine speed ranges","Changed intake sound under load"],2,1,["P2D32","P0660","P2076","P2077","P2078","P2070","P2071"],""],P2D32:["Intake Manifold Tuning Valve Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High Bank 1","P2D32 is an electrical self-protection code: the power stage that drives the motor of intake manifold tuning valve 1 has reported excessive current or overheating. Smart drivers watch both values internally and switch off before damage. Unlike P0661 and P0662, which describe a line shorted low or high, this code comes from the driver itself, often because the motor is overloaded.",["Valve jammed or stiff, so the motor draws excessive current","Internal short in the actuator motor","Chafed control wiring touching ground or another circuit","Faulty driver stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light","Tuning valve stays in one position, with less torque in some rev ranges","Code may return soon after clearing if the valve stays jammed"],2,1,["P2D31","P0660","P0661","P0662","P2070","P2071"],"שסתום כוונון סעפת יניקה — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2D33:["Hybrid/EV Battery Inductive Charger Control Module Processor Performance","P2D33 concerns the electronics on the vehicle side of a contactless charging system and states that the processor of the inductive charger module has failed one of its own self-tests, for example a memory checksum, a RAM test or a watchdog. Inductive charging moves energy across a gap between a ground coil and a vehicle coil;",["Internal fault of the inductive charger control module (memory, processor, watchdog)","Corrupted or outdated module software, for example after an interrupted update","Unstable 12 V supply or poor ground at the charger module causing resets"],["Wireless charging does not start or stops shortly after starting","Charging fault message in the instrument cluster or app","Code returns after clearing even though the vehicle is correctly positioned"],4,0,["P2D34","P2D36","P2D37","P2EB4","P0E5E"],"מעבד מודול בקרת מטען אינדוקטיבי סוללת מתח גבוה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D34:["Hybrid/EV Battery Inductive Charger Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2D34 points at the control line of the inductive charger, the wired path over which a vehicle controller wakes, enables or commands the charger module. The circuit is not open or shorted, but its level or duty cycle lies outside the expected window or does not follow the command. No manufacturer documents P2D34 publicly, and which signal the line carries depends on the design.",["Corroded or loose connector raising the resistance of the control line","Software levels of charger module and commanding controller that do not match","Faulty output or input stage in one of the two modules"],["Inductive charging is not offered or ends without a clear reason","Charging works intermittently depending on vibration or temperature"],3,0,["P2D33","P2D37","P2D36","P2EB4"],"מטען אינדוקטיבי סוללת מתח גבוה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2D35:["Hybrid/EV Battery Inductive Charging System High Voltage Interlock Circuit Performance","The inductive charger feeds its rectified DC power into the high-voltage system, so its connectors are usually part of a high voltage interlock loop (HVIL), a low-voltage circuit that breaks as soon as a plug or cover is opened. P2D35 means this loop delivers a signal, but not the one expected, for instance a level that does not track the test source being switched. A clear open is P2EB4.",["Interlock or high-voltage connector at the inductive charger not fully latched","Oxidised or spread interlock terminals with high contact resistance","Chafed interlock wire near the underbody pad, which is exposed to water and stone impact","Faulty interlock source or sense stage in the monitoring module"],["Inductive charging is refused","Fault appears after work on the underbody or after driving through deep water"],4,0,["P2EB4","P0D16","P0D15","P0A0B","P2D33"],"נעילת בטיחות מתח גבוה מערכת טעינה אינדוקטיבית סוללת מתח גבוה — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2D36:["Hybrid/EV Battery Inductive Charger Output Voltage Performance","P2D36 judges the DC side of the inductive charger: the voltage it hands to the traction battery is outside what the controller expects for the current state, too low to push charge current or above what the battery may accept. No manufacturer documents P2D36 publicly.",["Faulty rectifier, switching stage or output filter in the vehicle assembly","Output voltage sensor drifting against the battery voltage measurement","Vehicle parked off-centre over the ground pad, so the output cannot be held","Regulation software of the charger module"],["Inductive charging stops shortly after it begins","Charging power far below the expected value"],4,0,["P2D37","P2EB5","P2EB6","P2D33"],"מתח יציאת מטען אינדוקטיבי סוללת מתח גבוה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D37:["Hybrid/EV Battery Inductive Charger Input Circuit Range/Performance","P2D37 looks at the input of the inductive charger, the high-frequency AC that arrives from the vehicle pickup coil before rectification. The measured input is present but implausible: it fits neither the power being transferred nor the other readings, or it does not react when the transfer ramps up. Clear low and high readings have their own codes, P2EB5 and P2EB6. No manufacturer documents P2D37 publicly.",["Damaged or loose connection between pickup coil and charger module","Large coil offset, excessive ground clearance or metal object on the pad","Faulty input voltage or current sensing inside the charger module"],["Inductive charging starts with low power or not at all","Positioning aid reports the car as aligned, but charging still fails"],4,0,["P2EB5","P2EB6","P2D36","P2D34"],"כניסת מטען אינדוקטיבי סוללת מתח גבוה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2D38:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Heater Performance","P2D38 is the functional check of the traction battery heater: it was switched on, yet the pack or its coolant did not warm as expected, or the heater ran too hot. CARB asks for such a heating check wherever feasible. Toyota uses the code on the 2023 bZ4X as P2D384B, the failure type standing for over temperature;",["Heater element or its power switch delivering no or too little heat","Air, low coolant or a weak pump so that heat does not reach the pack sensors","Pack inlet or cell temperature sensor reading wrong, faking a missing rise or overheating","Control software that judges the heating too strictly (Toyota bZ4X case under investigation)"],["Malfunction indicator lamp or hybrid/EV system warning on","Slow charging or reduced power in cold weather","Battery stays cold although preconditioning was requested"],4,3,["P0E15","P0E19","P0AFD","P0C32","P0A7E"],"גוף חימום מארז סוללת מתח גבוה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D39:["Forced Hybrid/EV Battery Disconnect","P2D39 is an event record: the traction battery opened its contactors because another system demanded it, not because the battery found a fault of its own. The classic trigger is a crash. In Volkswagen patent US9586481B2 the airbag unit grades crash severity;",["Collision or crash signal from the airbag control module","Shutdown request from another controller after a safety fault (isolation, interlock)","Spurious signal on the hard-wired disable line or network message error"],["Vehicle cannot be switched to ready or drive mode","High-voltage system warning in the instrument cluster","Code persists until it is erased with a scan tool"],4,2,["P2D3A","P2C96","P2C97","P2C98","P2D3B"],""],P2D3A:["Forced Hybrid/EV System Shutdown","P2D3A records that the high-voltage system as a whole was shut down by force rather than in the normal power-down sequence. Stellantis uses it in the battery pack control module (BPCM) of its 400 V STLA Large electric cars, the 2025 Dodge Charger Daytona (bulletin 08-025-25) and the 2024–2025 Jeep Wagoneer S (08-011-25, 08-128-25).",["Battery control module reset or reprogramming leaving the shutdown latched (Stellantis BPCM)","Software fault in the battery or vehicle control module","Safety reaction to another high-voltage fault, which is stored alongside"],["Vehicle does not enter drive-ready mode","Wrench or service warning in the instrument cluster"],4,2,["P2D39","P2D3B","P0A1F","P0DE6"],""],P2D3B:["Hybrid/EV Discharge System Fault","After the contactors open, the capacitors of inverter and DC link still hold high voltage, so a discharge system, either a resistor or an active circuit in the power electronics, drains them within seconds. P2D3B is the general fault code for this system; the narrower ones are P0C75 and P0C76 for discharge time and P0EED for the discharge circuit. No manufacturer documents P2D3B publicly.",["Faulty active discharge switch or driver in the inverter","Open or degraded passive discharge resistor","Wrong high-voltage reading in the inverter or battery module","Contactor that does not open, so the bus stays fed from the battery"],["Hybrid/EV system warning lamp on","Vehicle does not become ready on the next start"],4,3,["P0C76","P0C75","P0EED","P0D5E","P2D39"],""],P2D3C:["Cold Start Hybrid/EV Drive Motor Performance","In a hybrid the electric drive motor can be part of the strategy that cuts emissions after a cold start, and P2D3C says it did not perform as that strategy required. CARB demands separate diagnostics for elements of the cold start strategy that are also monitored in normal operation, so a motor fault found during warm-up is kept apart from the general P0A90. No manufacturer documents P2D3C publicly.",["Motor output derated by temperature or another motor fault","Cold or weak traction battery limiting the power available to the motor","Calibration of the cold start strategy in the hybrid controller (software update)","Resolver or motor position sensor fault affecting torque delivery"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Engine starts earlier or runs rougher after a cold start than usual","Often no noticeable change in driving"],4,1,["P2D3D","P2D3E","P0A90","P2D28"],"מנוע הנעה היברידי/חשמלי התנעה קרה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D3D:["Cold Start Hybrid/EV Drive Motor Inverter Torque Performance","P2D3D narrows the cold start check to the inverter: during the cold start strategy, the torque it produced through the drive motor did not match the torque the hybrid controller commanded. Precise torque matters in this phase because motor and engine share the work.",["Phase current sensing error in the inverter distorting the delivered torque","Torque derating because of very low or high power electronics temperature","Torque coordination of the cold start strategy in software"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Slight jerk when the engine fires after a cold start"],4,1,["P2D3C","P2D3E","P0A78","P2D28"],"מומנט אינוורטר מנוע הנעה היברידי/חשמלי התנעה קרה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D3E:["Cold Start Hybrid/EV Battery Performance","P2D3E states that the traction battery could not support the cold start emission strategy as planned, typically because it could not deliver the power the strategy relied on. While the engine heats the catalyst at low output, the battery has to carry most of the driving load. Toyota patent US12679331B2 starts from the weakness that warm-up fails when the demand exceeds the battery output limit;",["Aged traction battery with raised internal resistance and voltage sag","Very cold pack after a long rest, limiting discharge power","State of charge too low to carry the load during warm-up","Weak module or cell imbalance pulling a single cell to its limit early"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Engine has to work harder right after a cold start, electric assist feels weak","Other battery capacity or temperature codes stored"],4,1,["P2D3C","P2D3D","P0A7F","P0AFD","P2D28"],"סוללת מתח גבוה התנעה קרה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D3F:["Hybrid/EV Battery Cooling System B Performance","P2D3F is the functional check of a second cooling path of the traction battery, alongside A (P0C32) and C (P2D40). Which path carries which letter is the manufacturer's choice; packs may be cooled by air, by a coolant radiator or by a refrigerant chiller, and some switch between them. No manufacturer documents P2D3F publicly.",["Low coolant or trapped air in the battery loop","Blocked radiator, cooler or air duct of this cooling path","Diverter valve or pump that does not route enough flow through path B","Coolant or cell temperature sensor reading wrong"],["Malfunction indicator lamp or hybrid system warning on","Reduced electric power or slower fast charging in hot weather"],3,3,["P0C32","P2D40","P0A7E","P0C4A"],"מערכת קירור סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D40:["Hybrid/EV Battery Cooling System C Performance","P2D40 is the functional check of the third cooling path of the traction battery. Ford uses it for the refrigerant chiller on the 2020–2023 Explorer, Aviator and Police Interceptor Utility hybrids (FHEV and PHEV); the code is stored in the secondary OBD module SOBDMC and lights the MIL.",["Low refrigerant charge in the A/C circuit feeding the battery chiller","Air in the coolant or pinched, kinked battery coolant hoses","Partly blocked battery chiller (high voltage battery cooler)","Coolant diverter valve or battery coolant pump not delivering flow through the chiller"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Battery temperature rises during hard driving or towing, power may be reduced","Weak cabin air conditioning if the refrigerant charge is low"],3,3,["P2D3F","P0C32","P0A7E","P0C4A"],"מערכת קירור סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D41:["A/C Compressor Motor Voltage B Performance","P2D41 is a plausibility check on the second voltage value that an electric A/C compressor reports for its motor drive: the reading is electrically valid but disagrees with a reference, for example the traction battery voltage or the first compressor voltage value. Which voltage the letter B stands for is up to the manufacturer; no manufacturer documents P2D41 on an official public source.",["Faulty voltage measurement inside the compressor control module","Contact resistance at the high-voltage connector of the compressor","Implausible reference value from the battery or hybrid control module"],["Hybrid or EV warning message, warning lamp depending on the manufacturer","A/C cooling reduced or switched off"],4,1,["P2D42","P2D43","P2D44","P0D69","P0EA9"],"מתח מנוע מדחס מזגן‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D42:["A/C Compressor Motor Voltage B Low","P2D42 is stored when voltage B at the electric A/C compressor motor stays below the lower limit of its working range, so the inverter cannot drive the motor properly and usually switches it off. Unlike a sensor circuit code, it refers to the voltage that is actually present. No manufacturer documents P2D42 on an official public source.",["Blown A/C high-voltage fuse, often after an internal compressor short","Loose or corroded high-voltage connector at the compressor","Internal fault in the compressor inverter or measurement"],["A/C blows warm air","Hybrid system warning, possibly reduced battery cooling or charging power"],4,1,["P2D41","P2D43","P0D6D","P0EAB"],"מתח מנוע מדחס מזגן‏ B — ערך נמוך"],P2D43:["A/C Compressor Motor Voltage B High","With P2D43 the controller reports that compressor motor voltage B has climbed above the level its power stage can withstand; the compressor controller normally stops the motor to protect its transistors. No manufacturer documents P2D43 on an official public source.",["Faulty voltage measurement in the compressor control module","Voltage spikes on the high-voltage bus during charging or regeneration","Faulty DC/DC converter or on-board charger"],["A/C switches off, sometimes only for a while","Hybrid or EV system warning"],4,1,["P2D41","P2D42","P0D6E","P0EAA"],"מתח מנוע מדחס מזגן‏ B — ערך גבוה"],P2D44:["A/C Compressor Motor Performance","P2D44 is the overall function check of the electric A/C compressor motor: it is commanded to run but does not deliver what is expected, typically a speed feedback that does not follow the request, while no single voltage or current fault is flagged. No manufacturer documents P2D44 on an official public source.",["Internal mechanical wear or lack of oil in the compressor","Wrong refrigerant charge or excessive high-side pressure","Fault in the compressor inverter or its speed evaluation"],["A/C cools poorly or not at all","Unusual noise from the compressor","Battery cooling restricted on plug-in hybrids and EVs"],4,1,["P2D29","P2D41","P0EC5","P0D6F"],"מנוע מדחס מזגן — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D45:["Reductant Temperature Too Low","P2D45 means the diesel exhaust fluid in the tank does not warm up as it should while the tank heater is working, so frozen or very cold fluid cannot be dosed. GM uses the code in its diesel OBD tables from 2021 to 2025 in two variants.",["Tank heater element degraded or partly failed","Low supply voltage to the heater, e.g. weak battery or poor ground","Tank temperature sensor reading too low"],["MIL after two trips in cold weather","DEF or SCR warning message, dosing delayed","Possible countdown to speed limitation if the fault persists"],2,3,["P24FF","P20B9","P205A","P2042"],"טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue) — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2D46:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack B Over Temperature","P2D46 extends the pack over-temperature check to a battery that is split into several separately watched sections: section B has run hotter than its protection limit, while section A, on undivided batteries the whole pack, uses P0A7E. No manufacturer documents P2D46 publicly.",["Restricted coolant or air flow through section B (blocked channel, kinked hose, clogged intake)","Sustained high load or repeated fast charging in hot weather","Temperature sensor in section B reading too high without a circuit fault","Aged modules in section B with raised internal resistance"],["Hybrid or EV system warning and check engine light","Reduced electric drive power and regeneration","Charging slowed or interrupted"],4,3,["P0A7E","P2D47","P0EDD","P0A9C","P0C32"],"מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — חום יתר"],P2D47:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack C Over Temperature","With P2D47 the battery controller reports that the third section of a divided traction battery, C, has exceeded its temperature limit. Because neighbouring sections share the same coolant or air supply, a fault confined to one letter usually points to a local cause: a blocked cooling channel, a cold plate that lost contact with its modules, or an air duct obstructed in that area.",["Blocked cooling channel or air duct serving section C","Poor thermal contact between section C modules and the cooling plate (missing or displaced thermal paste/pad)","Temperature sensor in section C reading high"],["Check engine or hybrid system warning light","Less electric power, especially after longer drives","Battery cooling fan or pump running at high speed"],4,3,["P2D46","P2D48","P0A7E","P0EDE","P0C32"],"מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C — חום יתר"],P2D48:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack D Over Temperature","P2D48 is the over-temperature code for the fourth section, D, of a sectioned high-voltage battery. Before treating it as real heat, a technician should ask whether the temperature value itself can be trusted. Porsche's 2025 911 GTS T-Hybrid shows why: P0A7E00 was stored together with a thermal run-through code and a red fire warning that blocked starting, yet no hot surface or smell was found;",["Implausible temperature data from the battery electronics (internal communication or software fault)","Insufficient cooling of section D (coolant flow, pump, chiller, air path)","Genuine cell overheating in section D due to an internal cell defect"],["Hybrid system or battery warning, possibly a fire hazard message","Vehicle may refuse to start or enter drive-ready mode","Reduced electric power and charging"],4,3,["P2D47","P2D49","P0A7E","P0EDF","P0A9C"],"מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ D — חום יתר"],P2D49:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack E Over Temperature","P2D49 says that section E, the fifth separately monitored part of a traction battery, is hotter than permitted. One trap with every pack over-temperature code is heat produced after the car has been switched off.",["Battery controller logic or threshold too strict for normal post-shutdown warming (software update)","Reduced cooling of section E (coolant flow, fan, duct)","Parking in strong sun or heat after hard use"],["Hybrid warning light, sometimes only after the car has stood","Motor assist and regeneration unavailable","Auto start-stop no longer works"],4,3,["P2D48","P2D4A","P0A7E","P0EE0"],"מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ E — חום יתר"],P2D4A:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack F Over Temperature","P2D4A covers section F, the sixth part of a battery whose controller watches temperature section by section. It pairs naturally with P0EE1, the deterioration code of the same section: aged cells with higher internal resistance turn more current into heat, and repeated overheating speeds up ageing, so both entries on one letter point at the modules themselves rather than at cooling.",["Aged modules in section F producing extra heat (often with P0EE1)","Insufficient cooling flow to section F","Sensor in section F reading too high"],["Warning light; timing depends on manufacturer (first or second trip)","Shorter electric range and weaker electric drive","Battery fan or coolant pump louder than usual"],4,3,["P2D49","P2D4B","P0EE1","P0A7E","P0BBD"],"מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ F — חום יתר"],P2D4B:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack G Over Temperature","P2D4B reports overheating in section G, the seventh separately supervised part of the traction battery. Such a letter only makes sense for big packs with many groups. The Audi Q5 PHEV is a documented example of such a split: its hybrid battery unit 008C reports eight battery groups through the deterioration codes P0A7F00 to P2CCD00, group 7 being P2CCC00, and Audi bulletins 2076982/1 and 2079556/1 of 2025 deal with…",["Insufficient cooling of section G (coolant distribution, trapped air, pump)","Worn module in section G (compare with P2CCC)","Temperature sensor of section G reading too high"],["Engine or hybrid warning lamp","Displayed electric range shorter than usual","Reduced charging power"],4,3,["P2D4A","P2D4C","P2CCC","P0A7E","P0A7F"],"מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ G — חום יתר"],P2D4C:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack H Over Temperature","P2D4C stands for overheating of section H, the eighth monitored portion of a traction battery. Eight sections is also the largest split found in public service information, the Audi Q5 PHEV with groups 1 to 8, so H marks the edge of documented practice; Audi publishes only the ageing code P2CCD00 for its group 8, and no manufacturer documents P2D4C.",["Battery cooling loop fault (low coolant, pump, chiller, valve) affecting section H","Local flow restriction or poor cold-plate contact at section H","Worn module in section H (see P2CCD)"],["Warning lamp and possibly further battery cooling codes","Limited acceleration in electric mode","Charging stops or slows down"],4,3,["P2D4B","P2D4D","P2CCD","P0C32","P2D3F"],"מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ H — חום יתר"],P2D4D:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack I Over Temperature","P2D4D is meant for section I, the ninth subdivision of a battery that is supervised section by section; no published battery has that many monitored groups, and no manufacturer documents the code. Where it is used, the reaction depends on how much margin the controller keeps.",["Heavy charging or discharging current (fast charging, towing, climbs) beyond cooling capacity","Reduced cooling at section I","Temperature sensor of section I reading high"],["Charging power drops sharply during fast charging","Reduced drive power with warning message","Check engine or EV system light"],4,3,["P2D4C","P2D4E","P2CCE","P0A7E"],"מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ I — חום יתר"],P2D4E:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack J Over Temperature","P2D4E marks overheating of section J, the tenth separately judged part of a sectioned pack; its ageing counterpart is P2CCF. No manufacturer documents P2D4E publicly. The useful first step is to compare the temperatures of section J with those of its neighbours in live data. If only one sensor stands out while the others agree, a drifting sensor is more likely than real heat;",["One temperature sensor in section J drifting high while neighbours read normal","Restricted cooling of section J","Worn modules in section J (check P2CCF)"],["Warning light with reduced electric power","Section J temperature clearly above its neighbours in live data","Charging limited"],4,3,["P2D4D","P2D4F","P2CCF","P0A9C","P0A7E"],"מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ J — חום יתר"],P2D4F:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack K Over Temperature","P2D4F reports that section K, the eleventh supervised section of a high-voltage battery, has gone over its temperature limit; overheating and ageing of the same section are kept apart, the latter being P2CD0. No manufacturer documents P2D4F publicly.",["Low coolant level or air trapped in the battery loop, often after service","Weak or intermittently failing battery coolant pump","Worn modules in section K (compare with P2CD0)"],["Warning light, often under load or in summer","Reduced electric drive and charging power","Coolant pump or fan audible for a long time after driving"],4,3,["P2D4E","P2D50","P2CD0","P0C47","P0A7E"],"מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ K — חום יתר"],P2D50:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack L Over Temperature","P2D50 is the last code in the lettered over-temperature series: after P0A7E for section A, or the whole pack if it is undivided, and sections B to K (P2D46 to P2D4F), L is the twelfth section. The deterioration series runs further to N (P2CD3), but sections M and N have no matching heat code in the current lists. No manufacturer documents P2D50 publicly.",["Insufficient cooling of section L","Worn or imbalanced modules in section L (see P2CD1, P0BBD)","Temperature sensor of section L reading high"],["Hybrid or EV warning lamp","Reduced electric power and regeneration","Slower charging"],4,3,["P2D4F","P2CD1","P0A7E","P0BBD","P2D46"],"מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ L — חום יתר"],P2D51:["Air Assisted Injector Control Circuit","P2D51 is the general electrical code for the control circuit of an air-assist injection system, the circuit counterpart to P0065 to P0067. Assist air flowing around the injector tip breaks the fuel spray into finer droplets.",["Open or shorted coil in the air-assist solenoid valve","Damaged wiring or corroded connector at the valve","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["MIL on","Unsteady idle or harder cold starts","Slightly higher hydrocarbon emissions"],2,1,["P0065","P0066","P0067"],""],P2D52:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit","P2D52 is the general circuit code for a third coolant temperature sensor, C, in the liquid loop of a hybrid or EV battery. Sensors A and B are commonly the pack inlet and outlet; where C sits is not published and depends on the design. The code says only that the signal is unusable, without saying whether it lies under or over its limits. No manufacturer documents P2D52 publicly.",["Loose connector, damaged wire or corroded pin in the sensor C circuit","Failed coolant temperature sensor C","Battery controller software flagging the circuit wrongly (update)"],["Check engine or hybrid system light","Battery heating or cooling not working as expected","Charging or electric power may be limited"],3,3,["P2D53","P2D54","P2D55","P0C42","P0CD5"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2D53:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P2D53 means coolant temperature sensor C of the battery loop delivers an electrically valid value that does not fit its surroundings. Unlike P2D2B, which only sees that sensors A and B disagree, this code blames sensor C itself. No manufacturer documents P2D53 publicly.",["Sensor C drifting or reacting slowly","Plausibility limits in the controller software too tight (update)","Contact resistance in the connector or air pocket at the sensor"],["Warning light, often after the car has stood for hours","No obvious driveability change at first","Battery conditioning less effective"],3,1,["P2D52","P2D56","P2D2B","P0C43","P0CD6"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2D54:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit Low","P2D54 flags the signal voltage of battery coolant temperature sensor C as too low. These sensors are NTC thermistors pulled up to a reference, so a falling voltage reads as rising temperature; a short to ground or an internally shorted sensor therefore looks like boiling coolant, while the loop itself may be cold. No manufacturer documents P2D54 publicly.",["Signal wire of sensor C shorted to ground (chafed harness)","Sensor C shorted internally","Moisture or coolant in the connector bridging the pins"],["Live data shows an implausibly hot coolant reading for sensor C","Battery cooling runs constantly","Warning light and possibly reduced power"],3,3,["P2D52","P2D55","P0C44","P0CD7","P2E76"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2D55:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit High","P2D55 is the counterpart to P2D54: the signal of battery coolant temperature sensor C sits at or near the reference voltage. On an NTC circuit with pull-up that is what an open circuit produces, so the controller sees an impossibly cold coolant value. Typical findings are a connector not plugged back after battery work, a broken wire, a spread terminal, or a short to a supply line;",["Open circuit: connector unplugged, broken wire or spread terminal","Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage","Open sensor element"],["Live data shows about -40 °C for sensor C","Battery heating or cooling uses substitute values","Warning light; reduced power in cold weather possible"],3,3,["P2D52","P2D54","P0C45","P0CD8","P2E77"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2D56:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2D56 points to a coolant temperature signal from sensor C that jumps around faster than liquid in the battery loop can really change temperature, while mostly staying inside the electrical limits. No manufacturer documents P2D56 publicly.",["Loose or corroded terminal in the sensor C connector","Harness rubbing or moving with the battery, causing brief interruptions","Detection logic reacting to normal conditions (software update)"],["Warning light that comes and goes","Sensor C value jumps in live data, especially when wiggling the harness","Usually no noticeable driveability change"],3,1,["P2D52","P2D53","P0C46","P0CD9","P2E78"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2D57:["Generator B Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2D57 belongs to a second alternator, called generator B, as fitted to some heavy trucks; GM, for instance, offered a secondary generator (option KHB) on 2019 Silverado medium-duty trucks with the 6.6 L diesel. The code concerns the control channel of that machine: the engine computer's command and the regulator's response do not fit together, or the signal leaves its plausible band.",["Damaged control line (LIN or command wire) or corroded connector","Faulty voltage regulator of the second alternator","Replacement alternator with an incompatible regulator"],["Charge warning lamp or message","Second alternator charges at a fixed default voltage or not at all"],2,0,["P2D58","P2D59","P065B","P2CC1","P0620"],"גנרטור‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2D58:["Generator B Mechanical Performance","P2D58 reports that generator B, the second alternator of a dual charging system, does not deliver as commanded for mechanical reasons, most often because its drive slips. Such machines often sit on their own belt and idler.",["Worn, glazed or oil-soaked drive belt slipping","Weak tensioner or loose idler pulley mounting","Stiff alternator bearing or faulty overrunning pulley"],["Charge warning lamp, low charging voltage","Belt squeal or noise from the second alternator"],1,0,["P2D57","P2D59","P065C","P065B"],"מכני גנרטור‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D59:["Generator B Over Temperature","P2D59 indicates that generator B has become too hot. Which machine B means is up to the manufacturer: a second alternator in a dual charging system or a second motor-generator in a hybrid. No manufacturer documents P2D59 publicly. For generator A, Mitsubishi describes the hybrid case under P0A3B on the 2023 Outlander PHEV: a W-phase coil temperature of 199 °C or more for one second sets the code.",["Obstructed cooling air path or reduced oil/coolant flow to the generator","Sustained high electrical load at low engine speed","Temperature sensor or regulator measuring wrongly"],["Reduced charging output or charge warning","On hybrids, limited electric or series-mode power"],3,2,["P2D57","P2D58","P0A3B","P0A3E"],"גנרטור‏ B — חום יתר"],P2D5A:["Reductant Level Sensor A/B Correlation","P2D5A compares two level sensors of the diesel exhaust fluid system: each delivers a valid signal, yet together they describe a fill level that cannot be true. Tanks with several level contacts, or vehicles with a main and an auxiliary tank, can cross-check their sensors this way. No manufacturer documents P2D5A on an official public source.",["One level sensor failed or contaminated","Urea crystals or deposits on the sensing elements","Corrosion or poor contact at the tank sensor connector"],["Implausible or jumping DEF level display","MIL and DEF warning message","Possible inducement countdown despite sufficient fluid"],2,3,["P203B","P21A9","P21C5","P21C6","P203A","P21A8"],"חיישן מפלס אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2D5B:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor C Circuit","P2D5B is the umbrella electrical fault for charging-system contactor C on the plus pole, a third plus-side switch next to contactors A (P0D07) and B (P2BC4). Which charging path C serves is left to each maker, and none states it in public: the bulletins that cite contactor B codes (Mercedes, Mazda, Audi) never mention a C contactor, nor do the published GM tables, and no document lists P2D5B itself.",["Coil of contactor C open or shorted internally","Damaged wiring or loose plug at the contactor or its module","Output stage or software of the controlling module"],["One charging mode refused or aborted","Charging or high-voltage warning in the cluster","Driving otherwise normal"],4,0,["P2D5C","P2D5D","P2D5E","P2D62","P2BC4","P0D07"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2D5C:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor C Stuck Closed","P2D5C is set when positive charging contactor C still conducts after the module commanded it to open; fused contacts are the usual reason. No manufacturer documents P2D5C publicly. Patents describe how a weld shows up: Ford opens its charge contactors one at a time after a session and treats one as welded if the voltage measured at the charger stays within a set margin of the battery voltage;",["Main contacts of contactor C welded, e.g. after switching under load","Coil output stage does not switch off","Faulty voltage measurement on the charger side simulating a weld"],["Charging blocked after the previous session","High-voltage warning, possibly no ready mode","Code appears at the end of a charging session or at start-up"],4,2,["P2D5B","P2D5D","P2D63","P2BC5","P0D08"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2D5D:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor C Stuck Open","P2D5D means positive charging contactor C stays open although it was commanded closed, so the plus pole of that charging path never connects and the session fails right at the start. No manufacturer documents P2D5D publicly; Mazda, which lists the non-closing case for contactor B (P2BC6), says nothing about a C contactor.",["Contactor C does not pull in (burnt contacts, jammed armature)","Insufficient coil supply due to wiring or connector resistance","Control software misjudges the precharge voltage"],["Charging in the affected mode does not start","Charging station reports an aborted session","Driving not affected"],4,0,["P2D5B","P2D5C","P2D5E","P2D64","P2BC6","P0D09"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2D5E:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor C Control Circuit/Open","P2D5E concerns the wire that energises the coil of plus-side contactor C, not its power contacts: the module finds that the state of its output driver and that of the line disagree, typically because a wire or the coil winding is broken. No manufacturer documents P2D5E publicly.",["Broken coil feed wire or pushed-back terminal","Coil winding of contactor C open","Output stage in the module defective"],["Charging in the affected mode not possible","Fault present continuously, not only while charging","Charging warning in the cluster"],4,0,["P2D5B","P2D5F","P2D60","P2D61","P2D65","P2BC7","P0D0A"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2D5F:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor C Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2D5F reports that the coil circuit of plus-side charging contactor C is intact yet behaves in a way that does not match the command: the coil current, the voltage on the line or the pull-in delay drift out of their expected band without amounting to a clear open, low or high condition. No manufacturer documents P2D5F publicly, and the published GM tables contain no range test for the coil of any charge contactor.",["Corroded or loose pins raising resistance in the coil circuit","Coil resistance of contactor C out of tolerance","Ageing output stage in the module"],["Charging interrupts sporadically","Contactor clicks late or audibly chatters","Code returns after clearing"],4,0,["P2D5E","P2D60","P2D61","P2D66","P2BC8","P0D0B"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2D60:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor C Control Circuit Low","P2D60 is logged when the coil feed of positive charging contactor C reads lower than commanded – usually the wire has found ground or the driver output is dragged low. Where the driver switches the supply side, the coil then gets too little current and the contactor stays open, or the driver shuts itself off for protection. No manufacturer documents P2D60 publicly.",["Coil feed wire shorted to ground","Moisture or corrosion in the contactor plug","Shorted turns in the coil of contactor C"],["Affected charging mode refused","Fault may appear only in wet weather","Charging warning shown"],4,0,["P2D5E","P2D5F","P2D61","P2D67","P2BC9","P0D0C"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2D61:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor C Control Circuit High","P2D61 points to excess voltage on the wire feeding the coil of plus-side contactor C, caused by touching a 12 V feed or by an output stage that no longer switches off. The real danger is a coil energised without command, closing the plus pole of the charging path while the module assumes it is open; charging is therefore normally inhibited. No manufacturer documents P2D61 publicly.",["Coil feed wire shorted to a 12 V supply","Output stage does not switch off","Wires swapped at a connector after repair work"],["Charging blocked as a precaution","Contactor may click without a charging request","High-voltage or charging warning"],4,0,["P2D5E","P2D5F","P2D60","P2D68","P2BCA","P0D0D"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2D62:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor C Circuit","P2D62 is the collective electrical code covering minus contactor C, which connects the return conductor of the third charging path to the traction battery. Neither the code nor the meaning of C is documented by any manufacturer.",["Coil of minus contactor C open or shorted","Wiring or plug fault on the minus contactor","Module output stage or software"],["One charging mode unavailable","Charging warning in the cluster","Driving unaffected"],4,0,["P2D63","P2D64","P2D65","P2D5B","P2BCB","P0D0E"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2D63:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor C Stuck Closed","P2D63 says negative charging contactor C has not opened on command; the return-side contacts are almost certainly fused. No manufacturer documents P2D63 publicly, and the Mercedes and Mazda bulletins that report a welded minus contactor B (P2BCC) do not mention C.",["Fused main contacts of minus contactor C","Charger still supplying voltage during the check (false detection)","Coil output stage stuck on"],["Charging blocked after a session","High-voltage warning at start-up","Vehicle may not become ready if the plus side is welded too"],4,2,["P2D62","P2D64","P2D5C","P2BCC","P0D0F"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2D64:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor C Stuck Open","P2D64 appears when minus charging contactor C does not close; the third charging path then lacks its return conductor and no current flows even with the plus contactor in. No manufacturer documents P2D64 publicly.",["Minus contactor C does not pull in or contacts burnt","Weak coil supply from wiring or connector faults","Software misreads the precharge result"],["Charging in the affected mode never starts","Charging station aborts immediately","Driving unaffected"],4,0,["P2D62","P2D63","P2D65","P2D5D","P2BCD","P0D10"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2D65:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor C Control Circuit/Open","P2D65 concerns the line that drives the coil of minus-side charging contactor C: the module notices that what it commands and what the line actually shows do not match, which usually means a broken wire, a loose terminal or an open coil. No manufacturer documents P2D65 publicly.",["Broken coil-drive wire or terminal pushed out of the connector","Open winding in the coil of minus contactor C","Faulty output stage in the controlling module"],["The charging mode routed through contactor C does not start","Code is stored even without a charging request","Charging fault message in the cluster"],4,0,["P2D62","P2D66","P2D67","P2D68","P2D5E","P2D73","P2BCE","P0D11"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2D66:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor C Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2D66 flags a coil circuit of minus charging contactor C that is connected but responds outside its expected band while showing neither a break nor a short. P2D66 is not described by any manufacturer, and GM's public tables list no range test for charge contactor coils.",["Corroded or loose terminals raising circuit resistance","Coil resistance drifted through ageing or overheating","Module software with an unsuitable reference or calibration"],["Charging via contactor C drops out now and then","Fault occurs mainly in very cold or very hot conditions","Code returns after clearing"],4,0,["P2D62","P2D65","P2D67","P2D68","P2D5F","P2D74","P2BCF","P0D12"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2D67:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor C Control Circuit Low","P2D67 is stored when the drive line of minus charging contactor C sits lower than the module expects, typically because the wire touches ground or the connector has taken in water. No manufacturer documents P2D67 publicly.",["Drive wire chafed against the battery housing or body","Moisture or corrosion in the contactor connector","Shorted turns in the coil of minus contactor C"],["Charging mode via contactor C refused","Fault more frequent after rain or washing","Charging warning in the cluster"],4,0,["P2D65","P2D66","P2D68","P2D60","P2D75","P2BD0","P0D13"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2D68:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor C Control Circuit High","P2D68 means the wire energising minus charging contactor C carries more voltage than commanded, for instance where it rubs on a 12 V line or the output stage keeps conducting. No manufacturer documents P2D68 publicly.",["Drive wire chafed against a 12 V supply line","Output stage in the module no longer switches off","Wires swapped or pinched after repair work"],["Charging blocked as a precaution","Contactor may click without a charging request","High-voltage or charging warning"],4,0,["P2D65","P2D66","P2D67","P2D61","P2D76","P2BD1","P0D14"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2D69:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor D Circuit","P2D69 collects electrical faults of positive charging contactor D, a fourth plus-side switch after A (P0D07), B (P2BC4) and C (P2D5B). What D connects is not public: none of the makers documents P2D69, and the NHTSA bulletin index since 2015 names neither P2D69 nor any contactor D.",["Defective coil or contacts of plus contactor D","Wiring or connector fault between module and contactor D","Fault in the module that switches contactor D"],["One charging mode unavailable","Fault may only show when that charging mode is used","Driving unaffected"],4,0,["P2D6A","P2D6B","P2D6C","P2D70","P2D5B","P2BC4","P0D07"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2D6A:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor D Stuck Closed","P2D6A reports that positive charging contactor D still conducts after being told to open, nearly always because its contacts have welded. No manufacturer documents P2D6A publicly. A Ford patent explains where welds come from and how they are found: of the two charge contactors, the one closing last completes the circuit and takes the arcing, so Ford alternates the closing order between sessions.",["Contacts of plus contactor D welded by arcing","Coil kept energised by a faulty output stage","Faulty charger-side voltage measurement simulating a weld"],["Charging locked after the previous session","Vehicle may not become ready if the other pole is welded too","Fault appears at the end of a charging session"],4,2,["P2D69","P2D6B","P2D71","P2D5C","P2BC5","P0D08"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2D6B:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor D Stuck Open","P2D6B is logged when positive charging contactor D fails to close on command, leaving the plus pole of its charging path disconnected. No manufacturer documents P2D6B publicly. GM's Volt test for plus contactor A (P0D09) shows the usual principle: once charging and precharge are commanded on, the charger-side voltage has to climb, and the test fails when 8 of 9 samples, taken every 12.5 ms, stay below 10 V (Type A).",["Burnt contacts or jammed armature in plus contactor D","Insufficient coil supply voltage or poor ground","Module software misjudging the voltage rise"],["Charging in the affected mode never starts","Charging station reports an immediate abort","Driving unaffected"],4,0,["P2D69","P2D6A","P2D6C","P2D72","P2D5D","P2BC6","P0D09"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2D6C:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor D Control Circuit/Open","P2D6C covers the coil supply of positive charging contactor D rather than its main contacts. The module finds the line in a state that contradicts the command to its driver, mostly due to an interrupted wire or coil. No manufacturer documents P2D6C publicly. GM's 2016 check of plus contactor A (P0D0A) looks at both driver states: with the driver off, more than 4 V on the line means open;",["Interrupted coil supply wire or backed-out terminal","Open coil in plus contactor D","Output stage of the module defective"],["Affected charging mode not possible","Fault present permanently, not only while charging","Charging warning displayed"],4,0,["P2D69","P2D6D","P2D6E","P2D6F","P2D5E","P2D73","P2BC7","P0D0A"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2D6D:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor D Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2D6D points to a coil circuit of positive charging contactor D that works but behaves implausibly: current or voltage on the line drifts out of its normal window although no open or short is present. No manufacturer documents P2D6D publicly, and GM's published tables contain no such range test for charge contactors.",["Raised contact resistance in the coil circuit","Sluggish or partly jammed armature in contactor D","Ageing output stage delivering too little current"],["Charging via contactor D interrupted sporadically","Contactor pulls in late or chatters","Code returns after clearing"],4,0,["P2D6C","P2D6E","P2D6F","P2D5F","P2D74","P2BC8","P0D0B"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2D6E:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor D Control Circuit Low","P2D6E is set when the voltage on the coil supply of plus contactor D reads too low, usually a wire touching ground. No manufacturer documents P2D6E publicly. In a layout where the module switches the supply side of the coil, which a GM patent names as one option besides switching the ground side, a ground short means the driver works into a short circuit: the coil gets no usable current, contactor D stays open and…",["Coil feed wire shorted to ground","Water or corrosion in the connector of contactor D","Shorted coil in plus contactor D"],["Charging mode via contactor D refused","Fault set as soon as the contactor is commanded","Charging warning shown"],4,0,["P2D6C","P2D6D","P2D6F","P2D60","P2D75","P2BC9","P0D0C"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2D6F:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor D Control Circuit High","P2D6F says the supply wire to the coil of plus contactor D sits above its commanded level. No manufacturer documents P2D6F publicly. GM's 2016 drive test for plus contactor A (P0D0A) treats an idle output within 0.4 V of the supply voltage as shorted to power.",["Coil feed shorted to a 12 V supply","Output stage stuck switched on","Wires swapped after a repair"],["Charging locked","Contactor clicks unexpectedly with ignition on","High-voltage warning possible"],4,0,["P2D6C","P2D6D","P2D6E","P2D61","P2D76","P2BCA","P0D0D"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2D70:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor D Circuit","P2D70 groups electrical faults of negative charging contactor D, the return-side partner of plus contactor D (P2D69). What D switches and when P2D70 is set remain undocumented. Separate contactors in both poles of a charging path exist so that the inlet can be fully cut off; for diagnosis that means each pole must be tested alone.",["Defective coil or contacts of minus contactor D","Wiring or connector fault on the contactor D circuit","Fault in the switching module"],["One charging mode unavailable","Charging connector may stay locked after a session","Driving unaffected"],4,0,["P2D71","P2D72","P2D73","P2D69","P2D62","P2BCB","P0D0E"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2D71:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor D Stuck Closed","P2D71 indicates that negative charging contactor D has stayed closed after an open command, as happens when the contacts fuse. No manufacturer documents P2D71 publicly. A Toyota patent addresses a pitfall of this check: after DC charging the car asks the station to stop, but some stations keep feeding, and the leftover inlet voltage would wrongly suggest welded relays.",["Fused contacts in minus contactor D","Station kept supplying voltage during the check","Coil held on by a faulty output stage"],["Charging locked after a DC session","Vehicle may refuse to become ready if the plus side is welded as well","High-voltage warning at start-up"],4,2,["P2D70","P2D72","P2D6A","P2D63","P2BCC","P0D0F"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2D72:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor D Stuck Open","P2D72 appears when negative charging contactor D will not close, leaving its path without a return lead; even with plus contactor D pulled in, nothing can be charged. No manufacturer documents P2D72 publicly. Detection can work like GM's Volt test P0D09 for plus contactor A, which expects the charger-side voltage to rise once the contactors are commanded on and fails below 10 V.",["Minus contactor D does not close mechanically","Weak coil supply or poor ground at contactor D","Module software misattributing a station fault"],["Charging in the affected mode never begins","Station aborts right after plugging in","Driving unaffected"],4,0,["P2D70","P2D71","P2D73","P2D6B","P2D64","P2BCD","P0D10"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2D73:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor D Control Circuit/Open","P2D73 concerns the coil drive of negative charging contactor D: commanded and measured state of the line differ, pointing to an open wire, terminal or winding. No manufacturer documents P2D73 publicly. GM's test for the minus charge contactor (P0D11) is the direct analogue.",["Open coil drive wire or loose terminal","Broken winding in minus contactor D","Defective driver or current sensing in the module"],["Charging mode via contactor D not available","Code present at every key-on","Charging fault message"],4,0,["P2D70","P2D74","P2D75","P2D76","P2D6C","P2D65","P2BCE","P0D11"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2D74:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor D Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2D74 says the coil circuit of minus charging contactor D answers commands in an unexpected way, although it is neither open nor shorted. No manufacturer documents P2D74 publicly, and no published GM table has a range test for charge contactor coils. One measure a GM patent proposes is timing: how quickly the coil current climbs to a set level after the driver switches on.",["Aged connector adding resistance to the coil circuit","Coil of minus contactor D with changed resistance or inductance","Output stage no longer delivering full current"],["Charging via contactor D stops intermittently","Delayed contactor click when charging starts","Code reappears after clearing"],4,0,["P2D73","P2D75","P2D76","P2D6D","P2D66","P2BCF","P0D12"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2D75:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor D Control Circuit Low","P2D75 is stored when the drive line of negative charging contactor D reads low. No manufacturer documents P2D75 publicly. How serious this is depends on wiring: a GM patent shows the coil switch either on the supply side or on the ground side.",["Drive wire of contactor D shorted to ground","Moisture in the contactor D connector","Output stage shorted inside the module"],["Charging locked","Contactor may click without a command","Fault worse in damp weather"],4,0,["P2D73","P2D74","P2D76","P2D6E","P2D67","P2BD0","P0D13"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2D76:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor D Control Circuit High","P2D76 means the control wire of minus contactor D shows more voltage than the module asked for. No manufacturer documents P2D76 publicly. GM's 2016 test for the minus charge contactor (P0D11) flags a power short when the idle output gets within 0.4 V of the supply.",["Drive wire of contactor D touching a 12 V feed","Output stage that no longer switches off","Crossed wires after work on the battery"],["Charging mode via contactor D blocked","Fault appears as soon as ignition is on","Charging or high-voltage warning"],4,0,["P2D73","P2D74","P2D75","P2D6F","P2D68","P2BD1","P0D14"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2D77:["Battery Charger Control Module B Performance","P2D77 says the control electronics of charger B, a second on-board charger or charger stage, do not work as intended; faults of its processor are filed separately under P2D78. No manufacturer documents P2D77 publicly.",["Internal power or control stage of charger B failed (unit replacement)","Internal low-voltage supply rail of charger B out of tolerance","Weak 12 V supply or poor ground at the charger","Charger software fault, cured by an update where one exists"],["AC charging does not start or stops after a short time","Charging fault message or warning in the instrument cluster","Charging possible only at reduced power, if the other charger path still works"],4,0,["P2D78","P0D67","P0E89","P2D83"],"מודול בקרת מטען סוללה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D78:["Battery Charger Control Module B Processor Performance","P2D78 points at the processor inside the control module of charger B: its self-tests of program or working memory have failed, so the module no longer trusts its own computations. All other functional faults of that module belong to P2D77. No manufacturer documents P2D78 publicly.",["Memory or processor hardware in the charger B control unit defective","Corrupted charger software, e.g. after an interrupted update","12 V supply dip while the charger boots"],["Plug-in charging is refused right after connecting","Charging system warning in the cluster"],4,0,["P2D77","P0E5E","P0D67"],"מעבד מודול בקרת מטען סוללה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D79:["Charging Stop Switch Circuit","P2D79 covers the circuit of a charging stop switch as a whole, a button the driver presses to end external charging before the battery is full. The code is set when the switch line carries no valid signal at all; high, low, performance and intermittent faults of the same line have their own codes P2D7A to P2D7D. No manufacturer documents P2D79 publicly.",["Loose, corroded or unplugged connector at the stop switch","Broken wire between stop switch and charging control unit","Stop switch itself defective"],["Charging cannot be ended with the stop button","Charging may be refused as a precaution"],2,0,["P2D7A","P2D7B","P2D7C","P2D7D","P2D7E"],"מתג עצירת טעינה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2D7A:["Charging Stop Switch Circuit High","P2D7A means the voltage on the charging stop switch line stays above the band the control unit accepts. This refers to the signal, not to the button position: typical causes are a broken wire or switch contact on a line held up by a pull-up resistor, or a short to a supply voltage. No manufacturer documents P2D7A publicly. What the driver notices depends on the circuit layout.",["Open circuit in the stop switch line or connector (pull-up design)","Stop switch signal wire chafed through and touching a supply voltage","Burnt or broken contact inside the stop switch"],["Charging does not start although the plug is connected","Pressing the stop button has no effect during charging"],2,0,["P2D7B","P2D79","P2D7C","P2D7F"],"מתג עצירת טעינה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2D7B:["Charging Stop Switch Circuit Low","P2D7B is stored when the charging stop switch line is pulled below its permitted voltage, most often by a short to ground in the wiring, water in the switch or a contact that no longer opens on a switch that grounds the line when pressed. No manufacturer documents P2D7B publicly. Here the effect is mostly the reverse of P2D7A: on the common ground-switching layout a grounded line reads as a stop button held down.",["Stop switch signal wire shorted to body ground","Moisture or corrosion bridging the stop switch contacts","Stop switch contact stuck closed (ground-switching design)"],["Charging does not begin or ends immediately after plugging in","Charging indicator shows no active session"],2,0,["P2D7A","P2D79","P2D7D","P2D80"],"מתג עצירת טעינה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2D7C:["Charging Stop Switch Circuit Performance","P2D7C covers a stop switch signal that is electrically valid but does not make sense. A typical rationality test asks whether the reported state fits the situation, for instance a stop request that never ends although no one can hold a button that long, or a switch that reports pressed before any charging session has begun. No manufacturer documents P2D7C publicly.",["Stop button mechanically sticking in the pressed position","Internal leakage in the switch giving an in-between signal","Trim panel or object pressing on the button"],["Charging blocked although the plug is seated correctly","Stop button feels stiff or does not spring back"],2,0,["P2D79","P2D7D","P2D81"],"מתג עצירת טעינה — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2D7D:["Charging Stop Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2D7D flags a stop switch signal that jumps between states without a matching button press, or drops out briefly and returns. Since the charging control treats a stop signal as an order to end charging, as both the Toyota and the Honda patents describe, a flickering line can end a session without anyone touching the button. No manufacturer documents P2D7D publicly.",["Loose or fretting terminal at the stop switch connector","Cracked solder joint or worn contact inside the switch","Wire chafing that shorts only intermittently"],["Charging stops unexpectedly, e.g. overnight","Battery not full in the morning despite being plugged in"],2,0,["P2D79","P2D7C","P2D82"],"מתג עצירת טעינה — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2D7E:["Charging Start Switch Circuit","P2D7E is the umbrella circuit code for a charging start switch, the control with which a person begins a charging session by hand, for example to override a charging timer. It is set when the start switch line delivers no usable signal; the split into high, low, performance and intermittent follows in P2D7F to P2D82. No manufacturer documents P2D7E publicly.",["Loose, corroded or unplugged connector at the start switch","Broken wire between start switch and charging control unit","Start switch itself defective"],["Pressing the start button does not begin charging","Charging only begins at the programmed timer time"],2,0,["P2D7F","P2D80","P2D81","P2D82","P2D79"],"מתג התנעת טעינה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2D7F:["Charging Start Switch Circuit High","P2D7F reports a start switch line sitting above its allowed voltage, caused by an open wire or contact on a pulled-up input or by contact with a supply voltage. No manufacturer documents P2D7F publicly. With a start button the consequences run the other way than with the stop switch P2D7A.",["Open circuit in the start switch line or connector (pull-up design)","Start switch signal wire shorted to a supply voltage","Start switch contact no longer closes"],["Start button has no effect","Charging begins only by timer or after re-plugging"],2,0,["P2D80","P2D7E","P2D7A"],"מתג התנעת טעינה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2D80:["Charging Start Switch Circuit Low","P2D80 is set when the start switch line is dragged below its valid voltage, typically through a short to ground or a contact that stays closed on a button that grounds the input when pressed. No manufacturer documents P2D80 publicly. In that common layout a grounded line reads as a start button held down forever.",["Start switch signal wire shorted to ground","Start switch contact stuck closed or bridged by moisture","Corrosion in the connector creating a path to ground"],["Charging ignores the timer or starts unexpectedly before the code is set","Start button no longer works after the fault is detected"],2,0,["P2D7F","P2D7E","P2D7B"],"מתג התנעת טעינה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2D81:["Charging Start Switch Circuit Performance","P2D81 is the plausibility code of the charging start switch: the wiring reads as healthy, yet the reported switch behaviour cannot be right. Examples of what a control unit can check are a start request lasting far longer than any real press, a request that appears while no charging connector is plugged in, or a press that never produces the expected change of state. No manufacturer documents P2D81 publicly.",["Start button sticking or not returning","Worn switch contacts giving an unclear signal","Connector detection signal wrong, so a valid press seems implausible"],["Start button works only sometimes or not at all","Charging message about a switch fault"],2,0,["P2D7E","P2D82","P2D7C"],"מתג התנעת טעינה — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2D82:["Charging Start Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2D82 describes a start switch signal that toggles on its own or vanishes for moments. Because a start command is a trigger rather than a stop order, the visible effect is different from P2D7D: a flickering contact may start a charging session nobody asked for, for example ahead of a cheaper overnight tariff set in the timer, or swallow a deliberate press. No manufacturer documents P2D82 publicly;",["Loose or fretting terminal at the start switch connector","Worn contacts bouncing inside the start switch","Wire damage that makes contact only at times"],["Charging starts at unexpected times despite a timer","Start button needs several presses"],2,0,["P2D7E","P2D81","P2D7D"],"מתג התנעת טעינה — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2D83:["Battery Charger B Input Current Sensor Circuit Low","P2D83 says the current sensor at the input of charger B outputs a signal under its valid range. No manufacturer documents P2D83 publicly. For charger A the same fault is P0D3A, which Mitsubishi interprets on the 2022 Outlander PHEV as a ground short. Below 0.344 V of sensor output (roughly -54 A) for half a second, with 10-16 V on the charger, ends the charge, and the repair is a replacement charger/DC-DC assembly.",["Current sensor of charger B or its signal path shorted to ground inside the unit","Sensor supply inside the charger missing","Damaged internal connection or external harness where the sensor is separate"],["AC charging aborts shortly after starting","Reduced charging power if only charger A is still used"],4,0,["P2D84","P2D85","P0E8A","P0D3A","P0E89"],"חיישן זרם כניסת מטען סוללה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2D84:["Battery Charger B Input Current Sensor Circuit High","P2D84 is the high-side fault of charger B's input current sensor: its signal climbs above what the measuring range allows. No manufacturer documents P2D84 publicly, so the A-side code P0D3B serves as reference. For the 2022 Outlander PHEV, Mitsubishi counts half a second of sensor output above 4.658 V (around +54 A) as a supply-side short and halts charging.",["Charger B current sensor output shorted toward its supply inside the unit","Current sensor of charger B failed (charger repair or replacement)","Reference or ground of the sensor lost, pushing the signal up"],["AC charging does not start or stops within seconds","Charging fault warning in the cluster"],4,0,["P2D83","P2D85","P0E8A","P0D3B","P0E89"],"חיישן זרם כניסת מטען סוללה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2D85:["Battery Charger B Input Current Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2D85 is for an input current reading of charger B that lies within the electrical limits yet cannot be true. No manufacturer documents P2D85 publicly. Its A-side model P0D39 shows the usual test, a check of the zero point while no current should flow: Mitsubishi sets it on the 2022 Outlander PHEV if at least 1.5 A shows up for 2 s while charging is not yet permitted by the PHEV control unit;",["Zero-point drift of the charger B current sensor","Real residual current through a defective input stage while charging is not released","Calibration or software fault of the charger"],["Charging refused or stopped soon after plugging in","Charging power lower than expected"],4,0,["P2D83","P2D84","P0E8A","P0D39","P0E88"],"חיישן זרם כניסת מטען סוללה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2D86:["Fuel Temperature Sensor A/B Correlation","P2D86 checks two fuel temperature sensors against each other. Where both ought to show nearly the same value, because they measure the same fuel or after a long engine-off soak, a gap larger than a calibrated margin makes the pair implausible, without telling which sensor lies. No manufacturer documents P2D86 publicly.",["One of the two fuel temperature sensors has drifted and reads too warm or too cold","Corroded or loose connector adding resistance to one sensor signal","Replacement sensor of the wrong type or fitted in the wrong position","Engine control software with too tight a comparison limit"],["Malfunction indicator lamp, usually after two drives","Often no noticeable change in how the engine runs","Occasionally rougher hot restarts if fuel quantity correction is off"],2,1,["P0181","P0186","P0182","P0187","P0183","P0188","U0670","U0671"],"חיישן טמפרטורת דלק‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2D87:["Fan 1 Control Module Over Temperature","Current electric radiator fans carry their own electronics, which turn the PWM or LIN request of the engine controller into motor current. P2D87 means this control module of fan 1 reports that it has become too hot.",["Worn bearings or debris make the fan motor stiff, so the module overheats from excess current","Clogged radiator or condenser fins, missing air guides, heat build-up at standstill","Ageing power stage or thermal contact inside the fan control module"],["Fan runs slower or switches off temporarily","Rising coolant temperature in slow traffic","Weaker air conditioning at standstill"],2,1,["P2D88","P2D89","P2D8A","P0480","U0632","P0494","P0217"],"מודול בקרת מאוורר‏ 1 — חום יתר"],P2D88:["Fan 1 Control Module Performance","P2D88 means the electronics of fan 1 do not behave as expected although supply and communication are present: the module reports an internal fault, or the speed it sends back does not fit the request. Audi documents the code for 2025 Q5, Q5 Sportback, SQ5 and SQ5 Sportback in TSB 2081184/1.",["Poor or wrongly fitted ground connection of the fan","Internal fault of the fan control electronics","Fan blocked or slowed by debris or bearing wear","Moisture or corrosion in the fan connector or LIN line"],["Engine warning lamp on","Air conditioning stops cooling","Fan does not run or runs irregularly"],2,1,["P2D87","P2D89","P2D8B","U0632","P0480","P0494","P0483"],"מודול בקרת מאוורר‏ 1 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D89:["Fan 1 Control Module Supply Voltage Circuit","P2D89 concerns the power feed of the fan 1 control module: the voltage at its supply terminal, or the value the module reports back, is missing or outside the permitted window. Porsche uses the code in the DME of the 2021–2023 718 Cayman GTS 4.0, Boxster GTS 4.0, Cayman GT4 and Spyder and names it radiator fan 1 (left), power supply.",["Blown fuse, loose terminal or high-resistance supply cable to the fan module","Engine control software that misjudges the fan supply during start-up (Porsche 198/22)","Corroded or loose ground of the fan module","Weak battery or charging system dropping the supply during high fan load"],["Radiator fan intermittently without function","Reduced air-conditioning performance","Engine control warning in the instrument cluster"],2,1,["P2D87","P2D88","P2D8C","P0485","P0480"],"מודול בקרת מאוורר‏ 1 — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2D8A:["Fan 2 Control Module Over Temperature","P2D8A is the second-fan twin of P2D87: the electronics that power fan 2 signal that they have reached their temperature limit. On cars with two radiator fans the second one usually sits on the other side of the shroud; Porsche, for instance, calls its right-hand fan number 2. No manufacturer publicly documents P2D8A.",["Stiff or partly blocked fan 2 motor overloading its electronics","Heat build-up around the module, e.g. clogged fins or damaged air guides","Defective temperature sensing or power stage in the fan 2 module"],["Second fan slows down or cuts out after long idling","Coolant temperature climbs at standstill","Air conditioning blows warmer"],2,1,["P2D8B","P2D8C","P2D87","P0481","U0633","P2CB9","P0217"],"מודול בקרת מאוורר‏ 2 — חום יתר"],P2D8B:["Fan 2 Control Module Performance","With P2D8B the module that drives fan 2 fails a plausibility or self-test: it has supply and receives a request, yet the status or speed it reports does not fit. Audi's TSB 2081184/1 for the 2025 Q5 family lists P2D8B next to P2D88 and the local LIN bus error U366500, all stored in the thermal management control unit (address 00C5).",["Damaged or incorrectly fitted ground point of fan 2","Foreign objects or worn bearings slowing fan 2","Internal electronics fault of the fan 2 module","Water ingress or corrosion at connector or LIN line"],["Engine warning lamp on","Air conditioning without cooling","Fault stored intermittently or permanently"],2,1,["P2D88","P2D8A","P2D8C","U0633","P0481","P2CB9","P2B31"],"מודול בקרת מאוורר‏ 2 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D8C:["Fan 2 Control Module Supply Voltage Circuit","P2D8C concerns the supply circuit of the fan 2 control module. The engine controller registers that the module does not get proper operating voltage, whether through an open or high-resistance feed, a blown fuse, a poor ground or a reported voltage outside its window. Porsche lists P2D8C in the DME of the 718 GTS 4.0, GT4 and Spyder from model years 2021 to 2023 as radiator fan 2 (right), power supply.",["Blown fuse or high-resistance supply line to the fan 2 module","Engine control software error at start-up (Porsche 198/22)","Loose or corroded ground connection"],["Second radiator fan fails now and then","Air conditioning loses cooling power","Engine control warning displayed"],2,1,["P2D89","P2D8A","P2D8B","P0485","P0481"],"מודול בקרת מאוורר‏ 2 — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2D8D:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Mechanical Performance","In a P2 hybrid a disconnect clutch between combustion engine and electric machine lets the car drive on electric power alone and couples the engine in when needed. P2D8D aims at the clutch hardware itself, not at its actuator, pressure sensor or wiring, which have their own codes: the clutch does not take up or release torque the way the control expects. No manufacturer documents P2D8D publicly.",["Worn or glazed clutch plates that slip or no longer hold torque","Mechanically binding piston or plates so the clutch does not release fully","Pressure regulating valve of the clutch mechanically faulty","Wrong, aged or contaminated transmission fluid changing friction behaviour"],["Engine does not couple in or starts with a jerk","Transmission or hybrid warning in the cluster","Limp mode with reduced power or electric-only driving"],4,3,["P2884","P2886","P2882","P2885","P28EF","P28F0","P2DF3"],"מכני מצמד ניתוק מנוע — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2D8E:["Engine Oil Pressure Sensor/Switch C Circuit","Some engines have more than one oil pressure sensor or switch; which one is labelled A, B or C is up to the manufacturer. P2D8E is the general circuit code for sensor or switch C: the controller sees an electrical fault, or with a digital SENT sensor a message or internal error, that it cannot classify as too low or too high. No manufacturer documents P2D8E publicly;",["Oil-soaked, corroded or loose connector at sensor C","Internal electronics fault of the sensor or switch","Chafed or broken wire between sensor and engine control unit"],["Malfunction indicator lamp, depending on make","Oil pressure warning may come on without real pressure loss","Switchable oil pump may stay in its safe high-pressure stage"],1,1,["P2D8F","P2D90","P2D91","P0520","P055A"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ שמן מנוע‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2D8F:["Engine Oil Pressure Sensor/Switch C Circuit Low","P2D8F means the signal of oil pressure sensor C lies below its valid electrical range, which usually points to a short to ground, a lost supply or a defective sensor. Audi uses the code on 2025–2026 A5, S5, Q5 and SQ5 models with the 2.0 TFSI EA888 evo5 (TSB 2079097): engine control unit J623 stores it with symptom 17004, and the cluster may show the oil pressure and emission warnings.",["Signal or supply wire of sensor C shorted to ground","Voltage spike from a workshop charger switched on with the ignition (Audi EA888 evo5)","Sensor C defective with output stuck near zero","Engine control calibration that sets the fault too readily"],["Oil pressure warning without real pressure loss","Emission control warning lamp","Warning message in the instrument cluster"],1,1,["P2D8E","P2D90","P2D91","P0522","P055C"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ שמן מנוע‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2D90:["Engine Oil Pressure Sensor/Switch C Circuit High","P2D90 is set when sensor C delivers a voltage above its valid range. Typical reasons are a broken ground or signal wire that lets the input float up, a short to battery voltage or a sensor with a failed output stage. No manufacturer publicly describes P2D90; for the EA888 evo5 Audi documents only the low counterpart P2D8F.",["Open ground or signal wire of sensor C","Signal wire shorted to battery or reference voltage","Sensor C output stage defective"],["Malfunction indicator lamp, depending on make","Oil pressure gauge or warning shows implausible values","Variable oil pump may stay in its safe stage"],1,1,["P2D8E","P2D8F","P2D91","P0523","P055D"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ שמן מנוע‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2D91:["Engine Oil Pressure Sensor/Switch C Circuit Range/Performance","P2D91 says sensor C is electrically in range, but its reading does not fit the engine's state: pressure while the engine stands still, too little at speed, or a value that stays frozen while conditions change. Ford's 2024 summary handles sensor A this way under P0521, catching a signal stuck high, low or mid-range and readings that depart from a modelled pressure in either direction for 5 to 10 s.",["Sensor C drifted or stuck at one value","Real oil pressure deviation from worn pump, wrong oil or low oil level","Sticking oil pressure control valve of a variable pump","Sludge or debris in the sensor bore"],["Malfunction indicator lamp after two drives on some makes","Oil pressure warning flickers or appears without reason","Possible engine noise if pressure is really low"],2,1,["P2D8E","P2D8F","P2D90","P0521","P055B","P0524"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ שמן מנוע‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2D92:["Starter/Generator Phase X Current Sensor Circuit High","P2D92 is set when the signal from the phase X current sensor of a belt or crankshaft starter/generator rises above the range the control electronics treat as valid. Such sensors, commonly Hall devices placed around the phase conductor, put out a voltage that tracks the current, so a value stuck near the top of the scale points to the circuit rather than to real current: a signal lead touching a supply voltage, a…",["Phase X sensor signal wire shorted to a supply or reference voltage","Current sensor output failed at the upper end of its range","Damaged, corroded or water-contaminated connector at the starter/generator","Fault in the evaluation circuit of the starter/generator control module"],["Warning lamp or MIL, often only after the fault has been seen on two trips","Reduced electric assist and weaker restarts after automatic engine stop","Automatic stop-start no longer active"],3,3,["P2D95","P2D93","P2D94","P2DC1","P2DC2","P2D98"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ X — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2D93:["Starter/Generator Phase Y Current Sensor Circuit High","P2D93 reports that the current reading for phase Y of the starter/generator has climbed past its upper validity limit. Y is the middle letter of the X/Y/Z set this code series uses; the same list also has U/V/W variants (P2D9B to P2D9D), and no maker explains publicly how it assigns them. Not every design measures every phase.",["Phase Y sensor signal lead chafed and touching a voltage-carrying wire","Internal fault of the phase Y current sensor in the machine electronics","Defective input stage in the starter/generator control module"],["Hybrid or charging system warning on the instrument cluster","Boost function during acceleration missing or reduced","Engine restarts by the conventional starter or not at all after auto stop"],3,3,["P2D96","P2D92","P2D94","P2DC3","P2DC4","P2D99","P2DCB"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ Y — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2D94:["Starter/Generator Phase Z Current Sensor Circuit High","P2D94 completes the high-side series: the phase Z current sensor of the starter/generator outputs a value above its valid window. Inverters for 48 V starter/generators are built for three- or six-phase machines, and the controller relies on measured phase currents to set torque for engine restarts, boost and energy recovery.",["Pinched sensor lead or loose plug at the starter/generator","Water ingress into the machine-mounted electronics","Phase Z current sensor defective, output reads too high"],["MIL or system warning lamp","Stop-start and recuperation switched off","Battery warning because the machine charges less or not at all"],3,3,["P2D97","P2D92","P2D93","P2DC5","P2DC6","P2D9A"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ Z — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2D95:["Starter/Generator Phase X Current Sensor Circuit Low","P2D95 means the phase X current sensor of the starter/generator delivers a signal below the lowest value the controller accepts. The machine works as motor and as generator, so its phase currents change direction and the sensor reports signed values; GM's eAssist table, for example, uses limits of minus and plus 440 A.",["Phase X sensor signal wire shorted to ground or housing","Sensor supply voltage missing because of an open wire or terminal","Current sensor output failed at the lower end of its range"],["Warning lamp after repeated detection","Starter/generator runs in a restricted mode with less torque","Stop-start unavailable"],3,3,["P2D92","P2D96","P2D97","P2DC1","P2DC2","P2D98"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ X — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2D96:["Starter/Generator Phase Y Current Sensor Circuit Low","P2D96 covers the phase Y current sensor of the starter/generator when its signal drops below the valid range, for instance through a short to ground or a missing sensor supply. For the driver the more important part is how the controller reacts: without a trustworthy phase current it will usually limit or stop electric assist, stop-start can be suspended and charging through the machine may fall back, with a warning…",["Phase Y sensor signal pulled to ground by damaged insulation","Open circuit in the sensor supply or a backed-out terminal","Phase Y current sensor defective"],["Electric assist reduced or switched off","Stop-start suspended","Battery or system warning, charging may be reduced"],3,3,["P2D93","P2D95","P2D97","P2DC3","P2DC4","P2D99"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ Y — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2D97:["Starter/Generator Phase Z Current Sensor Circuit Low","P2D97 is the last of the three low codes: the Z-phase current sensor of the starter/generator reports a value under the bottom of its valid window. Because the machine both drives the engine and charges, its phase current is signed, so a low fault stands for an impossible negative reading or a collapsed output, not for a weak current.",["Phase Z sensor signal lead shorted to ground or to the machine housing","Sensor supply interrupted by an open wire or a pushed-back terminal","Phase Z current sensor output stuck at the bottom of its range"],["Warning lamp or MIL, typically after the fault has repeated on a second trip","Electric boost and recuperation reduced or switched off","No automatic engine stop, or restarts via the conventional starter"],3,3,["P2D94","P2D95","P2D96","P2DC5","P2DC6","P2D9A"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ Z — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2D98:["Starter/Generator Phase X Current Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2D98 points to a phase X current signal of the starter/generator that briefly drops out, jumps or flickers, even though most individual samples may still sit inside the accepted range. That pattern usually comes from a contact that opens under vibration or heat, a chafed lead or an ageing sensor; in many designs the signal is produced by a Hall element sitting in a ferrite ring around the phase conductor.",["Connector contact at the starter/generator opening under engine vibration","Phase X sensor lead chafed against the belt drive or a bracket","Ageing current sensor with unstable output at high temperature"],["Warning that appears and disappears between trips","Stop-start occasionally unavailable","Electric assist briefly cut during acceleration"],3,3,["P2D99","P2D9A","P2D92","P2D95","P2DC1","P2DC2"],"זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ X — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2D99:["Starter/Generator Phase Y Current Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2D99 is stored when the phase Y current value of the starter/generator behaves in a way a real winding current cannot: sudden steps, dropouts to zero or noise between consecutive samples. The winding inductance smooths the true current, so such jumps implicate the measuring path. Only systems that actually sense phase Y can raise this code;",["Corrosion or weak pin tension in the phase Y sensor connector","Harness damaged by heat from the exhaust side or by contact with moving parts","Phase Y current sensor producing a noisy or unstable signal"],["Sporadic hybrid or charging system warning","Recuperation occasionally interrupted"],3,3,["P2D98","P2D9A","P2D93","P2D96","P2DC3","P2DC4"],"זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ Y — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2D9A:["Starter/Generator Phase Z Current Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2D9A marks an unsteady current signal on phase Z of the starter/generator. Before replacing hardware it is worth asking whether the detection itself is too sharp. Mazda met exactly that on 2022 and 2023 CX-30 and Mazda3 models built in Mexico: its integrated starter generator flagged faults in the U-V-W and X-Y-Z stator driver groups because its overcurrent detection logic misjudged the current, and bulletin…",["Starter/generator software with overly sensitive detection, update available","Loose or spread terminal in the phase Z sensor plug","Water in the connector after washing or driving through deep water"],["Battery and engine warning lamps that come on now and then","Mild-hybrid functions occasionally unavailable"],3,3,["P2D98","P2D99","P2D94","P2D97","P2DC5","P2DC6"],"זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ Z — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2D9B:["Starter/Generator Phase U Current Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2D9B concerns phase U, the first phase of the starter/generator's main U-V-W group, when its current signal is unsteady rather than permanently out of range. GM's eAssist system, whose belt-driven machine appears in its tables as drive motor A, shows how a manufacturer separates hard limits from short events: the U sensor fails high or low beyond 440 A in either direction within 41.6 ms, while a fast, repeated…",["Marginal contact in the phase U sensor connector","Phase U sensor lead with damaged insulation or a partly broken strand","Phase U current sensor beginning to fail"],["Intermittent warning lamp, sometimes only after several trips","Sudden loss of electric assist, returning after a restart"],3,3,["P2D9C","P2D9D","P2D98","P0BE7","P0BE8","P0C01"],"זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ U — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2D9C:["Starter/Generator Phase V Current Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2D9C reports an erratic current signal on phase V of the starter/generator. V is the phase that some designs never measure: in a star-connected three-phase winding the three currents add up to zero, so GM's eAssist table runs sensor checks only on U and W. Other inverters fit a sensor to every phase conductor, often a Hall chip in a ring core whose output voltage follows the current.",["Phase V sensor plug not fully latched or with fretting corrosion","Intermittent break in the phase V sensor wiring","Phase V current sensor with unstable output"],["Sporadic system warning on the instrument cluster","Short interruptions of stop-start or boost"],3,3,["P2D9B","P2D9D","P2D99","P0BE9","P0BEA"],"זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ V — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2D9D:["Starter/Generator Phase W Current Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2D9D covers phase W of the starter/generator when its current signal flickers or drops out for moments. The W sensor is one of the two that GM's eAssist belt machine monitors. GM's checks there look at solid failures: below -440 A or above 440 A for 41.6 ms, Type B, and a learned zero offset beyond 30 A while the inverter is off.",["Moisture inside the starter/generator electronics","Cracked solder joint in the sensor path after many heat cycles","Poor contact in the phase W sensor connector"],["Warning lamp that shows up mostly when the engine is hot or the weather is wet","Charging through the starter/generator briefly interrupted"],3,3,["P2D9B","P2D9C","P2D9A","P0BEE","P0BEF","P0BF0"],"זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ W — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2D9E:["High Voltage System Voltage Low","P2D9E reports that the voltage of the high-voltage system – the DC network joining traction battery, inverters, DC/DC converter and other HV consumers – has dropped below its lower limit while the system is switched on. P0AFA judges the battery pack itself; P2D9E looks at the network side. No manufacturer documents P2D9E publicly or names its threshold.",["Traction battery deeply discharged or cell groups weak","Main contactor dropping out or precharge circuit faulty","Loose or corroded HV connector or busbar under load","Voltage sensing in the inverter or controller reads too low"],["Hybrid or EV system warning and check engine light","Noticeably reduced drive power or limp mode","Vehicle does not reach ready mode or engine does not start"],4,3,["P2D9F","P2DA0","P0AFA","P0AF8","P0C78"],"מערכת מתח גבוה — מתח נמוך"],P2D9F:["High Voltage System Voltage High","P2D9F is the over-voltage case: the DC voltage on the high-voltage network rises above the permitted maximum. Too much voltage stresses capacitors, power semiconductors and cells, so controllers react within milliseconds by cutting regeneration or charging. No manufacturer documents P2D9F publicly.",["Regenerative braking or charging while the battery is already full or cold","Contactor or HV connection opening while the motor generates","Voltage measurement in the inverter or controller reads too high","Voltage limits in control software too tight, update available"],["Hybrid or EV system warning and check engine light","Little or no regenerative braking, more wear on the friction brakes","Power limited or HV system shut down"],4,3,["P2D9E","P2DA0","P0AFB","P0C79","P0AF8"],"מערכת מתח גבוה — מתח גבוה"],P2DA0:["High Voltage System Performance","P2DA0 is the plausibility code of this group: the high-voltage system is neither clearly too low nor too high, but its readings or behaviour do not fit together. CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 asks for such rationality checks on inputs, stored separately from circuit and range faults. No manufacturer documents P2DA0 publicly.",["Voltage sensors in battery and inverter disagree","High resistance in an HV connector, busbar or fuse","Main contactor contacts burnt or welded","Calibration or software of a controller, update available"],["Hybrid or EV system warning, check engine light","Reduced drive power or no electric drive","Fault appears under heavy load or after a long stop"],4,3,["P2D9E","P2D9F","P0AF8","P0ABC","P0C78"],"מערכת מתח גבוה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DA1:["Gear Shift Control Module B Supply Voltage Low","With shift-by-wire, the selector the driver touches is an electronic module; module B is a second one, such as a further selector station or a redundant unit. Allison's 6th-generation controls show such a pair: for module 2 they list performance, lost communication, incompatibility and invalid data (P085E, U0291, U0333, U0592), but no supply codes.",["Weak 12 V battery or voltage dip during cranking","Corroded ground, loose connector or high-resistance feed to module B","Fuse for module B blown or with poor contact","Voltage evaluation in module software too strict"],["Shifter warning in the instrument cluster","Range selection at the second selector ignored, vehicle stays in P","Fault appears together with other low-voltage codes"],2,3,["P2DA2","P2DA3","P273C","P085E","U0291"],"אספקת מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים‏ B — מתח נמוך"],P2DA2:["Gear Shift Control Module B Supply Voltage High","P2DA2 is the over-voltage counterpart of P2DA1: gear shift control module B, the second selector unit of a shift-by-wire system, sees a supply above its permitted maximum. No manufacturer documents P2DA2 publicly or names the limit.",["Alternator regulator or DC/DC converter delivering too much voltage","Jump start with 24 V or charger connected during operation","Module feed shorted to a circuit with higher voltage","Voltage measurement inside module B faulty"],["Shifter warning in the instrument cluster","Second selector does not respond, main selector may still work","Further overvoltage codes in other modules, flickering lights"],2,3,["P2DA1","P2DA3","P273D","P0563","U0291"],"אספקת מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים‏ B — מתח גבוה"],P2DA3:["Gear Shift Control Module B Overtemperature","P2DA3 is a condition code: gear shift control module B reports that its internal temperature exceeds the safe limit. The circuit is fine, the module simply runs too hot. No manufacturer documents P2DA3 or a threshold publicly; Allison's 6th-generation controls, which give module 2 its own performance and communication codes, do not list it.",["Strong sun load or nearby heat source at the mounting location","Output stage for lock solenoid, display or lighting drawing excess current","Internal defect or faulty temperature sensing in module B"],["Shifter warning, mainly in hot weather or after long operation","Second selector temporarily ignores range requests","Fault disappears after the module has cooled down"],2,3,["P2DA1","P2DA2","P273E","P085E","U0291"],"מודול בקרת העברת הילוכים‏ B — חום יתר"],P2DA4:["Coolant Heater A Internal Control Module Performance","Coolant heater A here is an electric heater with built-in electronics, usually a high-voltage PTC or wire-element unit that warms coolant for cabin and battery in hybrids and EVs; it is separate from the engine block heater codes P01E8 ff. P2DA4 says that heater's own controller has found a fault in itself – a power switch that shorted, a temperature or current measurement that fails, or a processor error.",["Power switch inside the heater shorted or failed","Internal temperature or current measurement faulty","Coolant or moisture inside the electronics housing","Software fault in heater or commanding module, update available"],["Little or no cabin heat in electric mode","Engine of a hybrid runs more often just to supply heat","Climate system message, usually without check engine light"],3,0,["P2DA5","P2DA6","P2DA7","U069E","P2B75"],"מודול בקרה פנימי גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DA5:["Coolant Heater A Supply Voltage Circuit","P2DA5 concerns the feed that powers coolant heater A, the electric coolant heater with its own electronics found in hybrids and EVs. The heater's controller finds its supply input missing or outside the expected window and reports it as a circuit fault, unlike P2DA7, which rates the voltage level of the module. Which feed is meant is up to the maker.",["12 V or HV fuse for the heater open","Corroded or loose pin in the heater supply connector","Poor ground connection of the heater electronics","Supply input inside the heater electronics faulty"],["No heat from the electric coolant heater","Cabin heat only when the engine of a hybrid runs","Possibly lost communication with the heater stored at the same time"],2,0,["P2DA4","P2DA7","U069E","P2B72"],"גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ A — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2DA6:["Coolant Heater A Over Temperature","P2DA6 says coolant heater A, the electric coolant heater of a hybrid or EV, has become too hot. Such heaters measure outlet coolant or housing temperature and switch off above a limit; a Hyundai/Kia patent (US11378000B2) does exactly that, mainly to protect the elements when coolant is missing.",["Software of the controlling module (Ford Lightning SOBDMC), reprogramming","Low coolant level or air trapped in the heater loop","Heater loop coolant pump not running or valve blocking flow","Temperature sensor in heater or loop reading too high"],["Often no noticeable symptom, code found during service","Heater switches off, cabin warms only weakly","Climate system message, no check engine light"],2,0,["P2DA4","P2DA7","P2B75","U069E"],"גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ A — חום יתר"],P2DA7:["Coolant Heater A Control Module System Voltage","P2DA7 is logged when the electronics built into coolant heater A – the HV heater of a hybrid or EV – see a system voltage outside the window in which it may work. While P2DA5 points to the feed circuit, this code judges the level. High-voltage heaters have a defined range;",["Traction battery voltage at the edge of the heater's range (very low or very high charge)","Weak 12 V battery or poor ground of the heater electronics","Voltage measurement inside the heater faulty"],["Electric heater temporarily without function","Fault occurs with very low or very high battery charge","Cabin heat only from the engine of a hybrid"],2,0,["P2DA4","P2DA5","P2D9E","U069E"],"מתח מערכת מודול בקרת גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ A"],P2DA8:["DC/AC Converter Control Module A Switch A Circuit","DC/AC converter control module A is the inverter that turns direct current from the vehicle battery into household AC for sockets in the vehicle; Ford calls it DCACA and uses it for Pro Power Onboard on the F-150, where TSB 21-2127 handles a related fault, P0364 in the PCM. P2DA8 reports an electrical fault – open, short or no valid signal – in the circuit of switch A of this module.",["Open or shorted wire or corroded connector between switch A and the module","Switch A or its relay failed","Water ingress at an outlet panel in the bed or cargo area","Internal fault of the DC/AC converter module"],["AC outlets of group A without power","Message that onboard power is unavailable","Outlet button without reaction"],2,0,["P2DA9","P2DAA","P0364","U0288"],"מתג מודול בקרת ממיר DC/AC‏ A A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2DA9:["DC/AC Converter Control Module A Switch A Circuit Range/Performance","P2DA9 belongs to switch A of the DC/AC converter control module A, the inverter that supplies AC sockets in the vehicle. Unlike P2DA8 the circuit is intact, but the switch does not behave as expected: its signal sits between valid states, or the commanded state does not show up at the output. CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 describes this type of check as a rationality or functional test kept apart from circuit faults.",["Worn, sticking or burnt contacts of switch A or its relay","High contact resistance in connector or outlet wiring","Outlet button jammed by dirt or damage","Voltage sensing in the converter module implausible"],["Outlets of group A work only intermittently","Outlet power switches off unexpectedly under load","Switch position in the display does not match the outlet state"],2,0,["P2DA8","P2DAB","P0364","U0589"],"מתג מודול בקרת ממיר DC/AC‏ A A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2DAA:["DC/AC Converter Control Module A Switch B Circuit","P2DAA flags an electrical fault in the line of switch B belonging to DC/AC converter control module A, the vehicle's inverter for 120/230 V sockets. The module finds the switch B line open, shorted to ground or to supply, or without a usable signal.",["Open or shorted wire or corroded connector in the switch B circuit","Switch B or its relay failed","Shared feed, ground or converter module faulty (when group A also fails)"],["AC outlets of group B without power, other outlets work","Message that onboard power is limited or unavailable"],2,0,["P2DAB","P2DA8","P0364","U0288"],"מתג מודול בקרת ממיר DC/AC‏ A B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2DAB:["DC/AC Converter Control Module A Switch B Circuit Range/Performance","With P2DAB, switch B of converter module A – the unit feeding the vehicle's AC sockets – fails a plausibility test. Wiring tests pass, yet switch B does not deliver what was asked of it: it stays closed after an off command, opens under load, or reports a position that disagrees with the measured output. CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 calls for such functional checks on output components.",["Contacts of switch B or its relay welded, sticking or worn","Moisture or dirt at the outlet panel of group B","Load management or software in the converter module, update available"],["Outlets of group B switch off unexpectedly or cannot be switched off","Warning about onboard power in the display","Fault appears mainly with high loads connected"],2,0,["P2DAA","P2DA9","P0364","U0589"],"מתג מודול בקרת ממיר DC/AC‏ A B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2DAC:["Drive Motor A Temperature Sensor B Circuit","P2DAC is the general circuit fault of a second temperature sensor (B) in drive motor A; sensor A has its own series from P0A2A. A motor carries a second probe either as a backup element beside the first – Sensata's hairpin sensor patent allows two NTCs, or an NTC plus a PTC, in one housing – or as a probe on another phase winding. No manufacturer documents P2DAC publicly.",["Broken or shorted sensor B lead between motor and inverter","Loose, corroded or pushed-out terminal at the motor connector","Sensor B thermistor failed inside the stator","Faulty sensor input in the inverter or motor control unit"],["Hybrid system warning or check engine light","Electric drive power limited","Sensor B shows a fixed or missing value in live data while sensor A looks normal"],4,3,["P2DAD","P2DAE","P2DAF","P2DB0","P0A2A","P2DB1"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מנוע הנעה‏ A B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2DAD:["Drive Motor A Temperature Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2DAD covers a sensor B signal that stays inside the electrical window yet does not fit the situation. CARB asks for rationality checks on hybrid input components where feasible, logged under a code of their own apart from circuit and range faults.",["Sensor B thermistor drifted from its resistance curve","Added resistance at a worn or corroded terminal","Probe no longer seated firmly against the winding","Fault in the reference value, e.g. sensor A or coolant temperature"],["Hybrid system warning or check engine light","Sensor B differs clearly from sensor A after the car has stood overnight","Electric drive power limited in some situations"],4,3,["P2DAC","P2DAE","P2DAF","P0A2B","P2DB2"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מנוע הנעה‏ A B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2DAE:["Drive Motor A Temperature Sensor B Circuit Low","P2DAE means the sensor B voltage has fallen below the lowest value a healthy sensor can deliver. Winding probes are mostly NTC thermistors whose resistance collapses as they heat – Thinking Electronic quotes roughly 0.46 kOhm at 180 °C for its stator probes – so with the usual pull-up circuit a near-zero voltage would read as an impossibly hot winding.",["Sensor B signal lead shorted to ground or motor housing","Thermistor shorted internally (often replaceable only with the motor)","Lead pinched or chafed after work on the drive unit"],["Hybrid system warning or check engine light","Sensor B shows an extremely high fixed temperature in live data","Electric drive power reduced"],4,3,["P2DAC","P2DAD","P2DAF","P0A2C","P0A2F","P2DB3"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מנוע הנעה‏ A B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2DAF:["Drive Motor A Temperature Sensor B Circuit High","P2DAF is the high-side counterpart: the sensor B voltage rises close to the reference. For an NTC probe that would be an impossibly cold winding, so the controller treats it as an interrupted circuit – broken lead, unplugged or corroded connector, cracked thermistor – or, less often, a short to a supply voltage.",["Open signal or ground lead of sensor B","Connector unplugged or terminal backed out, often after drive unit work","Thermistor open or cracked inside the stator","Signal lead shorted to a supply voltage"],["Hybrid system warning or check engine light","Sensor B shows an implausibly low temperature in live data","Electric drive power limited"],4,3,["P2DAC","P2DAD","P2DAE","P0A2D","P2DB4"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מנוע הנעה‏ A B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2DB0:["Drive Motor A Temperature Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","P2DB0 logs short dropouts or jumps in the sensor B signal that come and go too fast for the steady low and high checks. Because CARB requires circuit monitoring of input components to run continuously, such glitches are caught while driving.",["Resistance jumps in the sensor crimp at high temperature","Worn or loose terminals in a connector of the sensor B line","Chafed lead with intermittent contact under vibration"],["Warning light that comes and goes, often after hard driving","Sensor B value spikes briefly in live data","Electric drive power briefly limited on some models"],4,3,["P2DAC","P2DAE","P2DAF","P0A2E","P2DB5"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מנוע הנעה‏ A B — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2DB1:["Drive Motor A Temperature Sensor C Circuit","P2DB1 reports a circuit fault on a third temperature sensor (C) in drive motor A. Three probes in one motor make most sense when each phase winding of the three-phase machine gets its own: Mitsubishi equips the front motor of the 2023 Outlander PHEV with U-, V- and W-phase coil sensors, and a fault on any of them lights both the hybrid warning and the MIL.",["Broken or shorted sensor C lead between motor and inverter","Loose or corroded terminal at the motor connector","Sensor C thermistor failed in its phase winding","Faulty sensor input in the inverter or motor control unit"],["Hybrid system warning and check engine light","Sensor C missing or frozen in live data while the other motor sensors read normally","Electric drive power capped"],4,3,["P2DB2","P2DB3","P2DB4","P2DB5","P2DAC","P0A2A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מנוע הנעה‏ A C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2DB2:["Drive Motor A Temperature Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P2DB2 flags a sensor C reading that is electrically valid but disagrees with what the motor should show. With three probes a cold-soak comparison is the natural test: Mitsubishi checks its W-phase sensor (sensor 3, own code P3057) on the 2023 Outlander PHEV once per driving cycle after more than 90 minutes off, inverter switched off, and rejects it when it lies over 26 °C away from the U-phase reading for 0.8 s or…",["Sensor C thermistor drifted from its resistance curve","Extra resistance at a corroded or worn terminal","Probe loose on its phase winding"],["Hybrid system warning or check engine light","Sensor C stands well apart from the other motor sensors after a cold start","No noticeable driving change in many cases"],4,3,["P2DB1","P2DB3","P2DB4","P2DAD","P0A2B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מנוע הנעה‏ A C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2DB3:["Drive Motor A Temperature Sensor C Circuit Low","P2DB3 sets when the sensor C voltage drops below its valid floor. For an NTC probe this would stand for a temperature far beyond any real winding heat, so a short is much more likely than a genuine hot spot: signal lead to ground or motor housing, insulation damaged inside the stator, or a thermistor shorted internally.",["Sensor C signal lead shorted to ground or motor housing","Probe insulation damaged inside the stator","Thermistor shorted internally"],["Hybrid system warning and check engine light","Sensor C reads extremely hot while the other sensors look normal","Electric drive power reduced"],4,3,["P2DB1","P2DB2","P2DB4","P2DAE","P0A2F"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מנוע הנעה‏ A C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2DB4:["Drive Motor A Temperature Sensor C Circuit High","P2DB4 is the open-circuit side of sensor C: the voltage climbs toward the reference because hardly any current still flows through the thermistor. A broken wire, a terminal backed out of the motor connector, corrosion or a cracked thermistor are the likely finds; a short to a supply voltage is rarer. With an NTC the value shown would be an impossibly cold winding.",["Open signal or ground lead of sensor C","Terminal backed out or corroded in the motor connector","Thermistor open inside the stator","Signal lead shorted to a supply voltage"],["Hybrid system warning and check engine light","Sensor C reads far below ambient temperature in live data","Electric drive power limited"],4,3,["P2DB1","P2DB2","P2DB3","P2DAF","P0A2D"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מנוע הנעה‏ A C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2DB5:["Drive Motor A Temperature Sensor C Circuit Intermittent","P2DB5 is set when the sensor C signal drops out or jumps briefly and then recovers – a flickering contact rather than a lasting open or short. No manufacturer documents P2DB5. The closest published case concerns sensor A: Bentley's P0A2E00 bulletin for 2020–23 Bentayga and Flying Spur hybrids traces temperature jumps to a sensor crimp whose resistance changes suddenly when hot, cured by a new sensor rather than a…",["Crimp of sensor C changing resistance when hot","Loose or fretted terminals in the sensor C connector","Lead rubbing through and touching intermittently"],["Warning light that disappears and returns","Brief spikes or gaps in the sensor C value in live data","Fault mainly after long or hard drives"],4,3,["P2DB1","P2DB3","P2DB4","P2DB0","P0A2E"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מנוע הנעה‏ A C — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2DB6:["Battery Charger B Cooling System Performance","P2DB6 is set when the cooling of a second on-board charger, charger B, cannot hold the unit inside its permitted temperature window, so the charger has to cut its power or stop. No manufacturer documents P2DB6 publicly.",["Low coolant level or trapped air in the charger cooling circuit","Electric coolant pump of the low-temperature circuit weak or failed","Coolant hoses connected to the wrong circuit after assembly or repair","Low-temperature radiator clogged or its airflow obstructed"],["Charging power reduced at the charge station","Plug-in charging stops after some minutes","Charging fault message in the instrument cluster"],2,0,["P0D8F","P0E85","P0A93"],"מערכת קירור מטען סוללה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DB7:["Battery Charging System B High Voltage Interlock Circuit/Open","P2DB7 reports that the high voltage interlock loop of charging system B is broken. Such a loop is a low-current wire run in series through the HV plugs and covers of a charging path; once it opens, the control unit treats the path as unsafe and keeps it switched off. B denotes a second charging path, for example a further on-board charger. No manufacturer documents P2DB7 publicly.",["HV connector in the charging path not fully seated or its catch not closed","Broken interlock wire or pushed-out terminal","Service cover or HV cover of the charger not closed properly","Fault in the interlock evaluation of the control module"],["No charging through charging path B","Charging system warning in the instrument cluster"],2,0,["P2DB8","P2DB9","P2DBA","P2DBB","P0D15"],"נעילת בטיחות מתח גבוה מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2DB8:["Battery Charging System B High Voltage Interlock Circuit Performance","P2DB8 means the interlock loop of charging system B carries a signal, but one that does not behave as the control unit expects. A common test switches the module's test source on and off and checks that the sensed level follows; a reading that stays put or hovers between the valid bands points to contact resistance, a half-seated plug or corrosion rather than a clean break. No manufacturer documents P2DB8 publicly.",["Raised contact resistance in an interlock terminal","Plug in the charging path inserted only partway","Corrosion or moisture in an interlock connector","Test source or measuring stage of the module not working correctly"],["Charging via path B refused or interrupted","Charging system warning message"],2,0,["P2DB7","P2DB9","P2DBA","P2DBB","P0D16"],"נעילת בטיחות מתח גבוה מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2DB9:["Battery Charging System B High Voltage Interlock Circuit Low","P2DB9 is stored when the sensed voltage of the charging system B interlock loop stays too low. Since the module feeds a test voltage into the loop, a low reading usually means current is escaping to ground: a chafed wire touching the body, moisture in a connector, or a failing measuring stage inside the module. No manufacturer documents P2DB9 publicly.",["Interlock wire chafed through and touching ground","Water or dirt in an interlock connector causing leakage to ground","Defective interlock source or measuring stage in the control module"],["Charging through path B not possible","Charging system warning message"],2,0,["P2DB7","P2DB8","P2DBA","P2DBB","P0D17"],"נעילת בטיחות מתח גבוה מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2DBA:["Battery Charging System B High Voltage Interlock Circuit High","P2DBA flags an interlock signal of charging system B that reads too high. A loop fed from a test source and measured at its far end shows a raised level when it is shorted to a supply voltage, or, depending on the circuit, when added resistance or a break lets the measuring input float upward. No manufacturer documents P2DBA publicly.",["Interlock wire shorted to a supply voltage","Added resistance or partial break in the interlock loop","Faulty measuring input in the control module"],["No charging via path B","Charging system warning message"],2,0,["P2DB7","P2DB8","P2DB9","P2DBB","P0D18"],"נעילת בטיחות מתח גבוה מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2DBB:["Battery Charging System B High Voltage Interlock Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2DBB covers an interlock loop of charging system B that keeps dropping out and recovering, so its state flips between valid and invalid. The trigger is usually mechanical: a terminal with low contact pressure, a plug that is not fully latched, or a wire that only loses contact when the body flexes or the parts heat up. No manufacturer documents P2DBB publicly.",["Loose or widened terminal in an interlock connector","Connector in the charging path not fully latched","Chafed interlock wire that loses contact only with movement or heat"],["Charging via path B stops without warning","Fault comes and goes, often depending on temperature"],2,0,["P2DB7","P2DB8","P2DB9","P2DBA","P0D19"],"נעילת בטיחות מתח גבוה מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2DBC:["Battery Charger B Coupler Lock Position Sensor Circuit","P2DBC is the general circuit fault of the lock position sensor at charger B's coupler, the feedback telling the vehicle whether the pin that holds the charging plug in the inlet has moved out or back in. B marks a second inlet or charging path. No manufacturer documents P2DBC publicly.",["Open or shorted wire between lock actuator and control module","Lock pin broken after the plug was pulled while still latched","Corroded or loose connector at the lock actuator","Faulty sensor input in the control module"],["DC fast charging not possible at inlet B","Charger service warning in the instrument cluster"],2,0,["P2DBD","P2DBE","P2DBF","P2DC0","P0D9E"],"חיישן מצב נעילת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2DBD:["Battery Charger B Coupler Lock Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2DBD is the plausibility fault of the coupler lock feedback on charger B: the signal is electrically valid yet does not fit what the lock is doing, for example a travel that is too short after a lock command, or longer than the pin could ever move with a plug inserted. No manufacturer documents P2DBD publicly.",["Lock pin broken off or missing, so the measured travel is implausible","Lock mechanism sticking or jammed by dirt or ice","Loose low-voltage contacts at the charger or actuator"],["Charging at inlet B refused","Plug cannot be locked or released normally"],2,0,["P2DBC","P2DBE","P2DBF","P2DC0","P0D9F"],"חיישן מצב נעילת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2DBE:["Battery Charger B Coupler Lock Position Sensor Circuit Low","P2DBE means the coupler lock sensor of charger B delivers a voltage below its valid band. No manufacturer documents P2DBE publicly. The A-side code P0DA0 is documented by Mitsubishi for the 2023 Outlander PHEV: with the ignition-controlled supply on, the PHEV-ECU sets it on a low input from the inlet's lock sensor.",["Sensor signal line shorted to ground","Lock position sensor with internal short or wrong resistance","Damaged lock actuator after the plug was pulled while latched","Faulty sensor input in the control module"],["Charging at inlet B refused","Charging system warning lamp or message"],2,0,["P2DBC","P2DBD","P2DBF","P2DC0","P0DA0"],"חיישן מצב נעילת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2DBF:["Battery Charger B Coupler Lock Position Sensor Circuit High","P2DBF is set when the lock position signal of charger B's coupler stays above its permitted range. No manufacturer documents P2DBF publicly. Mitsubishi's procedure for the A-side code P0DA1 on the 2023 Outlander PHEV points to the usual culprits of a high reading: the sensor's ground pin at the lock actuator connector must show continuity to body ground (2 Ω or less), its supply pin must carry battery voltage, and…",["Open ground connection of the lock position sensor","Open signal line between sensor and control module","Signal line shorted to a supply voltage","Faulty inlet assembly with integrated lock actuator"],["Fast charging at inlet B not possible","Charging system warning message"],2,0,["P2DBC","P2DBD","P2DBE","P2DC0","P0DA1"],"חיישן מצב נעילת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2DC0:["Battery Charger B Coupler Lock Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2DC0 describes lock feedback at the charger B inlet that jumps or drops out for short moments instead of failing steadily. Because the lock state is a release condition for charging, a flickering signal can end a session or stop it from starting even though the plug is held properly. No manufacturer documents P2DC0 publicly.",["Loose low-voltage plug at the lock actuator or charger","Sensor wire chafed near the charging inlet","Water ingress into the inlet or actuator connector"],["Charging at inlet B stops or fails to start sporadically","Fault appears only at certain temperatures"],2,0,["P2DBC","P2DBD","P2DBE","P2DBF","P0DA2"],"חיישן מצב נעילת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2DC1:["Starter/Generator Phase X Current Sensor Circuit","P2DC1 is the general circuit code for the phase X current sensor of the starter/generator: the controller sees an electrical fault in the sensor path without, or in place of, a separate high or low verdict. CARB's OBD rule normally wants wiring faults and out-of-limit readings stored apart, yet it allows them to share one code when the sensor sits on a circuit board inside the control unit.",["Phase X current sensor on the integrated electronics board defective","Open or shorted lead between an external phase X sensor and the controller","Unstable 12 V supply or ground of the starter/generator electronics"],["MIL or system warning lamp","Starter/generator in a reduced mode or switched off","Stop-start and boost unavailable"],3,3,["P2DC2","P2D92","P2D95","P2D98","P2DC3","P2DC5"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ X — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2DC2:["Starter/Generator Phase X Current Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2DC2 means the starter/generator's phase X current sensor delivers values that are electrically valid but do not make sense. CARB requires such rationality faults to be detected where feasible and kept in a code of their own, separate from wiring and out-of-limit faults. One published method is the zero check: when the inverter is not switching, no phase current flows, so the reading should be near zero.",["Zero point of the phase X sensor drifted, for example through ageing or heat","Sensor reference voltage out of tolerance","Phase X current sensor with gain error or slowly failing"],["Warning lamp after the plausibility check has failed on two trips","Less electric torque because current control runs in a substitute mode"],3,3,["P2DC1","P2D92","P2D95","P2D98","P2DC4","P2DC6","P2DCB"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ X — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2DC3:["Starter/Generator Phase Y Current Sensor Circuit","P2DC3 flags an electrical fault in the circuit of the phase Y current sensor of the starter/generator. Such a sensor needs a supply, a ground and a signal line, and a break or short in any of the three can end up here when the controller cannot or does not tell high from low.",["Missing supply or ground at the phase Y sensor","Open phase Y signal line between sensor and controller","Phase Y current sensor without output"],["MIL or hybrid warning","Automatic stop-start disabled","Battery charged less by the starter/generator"],3,3,["P2DC4","P2D93","P2D96","P2D99","P2DC1","P2DC5"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ Y — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2DC4:["Starter/Generator Phase Y Current Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2DC4 says the phase Y current reading of the starter/generator is inside its electrical limits but fails a plausibility test. One way to test it is an energy balance: the power drawn or delivered on the phase side must match the current on the DC side. GM's eAssist machine compares the sum derived from its phase sensors with the DC-DC converter input and battery pack current;",["Phase Y current sensor reading consistently too high or too low","Zero offset of the phase Y sensor drifted","Comparison value wrong because the DC-side current measurement is faulty"],["Warning lamp after two trips with the fault","Noticeably weaker boost and smoother but slower restarts"],3,3,["P2DC3","P2DC2","P2DC6","P2DCB","P2D93","P2D96","P0BFD"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ Y — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2DC5:["Starter/Generator Phase Z Current Sensor Circuit","P2DC5 records a circuit fault of the phase Z current sensor in the starter/generator. A Z phase only exists on machines with more than one phase group. Mazda, for one, gives an integrated machine a second set of stator drivers labelled X, Y and Z, and CARB asks for circuit checks on such hybrid inputs.",["Phase Z sensor inside the starter/generator electronics failed","Low-voltage connector of the starter/generator damaged or not latched","Supply or ground fault of the machine electronics"],["MIL and battery warning","No recuperation and no electric boost"],3,3,["P2DC6","P2D94","P2D97","P2D9A","P2DC1","P2DC3"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ Z — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2DC6:["Starter/Generator Phase Z Current Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2DC6 is the plausibility code for the starter/generator's phase Z current sensor. The reading stays within its electrical window but does not match what the controller expects from commanded current and machine state.",["Phase Z sensor has lost sensitivity or drifted","Real current deviation from a poor phase Z connection or winding fault","Controller software or calibration judging the signal wrongly"],["Warning lamp, usually after two trips","Reduced starter/generator output or rough automatic restarts"],3,3,["P2DC5","P2DC2","P2DC4","P2DCB","P2D94","P2D97","P0C05"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ Z — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2DC7:["Starter/Generator Excitation Current","P2DC7 is the general fault for the excitation current of a starter/generator, meaning the DC current in the rotor field winding does not behave as commanded. Only wound-field machines have one. Valeo's 48 V belt starter generator, for instance, is a synchronous claw-pole machine;",["Worn brushes or contaminated slip rings on the rotor","Fault in the excitation H-bridge of the starter/generator electronics","Rotor field winding with interrupted turns or a short"],["Battery or charging warning lamp","Starter/generator stops charging and assisting","Stop-start disabled"],3,3,["P2DC8","P2DC9","P2DCA","P065B"],"זרם עירור מתנע/גנרטור"],P2DC8:["Starter/Generator Excitation Current Low","P2DC8 reports that too little excitation current reaches the rotor field winding of a wound-field starter/generator. With a weak field the claw-pole machine produces little torque and little voltage, so both charging and electric assist fade.",["Brushes worn down so they no longer contact the slip rings reliably","Open circuit in the rotor field coil or its connections","Excitation driver stage in the electronics unable to deliver current"],["Charging warning and falling battery voltage","No electric boost and weak or no belt-driven restarts"],3,3,["P2DC7","P2DC9","P2DCA","P065B"],"זרם עירור מתנע/גנרטור — ערך נמוך"],P2DC9:["Starter/Generator Excitation Current High","P2DC9 means a starter/generator with an electrically excited rotor draws more field current than its controller expects or allows. In such machines, for example Valeo's 48 V claw-pole belt starter generator, the stator windings get their three-phase supply from an inverter, and an extra full bridge sets the rotor's DC field via brushes on slip rings.",["Excitation driver stage in the controller shorted or no longer regulating","Shorted turns in the rotor field coil lowering its resistance","Faulty field current measurement inside the controller","Field lead chafed and shorted to a supply voltage"],["Check engine light and 48 V or charging system warning","Start-stop and electric boost switched off","Overvoltage protection cuts in, electrical consumers may flicker"],3,3,["P2DC7","P2DC8","P2DCA","P065B"],"זרם עירור מתנע/גנרטור — ערך גבוה"],P2DCA:["Starter/Generator Excitation Current Intermittent","P2DCA is set when the field current of a starter/generator with electrically excited rotor does not stay steady but drops out or jumps for short moments, without staying beyond the low or high limit long enough for P2DC8 or P2DC9.",["Worn or sticking brushes, dirty or worn slip rings","Loose connector or terminal on the field leads","Cracked solder joint in the excitation bridge of the controller"],["Charge warning that comes and goes","Jerky or delayed restarts after start-stop","Electric boost and recuperation work only at times"],3,3,["P2DC7","P2DC8","P2DC9","P065B"],"זרם עירור מתנע/גנרטור — תקלה לסירוגין"],P2DCB:["Starter/Generator Phase X-Y-Z Current Sensor Correlation","P2DCB compares the three current sensors of the starter/generator's X-Y-Z phase group with one another or with the DC side. In a star-connected winding the instantaneous phase currents must add up to roughly zero; if they do not, at least one sensor is wrong, even though each may sit inside its own limits.",["Gain or zero drift of one phase current sensor","Disturbed supply or reference voltage shared by the sensors","Calibration or software fault in the starter/generator controller"],["Check engine light with hybrid or 48 V system warning","Reduced electric boost and recuperation in substitute mode","Start-stop may be disabled"],3,3,["P2DC2","P2DC4","P2DC6","P2DC1","P2DC3","P2DC5","P0BFD"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מתנע/גנרטור‏ X-Y-Z — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2DCC:["Starter/Generator Position Sensor Correlation","P2DCC reports that the rotor position or speed the starter/generator derives from its own sensor disagrees with an independent reference. For a belt-driven machine the natural reference is the crankshaft: engine speed times the pulley ratio has to match machine speed.",["Slipping drive belt or weak belt tensioner","Rotor position sensor degraded or shifted","Faulty engine speed reference from the crankshaft sensor or its CAN signal"],["Start-stop and electric assist disabled","Belt squeal or engine restart via 12 V starter instead","Check engine light"],3,3,["P0A90","P2BA3","P0A40","P2DCB","P2CF9"],"חיישן מצב מתנע/גנרטור — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2DCD:["Particulate Filter B Incorrect","P2DCD is meant for a second particulate filter, labelled B, that the engine control unit finds to be absent or not the specified part, for instance after the filter has been cut out, replaced by an empty housing or swapped for an unsuitable aftermarket unit. No manufacturer documents P2DCD publicly, and makers catch such tampering with other codes.",["Filter B removed or replaced by an empty housing or pipe","Unsuitable replacement filter fitted","Filter substrate cracked, melted or blown out","Leaking or blocked pressure lines misleading the detection"],["Check engine light on","Failed emissions inspection","Louder exhaust or visible soot at the tailpipe"],2,1,["P24FD","P226E","P226D","P2003","P243B"],""],P2DCE:["Control Pilot Charging Switch B Circuit/Open","P2DCE reports an open or otherwise faulty control circuit of charging switch B, a vehicle-side switch on the control pilot line. Under SAE J1772 the car first loads the pilot with about 2.74 kΩ, pulling the 12 V supplied by the station down to roughly 9 V; closing a charging switch puts another 1.3 kΩ in parallel, the level falls to about 6 V and the station energises the cable.",["Broken wire or pushed-back pin in the switch B circuit","Switch or its driver inside the charging module open","Corroded contacts at the charge inlet or module connector"],["Station detects the car but charging never starts","Charging fault message in the instrument cluster"],2,0,["P2DCF","P2DD0","P2DD1","P2DD2","P2DD3","P2DD4","P0CF8"],"מתג טעינת פיילוט בקרה‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2DCF:["Control Pilot Charging Switch B Range/Performance","P2DCF means charging switch B responds electrically, but the pilot level it creates is not plausible. The only public description of such a test concerns switch A: in a GM check for the Chevrolet Volt, run only while no cable is inserted, the module shuts its internal test switch and the charging switch simultaneously, and the pilot-to-battery voltage ratio then has to lie from 0.14 to 0.28;",["Resistor in the switch B branch drifted out of tolerance","High contact resistance in switch, inlet or connector","Fault in the pilot voltage measuring path of the charging module"],["Charging refused or stopping after a short time","Charging error message"],4,0,["P2DCE","P2DD0","P2DD1","P2DD2","P0CF9","P0CF4"],"מתג טעינת פיילוט בקרה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DD0:["Control Pilot Charging Switch B Circuit Low","P2DD0 says the drive or sense wire of switch B reads below its valid range. The usual reasons are a wire chafed through to body ground or a shorted transistor stage in the charging electronics. Depending on how the switch is driven, a grounded line can hold it permanently closed, so the pilot stays at the charge-request level of about 6 V, or keep it from ever closing.",["Switch B wire chafed and shorted to ground","Output stage in the charging module failed shorted","Moisture in the charge inlet creating a leakage path"],["Charging starts immediately on plug-in or not at all","Timed charging not followed","Charging fault message"],2,0,["P2DD1","P2DCE","P2DCF","P2DD2","P0CFA"],"מתג טעינת פיילוט בקרה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2DD1:["Control Pilot Charging Switch B Circuit High","P2DD1 reports a voltage on the drive or feedback wire of switch B that is higher than it should be. Likely culprits are a wire touching battery voltage or another feed somewhere between inlet and module, or a transistor stage that has lost the ability to pull its output low. Whether the switch then stays open or closed depends on the design.",["Switch B line shorted to a supply voltage","Driver stage in the charging module no longer pulling low","Moisture or pushed-back pins at inlet or module connector"],["Car stays in plugged-in state, station supplies no power","Charging session cannot be ended cleanly"],2,0,["P2DD0","P2DCE","P2DCF","P2DD2","P0CFB"],"מתג טעינת פיילוט בקרה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2DD2:["Control Pilot Charging Switch B Intermittent/Erratic","P2DD2 is stored when the signal of charging switch B changes state erratically: it drops out or toggles for brief moments, while lasting faults would end up as P2DCE, P2DD0 or P2DD1. Loose terminals, green corrosion at inlet pins or the module plug, and conductors that break contact only when the car moves or temperatures change are the usual suspects.",["Loose terminal in the charge inlet or module connector","Corrosion from water ingress at the charge inlet","Chafed wire losing contact with movement or temperature"],["Charging stops and restarts repeatedly","Battery not fully charged after a charging session"],2,0,["P2DCE","P2DD0","P2DD1","P2DCF","P0CFC"],"מתג טעינת פיילוט בקרה‏ B — אות לא יציב"],P2DD3:["Control Pilot Charging Switch B Stuck Off","Stuck Off: although the module orders charging switch B to close, nothing changes on the pilot; the voltage sits near 9 V, the plugged-in level, rather than dropping to about 6 V. Through this switch the station thus never sees a request for energy. A contact or relay that will not close, a broken 1.3 kΩ resistor or an error in the pilot measurement can each cause this.",["Switch or relay B no longer closing","Open resistor in the charge-request branch","Pilot voltage measurement in the module faulty"],["Car recognised at the station but no charging","Charging error message"],4,0,["P2DD4","P2DCE","P2DCF","P2DD0","P2DD1","P0CFD"],"מתג טעינת פיילוט בקרה‏ B — תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2DD4:["Control Pilot Charging Switch B Stuck On","P2DD4 describes the reverse case: switch B remains closed against the module's command to open, and the pilot goes on asking for energy at about 6 V although charging should have ended or paused. Welded or sticking contacts, a driver stage shorted on, or software that does not release the switch are all possible.",["Charger software not releasing the switch","Welded or sticking switch contacts","Driver stage permanently switched on"],["Charging does not end or pause as planned","Charging error message after the session"],4,0,["P2DD3","P2DCE","P2DCF","P2DD0","P2DD1","P0CFE"],"מתג טעינת פיילוט בקרה‏ B — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2DD5:["Fuel Injection Quantity B Lower Than Expected","P2DD5 reports that the injection path the manufacturer calls B delivers less fuel than the engine control commanded. SAE leaves open what B is: a second injector set, an injector group or a separate operating mode. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The underlying check is the one CARB has demanded from diesels since 2010: the module compares requested fuel with what airflow and lambda say was burned.",["Injectors of group B coked or partly blocked","Supply or rail pressure for this path too low (filter, pump)","Airflow or lambda measurement off, so the computed fuel looks too small","Engine control software or injector calibration data"],["Check engine light on","Less power, sluggish response under load","Uneven idle"],3,1,["P2DD6","P2DD7","P026C","P2DDC","P2DDE","P0171"],""],P2DD6:["Fuel Injection Quantity B Higher Than Expected","With P2DD6 the engine control has found that path B injects more fuel than requested, so the mixture ends up richer than planned. Typical reasons are an injector that drips after closing, a worn nozzle passing extra fuel, or rail pressure above target; a sensor that under-reads airflow can fake the same result. On diesels this shows up as soot: more black smoke and shorter intervals between filter regenerations.",["Injector in group B dripping or nozzle worn","Rail pressure above target (regulator, pressure sensor)","Airflow sensor reading low or intake leak after the sensor","Wrong injector part fitted"],["Check engine light on","Black smoke, more frequent particulate filter regeneration","Higher fuel consumption"],3,1,["P2DD5","P2DD8","P026D","P2DDD","P2DDF","P0172"],""],P2DD7:["Cold Start Fuel Injection Quantity B Lower Than Expected","P2DD7 limits the shortfall of P2DD5 to the cold-start phase. Many engines inject differently just after a cold start, with extra or shifted injections that heat the catalyst or SCR system. CARB section 1968.2 (f)(12.1.2) requires diesels to keep faults found while this strategy runs apart from the same faults in normal operation, and (f)(12.2.3) adds a check that the commanded injection quantity actually responds,…",["Fuel filter restricted, fuel waxing in cold weather","Rail pressure builds too slowly after start","Injectors of group B sluggish or partly blocked","Coolant or fuel temperature signal implausible"],["Check engine light on after a cold start","Hard cold start, rough running while cold","Longer warm-up"],3,1,["P2DD8","P2DD5","P027E","P2DE0","P2DE2","P2C1F","P05EC"],""],P2DD8:["Cold Start Fuel Injection Quantity B Higher Than Expected","P2DD8 means path B delivered more fuel than requested while the cold-start routine ran. A cold engine burns surplus fuel poorly, so it leaves as white or blue smoke and raw hydrocarbons before the catalyst is warm, and some of it can reach the oil. No manufacturer uses P2DD8 in public documents.",["Injector of group B leaking or sticking slightly open","Pressure regulation overshooting when cold","Coolant temperature signal reads colder than real, too much start fuel","Cold-start calibration in engine control software"],["Check engine light on after a cold start","White or blue smoke and fuel smell after a cold start","Rising oil level from fuel dilution"],3,1,["P2DD7","P2DD6","P027F","P2DE1","P2DE3","P0263"],""],P2DD9:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Control Circuit Performance","P2DD9 means the drive circuit of the evaporative leak detection pump is electrically intact, yet the pump does not react the way the command implies: the feedback the engine computer reads back, usually motor current or driver state, does not match the on or off request.",["Pump motor worn or sluggish, current draw off target","Corroded connector or chafed wire adding resistance in the pump feed","Water or ice in the pump module (mounted near the wheel arch)","Faulty output stage or current sensing in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","EVAP readiness monitor stays incomplete","No noticeable change in driving"],2,1,["P2400","P2401","P2402","P2404","P2DDA","P2DDB"],"משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2DDA:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Performance/Stuck Off","P2DDA is stored when the leak detection pump fails to create the pressure change the leak test expects, as if it never started or moves too little air. GM performs this check on its electric leak check pumps (ELCP) under its own code P145C: at engine-off wake-ups between roughly 4.3 and 11 hours after shutdown the pump runs against a 0.020 in reference orifice, and if vacuum stays under 100 Pa after 60 s on the…",["Pump motor or vane inside the leak check module seized or worn out","Fresh-air filter or vent line of the module blocked by dirt or water","Switching valve in the module not moving, so the pump works against the wrong path","Hose between module and canister split or off"],["Check engine light on","Evaporative leak test never completes, readiness stays open","Possible refuelling message or locked filler flap on some hybrids"],2,1,["P2DDB","P2DD9","P24C0","P24C1","P0455","P0456"],"משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2DDB:["EVAP System Leak Detection Pump Stuck On","P2DDB reports a leak detection pump that keeps running, or keeps moving air, after the engine computer has turned it off. GM names P2DDB in its 2025 summary tables only as a blocking code for the ELCP leak test, while its own stuck-on check runs as P145D: with the pump commanded off, the switching valve is moved from vent to pump position halfway through the test, and a pressure shift above 1,000 Pa within 8 s, or…",["Internal fault of the leak check module (pump or its electronics)","Pump supply permanently live, e.g. stuck relay or shorted output stage","Control wire chafed against a powered line"],["Check engine light on","Humming from the tank area after the car is switched off","Leak test results unusable, EVAP readiness incomplete"],2,1,["P2DDA","P2DD9","P2401","P2402","P24C0","P24B9"],"משאבת זיהוי דליפת מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2DDC:["Fuel Injection Quantity C Lower Than Expected","P2DDC is the shortfall code for a third injection path, C. Engines that need it split their injection into more parts than A and B, for example by injector group or by operating mode; the split is defined by the maker, and none documents P2DDC openly.",["Injectors of group C coked or partly blocked","Low-pressure supply weak (lift pump, filter, air in fuel)","High resistance in injector wiring of group C"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power at part load","Hesitation when accelerating"],3,1,["P2DDD","P2DE0","P2DD5","P2DDE","P026C"],""],P2DDD:["Fuel Injection Quantity C Higher Than Expected","P2DDD flags excess fuel from injection path C: the quantity really burned, as estimated from airflow and lambda, sits above the request. Besides the classic leaking injector, a possible trigger after repairs is a replacement injector whose individual flow code was not programmed into the engine control, so the module calculates with the wrong flow curve.",["Injector of group C leaking or nozzle worn","Injector correction code not programmed after replacement","EGR valve not closing fully, too little fresh air"],["Check engine light on","Dark smoke under load","Higher fuel consumption"],3,1,["P2DDC","P2DE1","P2DD6","P2DDF","P026D"],""],P2DDE:["Fuel Injection Quantity D Lower Than Expected","P2DDE covers a fourth injection path, D, delivering too little fuel. The letter is assigned by the manufacturer; no one documents this code openly. CARB section 1968.2 (f)(4.2.2) sets two ways to catch it: either the shortfall is detected before emissions pass the malfunction threshold, or, where no injection fault can push emissions that high, once the control has used up its range and the commanded quantity cannot…",["Injectors of group D blocked or worn","Fuel supply weak (pump, filter, rail pressure)","Air mass or lambda signal inaccurate"],["Check engine light on","Lack of power","Occasional stumbling or misfire-like running"],3,1,["P2DDF","P2DE2","P2DD5","P2DDC","P026C","P0171"],""],P2DDF:["Fuel Injection Quantity D Higher Than Expected","P2DDF says injection path D sends more fuel than the engine control asked for. The estimate behind it depends heavily on the air side: if the airflow meter reports too little air, or the NOx or oxygen sensor shows a richer lambda than real, the module sees a surplus that the injectors never delivered, so sensors deserve a check before injectors are replaced.",["Airflow, NOx or oxygen sensor reading wrong","Injector of group D leaking or nozzle eroded","Boost or intake leak after the airflow meter"],["Check engine light on","Black smoke, particulate filter loading faster","Fuel consumption up"],3,1,["P2DDE","P2DE3","P2DD6","P2DDD","P026D","P0172"],""],P2DE0:["Cold Start Fuel Injection Quantity C Lower Than Expected","P2DE0 is the cold-start shortfall for path C. Its partner P2DE1 is used by Honda, which treats it as a rich fault of its cold-start mixture control: that check compares the ratio the PCM commands just after a cold start with what the wide-band sensor measures. By the logic of the pair, P2DE0 would be the lean side, but no public Honda or other maker document covers P2DE0 itself.",["Fuel pressure too low at start (pump, regulator, check valve)","Unmetered air entering behind the airflow meter","Injectors of group C dirty, poor spray when cold","Cold-start calibration in engine control software"],["Check engine light on after a cold start","Stalling or stumbling shortly after a cold start","Long cranking when cold"],3,1,["P2DE1","P2DDC","P2DD7","P2DE2","P027E"],""],P2DE1:["Cold Start Fuel Injection Quantity C Higher Than Expected","P2DE1 is the only code of this family with public manufacturer use. Honda names it Cold Start Air Fuel Ratio Control System Rich: during the cold-start emission strategy the PCM checks whether the mixture measured by the LAF (wide-band) sensor is richer than commanded. Bulletin 22-009 for the 2021 Accord Hybrid says the LAF sensor may misjudge the mixture as rich under certain fuel and shutdown conditions;",["PCM software (Honda bulletins 22-009, 23-100)","Injector leaking, extra fuel during cold start","Coolant temperature or airflow signal wrong","Air-fuel ratio (LAF) sensor faulty"],["Check engine light on after a cold start","Usually no noticeable driving problem","Oil level above the upper mark possible"],2,1,["P2DE0","P2DDD","P2DD8","P2DE3","P027F"],""],P2DE2:["Cold Start Fuel Injection Quantity D Lower Than Expected","P2DE2 reports that path D fell short of its fuel request during the cold-start strategy. On petrol direct-injection engines this phase is short and precise: GM's 2025 tables run catalyst heating with a split injection only while the catalyst is under 550 °C, coolant between -12 and 66 °C and the engine has run less than 20 seconds, and they check missing pulses separately under P2B95.",["Deposits on injector tips of group D","High-pressure pump slow to build pressure after start","Low-pressure supply weak when cold"],["Check engine light on after a cold start","Rough idle in the first seconds after a cold start","Often nothing noticeable once warm"],3,1,["P2DE3","P2DDE","P2DD7","P2DE0","P2B95","P027E"],""],P2DE3:["Cold Start Fuel Injection Quantity D Higher Than Expected","P2DE3 is the excess counterpart of P2DE2: during the cold-start strategy path D injected more than commanded. Nobody publishes this exact code, and the big diesel makers show why it is rare: GM's 2025 diesels judge fuel quantity in the SCR warm-up mode with the ordinary A codes P026C/P026D, keeping only rail pressure (P2C1F, more than 16 MPa below target) and injection timing (P05EC) as separate cold-start codes;",["Injector of group D dripping","Pressure regulator sticking, rail pressure too high when cold","Coolant temperature sensor reading too cold"],["Check engine light on after a cold start","White smoke and fuel smell when cold","Rising oil level over time"],3,1,["P2DE2","P2DDF","P2DD8","P2DE1","P027F","P2C1F"],""],P2DE4:["Drive Motor A Clutch Stuck Engaged","Some hybrids and electric drive units can uncouple electric drive motor A from its axle through a clutch, so the motor stops turning when its torque is not needed. P2DE4 means the clutch stays closed although the control module has asked it to open; position feedback or speeds still show a coupled motor. No manufacturer documents P2DE4 publicly.",["Disconnect clutch actuator does not move to the open position (motor, solenoid or linkage)","Clutch position switch reports engaged although the clutch has opened","Shift sleeve, pawl or teeth jammed or loaded with torque in the engaged state","Control module software or calibration error in the disconnect strategy"],["Warning lamp or hybrid/drive system message","Higher energy consumption, electric range reduced","Drive unit noise at speed, possible speed or mode limitation"],4,3,["P2DE5","P2DE6","P08ED","P08EA","P08E7"],"מצמד מנוע הנעה‏ A — תקוע במצב משולב"],P2DE5:["Drive Motor A Clutch Stuck Disengaged","P2DE5 is the reverse of P2DE4: the module commands the clutch of drive motor A to close, yet the motor stays uncoupled from the wheels. The motor may spin up without the axle following, or the position signal never reaches the engaged state. No manufacturer documents P2DE5 publicly.",["Actuator motor or solenoid fails to push the clutch into engagement","Clutch teeth blocking on each other, speed synchronisation not reached","Position switch or sensor stuck at disengaged","Worn or broken internal parts of the clutch or fork"],["Warning lamp, hybrid or all-wheel-drive fault message","No electric drive or reduced traction from the affected axle","Combustion engine starts more often, reduced recuperation"],4,3,["P2DE4","P2DE6","P08ED","P08E7"],"מצמד מנוע הנעה‏ A — תקוע במצב מנותק"],P2DE6:["Drive Motor A Clutch Actuator Performance","Whereas P2DE4 and P2DE5 describe the clutch end state, P2DE6 judges the actuator that moves the clutch of drive motor A: its circuit is intact, but it acts too slowly, draws implausible current or does not reach the commanded position within the expected time. No manufacturer documents P2DE6 publicly.",["Actuator motor or gearing worn, sluggish movement","Increased friction at fork, sleeve or pawl, e.g. from contaminated fluid","Low supply voltage or resistance in the actuator feed","Position switch or sensor reporting late or erratically"],["Warning lamp or drive system message","Delayed or jerky coupling of the electric axle","Electric drive of that axle temporarily disabled"],3,3,["P2DE4","P2DE5","P08E7","P08E8","P08E9","P08ED"],"מפעיל מצמד מנוע הנעה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DE7:["Cold Start Engine Coolant Bypass Valve C Range/Performance","California requires a fault found while the cold-start warm-up strategy runs to be stored apart from the same fault found later. P2DE7 is that cold-start counterpart of P26BB for coolant valve C. GM's 2025 ECM tables (25OBDG03B) set it when the valve's measured angle is more than 12° off its target after the target has settled, or when the valve moves slower than calibrated, during 4 of 5 seconds.",["Rotary valve sluggish from deposits or worn seals","Valve actuator motor or gearing weak","Position sensor reading drifting without a circuit fault","Engine control software needing an update"],["Check engine light on (after two trips)","Engine and cabin heater warm up more slowly","Usually no change in driveability"],2,1,["P26BB","P23C3","P2DE8","P2E81","P2DE9"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע התנעה קרה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DE8:["Cold Start Engine Coolant Bypass Valve D Stuck Open","P2DE8 is GM's cold-start variant of P26C0 for valve D, the block rotary valve that sits between two mechanical end stops and meters coolant through the engine block. In the 2025 ECM tables (25OBDG03B) a failure counts when requested and measured position differ by more than 5° while the raw feedback is above 50°, i.e. on the open side; 4 of 5 seconds give a Type B fault, MIL on the second trip.",["Block rotary valve sticking in an open position (deposits, wear)","Valve actuator unable to drive the valve to the closed side","Chafed or corroded engine harness to the valve","End-stop learn values implausible after repair or power loss"],["Check engine light on after two trips","Slow warm-up, weak cabin heating in cold weather","Possibly higher fuel consumption on short trips"],2,1,["P2E81","P26C0","P26C2","P2DE7","P2DE9"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע התנעה קרה‏ D — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2DE9:["Cold Start Engine Coolant Pump Underspeed","Engines with an electric main water pump run it at a tightly metered speed after a cold start so the block heats quickly. P2DE9 flags that during this phase the pump turns too slowly. GM's 2025 ECM tables (25OBDG03B) filter the gap between requested and reported pump speed and fail the check when it exceeds 200 rpm for 8 of 10 seconds, with low-flow coolant mode and catalyst warm-up active, the request steady within…",["Worn pump bearing or debris at the impeller slowing the rotor","Low supply voltage at the pump (battery, ground, connector)","Faulty pump electronics or speed feedback","Wrong or aged coolant, very thick when cold"],["Check engine light on after two trips","Uneven warm-up, local hot spots possible","Often no noticeable symptom"],2,1,["P2B85","P2E82","P26CE","P2C37","P2DE8"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע התנעה קרה — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2DEA:["Cylinder 1 Intake Valve Lift Range/Performance","P2DEA says the intake valves of cylinder 1 do not reach the lift the engine computer asks for, or get there too slowly. It is the first of a row of per-cylinder lift checks. CARB's rule for valve timing and lift systems demands that such systems be watched for missing the commanded position and for reacting too slowly, and explicitly lists one cylinder's lift pin failing to move as a case the failure analysis must…",["Switching element or hydraulic link of cylinder 1 sticking (sludge, wear)","Low oil level, wrong oil or restricted oil feed to the lift actuator","Cylinder 1 lift solenoid sluggish though electrically intact","Damaged cam follower, valve spring or lifter on cylinder 1"],["Check engine light on","Rough idle or shaking at low load","Misfire code for cylinder 1 at the same time"],3,3,["P2DEB","P2DF0","P2DF2","P0301","P2CDB"],"הרמת שסתום יניקת צילינדר‏ 1 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DEB:["Cylinder 2 Intake Valve Lift Range/Performance","P2DEB singles out cylinder 2: its intake valve lift misses the target or follows a command too late. Lift control for each cylinder separately is the hallmark of electro-hydraulic systems like Fiat's MultiAir, sold by Schaeffler as UniAir: per cylinder, a solenoid decides how much of the cam stroke is passed through an oil-filled chamber to the intake valves;",["Cylinder 2 solenoid in the lift actuator responding slowly or leaking internally","Aged, contaminated or wrong-grade engine oil in the hydraulic chamber","Air in the high-pressure chamber after oil starvation or service","Damaged driver stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Misfire felt at idle, cylinder 2 misfire count rising","Reduced power at higher load"],3,3,["P2DEA","P2DEC","P2DF0","P0302","P2CDC"],"הרמת שסתום יניקת צילינדר‏ 2 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DEC:["Cylinder 3 Intake Valve Lift Range/Performance","P2DEC applies only to cylinder 3: the lift its intake valves actually achieve is outside the commanded window or arrives too late. Under the CARB rule, a maker must run a failure analysis of any plausible hydraulic or mechanical defect, naming broken return springs, blocked oil passages and a single cylinder's lift pin as examples, and must catch the resulting errors before tailpipe emissions pass the threshold.",["Lock pin or switching follower of cylinder 3 not latching","Partly blocked oil passage to the cylinder 3 element","Broken return spring in the lift mechanism"],["Check engine light on","Uneven idle, often with a cylinder 3 misfire entry","Higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P2DEB","P2DED","P2DF0","P0303","P2CDD"],"הרמת שסתום יניקת צילינדר‏ 3 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DED:["Cylinder 4 Intake Valve Lift Range/Performance","P2DED is the cylinder 4 member of the per-cylinder lift checks: the engine computer finds this cylinder's lift off target or slow to follow. On four-cylinder engines with hydraulic lift control the oil comes first.",["Low, aged, diluted or wrong-viscosity oil","Clogged oil screen in the gallery feeding the lift unit","Oil filter not meeting the maker's specification","Worn cylinder 4 section of the lift actuator"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 4, rough idle","Hesitation when accelerating"],3,3,["P2DEC","P2DEE","P2DF0","P0304","P2CDE"],"הרמת שסתום יניקת צילינדר‏ 4 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DEE:["Cylinder 5 Intake Valve Lift Range/Performance","P2DEE can only occur on engines with five or more cylinders and means the intake valve lift of cylinder 5 is outside the commanded range or late. Two-step lift reached V6 engines such as the 3.6 L Pentastar, which FCA updated for 2016.",["Switching roller finger follower of cylinder 5 stuck in one mode","Oil control valve for the lift switching sticking or contaminated","Oil pressure too low to move the lock pins"],["Check engine light on","Misfire on cylinder 5","Ticking from the valvetrain on one bank"],3,3,["P2DED","P2DEF","P2DF1","P0305","P2CDF"],"הרמת שסתום יניקת צילינדר‏ 5 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DEF:["Cylinder 6 Intake Valve Lift Range/Performance","P2DEF covers cylinder 6, typically on a V6 or straight six: its intake valves do not reach the commanded lift or take too long to switch. Detection follows the same idea as for the other cylinders; for the driver the reaction matters more.",["Lift mechanism of cylinder 6 stuck in high or low lift","Restricted oil feed to the cylinder 6 element","Actuator for cylinder 6 slow despite correct wiring"],["Check engine light on","Engine speed limited or lift switching disabled (substitute mode)","Cylinder 6 misfire, rough running"],3,3,["P2DEE","P2DEA","P2DF1","P0306","P2CE0"],"הרמת שסתום יניקת צילינדר‏ 6 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DF0:["Intake Valve Lift Range/Performance Bank 1","P2DF0 means that intake valve lift on bank 1 as a whole does not follow the command, rather than one cylinder. Continuously variable systems explain why: BMW's Valvetronic turns an eccentric shaft with an electric motor controlled by the DME, moving an intermediate arm between camshaft and rocker, while Nissan's VVEL uses a DC motor to rotate a control shaft;",["Eccentric or control shaft on bank 1 stiff from wear or sludge","Lift adjusting motor of bank 1 worn or weak","Shaft position sensor reading offset or loosened","Air mass meter error or intake leak making the lift appear wrong"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power, engine may fall back to throttle control","Rough idle across several cylinders"],3,3,["P2DF1","P2DF2","P2DEA","P0026","P2646","P0101"],"הרמת שסתום יניקה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2DF1:["Intake Valve Lift Range/Performance Bank 2","P2DF1 is the bank 2 counterpart of P2DF0 and therefore only appears on V engines or boxers, on the side without cylinder 1. Nissan's VVEL, used on the VQ37VHR V6 and on V8 engines, is a good example: on the 2014 QX80 V8 both banks carry a separate VVEL ladder assembly with an actuator and a control shaft position sensor.",["Control shaft or ladder assembly on bank 2 binding","Control shaft position sensor on bank 2 moved or faulty","Lift actuator motor of bank 2 weak","Oil sludge in the bank 2 lift mechanism"],["Check engine light on","Uneven running between the banks, possible fuel trim difference","Reduced power"],3,3,["P2DF0","P2DF2","P2DEF","P0028","P2656"],"הרמת שסתום יניקה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P2DF2:["Intake Valve Lift System Range/Performance","P2DF2 points to the intake valve lift system as a whole rather than to one cylinder or bank, typical for inline engines where one actuator sets lift for every cylinder, as on four-cylinder Valvetronic engines; Toyota's Valvematic also varies lift continuously.",["Lift actuator motor or its gear worn","Engine control software needing an update (known on some models)","Eccentric or control shaft stiff from wear or sludge","Faulty air mass reading or intake leak falsifying the plausibility check"],["Check engine light on","Noticeably reduced power, engine in substitute mode","Rough idle and higher fuel consumption"],3,3,["P2DF0","P2DF1","P2DEA","P0068","P0101"],"מערכת הרמת שסתום יניקה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2DF3:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Position Not Learned","The clutch between combustion engine and electric machine in a P2 hybrid is only usable when the controller knows where its actuator begins to transmit torque. P2DF3 is a status code: that learned position is missing or invalid, often after a battery disconnect, module replacement, software update or clutch repair, before the learn routine has completed. No manufacturer documents P2DF3 publicly.",["Learn routine not yet completed after battery disconnect, repair or module replacement","Learn repeatedly aborted because enable conditions were not met","Actuator position sensor delivering implausible values during the learn","Clutch wear or actuator fault pushing the learned value out of its window"],["Warning lamp or hybrid system message","Jerky engine start or clutch engagement","Electric-only driving restricted"],2,2,["P2D8D","P287F","P28EF","P2884","P2886"],"מצב מפעיל מצמד ניתוק מנוע — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2DF4:["Coolant Pump E Control Circuit/Open","Electric coolant pumps are usually commanded through a PWM wire or a LIN bus, and pump E is the fifth such pump in a vehicle's lettering; what it cools depends on the manufacturer. P2DF4 reports an open or otherwise faulty command line to pump E. No manufacturer documents P2DF4 publicly.",["Pump connector loose, corroded or with pushed-back pin","Broken command wire in the harness","Pump electronics with failed control input","Faulty output driver in the commanding module"],["Warning lamp on","Pump runs at fixed speed or not at all","Temperature warning or power reduction of the cooled component"],2,3,["P2DF5","P2DF6","P2D26","P2DFA","U0698"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ E — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2DF5:["Coolant Pump E Control Circuit Low","P2DF5 means the command line of coolant pump E sits too low, typically shorted to ground, so the module's driver cannot pull it up to the commanded level. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. In Ford's 2024 gasoline OBD summary the matching fault type is 11 (circuit low), again flagged by the smart driver for pumps A and B, continuously above 11 V.",["Command wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Moisture or corrosion bridging the command pin to ground","Internal short in the pump's control input","Output stage of the commanding module defective"],["Warning lamp on","Pump stopped or stuck at one speed","Rising temperature of the component served by pump E"],2,3,["P2DF4","P2DF6","P2DFA","P2D26"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ E — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2DF6:["Coolant Pump E Control Circuit High","P2DF6 is set when the command line of coolant pump E stays high although the module wants it low, most often because it touches a battery-voltage wire. No manufacturer documents P2DF6 publicly. For pumps A and B, Ford's 2024 gasoline document assigns fault type 12 (circuit high), raised by the smart driver once battery voltage reaches 11 V.",["Command wire shorted to a battery-voltage wire","Internal fault in the pump electronics pulling the line high","Corrosion bridging adjacent pins in the connector","Commanding module's output stage stuck high"],["Warning lamp on","Pump audible at full speed all the time","Slower warm-up of the affected loop"],2,1,["P2DF4","P2DF5","P2DFA","P2DF7"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ E — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2DF7:["Coolant Pump E Overspeed/Air in System","When an electric pump draws air instead of liquid, its impeller loses load and the rotor races above the commanded speed. P2DF7 reports this for coolant pump E; the title already names trapped air as the usual cause. No manufacturer documents P2DF7 publicly.",["Air pocket left after coolant service or component replacement","Low coolant level from a leak in the loop","Damaged or loose impeller, rotor spins freely","Implausible speed feedback from the pump electronics"],["Warning lamp or coolant level message","Gurgling or whining from the pump area","Overheating or derating of the cooled component"],1,3,["P2DF8","P2DF9","P2DFB","P2D26","P26CE"],""],P2DF8:["Coolant Pump E Underspeed","P2DF8 means coolant pump E keeps turning, but slower than the module asked for. No manufacturer documents P2DF8 publicly. Ford's 2024 gasoline summary treats underspeed as fault type B2 of its pumps A and B, monitored continuously from 11 V over 5 seconds.",["Bearing wear or debris dragging on the rotor","Air pocket causing the pump to slow or pause for self-protection","Voltage drop in the pump feed or ground","Weak pump motor or electronics"],["Warning lamp on","Insufficient cooling or heating of the served circuit","Power reduction possible at high load"],2,3,["P2DF7","P2DF9","P2DFA","P2D26","P2B85"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ E — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2DF9:["Coolant Pump E Stuck/Stalled","P2DF9 covers the hard case: coolant pump E is powered and commanded, but its rotor does not start or comes to a standstill. Brushless pumps sense this internally, for instance from current flowing without commutation feedback, and pass the result to the commanding module. No manufacturer documents P2DF9 publicly.",["Seized bearing or impeller jammed by debris","Frozen, gelled or sludged coolant (wrong mixture)","Burnt winding or failed pump electronics","Rotor stuck after long standstill, deposits on the bearing"],["Warning lamp on","No coolant flow in the affected circuit","Overheating warning or power limitation"],2,3,["P2DF8","P2DF7","P2DFB","P2D26"],""],P2DFA:["Coolant Pump E Supply Voltage Circuit","Unlike P2DF4 to P2DF6, which concern the command line, P2DFA concerns the power feed of coolant pump E. Smart pumps measure the voltage at their own supply pin and report when it leaves the window they need to run reliably. No manufacturer documents P2DFA publicly.",["Blown fuse or relay with burnt contacts in the pump feed","Loose or corroded ground of the pump","Weak 12 V battery or charging fault","Resistance in feed wire or connector"],["Warning lamp on","Pump stops intermittently, often with other low-voltage faults","Reduced cooling of the served component"],1,3,["P2DF4","P2DF5","P2DF6","P2DF8","P2DFB"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ E — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2DFB:["Coolant Pump E Control Module Overtemperature","Electric coolant pumps carry their own driver electronics, and P2DFB reports that those of coolant pump E have run too hot. Which loop pump E serves differs between makers. No manufacturer documents P2DFB publicly, but its siblings show the pattern: Ford's 2024 gasoline summary lists over temperature as fault type 98 of its auxiliary pumps A and B, watched continuously from 11 V with a 5 second monitoring time, and…",["Coolant level too low or air trapped in the pump, so the electronics lose their cooling","Impeller or bearing running stiff, motor draws high current and heats up","Driver electronics inside pump E faulty or reporting temperature wrongly","Heat shield missing or pump too close to hot exhaust or turbo parts"],["Warning lamp or message about the cooling system","Reduced cabin heating or cooling of the component served by pump E","Pump runs at reduced speed or stops for a while, often together with air or stall codes"],2,3,["P2DF7","P2DF9","P2DFA","P2B9E","P2B64","P26D2","U0698"],"מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור‏ E — חום יתר"],P2DFC:["Hybrid/EV Battery Coolant Leak Detected","P2DFC states that the liquid loop cooling the high-voltage battery is losing coolant. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly. A GM patent explains how such a verdict is reached: a float or reed switch in the reservoir at the highest point of the loop is sampled in windows of a few seconds, only while the car stands level, the pump turns fast enough to purge air and pack temperature is in range;",["Leaking hose, clamp or quick connector in the battery coolant loop","Leak at the battery chiller, heat exchanger or cooling plates inside the pack","Cracked reservoir or leaking cap","Loop not filled or bled correctly after a repair","Level sensor reporting low although the level is correct"],["Hybrid or EV system service message and MIL","Charging blocked or drive power reduced","Coolant level in the battery reservoir visibly low, possibly traces of coolant under the car"],4,3,["P2BE0","P2BE1","P0C4A","P0E3B","P2B28"],"נוזל קירור סוללת מתח גבוה — זוהתה דליפה"],P2DFD:["EVAP System Purge Pump Performance","Some turbocharged and hybrid engines cannot count on intake vacuum to empty the charcoal canister, so an electric purge pump moves the fuel vapour into the intake. P2DFD means this pump does not achieve the expected effect, for instance the pressure or speed it should reach.",["Pump connector not fully latched (Nissan Rogue 2022)","Purge pump motor or impeller worn, pump no longer reaches its speed or pressure","Purge hose cracked, disconnected or blocked between canister, pump and intake","Condensation or ice in the intake path, needs ECM update (Hyundai hybrids)"],["MIL on, usually without noticeable change in driving","EVAP readiness not complete, emissions inspection may fail","Occasional fuel smell when the canister is not purged"],2,1,["U02BB","P0441","P0496","P0497","P0443"],"משאבת טיהור מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP) — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E00:["Gear Lever Position Sensor A Circuit","Gear lever position sensor A is the first of up to four sensors through which an electronic selector tells its control module where the lever sits. In the designs GM and Toyota document, A and B form a redundant pair that each report the full lever position; GM's patent US9249877 has each of its two sensors deliver an x and a y value.",["Loose connector or chafed wire at the selector assembly","Supply or ground of sensor A interrupted","Sensor A inside the selector assembly failed","Input stage of the evaluating module faulty"],["Warning lamp or shift-system message","Gear selection still possible through sensor B, sometimes delayed","With a second fault, the vehicle may stay in P or N"],2,3,["P2E01","P2E02","P2E03","P2E04","P0820"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E01:["Gear Lever Position Sensor A Range/Performance","Here sensor A of the gear lever delivers values that are electrically valid but not believable. Two makers document the code. Lexus lists it as a signal plausibility failure (internal code P2E00-64) on 2022–24 NX models; bulletin L-SB-0050-22 cures it, together with P2E05, by reflashing the floor shift unit with revised logic, expressly without replacing it.",["Selector logic needs a software update (Lexus NX 2022–24)","Sensor A reports an internal error","Magnet or lever mechanism shifted, so sensor A reads off the gate"],["MIL on after two trips","Shift-system message, selector still works through sensor B","Often no noticeable driving difference"],2,3,["P2E00","P2E05","P082A","P082D","P2E09"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E02:["Gear Lever Position Sensor A Circuit Low","P2E02 says the signal of gear lever position sensor A is stuck below the lowest value a healthy sensor can output. Typical reasons: the signal wire touches ground, the reference voltage is missing, or the sensor output has collapsed. No manufacturer publishes P2E02.",["Signal wire of sensor A shorted to ground","Sensor reference voltage missing or pulled down","Sensor A output failed low"],["Warning lamp and shift-system message","Lever position shown on the display jumps or is missing","If sensor B also fails, no range can be selected"],2,3,["P2E03","P2E00","P2E06","P082B","P082E"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E03:["Gear Lever Position Sensor A Circuit High","With P2E03 the module sees the signal of sensor A above the highest value the sensor can legitimately send. On a pulled-up input this happens when the signal wire is open; it also follows a short to the supply or a lost sensor ground. No manufacturer publishes P2E03.",["Signal wire of sensor A open at a connector","Signal wire shorted to supply voltage","Ground of sensor A interrupted"],["Warning lamp after two trips","Shift-system message, ranges still selectable via sensor B","Start or range change refused if both sensors are affected"],2,3,["P2E02","P2E00","P2E07","P082C","P082F"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E04:["Gear Lever Position Sensor B Circuit","Sensor B is the second, redundant gear lever position sensor; it measures the same lever travel as sensor A so that a single failure does not leave the driver without range selection. Toyota names it gear lever position sensor B in the floor shift assembly of the Lexus NX, and GM's tables call the equivalent device sensor 2, with X and Y values of its own (P089B to P08A2).",["Connector or wire of sensor B at the selector loose or damaged","Sensor B in the selector assembly failed","Separate supply branch of sensor B interrupted"],["Warning lamp or shift-system message","Selector works normally on sensor A alone","Any further sensor fault can block range changes"],2,3,["P2E05","P2E06","P2E07","P2E00","P089A"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E05:["Gear Lever Position Sensor B Range/Performance","P2E05 flags implausible data from sensor B, the backup gear lever sensor. It is one of the few codes of this family with public manufacturer use. On 2022–24 Lexus NX 250/350 and 2022 NX 350h/450h+, Toyota stores it as P2E04-64, a plausibility failure of sensor B, often alongside P2E01; bulletin L-SB-0050-22 (revised October 2023) changes the floor shift assembly logic by reflash, with 0.8 h labour and no part swap.",["Floor shift assembly logic outdated (Lexus NX bulletin L-SB-0050-22)","Sensor B signals an internal error","Sensor B or its magnet misaligned after a repair in the console"],["MIL on, usually without a driveability change","Shift-system warning may appear and disappear","Often stored together with P2E01"],2,3,["P2E01","P2E04","P089B","P08A0","P2E0D"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E06:["Gear Lever Position Sensor B Circuit Low","The signal of sensor B, the redundant gear lever sensor, has dropped under its permitted minimum. Electrically that points to a short to ground in its signal line, a dead sensor or a missing feed on its own supply branch. P2E06 is not published by any manufacturer.",["Signal line of sensor B shorted to ground","Supply branch of sensor B dead","Sensor B output stuck low"],["Warning lamp after two trips","Selector keeps working on sensor A","Range selection lost if sensor A fails as well"],2,3,["P2E07","P2E04","P2E02","P089C","P08A1"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E07:["Gear Lever Position Sensor B Circuit High","P2E07 is the high-side circuit fault of gear lever position sensor B: its signal reads above anything the sensor may legitimately produce. An interrupted signal line on an input with pull-up, a short to battery or reference voltage, or a broken sensor ground are the classic causes. No maker publishes P2E07.",["Signal line of sensor B open","Ground of sensor B broken","Signal line shorted to battery or reference voltage"],["Warning lamp and shift-system message","Normal shifting via sensor A","With P2E03 present as well, range selection may be blocked"],2,3,["P2E06","P2E04","P2E03","P089D","P08A2"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E08:["Gear Lever Position Sensor C Circuit","A third gear lever position sensor, C, only exists on selectors with more than the usual redundant pair. Toyota's patent US10180184 shows such a design: four Hall sensors in a row face a magnet in the shift lever, the voltages they produce encode the position, and if any one of them is faulty the other three still allow limp-home driving. Which job the letter C has in a given vehicle is not published;",["Connector or wiring at the selector assembly faulty","Sensor C inside the selector failed","Evaluating module input faulty"],["Warning lamp or shift-system message","Shifting continues on the remaining sensors","A further sensor fault may force neutral"],2,3,["P2E09","P2E0A","P2E0B","P2E0C","P2E00"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E09:["Gear Lever Position Sensor C Range/Performance","P2E09 means sensor C produces an electrically valid signal that contradicts the lever position given by the other sensors. No manufacturer documents this code or names the role of a sensor C, so the logic can only be inferred from the component.",["Sensor C output frozen at an intermediate value","Magnet or lever mechanism worn or displaced","Plausibility logic of the selector software too strict"],["Warning appears only after certain lever movements","Range display briefly disagrees with lever position","Limp-home with restricted selection possible"],2,3,["P2E08","P2E01","P2E05","P2E0D","P08A6"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E0A:["Gear Lever Position Sensor C Circuit Low","For P2E0A the module reads the signal of gear lever sensor C below the window a working sensor can occupy. On a voltage-output Hall sensor like those in Toyota's four-sensor selector patent (US10180184), this means a signal line pulled to ground, a missing feed or a sensor that has stopped driving its output.",["Signal wire of sensor C shorted to ground","Supply of sensor C missing","Sensor C output failed low"],["Warning lamp or shift message","Limp-home on the remaining sensors","No noticeable change while other sensors are valid"],2,3,["P2E0B","P2E08","P2E02","P2E0E","P082B"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E0B:["Gear Lever Position Sensor C Circuit High","P2E0B: sensor C of the gear lever reports more than its maximum valid signal. That is the typical picture of a broken signal wire on a pulled-up input, contact with the feed line or a lost sensor ground. No manufacturer documents P2E0B, and the function of a third lever sensor is nowhere specified publicly.",["Signal wire of sensor C open","Ground of sensor C interrupted","Signal wire shorted to supply voltage"],["Warning lamp or shift message","Selector keeps working with the other sensors","Neutral forced if another sensor also fails"],2,3,["P2E0A","P2E08","P2E03","P2E0F","P082C"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E0C:["Gear Lever Position Sensor D Circuit","Sensor D is the fourth and last letter in this family of gear lever position sensors. A layout that needs four is described in Toyota's patent US10180184: four Hall sensors lined up along the shift direction under one magnet, whose voltage pattern flips when the lever moves sideways, so both shift and select movement can be read.",["Selector connector or wiring of sensor D faulty","Sensor D failed","Module input for sensor D faulty"],["Warning lamp or shift-system message","Gear selection usually still works","Neutral fail-safe possible after a second sensor fault"],2,3,["P2E0D","P2E0E","P2E0F","P2E08","P2E04"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E0D:["Gear Lever Position Sensor D Range/Performance","With P2E0D the fourth lever sensor, D, stays within its electrical limits but its reading does not fit the lever position. No manufacturer documents P2E0D. Toyota's four-sensor patent (US10180184) gives a model for such a test: the module compares the voltage differences between the Hall sensors with a preset tolerance and declares one abnormal if it falls outside.",["Sensor D frozen at a middle value","Magnet position in the lever changed by wear or impact","Selector software tolerance needs an update"],["Code appears only after selecting a certain position","Warning lamp or shift message","Limp-home with fewer sensors"],2,3,["P2E0C","P2E09","P2E05","P2E01","P08A6"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E0E:["Gear Lever Position Sensor D Circuit Low","P2E0E is set when the output of gear lever position sensor D drops beneath its lowest plausible level, usually near 0 V or 0 % duty cycle. Likely reasons are a ground short in the D signal path, a sensor without feed or a Hall element whose output died. No maker publishes P2E0E or a meaning for sensor D.",["Signal path of sensor D shorted to ground","Sensor D without supply","Hall element of sensor D failed low"],["Shift-system warning","Selector still usable on the other sensors","Shift to neutral if another sensor fails"],2,3,["P2E0F","P2E0C","P2E0A","P2E06","P08A1"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E0F:["Gear Lever Position Sensor D Circuit High","P2E0F closes the series: sensor D, the fourth gear lever position sensor, reads above the top of its valid range. An open signal wire where the module input pulls up, contact with a voltage-carrying wire or a lost sensor ground produce this picture. No manufacturer documents P2E0F, nor the role of sensor D in a real selector.",["Signal wire of sensor D open","Ground of sensor D lost","Signal wire touching a voltage-carrying wire"],["Warning lamp or shift message","Normal shifting on the remaining sensors","Neutral fail-safe after a further fault"],2,3,["P2E0E","P2E0C","P2E0B","P2E07","P08A2"],"חיישן מצב ידית הילוכים‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E10:["Gear Selection Actuator Position Sensor Circuit","P2E10 is the general circuit code for the sensor reporting where the gear selection actuator stands, the motor-driven unit that moves the shift mechanism of an automated manual or dual-clutch gearbox to the wanted gear or gate. The control module stores it when signal or supply of that sensor are electrically faulty in a way the dedicated low, high or erratic codes do not cover.",["Corroded or loose connector, damaged harness at the actuator","Position sensor in the actuator failed (often only replaceable with the actuator)","Sensor reference voltage missing or loaded down by another fault","Input stage in the transmission control module faulty"],["Transmission warning and MIL","Gearbox holds one gear or goes to neutral (limp mode)","Shifts refused or engaging drive or reverse not possible"],3,3,["P2E11","P2E12","P2E13","P2E14","P2E15","P0904","P2831"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל בחירת הילוך — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E11:["Gear Selection Actuator Position Sensor Performance","With P2E11 the position sensor of the gear selection actuator delivers values that are electrically fine but do not fit the situation: the reading stays put although the actuator was driven, or it contradicts the gear that shaft speeds prove to be engaged. No manufacturer documents P2E11 publicly.",["Learned end positions lost or outdated, e.g. after battery disconnect or part replacement","Sensor magnet or sensor mounting shifted, reading offset","Wear or binding in the selection mechanism, actuator does not reach its target","Sensor characteristic drifted"],["Delayed or harsh shifts, gear sometimes not engaged","Transmission warning, possibly limp mode with fixed gear","Fault may clear after a relearn procedure"],3,3,["P2E10","P2E12","P2E13","P2E14","P2E16","P2832","P0905"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל בחירת הילוך — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E12:["Gear Selection Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Low","P2E12 sets when the signal of the gear selection actuator's position sensor stays below the lowest valid level. Usual reasons are a short to ground on the signal line, a missing 5 V reference or a defect inside the sensor; with many designs an interrupted signal wire also reads low. No manufacturer documents P2E12 publicly.",["Signal wire chafed through and shorted to ground","5 V reference missing or pulled down by another sensor on the same supply","Signal wire or terminal interrupted","Internal short in the position sensor"],["MIL and transmission warning immediately","Limp mode, no gear changes or only one gear","Further sensor codes if the shared 5 V supply is affected"],3,3,["P2E10","P2E11","P2E13","P2E14","P2E17","P2833","P0906"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל בחירת הילוך — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E13:["Gear Selection Actuator Position Sensor Circuit High","P2E13 is the opposite case to P2E12: the position signal of the gear selection actuator sits above its highest plausible value. A short between the signal line and a supply wire is the classic cause; an open ground or, on pull-up inputs, a broken signal wire produce the same picture. No manufacturer documents P2E13 publicly.",["Signal wire shorted to a supply or 5 V reference line","Sensor ground open or high resistance","Position sensor faulty, output stuck high","Moisture in the actuator connector bridging pins"],["MIL and transmission warning","Gearbox stays in one gear or in neutral","Shift lever input ignored"],3,3,["P2E10","P2E11","P2E12","P2E14","P2E18","P2834","P0907"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל בחירת הילוך — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E14:["Gear Selection Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2E14 covers a position signal from the gear selection actuator that is present but unsteady: it drops out for moments, jumps or carries an implausible frequency or pattern, without staying low or high long enough for P2E12 or P2E13. No manufacturer documents P2E14 publicly. Two related checks show what erratic means in practice.",["Loose or fretted terminal in the actuator connector","Harness chafing that only shorts or opens under vibration or heat","Interference from damaged shielding or nearby motor wiring","Sensor with an internal intermittent fault"],["Occasional refused or delayed shifts","Short drops to neutral while driving","Warning lamp that comes and goes"],3,3,["P2E10","P2E11","P2E12","P2E13","P2E19","P2835","P0908"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל בחירת הילוך — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2E15:["Intermediate Shaft Selection Actuator Position Sensor Circuit","P2E15 is the basic circuit code for the position sensor of a second selection actuator, one assigned to the intermediate shaft (layshaft) of the gearbox rather than to the main gear selection, which has P2E10 to P2E14. Which gearboxes use such an actuator, and what exactly it engages there, no manufacturer documents publicly for this code.",["Connector or harness to the intermediate shaft actuator damaged or corroded","Position sensor of the actuator failed","Sensor supply or ground missing","Faulty input stage in the transmission control module"],["Transmission warning and MIL","Some gears unavailable or gearbox in limp mode","Vehicle may only drive in a restricted range of gears"],3,3,["P2E16","P2E17","P2E18","P2E19","P2E10","P0910"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל בחירת ציר ביניים — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E16:["Intermediate Shaft Selection Actuator Position Sensor Range/Performance","P2E16 flags a position reading from the intermediate shaft selection actuator that is electrically valid but not credible, for example a travel that does not match the commanded movement or the learned end stops. No manufacturer documents P2E16 publicly.",["End stops not learned or lost after battery disconnect or repair","Actuator or selection linkage binding, target position not reached","Sensor or its magnet shifted, reading offset","Control software needs an update"],["Harsh, slow or failed shifts involving the intermediate shaft","Transmission warning, possibly limp mode","Fault returns until a relearn has been done"],3,3,["P2E15","P2E17","P2E18","P2E19","P2E11","P2832"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל בחירת ציר ביניים — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E17:["Intermediate Shaft Selection Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Low","P2E17 tells you the position signal of the intermediate shaft selection actuator is stuck at the bottom of its range or below it. On the bench this usually turns out to be a signal line touching ground, a dead reference supply, or a sensor whose output stage has failed. No manufacturer documents P2E17 publicly.",["Signal line shorted to ground","Sensor reference voltage missing","Output stage of the position sensor failed","Signal wire interrupted (on sensors that then read low)"],["MIL and transmission warning","Limp mode with limited gears","Code returns at once after clearing"],3,3,["P2E15","P2E16","P2E18","P2E19","P2E12"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל בחירת ציר ביניים — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E18:["Intermediate Shaft Selection Actuator Position Sensor Circuit High","Here the position sensor of the intermediate shaft selection actuator reports a value above its upper limit. Most often the signal line has contact with battery voltage or the 5 V feed, or the sensor has lost its ground so the output floats upward. No manufacturer documents P2E18 publicly.",["Signal line shorted to battery voltage or the 5 V feed","Sensor ground open or corroded","Position sensor output stuck high","Faulty input stage in the transmission control module"],["MIL and transmission warning","Certain gears blocked, limp mode","Poor acceleration because the gearbox holds an unsuitable gear"],3,3,["P2E15","P2E16","P2E17","P2E19","P2E13"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל בחירת ציר ביניים — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E19:["Intermediate Shaft Selection Actuator Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2E19 is stored when the intermediate shaft selection actuator's position sensor delivers a signal that flickers, drops out briefly or changes faster than the mechanism could physically move. Because the fault comes and goes, the code often shows as pending or with only a few occurrences. No manufacturer documents P2E19 publicly.",["Loose or corroded terminal at the actuator or gearbox connector","Harness rubbing on the housing, contact only under vibration","Electrical noise from damaged shielding","Sensor with an internal intermittent fault"],["Sporadic shift faults that disappear again","Warning lamp only now and then","Short limp-mode episodes"],3,3,["P2E15","P2E16","P2E17","P2E18","P2E14"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל בחירת ציר ביניים — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2E1A:["Drive Motor A Inverter Voltage Sensor A/B Correlation","P2E1A sets when the two DC voltage readings inside the drive motor A inverter, sensor A and sensor B, stop agreeing although they should describe the same high-voltage potential. Each value may pass its own range test; the fault lies in the mismatch. No manufacturer documents P2E1A publicly.",["One of the two voltage measuring channels in the inverter has drifted","Fault in the inverter or power drive unit electronics","Poor high-voltage connection between the two measuring points","Control software with an unsuitable comparison window"],["Hybrid system or drive warning lamp, MIL possible","Reduced or no electric drive power","Further inverter voltage codes stored at the same time"],4,3,["P0D2E","P0E8D","P0D2D","P0E8C","P0DA8"],"חיישן מתח אינוורטר מנוע הנעה‏ A A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2E1B:["Drive Motor A Phase X Current Sensor Circuit","P2E1B reports an electrical fault in the circuit of the phase X current sensor of drive motor A, without a separate low or high verdict. X, Y and Z name a second three-phase winding group: a Mitsubishi Electric patent on two-group motors for hybrid drives couples one current sensor to the conductor of each of the six phases. No manufacturer documents P2E1B publicly.",["Phase X current sensor in the inverter failed","Reference supply or ground of the current sensors faulty","Loose or corroded low-voltage connector at the inverter","Defect on the motor control board that evaluates the sensor"],["Hybrid system warning lamp and MIL","Reduced electric drive or no electric drive","Rough or noisy motor operation under load"],4,3,["P2E1C","P2E1D","P2E1E","P2E1F","P2E23","P2C69","P0BE5"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A X — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E1C:["Drive Motor A Phase X Current Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2E1C means the phase X current sensor of drive motor A delivers a value that is electrically valid but implausible. No manufacturer documents P2E1C publicly; GM's U/V/W counterparts show the usual test, a zero check.",["Zero offset of the phase X sensor has drifted","Sensor gain error after ageing or overheating","Unstable reference voltage for the current sensors","Fault in the measuring stage of the inverter control board"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Electric drive limited, uneven torque at low speed","Code returns after clearing at the next start"],4,3,["P2E1B","P2E1D","P2E1E","P2E20","P2E24","P2E27","P0BE6"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A X — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E1D:["Drive Motor A Phase X Current Sensor Circuit Low","P2E1D says the phase X current sensor signal of drive motor A lies below its lowest valid value. Phase current flows in both directions, so the sensor reports a signed quantity; low therefore means a reading more negative than any real current, not a weak current. That other case, too little current in an energised phase, is P2C6A. No manufacturer documents P2E1D publicly.",["Sensor signal shorted to ground inside the inverter","Supply voltage of the phase X sensor missing","Phase X current sensor failed"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Sharp loss of electric drive power","Vehicle may only drive in a reduced mode"],4,3,["P2E1B","P2E1C","P2E1E","P2E21","P2E25","P2C6A","P0BE7"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A X — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E1E:["Drive Motor A Phase X Current Sensor Circuit High","P2E1E flags a phase X current sensor signal of drive motor A above the top of its valid range. No manufacturer documents P2E1E publicly. GM's U-phase counterpart on the 2016 Volt trips above 700 A for 0.05 s within 0.1 s, Type A. The same table stops real overcurrent at 600 A through P0C01, and Ford's 2019 hybrids treat more than 600 A for 400 microseconds as motor overcurrent.",["Sensor signal shorted to the sensor supply","Open ground of the phase X current sensor","Phase X current sensor failed high"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Electric drive cut off or strongly limited","Possible jolt when the inverter shuts down"],4,3,["P2E1B","P2E1C","P2E1D","P2E22","P2E26","P2C6B","P0BE8"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A X — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E1F:["Drive Motor A Phase Y Current Sensor Circuit","P2E1F stands for a circuit fault of the phase Y current sensor of drive motor A that is not sorted into a low or high case. No manufacturer documents P2E1F publicly, and even the U/V/W equivalents of this general code see little use: GM's 2013 to 2019 hybrid tables cover the phase sensors with offset, low, high and sum checks only, while Ford's 2019 hybrid summary says that current sensor faults of its motor…",["Phase Y current sensor in the inverter failed","Poor contact at the inverter's low-voltage connector","Sensor supply or ground interrupted"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Electric drive limited or switched off","Other phase current codes may be stored as well"],4,3,["P2E20","P2E21","P2E22","P2E1B","P2E23","P2C6C","P0BE9"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Y — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E20:["Drive Motor A Phase Y Current Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2E20 is set when the phase Y current sensor of drive motor A reads within its electrical limits but not believably. No manufacturer documents P2E20 publicly. Besides the zero check, a current balance can expose a sensor with a wrong gain. GM's eAssist table checks whether motor DC current and the input current of the accessory power module match the battery pack current;",["Gain error of the phase Y sensor","Zero offset of the phase Y sensor shifted","Disturbed reference voltage of the current sensors","Motor control software needing an update"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Less electric assist, torque not as requested","Motor whine or slight vibration"],4,3,["P2E1F","P2E21","P2E22","P2E1C","P2E24","P2E27","P0BEA"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Y — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E21:["Drive Motor A Phase Y Current Sensor Circuit Low","P2E21 records that the phase Y current sensor of drive motor A reports a value under the bottom of its scale. No manufacturer documents P2E21 publicly. GM's eAssist logic shows a clean way to test for this: the low and high checks of its U and W sensors run while PWM output is disabled, so the inverter is not switching and no phase current can flow.",["Phase Y sensor signal shorted to ground","Sensor supply voltage missing","Phase Y current sensor failed"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Electric drive limited","Engine runs more often than usual on hybrids"],4,3,["P2E1F","P2E20","P2E22","P2E1D","P2E25","P2C6D","P0BEB"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Y — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E22:["Drive Motor A Phase Y Current Sensor Circuit High","P2E22 is stored when the phase Y current sensor signal of drive motor A sticks above its upper limit. No manufacturer documents P2E22 publicly. On GM's 2016 Cadillac ELR the U/V/W counterparts fail above 800 A, judged as 4 bad samples out of 6 at 10.4 ms intervals, Type A.",["Phase Y signal shorted to the sensor supply","Open ground of the phase Y sensor","Shared sensor reference faulty, other phases affected too"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Electric drive switched off or strongly limited","High codes of other phases stored at the same time"],4,3,["P2E1F","P2E20","P2E21","P2E1E","P2E26","P2C6E","P0BEC"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Y — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E23:["Drive Motor A Phase Z Current Sensor Circuit","P2E23 points to a wiring or circuit defect around the phase Z current sensor of drive motor A that is not classed as low or high. Whether a Z sensor exists at all depends on the design. A Hyundai patent on hybrid motor drives notes that an inverter may carry three sensors or only two, since the three currents of a star winding cancel out and the controller can compute the missing one.",["Loose or corroded low-voltage connector at the inverter","Phase Z current sensor in the inverter failed","Supply or ground of the Z sensor interrupted"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Electric drive limited or switched off","Fault may come and go with vibration or temperature"],4,3,["P2E24","P2E25","P2E26","P2E1B","P2E1F","P2C6F","P0BED"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Z — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E24:["Drive Motor A Phase Z Current Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2E24 concerns a phase Z current reading of drive motor A that passes the electrical checks yet fails a plausibility test. No manufacturer documents P2E24 publicly. Z completes the second winding group of a two-group motor; in the Mitsubishi Electric patent X, Y and Z are star-connected and controlled separately from U, V and W, so a biased Z sensor upsets only its own group.",["Zero offset of the phase Z sensor drifted","Gain error of the phase Z sensor","Faulty measuring stage on the inverter control board"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Electric drive limited","Uneven torque or motor noise"],4,3,["P2E23","P2E25","P2E26","P2E1C","P2E20","P2E27","P0BEE"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Z — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E25:["Drive Motor A Phase Z Current Sensor Circuit Low","P2E25 means the phase Z current sensor of drive motor A reports below its valid minimum. No manufacturer documents P2E25 publicly. A zero reading is not the same thing: if phase Z carries no current because a lead is open, the sensor correctly reads about zero and the open phase is judged by P2C70. Low here means beyond the negative end of the scale;",["Phase Z sensor signal shorted to ground","Shared sensor reference or ground faulty","Phase Z current sensor failed"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Reduced electric drive","Low codes of other phases possibly stored too"],4,3,["P2E23","P2E24","P2E26","P2E1D","P2E21","P2C70","P0BEF"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Z — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E26:["Drive Motor A Phase Z Current Sensor Circuit High","P2E26 reports a phase Z current sensor signal of drive motor A that sits above its permitted range. No manufacturer documents P2E26 publicly. The consequence goes beyond one lost reading: in GM's eAssist table the overcurrent check P0C01 and the missing-phase check P0C05 only run while no current sensor code is active, and current control falls back to a mode that ignores the sensors.",["Phase Z signal shorted to the sensor supply","Open ground of the phase Z sensor","Phase Z current sensor failed high"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Electric drive torque clearly reduced","Vehicle continues only in a reduced-power mode"],4,3,["P2E23","P2E24","P2E25","P2E1E","P2E22","P2C71","P0BF0"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A Z — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E27:["Drive Motor A Phase X-Y-Z Current Sensor Correlation","P2E27 compares the three current sensors of phases X, Y and Z of drive motor A with each other. Mitsubishi Electric's patent joins the X, Y and Z windings in a star, so their currents must add up to almost zero at every instant; a clear residual means at least one sensor is wrong, even if every reading passes its own checks. No manufacturer documents P2E27 publicly.",["One of the three X/Y/Z sensors drifted in offset or gain","Disturbed common reference of the current sensors","Leakage current from the X/Y/Z winding group to the housing","Motor control software calibration"],["Hybrid warning lamp and MIL","Electric drive limited or temporarily switched off","No single sensor code stored alongside"],4,3,["P0BFD","P2E1C","P2E20","P2E24","P2DCB"],"חיישן זרם פאזת מנוע הנעה‏ A X-Y-Z — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2E28:["Drive Motor A Excitation Current Sensor Performance","P2E28 concerns a drive motor with an electrically excited rotor, the type Nissan uses in the Ariya and BMW in its fifth-generation eDrive. Such a rotor carries a field coil that receives direct current through brushes and slip rings; a sensor measures that current for the closed field-control loop.",["Excitation current sensor drifted (offset or gain no longer correct)","Faulty excitation power stage, so actual and expected current differ","Worn brushes or dirty slip rings changing the field circuit resistance","Inverter or motor control software fault"],["Electric drive warning or service message","Noticeably reduced drive power","Vehicle may refuse to drive or stop driving"],4,3,["P2E7B","P2E29","P2E2A","P2E2B","P0A78"],"חיישן זרם עירור מנוע הנעה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E29:["Drive Motor A Excitation Current Sensor Circuit Low Voltage","P2E29 reports that the signal voltage of the excitation current sensor of drive motor A has dropped below the band the controller accepts. The sensor sits in the excitation stage that feeds direct current to the rotor field coil of an electrically excited motor; TI names shunts with isolated amplifiers or isolated Hall-effect sensors for this job.",["Sensor signal line shorted to ground","Sensor supply or reference voltage missing","Excitation current sensor or its isolated amplifier failed"],["Electric drive warning lamp on","Loss of drive power from motor A","Vehicle may not become ready to drive"],4,3,["P2E7B","P2E28","P2E2A","P2E2B"],"חיישן זרם עירור מנוע הנעה‏ A — מתח נמוך במעגל"],P2E2A:["Drive Motor A Excitation Current Sensor Circuit High Voltage","P2E2A is the counterpart to P2E29: the signal from the sensor that measures the rotor field current of drive motor A sits above the highest voltage a working sensor can deliver. Typical reasons are a signal line touching a supply rail, an open ground or reference connection that lets the input float up, or a failed sensor output stage.",["Sensor signal line shorted to a supply voltage","Open sensor ground or reference connection","Failed sensor output stage"],["Electric drive warning lamp on","Reduced or no drive power","Fault returns immediately after clearing"],4,3,["P2E7B","P2E28","P2E29","P2E2B"],"חיישן זרם עירור מנוע הנעה‏ A — מתח גבוה במעגל"],P2E2B:["Drive Motor A Excitation Current Too High","P2E2B does not blame the sensor: the measured field current of drive motor A itself exceeds what the controller allows. In TI's example of an excitation stage, two switches and two diodes sit between the high-voltage rails; with both switches on, the rotor coil sees the entire DC-link voltage, and switches of this kind are rarely sized above about 50 A.",["Excitation power switch shorted or stuck on","Field current control or gate driver fault in the inverter","Shorted turns in the rotor field winding"],["Electric drive warning lamp on","Sudden loss of drive power from motor A","Vehicle may not restart the drive system"],4,3,["P2E28","P2E29","P2E2A","P2E7B","P0A78"],"זרם עירור מנוע הנעה‏ A — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2E2C:["Battery Charger A Module Supply Voltage Performance","P2E2C covers the low-voltage supply that powers the control electronics of on-board charger A, not the AC input. The code means this supply voltage is present but behaves implausibly, for example it fluctuates or disagrees with what other modules see on the same 12 V network.",["Loose or corroded supply or ground connection at the charger","Ground offset between charger and other modules","Unstable 12 V supply from weak battery or DC/DC converter","Faulty voltage measurement inside the charger module"],["Plug-in charging does not start or stops early","Charging system warning message","Fault comes and goes with electrical load or vibration"],2,0,["P2E2D","P2E2E","P2E2F","P0D67","P0D27"],"מתח אספקה מודול מטען סוללה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E2D:["Battery Charger A Module Supply Voltage Low","P2E2D is set when the 12 V feed of the control board in on-board charger A stays below its lower limit. The usual suspects sit outside the charger: a discharged or failing 12 V battery, a DC/DC converter that is not keeping the network up, a blown fuse in the feed, or resistance in supply or ground wiring that eats voltage under load.",["Discharged or aged 12 V battery","Blown fuse or failed relay in the charger supply","High resistance in supply or ground wiring","DC/DC converter not maintaining the 12 V network"],["Plug-in charging refused or interrupted","Further low-voltage faults in other modules","Charging status display behaves erratically"],2,0,["P2E2C","P2E2E","P2E30","P0D67","P0562"],"אספקת מודול מטען סוללה‏ A — מתח נמוך"],P2E2E:["Battery Charger A Module Supply Voltage High","P2E2E reports the opposite of P2E2D: the low-voltage feed of on-board charger A rises above its upper limit. On a plug-in vehicle the 12 V network is held by the DC/DC converter, so a converter regulating too high is the first suspect; an external charger or jump-start device at excessive voltage can do the same, and a faulty measurement inside the charger can fake the reading.",["DC/DC converter regulating the 12 V network too high","External battery charger or jump starter with excessive voltage","Faulty voltage measurement inside the charger module"],["Plug-in charging stops or will not start","Overvoltage faults stored in other modules as well","Lamps unusually bright or 12 V battery overcharged"],2,0,["P2E2C","P2E2D","P2E31","P0D67","P0563"],"אספקת מודול מטען סוללה‏ A — מתח גבוה"],P2E2F:["Battery Charger B Module Supply Voltage Performance","P2E2F concerns the 12 V feed of the control electronics in a second on-board charger, charger B, not its grid input. The voltage is within limits but behaves implausibly, for example it jumps around or disagrees with the system voltage that other modules report. No manufacturer documents P2E2F publicly.",["Loose or corroded supply or ground terminal at charger B","Ground offset between charger B and the reference module","Fluctuating 12 V network from weak battery or DC/DC converter","Faulty supply voltage measurement inside charger B"],["Plug-in charging starts late, pauses or stops","Fault appears with electrical load changes or vibration","Charging system warning in the instrument cluster"],2,0,["P2E30","P2E31","P2E2C","P2D77","P2E91"],"מתח אספקה מודול מטען סוללה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E30:["Battery Charger B Module Supply Voltage Low","P2E30 is stored when the 12 V feed reaching the control board of charger B stays under its lower limit. Most causes lie upstream: a flat or aged 12 V battery, a blown fuse or failed relay in the charger feed, or corroded supply and ground contacts that lose voltage under load. No manufacturer documents P2E30 publicly, and no threshold is published.",["Discharged or aged 12 V battery","Blown fuse or failed relay in the charger B feed","Voltage drop across corroded supply or ground contacts","DC/DC converter not holding up the 12 V network"],["Charging through charger B does not start","Low-voltage or communication faults in other modules too","Reduced charging power if only one charger works"],2,0,["P2E2F","P2E31","P2E2D","P0562","P2E91"],"אספקת מודול מטען סוללה‏ B — מתח נמוך"],P2E31:["Battery Charger B Module Supply Voltage High","P2E31 is the high-side counterpart of P2E30: the low-voltage feed of charger B climbs above what its control electronics accept. On plug-in cars the DC/DC converter holds the 12 V network, so a converter regulating too high is the main suspect; a workshop charger or jump pack set too high, or a faulty measurement inside charger B, can give the same reading. No manufacturer documents P2E31 or a threshold publicly.",["DC/DC converter regulating the 12 V network too high","Workshop charger or jump starter with excessive voltage","Faulty supply voltage measurement inside charger B"],["Charging via charger B stops or will not start","Overvoltage codes stored in several modules","12 V battery gassing or lamps unusually bright"],2,0,["P2E2F","P2E30","P2E2E","P0563"],"אספקת מודול מטען סוללה‏ B — מתח גבוה"],P2E32:["Battery Charger A Module Forced Shutdown Voltage Performance","P2E32 belongs to the forced shutdown input of on-board charger A, a hardwired signal with which another module can switch the charger off regardless of bus messages. The code means this signal does not behave as expected although its level is in range, for instance the charger keeps converting power after a shutdown request, or the line reports shutdown while none was commanded.",["Contact resistance or partly corroded terminal in the shutdown line","Shutdown input stage inside charger A not responding correctly","Fault or software issue in the module driving the shutdown signal"],["Plug-in charging refused or ended unexpectedly","Charging system warning message"],3,0,["P2E33","P2E34","P2E3E","P2E2C"],""],P2E33:["Battery Charger A Module Forced Shutdown Voltage Low","P2E33 reports that the voltage on the forced shutdown line of charger A sits below its valid band. What that means in practice depends on the logic, which no manufacturer publishes for this code. Shutdown lines are often built fail-safe, as in Watt & Well's EVCC charging controller, where a missing loop current counts as an emergency stop.",["Shutdown line chafed through and shorted to ground","Broken wire or backed-out pin in the shutdown circuit","Moisture or corrosion in the charger signal connector","Output stage of the commanding module stuck low"],["Charger A never starts charging","Charging aborts when the car or harness is moved","Charging system warning message"],3,0,["P2E32","P2E34","P2E3F","P2E2D"],""],P2E34:["Battery Charger A Module Forced Shutdown Voltage High","P2E34 is set when the forced shutdown line of charger A reads above its permitted voltage. The usual cause is contact with a battery-fed or switched 12 V wire in the same harness, or an internal leak inside the charger or the commanding module. No manufacturer documents P2E34 publicly.",["Shutdown line shorted to a 12 V feed in the harness","Internal leakage in charger A or the commanding module","Incorrect wiring after a previous harness repair"],["Charger A disabled, plug-in charging not possible or slower","Charging system warning message"],3,0,["P2E32","P2E33","P2E40","P2E2E"],""],P2E35:["Battery Charger B Enable Circuit/Open","P2E35 covers the enable line of charger B, the hardwired 12 V signal that wakes the charger or allows it to work, and reports a general circuit fault, usually an open. No manufacturer documents P2E35 publicly.",["Broken enable wire or backed-out terminal","Signal connector at charger B not fully latched","Failed enable driver in the commanding module"],["Charger B does not wake when the cable is plugged in","Charging slower than usual or not at all","Charging system warning message"],3,0,["P2E36","P2E37","P2E38","P0E61"],"אפשור מטען סוללה‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2E36:["Battery Charger B Enable Circuit Low","P2E36 means the enable signal to charger B is pulled under the level its commanded state allows, most often by a short to ground or by a driver stage that cannot pull the line up. No manufacturer documents P2E36 publicly. On the common active-high layout, which Holley's 30-8405 charger unit uses with a 12 V wake-up input drawing about 20 mA, a grounded line simply means the charger never receives its wake request.",["Enable wire chafed and shorted to ground","Water or corrosion in the charger B signal connector","Damaged high-side driver in the commanding module"],["Charger B stays off whenever charging is requested","Lower charging power or no charging"],3,0,["P2E35","P2E37","P2E38","P0E62"],"אפשור מטען סוללה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E37:["Battery Charger B Enable Circuit High","P2E37 is stored when the enable line of charger B carries more voltage than its commanded state allows, typically because it touches a powered wire or the driver in the commanding module is stuck on. No manufacturer documents P2E37 publicly. The effect differs from P2E36: on an active-high wake line the charger is told to stay awake although no charging is planned.",["Enable wire shorted to a 12 V feed","Enable driver in the commanding module stuck on","Internal leakage in the charger B input circuit"],["12 V battery discharged after standing","Charger B fan or pump runs with nothing plugged in","Charging via charger B disabled"],3,0,["P2E35","P2E36","P2E38","P0E63"],"אפשור מטען סוללה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E38:["Battery Charger B Enable Circuit Range/Performance","P2E38 flags an enable circuit of charger B that is electrically sound, while the charger or its partner modules do not react to it as expected. No manufacturer documents P2E38 publicly. Ford shows the A-side logic for P0E64 in its 2019 plug-in hybrid OBD summary: once the charger is ready and the wake-up line Chrg_Wkup is high, the battery energy control module must report ready;",["Software mismatch between charger B and battery control module","Battery control module not waking or starting too slowly","Enable level marginal due to contact resistance"],["Charging begins only after a long delay or not at all","Fault appears only on some charging sessions"],4,0,["P2E35","P2E36","P2E37","P0E64","P2E3A"],"אפשור מטען סוללה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E39:["Battery Charger B Fuse","P2E39 concerns the high-voltage fuse in the branch between the traction battery and charger B. Battery management units usually judge such fuses by comparing the voltage behind the fuse with the pack voltage; Volvo's technical journal TJ 37376 on BECM codes P0A9500 and P0E2F00 has technicians read exactly those values at the fuse outputs. No manufacturer documents P2E39 publicly.",["Fuse opened by an internal short in charger B","Spurious entry from battery management software","Faulty voltage sensing behind the fuse"],["Charging through charger B no longer possible","Electrical system or high-voltage warning"],4,0,["P0E2E","P0A95","P0E2F","P2E3D"],"נתיך מטען סוללה‏ B"],P2E3A:["Battery Charger B Output Voltage Performance","P2E3A says the high-voltage output of charger B does not follow its target, typically in the constant-voltage phase near the end of a charge, without being clearly too low. No manufacturer documents P2E3A publicly. The A-side code P0D20 shows two readings of the same check. GM's 2011 Volt sets it in constant-voltage mode once the output deviates by 15 % or more, 30 times in 50 samples at 100 ms, One Trip Type A.",["Degraded power stage or regulation inside charger B","Drifting output voltage measurement","Charger or battery module software needing an update"],["Battery does not reach full charge","Charging stops early or takes longer","Charging system warning message"],4,0,["P2E3B","P2E3C","P0D20","P0D85"],"מתח יציאת מטען סוללה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E3B:["Battery Charger B Output Voltage Too Low","P2E3B is set when the high-voltage output of charger B stays below what the control unit expects while charging. No manufacturer documents P2E3B publicly. For the A-side code P0D21, GM's 2016 tables for the Cadillac ELR use a fixed floor: in constant-current as well as constant-voltage mode the charger bus must not drop under 150 V, and 8 failures in 10 samples set the code as Type B.",["Charger module software fault fixed by reprogramming","Failed power stage inside charger B","High resistance in the HV output connection"],["MIL on and vehicle will not charge","Level 2 charging fails, wall box breaker may trip"],4,0,["P2E3A","P2E3D","P0D21","P0E86"],"מתח יציאת מטען סוללה‏ B — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2E3C:["Battery Charger B Output Current Performance","P2E3C means charger B does not deliver the high-voltage current it has been asked for. No manufacturer documents P2E3C publicly. Its A-side model P0D22 is well covered: the 2011 Volt compares actual and desired current in constant-current mode against a table and sets the code after 150 bad samples in 300, One Trip Type A.",["Control software or calibration of charger or hybrid module","Weak power stage inside charger B","Inaccurate output current measurement"],["MIL after or during charging","Charging takes noticeably longer or aborts","Problem more frequent in cold weather"],4,0,["P2E3A","P2E3B","P2E3D","P0D22"],"זרם יציאת מטען סוללה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E3D:["Battery Charger B Output Shorted","P2E3D points to a short on the high-voltage output side of charger B. No manufacturer documents P2E3D publicly. GM's test for the A-side code P0D23 shows how such a short is found: while the charger contactor is only precharging and the multi-purpose contactor is open, hardly any current should flow, so more than 0.35 A on the charger bus in 4 of 5 samples at 100 ms sets the code as One Trip Type A, both in the 2011…",["Internal short in the charger B output stage","Damaged high-voltage cable between charger B and battery","Leaking or stuck contactor path in the charging circuit"],["Charging blocked as soon as the cable is plugged in","High-voltage or charging system warning"],4,0,["P2E3C","P2E3B","P2E39","P0D23"],"יציאת מטען סוללה‏ B — קצר"],P2E3E:["Battery Charger B Module Forced Shutdown Voltage Performance","P2E3E is the charger B version of P2E32: the forced shutdown signal of the second charger is electrically in range but its behaviour is implausible. Examples are a shutdown request that the charger ignores, or a level that changes state without a matching command, so the control unit can no longer trust its hardwired off-switch for path B. No manufacturer documents P2E3E or the underlying circuit publicly.",["Shutdown input stage inside charger B not responding correctly","Intermittent contact in the charger B shutdown line","Software issue in the module issuing the shutdown"],["Charging slower than usual because charger B is locked out","Charging system warning message"],3,0,["P2E3F","P2E40","P2E32","P2E2F"],""],P2E3F:["Battery Charger B Module Forced Shutdown Voltage Low","P2E3F reports a forced shutdown signal at charger B that stays below its permitted voltage. No manufacturer documents P2E3F or the shutdown logic behind it publicly. If the line is fail-safe, as at the EVCC controller from Watt & Well, where zero loop current or an unconnected input triggers the stop, then a ground short or a break looks like a standing shutdown command and charger B stays switched off for good.",["Shutdown line of charger B shorted to ground","Broken wire or loose pin in the signal plug","Output stage of the commanding module stuck low"],["Charger B never takes part in charging","Reduced charging power or no charging"],3,0,["P2E3E","P2E40","P2E33","P2E30"],""],P2E40:["Battery Charger B Module Forced Shutdown Voltage High","P2E40 means the forced shutdown signal of charger B reads above its valid band, typically from a short to a 12 V wire or a leak inside the charger or the module that drives it. No manufacturer documents P2E40 publicly.",["Shutdown line of charger B shorted to a 12 V wire","Internal leakage in charger B or the commanding module","Miswiring after a harness or charger repair"],["Charging slower or impossible with charger B locked out","Charging system warning message"],3,0,["P2E3E","P2E3F","P2E34","P2E31"],""],P2E41:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump B Control Circuit/Open","P2E41 flags an electrical fault on the line over which the controller commands electronics coolant pump B, the second pump serving inverter, DC/DC converter and frequently the charger; the maker decides which pump is B. No manufacturer publicly documents P2E41.",["Broken or disconnected control wire between module and pump B","Corroded or pushed-back pins at the pump connector","Pump B electronics no longer load the command line","Faulty output stage in the controlling module"],["Hybrid or electric drive warning and MIL","Pump B does not run, electronics loop warms up faster","Reduced drive power or interrupted charging under high load"],2,3,["P2E43","P2E44","P2E45","P2E42","P0CE9"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2E42:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump B Performance","P2E42 is the functional verdict on electronics coolant pump B: the circuits test fine, yet the controller concludes the pump is not doing its job. Two ways of reaching that verdict are documented for pump A. For the 2016 Cadillac ELR, GM checks the result, setting P0CEA when power electronics coolant and charger temperatures drift too far apart after the pump has been enabled for more than 300 s.",["Air pocket after service or slow coolant loss","Worn pump B delivering too little flow","Debris, kinked hose or clogged cold plate in the loop","Control software needing an update"],["MIL and hybrid system warning","Higher inverter or charger temperatures than usual","Power reduction or slower charging in hot conditions"],3,3,["P2E47","P2E48","P2E49","P0CEA","P0C74"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E43:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump B Control Circuit Low","P2E43 means the command signal of electronics coolant pump B sits too low, typically because the line has contact with ground or the output stage cannot drive it up. On PWM-controlled pumps this usually stops the pump outright. Pierburg's CWA pumps, a widespread design, read a duty cycle of 0 to 1 % as stop and pull their PWM input to ground through 10 kΩ, so a grounded line leaves the rotor standing.",["Control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the pump connector","Shorted input stage inside pump B","Output stage of the module stuck low"],["Pump B stops, electronics coolant heats up","MIL with hybrid or drive system message","Limited power or charging rate under load"],2,3,["P2E44","P2E41","P2E45","P0CEB"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2E44:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump B Control Circuit High","P2E44 is the opposite fault: the command line of electronics coolant pump B reads higher than its commanded state allows, mostly because it touches a battery-fed wire or the driver can no longer pull it down. Many PWM pumps react to a permanently high input with an emergency mode; Pierburg's interface runs the pump at about 95 % speed for a duty cycle of 98 to 100 %.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-voltage circuit","Module output stage unable to pull the line low","Moisture linking supply and signal pins in the connector"],["MIL with hybrid system message","Pump B runs continuously at high speed, audible hum","Pump does not respond to commanded speed changes"],2,1,["P2E43","P2E41","P2E45","P0CEC"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2E45:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump B Enable Circuit","Some designs switch electronics coolant pump B on through a separate enable line or a relay, independent of the speed command; P2E45 reports a fault in that path. GM's 2018 hybrid tables show the scheme for pump A: with the enable output active, more than 0.6 A on the line counts as a short to ground (P1F44);",["Enable wire open or shorted between module and pump","Pump relay or its fuse failed, where the design uses one","Faulty enable output in the controlling module"],["Pump B never starts although commanded","MIL and hybrid or charging warning","Power or charging limited as electronics heat up"],2,3,["P2E41","P2E43","P2E44","P0CED"],"אפשור משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E46:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump B Overspeed - Dry Run","P2E46 is the dry-run report of electronics coolant pump B: faster than commanded at lower current, the signature of air at the impeller. Porsche describes such self-monitoring on the traction-battery pump of the 2018 Panamera plug-in hybrid (code P0C4A00 there).",["Low coolant level from a leaking hose, joint or component","Air left in the loop after service without vacuum fill","Pump B damaged by earlier dry running"],["Coolant warning message and MIL","Pump starts briefly, then stops again","Gurgling noise or falling level in the electronics reservoir"],2,3,["P2E48","P2E47","P2E49","P2B2A","P2D06"],""],P2E47:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump B Underspeed","P2E47 is set when electronics coolant pump B keeps turning but clearly slower than requested. GM's 2018 hybrid tables describe the check for pump A (P19FC): the filtered difference between commanded and reported speed must stay within a calibrated band once the pump has run for 5 s at 11 to 90 % duty, otherwise a Type B fault results.",["Stiff bearing or worn pump B","Deposits or debris slowing the impeller","Voltage drop on pump supply or ground under load","Incorrect or aged coolant, too viscous when cold"],["MIL and hybrid system warning","Electronics temperatures rise during long drives or fast charging","Occasional power limitation"],3,3,["P2E48","P2E49","P2E42","P2C66","P2D07"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2E48:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump B Overspeed","With P2E48 the controller sees electronics coolant pump B turning faster than commanded, without the separate dry-run test (P2E46) having fired. The usual reason is lost load, since a centrifugal pump accelerates when its impeller gets less liquid, whether from a low level, a collapsed suction hose, partial air or an impeller slipping on its shaft.",["Low level or residual air in the electronics loop","Collapsed or kinked hose on the pump inlet side","Impeller slipping on the pump shaft","Implausible speed feedback from the pump electronics"],["MIL, sometimes with a coolant level warning","Louder pump noise than usual","Rising electronics temperatures and power limits"],2,3,["P2E46","P2E47","P2E49","P2C67","P2E7A"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B — מהירות יתר"],P2E49:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump B Stuck/Stalled","P2E49 reports that electronics coolant pump B is powered and commanded, but its rotor does not turn or comes to a standstill. Mitsubishi's 2022 Outlander PHEV shows such a test for its electric water pump: with more than 9 V supply the PHEV-ECU sets P10D9 once the reported speed stays under 100 rpm for 0.5 s, against about 500 rpm when healthy.",["Seized bearing or failed pump B motor","Debris or sealant residue jamming the impeller","Frozen coolant due to insufficient antifreeze","Supply or ground lost under load"],["MIL and hybrid or drive system warning","Rapid temperature rise in inverter or charger","Strong power reduction or charging stops"],3,3,["P2E47","P2E48","P2E42","P2C68","P2D05"],""],P2E4A:["Battery Charger Coupler Temperature Sensor C Circuit","P2E4A is the general electrical fault of a third temperature measuring point in the charging inlet, logged when the module sees a defective circuit but does not sort it into low, high or implausible. Unlike sensors A and B, the C row has no intermittent code of its own.",["Sensor lead or crimp between inlet and evaluating module broken","Low-voltage connector of the inlet harness loose or corroded","Temperature element C (or one element of a PTC chain) failed inside the inlet","Measuring input in the charger or charge control module defective"],["Charging refused or only possible at reduced power","Charging system warning in the cluster or the app","Charge indicator at the inlet signals a fault"],2,0,["P2E4B","P2E4C","P2E4D","P2E4E","P2E4F","P0D99"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E4B:["Battery Charger Coupler Temperature Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P2E4B concerns a sensor C value that is electrically valid yet does not fit the situation, for instance a reading that ignores a heavy charge current, departs from the other inlet sensors or jumps without cause. CARB wants such rationality faults kept under their own code, apart from codes for wiring faults and values beyond the limits.",["Worn or widened terminals in the charging station plug heating the contact unevenly","Sensor no longer in good thermal contact with its pin","Plausibility logic in the charging software too strict, update available","Temperature element drifted from its characteristic curve"],["Charging stops or starts at reduced power, often at busy public stations","Fault does not reappear until the car has been driven for a while","Charging warning message"],2,0,["P2E4A","P2E4C","P2E4D","P2E4E","P2E50","P0D9A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E4C:["Battery Charger Coupler Temperature Sensor C Circuit Low","P2E4C says the voltage on the sensor C input has fallen under its lower limit. Low is about the signal; the temperature it implies depends on the element. Volex fits its NACS inlet with NTC thermistors of 100 kΩ at 25 °C and a B value of 4150 K, whose resistance shrinks as they warm, so with a pull-up a very low voltage stands for an absurdly hot contact.",["Sensor C signal wire shorted to ground","Water or corrosion bridging the sensor terminals in the inlet or its connector","Temperature element C shorted internally","Measuring input of the evaluating module defective"],["Charging blocked at once or ended shortly after start","Charging system warning","Fault may follow rain or a car wash"],2,0,["P2E4A","P2E4B","P2E4D","P2E4E","P2E51","P0D9B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E4D:["Battery Charger Coupler Temperature Sensor C Circuit High","P2E4D is stored when the sensor C input rises above its upper limit. In a pull-up circuit that is the signature of an open loop, an unplugged connector or a short to a supply voltage. Read as temperature, it means very cold for an NTC, but very hot for a PT1000 or a PTC element.",["Sensor C loop open, for example a broken wire or unplugged connector","Signal wire shorted to a supply voltage","Temperature element C or one link of a PTC chain open inside the inlet","Measuring input of the evaluating module defective"],["Charging does not start or stops immediately","Charging system warning","Displayed inlet temperature stuck at an extreme value"],2,0,["P2E4A","P2E4B","P2E4C","P2E4E","P2E52","P0D9C"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E4E:["Battery Charger Coupler Temperature C Too High","P2E4E is no sensor fault: measuring point C works, but the contact it watches has become too hot, so charging is cut back or ended. For orientation, a DOE laboratory report from August 2025 compares the IEC 62196-1 ceiling, 90 °C when the air is at 40 °C, with the fixed 100 °C of SAE J3400. No manufacturer documents P2E4E publicly.",["Worn, widened or dirty pins in the station plug or the vehicle inlet","Charging cable with thin conductors heating up at high current (Porsche)","Long high-current session in strong heat or direct sun","Temperature logic in the charging software, update available"],["Charging slows down or stops partway through","Charge indicator at the inlet flashes a fault or reduced-power state","Discoloured or heat-marked pins at the plug or inlet"],2,0,["P2E4A","P2E4B","P2E4C","P2E4D","P2E53","P0E5F","P0EEE"],"טמפרטורת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ C — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2E4F:["Battery Charger Coupler Temperature Sensor D Circuit","P2E4F is the general circuit fault of the fourth inlet temperature sensor, used when the wiring is clearly wrong but not classed as low, high or implausible; the D row has no intermittent code either.",["Low-voltage connector between inlet harness and evaluating module loose (smart for sensor A)","Sensor D wiring chafed or broken","Temperature element D failed (normally replaced with the inlet)","Measuring input in the SOBDM or charger defective"],["DC fast charging refused or limited","Charging warning in the cluster","Fault may only show with a warm or cold inlet"],2,0,["P2E50","P2E51","P2E52","P2E53","P2E4A","P0EE7"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E50:["Battery Charger Coupler Temperature Sensor D Circuit Range/Performance","P2E50 flags sensor D for delivering a believable voltage that the logic still rejects. A module can test this in several ways: compare D with a sensor on a contact that carries the same current, check whether it warms as expected under load, or look for steps no metal pin could make. Inlets that monitor both DC+ and DC-, as Amphenol's NACS inlet does with PT1000 elements, offer such a partner.",["Sensor D has lost good thermal contact with its pin","One contact heating far more than its partner due to wear or dirt","Plausibility thresholds in the module software, update available","Temperature element D drifted"],["DC fast charging limited or ended early","AC charging may still work","Charging warning message"],2,0,["P2E4F","P2E51","P2E52","P2E53","P2E4B","P0EE8"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E51:["Battery Charger Coupler Temperature Sensor D Circuit Low","P2E51 reports a sensor D voltage below the valid band. TE Connectivity lists thermistors, thermocouples and resistance temperature detectors as candidate elements for inlet sensing (US10960781), and the patent also explains the stakes: contact resistance heats the inlet at high current and could melt parts or start a fire if nobody watches.",["Sensor D signal wire shorted to ground","Moisture or corrosion in the inlet harness connector","Temperature element D shorted internally","Measuring input of the evaluating module defective"],["DC fast charging refused","Charging warning message","Inlet temperature reading implausible in live data"],2,0,["P2E4F","P2E50","P2E52","P2E53","P2E4C","P0EE9"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E52:["Battery Charger Coupler Temperature Sensor D Circuit High","P2E52 is the mirror case of P2E51: the sensor D input sits above its valid band, usually because of an interrupted sensor lead, a connector that has backed out, or a short to a supply line. Volex quotes for its NACS inlet NTC thermistors with an operating range of -40 to +125 °C; an open NTC loop looks like a contact colder than that range, which hides any real heating.",["Sensor D lead broken or connector backed out","Signal wire shorted to a supply line","Temperature element D open inside the inlet","Measuring input of the evaluating module defective"],["DC fast charging does not start or stops at once","Charging warning message","Inlet temperature reading fixed at an extreme value"],2,0,["P2E4F","P2E50","P2E51","P2E53","P2E4D","P0EEA"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E53:["Battery Charger Coupler Temperature D Too High","P2E53 means measuring point D in the charging inlet reports a contact that is too hot, and charging is throttled or halted. Ford documents this exact code in SSM 55080: on Mustang Mach-E built up to 25 June 2023, E-Transit 2022-2025 and F-150 Lightning 2022-2023, DC fast charging can stop with P2E53:27 and/or P0EEE:27 in the SOBDM. The 27 is the J2012 subtype for a signal changing faster than allowed.",["SOBDM software misjudging DC fast-charge heating (Ford SSM 55080)","Worn or contaminated DC pins in the station plug or the inlet","Very high charging current in hot weather","Heat-damaged inlet contacts needing a new charge port"],["DC fast charging stops at level 3 stations","AC charging at home or level 2 still works","Charging power reduced during fast charging"],4,0,["P2E4F","P2E50","P2E51","P2E52","P2E4E","P0EEE","P0E5F"],"טמפרטורת מחבר טעינה מטען סוללה‏ D — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2E54:["Exhaust Pressure Sensor C Circuit","P2E54 is the general circuit fault of a third exhaust pressure sensor, C. Its position is set by the manufacturer; engines can carry several such sensors, as in a GE patent with one pressure sensor in each of two exhaust manifolds. No manufacturer publicly documents P2E54; Ford's 2023 diesels and its EcoBoost petrol engines use sensor A only.",["Exhaust pressure sensor C failed internally","Wiring near the exhaust damaged by heat or chafing","Corroded or loose connector at sensor C"],["MIL on","Reduced power if boost or EGR control falls back to substitute values","Other exhaust or EGR monitors may not run"],2,3,["P2E55","P2E56","P2E57","U069F","P0470","P047A"],"חיישן לחץ פליטה‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E55:["Exhaust Pressure Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P2E55 is the plausibility test of exhaust pressure sensor C: the voltage is in range, but the pressure does not suit the operating state. CARB wants such rationality faults stored apart from circuit faults. No maker documents P2E55; Ford's 2023 diesel summary shows the pattern for sensor A. With the engine stopped for at least 10 s the reading may differ from ambient pressure by no more than 15 kPa;",["Real back pressure from a clogged particulate filter or catalyst","Sooted or cracked sensing tube to sensor C","Sensor C offset drifted or stuck mid-range","Exhaust leak near the measuring point"],["MIL, often without noticeable driveability change","Particulate filter or EGR codes alongside","Reduced power if the pressure is really too high"],2,3,["P2E54","P2E56","P2E57","P0471","P047B"],"חיישן לחץ פליטה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E56:["Exhaust Pressure Sensor C Circuit Low","P2E56 means the signal of exhaust pressure sensor C stays under the lowest voltage a working sensor can produce. Analogue exhaust pressure sensors return a share of their 5 V reference; Ford's petrol transfer function for sensor A puts 49 kPa at 0.3 V and flags anything under 0.21 V for 5 s, while its 2023 diesels use 0.1 V for 2 s. No manufacturer publicly documents P2E56.",["Signal wire of sensor C shorted to ground","5 V reference open or pulled down by another sensor","Sensor C output stage failed"],["MIL on","Possible loss of power from substitute values","Further low codes of sensors sharing the reference"],2,3,["P2E57","P2E54","P2E55","P0472","P047C"],"חיישן לחץ פליטה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E57:["Exhaust Pressure Sensor C Circuit High","P2E57 reports a signal from exhaust pressure sensor C above the plausible ceiling. For sensor A Ford sets that ceiling at 4.80 V, on petrol engines checked while the EGR monitor runs and with 5 s to fail, on 2023 diesels with 2 s; in Ford's petrol transfer function 4.7 V already equals about 378 kPa.",["Open ground circuit of sensor C","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Open signal wire pulled high by the module input","Internally failed sensor C"],["MIL on","Boost or EGR control in substitute mode, possibly less power"],2,3,["P2E56","P2E54","P2E55","P0473","P047D"],"חיישן לחץ פליטה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E58:["Alternative Fuel Random/Multiple Cylinder Misfire Detected","P2E58 is the collective misfire code for running on the second fuel, mostly CNG or LPG: misfires are counted while gas is burned, but no single cylinder can be blamed, or several each carry a large share. CARB treats a bi-fuel car as alternate-fueled only while it runs on gas and asks for the same misfire monitor as on petrol; EPA likewise requires converters to keep OBD working on the conversion fuel.",["Gas pressure regulator or LPG vaporiser iced up or not heated enough (low coolant flow, moisture in the gas)","Too little gas pressure at the rail – clogged gas filter, nearly empty tank or weak regulator","Worn plugs or weak coils on several cylinders that cope with petrol but not with the harder-to-ignite gas mixture","Lean gas mixture from an intake air leak or wrong gas-system calibration"],["Rough running or jerking only while the engine runs on gas","Bi-fuel vehicle switches back to petrol on its own","Check engine light on or flashing, gas-mode indicator may flash"],2,3,["P0300","P2E61","P2E59","P2E60","P0171","P0174"],""],P2E59:["Cylinder 1 Alternative Fuel Misfire Detected","P2E59 means that, while the engine is burning its gaseous fuel, the misfire monitor puts the dropouts on cylinder 1; CARB allows a single-cylinder code once more than 90 % of counted misfires fall on one cylinder. In most numbering schemes cylinder 1 is the frontmost. No manufacturer publishes P2E59.",["Sticking or leaking gas injector on cylinder 1","Cracked injector hose or loose nozzle in the intake port of cylinder 1","Weak coil or worn plug on cylinder 1 that fails only under gas","Fault in the fuel changeover module or its programming (misfire only at the switch from petrol to gas)"],["Rough idle on gas that disappears in petrol mode","Stumble at the moment the system changes over to gas","Check engine light, possibly flashing under load"],2,3,["P2E58","P0301","P2E5A","P0201","P0351"],""],P2E5A:["Cylinder 2 Alternative Fuel Misfire Detected","P2E5A says cylinder 2 is the one losing combustion while the engine is supplied with alternative fuel; P0302 is its petrol twin. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. On inline engines cylinder 2 follows cylinder 1; on V engines it is either the foremost cylinder on the other bank (GM, Chrysler) or the second one of the first bank (Ford, Audi).",["Gas injector on cylinder 2 gummed or sluggish from compressor oil in the gas","Injector harness of the conversion routed crosswise, so cylinder 2 receives another cylinder's pulse","Injection nozzle of cylinder 2 not properly seated in the manifold port","Coil or plug on cylinder 2 too weak for gas operation"],["Uneven running on gas, normal on petrol","Higher gas consumption and loss of power","Check engine light"],2,3,["P2E58","P0302","P2E59","P2E5B","P0202"],""],P2E5B:["Cylinder 3 Alternative Fuel Misfire Detected","P2E5B flags misfire on cylinder 3 during operation on CNG or LPG; on petrol the matching code is P0303. No manufacturer publishes P2E5B. One cause that belongs to gas engines in particular is valve seat wear: dry gaseous fuels leave few combustion products, so valve and seat insert rub metal on metal and the seat recedes, as a Honda patent on seat materials explains.",["Faulty gas injector on cylinder 3","Valve seat recession on cylinder 3 from dry gas operation, valve no longer seals","Worn plug or failing coil on cylinder 3","Retrofit gas conversion on an engine without hardened valves and seats"],["Misfire on gas that slowly gets worse, later also on petrol","Low compression on cylinder 3, sometimes a ticking valve noise","Check engine light"],3,3,["P2E58","P0303","P2E5A","P2E5C","P0203"],""],P2E5C:["Cylinder 4 Alternative Fuel Misfire Detected","P2E5C is stored when the misfire counter blames cylinder 4 while gas is being burned; in petrol mode the code would be P0304. No manufacturer documents P2E5C publicly, and Deutz's fault list for its eControls LPG, CNG and bi-fuel engines reports such events with the ordinary P0301 to P0304. On four-cylinder engines cylinder 4 is the last one in the block.",["Spark plug on cylinder 4 worn or unsuited for gas (gap too wide, wrong heat range)","Coil or plug boot on cylinder 4 breaking down under the higher firing voltage","Gas injector on cylinder 4 sticking or delivering too little"],["Misfire mainly under load or acceleration on gas","Engine runs cleanly after switching to petrol","Check engine light, flashing during heavy misfire"],1,3,["P2E58","P0304","P2E5B","P0354","P0204"],""],P2E5D:["Cylinder 5 Alternative Fuel Misfire Detected","P2E5D assigns gas-mode misfire to cylinder 5, which exists only on engines with five or more cylinders, such as the 3.6-litre V6 in GM's 2015 Impala bi-fuel, V8 trucks or inline-six gas engines in buses. P0305 is the petrol equivalent. No manufacturer publishes P2E5D. With bank-wise numbering (Ford, Audi) cylinder 5 opens the second bank; with crank-order numbering (GM, Chrysler) it lies on the odd-numbered bank.",["Spark plug on cylinder 5 past its change interval or damaged when handled","Low-pressure oil separator/filter not serviced, oil reaches the gas injector of cylinder 5","Gas injector on cylinder 5 faulty","Cracked coil extension or boot on cylinder 5 (heavy-duty gas engines)"],["Vibration and power loss on gas","Bi-fuel vehicle drops back to petrol","Check engine light"],2,3,["P2E58","P0305","P2E5C","P2E5E","P0355"],""],P2E5E:["Cylinder 6 Alternative Fuel Misfire Detected","P2E5E names cylinder 6 as the misfiring one while the engine runs on alternative fuel; P0306 is its petrol twin. No manufacturer documents the code openly. On inline sixes cylinder 6 is the rearmost.",["Gas or liquid-propane injector on cylinder 6 sticking or leaking","Propane vapour in the liquid-injection rail (hot restart, low rail or tank pressure)","Plug or coil on cylinder 6 failing under gas","Low tank pressure in cold weather or nearly empty tank"],["Misfire or rough running shortly after a hot restart","Long cranking time when the engine is warm","Check engine light"],2,3,["P2E58","P0306","P2E5D","P2E5F","P0206"],""],P2E5F:["Cylinder 7 Alternative Fuel Misfire Detected","P2E5F puts alternative-fuel misfire on cylinder 7, so it concerns eight-cylinder engines, for instance GM's Vortec 6.0 V8 in the bi-fuel Silverado/Sierra or the dedicated CNG and LPG Express/Savana vans that GM lists in its gaseous-fuel overview bulletin. P0307 is the petrol counterpart. No maker documents P2E5F publicly. On GM V8s cylinder 7 is the rear cylinder of the odd-numbered bank;",["Gas injector on cylinder 7 faulty or sticking","Leaking injector sleeve or loose nozzle at cylinder 7's intake runner","Conversion injector harness damaged or misrouted near the rear of the engine","Coil or plug on cylinder 7 too weak for gas"],["Rough running on gas, smooth on petrol","Gas-mode indicator flashing or automatic return to petrol","Check engine light"],2,3,["P2E58","P0307","P2E5E","P2E60","P0357"],""],P2E60:["Cylinder 8 Alternative Fuel Misfire Detected","P2E60 is the last cylinder-specific code of the alternative-fuel misfire group and points to cylinder 8; the next code, P2E61, covers misfire with low fuel. Petrol twin: P0308. No manufacturer documents P2E60 openly. On GM V8s cylinder 8 is the rear cylinder of the even-numbered bank, on Ford V8s the rear of the second bank.",["Deposits from compressor oil in the gas injector serving cylinder 8","Coil or plug on cylinder 8, often hard to reach at the rear of the engine","Uneven gas split between the two rails starving the bank with cylinder 8 (older bi-fuel systems)","Valve seat wear on cylinder 8 after long gas operation"],["Misfire on gas, possibly with lean codes on one bank","Engine shakes at idle on gas","Check engine light"],2,3,["P2E58","P0308","P2E5F","P2E61","P0174"],""],P2E61:["Alternative Fuel Misfire Detected With Low Fuel","P2E61 records misfire that occurs while the engine burns its gaseous fuel and that fuel is almost used up. No manufacturer documents the code publicly. CARB treats a bi-fuel car as alternate-fueled only while it runs on gas and lets makers seek approval to suspend misfire monitoring at 15 % fuel or less, since a nearly empty tank can cause misfire by itself.",["Gas tank close to empty, so the regulator can no longer hold rail pressure","Tank pressure or level signal reads too high, so the system stays on gas too long","Restriction in the gas line (clogged filter, ice) that only shows when tank pressure is low","Worn plugs or coils that cannot ignite the leaner gas mixture near empty"],["Stumbling or power loss on gas when the gas gauge is near empty","Vehicle changes over to petrol on its own","Check engine light on"],1,1,["P2E58","P2E59","P0300","P0460","P0171"],""],P2E62:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve E Control Circuit/Open","Coolant bypass valve E is the fifth electrically driven coolant valve in the SAE lettering; which coolant path it controls (heater, radiator, transmission, block) is up to the carmaker. P2E62 says the engine computer sees an open or otherwise faulty drive circuit. No manufacturer documents valve E publicly.",["Loose, corroded or unplugged connector at the valve","Broken wire in the drive or supply line","Open winding in the valve actuator motor or solenoid","ECM software fault or defective output stage"],["Check engine light or service message","Heating, warm-up or cooling behaves differently, depending on what valve E controls","Valve stays in its de-energised default position"],2,1,["P2E63","P2E64","P2E66","P2681","P26BD"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ E — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2E63:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve E Control Circuit Low","P2E63 flags a drive line for coolant bypass valve E whose voltage is lower than the commanded state allows, typically a grounded wire or a heavy leakage path to ground in the harness or the actuator. No carmaker documents valve E publicly. CARB does not even force separate codes for open and shorted outputs, so many systems use only one code.",["Chafed drive wire touching engine ground","Internal short in the valve actuator, often after coolant got into it","Corrosion bridging pins in the connector","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light, sometimes a maintenance message","Valve does not move or stays in its default position","Slower warm-up or changed heater output"],2,1,["P2E62","P2E64","P2682","P26BE","P26B8"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ E — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2E64:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve E Control Circuit High","P2E64 is the high-side counterpart: the control line of coolant bypass valve E carries more voltage than expected, usually because it touches a supply wire, or the load has gone open in a way the output stage reads as high. Valve E itself appears in no public manufacturer document.",["Drive wire chafed through and touching a battery-voltage wire","Moisture or coolant in the connector creating a path to supply voltage","Open actuator winding that the output stage reads as high voltage","Defective output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light","Valve is not driven and stays in its de-energised position","Possible change in heater output or warm-up time"],2,1,["P2E62","P2E63","P2683","P26BF","P26B9"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ E — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2E65:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve E Stuck/Open","P2E65 is a functional fault: the electrics of valve E are fine, but the valve remains open although it was told to close. The official title is written Stuck/Open, though it means stuck open, the partner of P2E67. No carmaker documents valve E publicly.",["Valve body jammed open by deposits or worn seals","Broken gear or weak actuator that cannot drive the valve closed","Position sensor or its wiring reporting an open valve that is actually closed","Chafed engine harness disturbing drive or feedback signals"],["Engine and cabin heat take longer to come up","Check engine light","Slightly higher fuel use on short trips"],2,1,["P2E67","P2E66","P26C0","P26AF","P26BA"],""],P2E66:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve E Range/Performance","P2E66 is the broad plausibility code for valve E: the valve moves, but not to the right place, not fast enough, or its feedback does not match the command, without a clear stuck-open or stuck-closed verdict. No manufacturer documents valve E publicly.",["Cracked or worn gear inside the valve actuator","Valve sluggish from deposits, degraded coolant or worn seals","Position sensor drifting or lost end-stop learn values","Low supply voltage slowing the actuator"],["Check engine light, sometimes a coolant or maintenance message","Uneven heater output or warm-up","Possible fallback to a fixed valve position"],2,3,["P2E65","P2E67","P2E62","P26A3","P26C1"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ E — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E67:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve E Stuck Closed","P2E67 means valve E stays shut although the control asked it to open. No manufacturer documents valve E publicly. GM's closed-side test on block valve D (P26C2) shows the pattern: a gap of more than 5° between commanded and measured angle while the raw feedback stays below 50°, 4 of 5 seconds, Type B in the 2025 table 25OBDG03B; the test pauses during end-stop learning.",["Valve jammed closed by deposits, debris or swollen seals","Actuator motor or gearing unable to open the valve","Position feedback stuck at the closed value","Wrong coolant or trapped air after service upsetting the temperature-based check"],["Check engine light","Little or no heat from the heater, or rising engine temperature, depending on the circuit","Possible reduced engine power to protect the engine"],2,3,["P2E65","P2E66","P26C2","P2E81","P26B2"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ E — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2E68:["System Too Lean During Cylinder Deactivation Bank 1","P2E68 is a fuel trim fault that is judged only while cylinders are shut off: in that mode bank 1 needs more fuel correction than allowed. GM uses it on its 4.2-litre twin-turbo V8 (LTA, table 19OBDG07): the engine learns a separate multiplicative long-term trim for deactivation mode, and the code sets when that factor for bank 1 rises above 1.23 and has been steady for at least 10 s; Type B, MIL after two trips.",["Restricted injector on one of the cylinders that keep firing on bank 1","Unmetered air entering bank 1 (intake leak, seal, PCV)","Deactivating rocker or lifter on bank 1 not holding the valves shut, pumping air into the exhaust","Bank 1 oxygen sensor reading biased rich"],["Check engine light after two trips","Slight shake or surge at light cruise when cylinders are shut off","Cylinder deactivation may be used less often"],3,1,["P2E6A","P2E69","P2177","P0171","P3400"],""],P2E69:["System Too Rich During Cylinder Deactivation Bank 1","P2E69 is the rich mirror of P2E68: with cylinders deactivated, bank 1 has to pull fuel out beyond the permitted range. In GM's 19OBDG07 tables for the 4.2-litre twin-turbo V8 the separate long-term trim factor learned for deactivation mode must drop below 0.77 and stay steady; it shares the enable logic of P2E68 and is Type B, MIL on the second trip.",["A cylinder that should be off still breathing, so measured airflow and fuel delivery are too high","Leaking or dribbling direct injector on bank 1","Fuel vapour from diluted oil or a stuck-open purge valve","Bank 1 oxygen sensor reading biased lean"],["Check engine light after two trips","Higher fuel use, possible fuel smell","Rough running in deactivation mode"],3,1,["P2E6B","P2E68","P2178","P0172","P3400"],""],P2E6A:["System Too Lean During Cylinder Deactivation Bank 2","P2E6A applies the lean test to bank 2, the cylinder row without cylinder 1. GM sets it on the 4.2-litre twin-turbo V8 of the 2019 table 19OBDG07 when the trim factor learned for deactivation mode on bank 2 exceeds 1.23 while stable; Type B.",["Weak injector on cylinder 4 or 6, which carry bank 2 in deactivation mode","Bank 2 high-pressure fuel pump delivering too little","Deactivating rocker on bank 2 letting air pass into the exhaust","Exhaust leak ahead of the bank 2 oxygen sensor"],["Check engine light after two trips","Hesitation at light load in deactivation mode","Often no noticeable change in normal driving"],3,1,["P2E68","P2E6B","P2179","P0174"],""],P2E6B:["System Too Rich During Cylinder Deactivation Bank 2","P2E6B closes the set: bank 2 runs rich while cylinders are switched off. GM's 19OBDG07 tables (4.2-litre twin-turbo V8, LTA) fail the test when bank 2's deactivation-mode trim factor falls below 0.77 and has settled; Type B, two trips, same enable conditions as the other three codes. Typical systems keep the valves of the idle cylinders shut and stop fuelling them, so the shut cylinders act as air springs;",["Leaking injector on bank 2, including one on a cylinder that should be shut off","Deactivation rocker or its oil-control solenoid not switching on one cylinder","Excess purge vapour or fuel-diluted engine oil","Bank 2 oxygen sensor reading biased lean"],["Check engine light after two trips","Higher fuel consumption on the highway","Possible sooty tailpipe on bank 2 side"],3,1,["P2E69","P2E6A","P2180","P0175"],""],P2E6C:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack A Cell Thickness","P2E6C means the cells of high-voltage pack A have become thicker than the battery controller tolerates: the cells are swelling. A healthy cell only breathes a little while charging; GE and University of Michigan measured about 0.1 mm, 1 % of its thickness, on the Sanyo cell of Ford's Fusion HEV pack. Lasting growth comes from aging or from gas after overcharge or overheating.",["Aged cells in pack A that have grown permanently thicker","Gas build-up in cells after overcharging or overheating","Module clamping or end plates loosened, so cells can expand further"],["Hybrid or EV system warning, often with reduced power","Vehicle may not switch to READY because the main contactors stay open","Charging blocked or limited"],4,3,["P2E6D","P2E6E","P2E6F","P2E70","P0A7F","P0A7E"],"עובי תא מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A"],P2E6D:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack A Cell Thickness Sensor Circuit High","P2E6D says the signal from the cell thickness sensor of pack A sits above the range the controller accepts as a real reading. The code describes the voltage, not swollen cells. No manufacturer documents P2E6D publicly, and how such a sensor is built varies: a Ford patent uses a resistive gauge on a thinned cell wall whose resistance climbs as the wall bulges, LG uses a fibre grid read by a photoresistor, and classic…",["Open signal or ground wire, unplugged or corroded connector inside pack A","Signal wire chafed against a supply or reference line","Thickness or pressure sensing element itself failed open"],["Hybrid or EV warning light","Power or charging limited as a precaution","In some designs the vehicle will not go to READY"],4,3,["P2E6C","P2E6E","P2E6F","P2E71"],"חיישן עובי תא מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E6E:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack A Cell Thickness Sensor Circuit Low","P2E6E is the low-side counterpart to P2E6D: the thickness or swelling sensor of pack A delivers less signal than any intact circuit should, typically from a short to ground, a missing supply or a dead sensor amplifier. No manufacturer documents P2E6E publicly. Two patents show why a low reading can hide a real problem. LG places piezo elements in the cooling gap between cells;",["Signal wire shorted to ground or to the module housing","Sensor supply or amplifier supply missing","Sensing element or its amplifier failed","Moisture or coolant in a connector inside the pack creating a leakage path"],["Hybrid or EV warning light","Reduced power or limited charging"],4,3,["P2E6C","P2E6D","P2E6F","P2E72"],"חיישן עובי תא מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E6F:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack A Cell Thickness Sensor Circuit Performance","P2E6F covers a thickness sensor in pack A whose reading is electrically valid but does not behave as the controller expects. Cell thickness is not static: it rises and falls with state of charge, which is why Bosch and Samsung SDI propose using the swelling force of the winding to estimate charge and health, and a graphene film sensor studied at Warwick tracked charge level from expansion alone.",["Sensor loosened, shifted or no longer bonded to the cell or end plate","Sensor drifting with age or temperature","Contact resistance in connectors distorting the reading","Missing calibration or relearn after module replacement"],["Warning light without noticeable driving change at first","Charging or power may be restricted later"],4,3,["P2E6C","P2E6D","P2E6E","P2E73"],"חיישן עובי תא מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E70:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack B Cell Thickness","P2E70 is the swelling code for a second high-voltage pack, B, in vehicles that carry two; which pack is A and which B is set by the maker. The controller judges that cells in pack B have grown too thick. No manufacturer documents P2E70 publicly. Research explains why thickness is watched at all.",["Cells in pack B aged and permanently thicker","Gas generation after overcharge, deep discharge or heat","Poor cooling of pack B accelerating cell degradation"],["Hybrid or EV warning with power reduction","Reduced range or charging blocked","Vehicle may refuse READY"],4,3,["P2E71","P2E72","P2E73","P2E6C","P0EDD","P2D46"],"עובי תא מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B"],P2E71:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack B Cell Thickness Sensor Circuit High","P2E71 flags the thickness sensor circuit of pack B as reading too high. Not every swelling detector is analog: LG's module patent uses a panel that slides along a ramp until it touches a contact sensor, and a Lithium Energy and Power patent fits cells with insulated contact elements that close under pressure.",["Sensor connector in pack B not fully seated after battery work","Broken signal or ground wire to the sensor","Signal line shorted to a supply voltage"],["Hybrid or EV warning light","Possibly limited power or charging"],4,3,["P2E70","P2E72","P2E73","P2E6D"],"חיישן עובי תא מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E72:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack B Cell Thickness Sensor Circuit Low","P2E72 means the pack B thickness sensor reports a signal below its valid floor. On a bridge-type strain gauge, the output is a small fraction of the excitation voltage that grows with strain, so losing that excitation or shorting a bridge leg to ground pulls the reading towards zero.",["Signal line or sensor shorted to ground inside pack B","Sensor excitation or reference supply lost","Fault in the measuring circuit of the battery monitoring module"],["Hybrid or EV warning light","Power or charging may be reduced as a precaution"],4,3,["P2E70","P2E71","P2E73","P2E6E"],"חיישן עובי תא מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E73:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack B Cell Thickness Sensor Circuit Performance","P2E73 indicates that the thickness sensor of pack B delivers values within range that the controller cannot reconcile with what it otherwise knows about the pack. Free expansion of a healthy cell is small, about 1 % of its thickness on the Ford Fusion HEV cell measured by GE, so a sensor must resolve fractions of a millimetre; GE's thin eddy-current coils between cells covered 0 to 2 mm.",["Sensor mounting or gap changed, for example after module work","Sensor drift or degraded sensing element","Plausibility limits in the battery controller software too tight"],["Warning light, often with no other complaint","Battery controller may limit power or charging rate"],4,3,["P2E70","P2E71","P2E72","P2E6F"],"חיישן עובי תא מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E74:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor D Circuit","P2E74 covers any circuit fault of coolant temperature sensor D, the fourth such sensor a maker can fit to the battery's liquid cooling. Battery controllers typically watch coolant at the pack inlet and outlet; GM's Volt and ELR tables use sensor A for the inlet and B for the outlet. Where a sensor D sits is not public. No manufacturer documents P2E74 publicly. Such sensors are sealed NTC thermistors;",["Damaged wire, loose connector or corroded terminal at sensor D","Fault on the shared 5 V reference circuit of the battery controller","Coolant temperature sensor D failed"],["Hybrid system or check engine light","Battery cooling or heating not working as intended","Reduced electric power or charging rate"],3,3,["P2E75","P2E76","P2E77","P2E78","P2D52","P0CD5","P0C42"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E75:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor D Circuit Range/Performance","P2E75 means battery coolant sensor D gives a reading that is electrically fine yet does not match the other temperatures in the loop. No manufacturer documents P2E75 publicly. GM's sensor B (outlet) shows how such a check works: with the pump above 20 % the outlet value is compared with inlet and average cell temperature. The 2011 Volt fails it at more than 10 °C, 80 of 100 samples at 100 ms;",["Sensor D drifting or responding slowly","Plausibility logic in controller software too strict (update available)","Air pocket or poor coolant flow around the sensor"],["Warning light, frequently with no other symptom","Less effective battery cooling or heating"],3,1,["P2E74","P2E76","P2E77","P2D53","P0CD6","P0C43"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E76:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor D Circuit Low","P2E76 reports that the voltage on battery coolant sensor D has dropped below its lower limit. Because these sensors are NTC thermistors whose resistance falls as they warm, a low voltage stands for very hot coolant, and a grounded signal wire or a sensor with an internal short produces exactly that picture. No manufacturer documents P2E76 publicly.",["Signal wire of sensor D shorted to ground","Sensor D shorted internally, for example after coolant entered it","Actual overheating of the battery coolant loop"],["Hybrid or check engine warning","Cooling may run at full effort or power may be cut back"],3,3,["P2E74","P2E77","P2D54","P0CD7","P0C44"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E77:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor D Circuit High","P2E77 is set when the signal of battery coolant sensor D rises to or near the reference voltage. In a pull-up NTC circuit that is the signature of an open: a disconnected plug, a broken wire, a spread pin or a sensor element that has gone open, and the controller then sees a coolant temperature colder than physically plausible. No manufacturer documents P2E77 publicly.",["Sensor D connector unplugged or not latched after cooling system work","Broken wire or spread terminal in the sensor D circuit","Sensor D element open"],["Hybrid or check engine warning","Battery heating may switch on needlessly or behave oddly in winter"],3,3,["P2E74","P2E76","P2D55","P0CD8","P0C45"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E78:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Temperature Sensor D Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2E78 stands for a coolant temperature from sensor D that jumps around, mostly without leaving the electrical limits. A liquid loop changes temperature slowly, so fast swings point to a loose contact rather than to the coolant. No manufacturer documents P2E78 publicly.",["Loose or fretting terminal in the sensor D connector","Harness rubbing through near moving or vibrating parts","False detection by controller software (update)"],["Warning light that comes and goes","Coolant temperature in live data jumping"],3,1,["P2E74","P2E75","P2D56","P0CD9","P0C46"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ D — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2E79:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump C Performance","P2E79 is the functional verdict on a third pump in the coolant loop of the traction electronics: command and wiring look healthy, yet the pump does not move coolant the way the controller expects. No manufacturer documents P2E79 or says which pump it calls C.",["Air trapped in the electronics coolant loop after service or a leak","Pump C worn or impeller fouled, delivering too little flow","Kinked hose or clogged cooler passages in the loop","Control software misjudging pump function (update available)"],["Hybrid or EV system warning lamp, possibly MIL","Drive power or charging rate limited because electronics run warm","Gurgling or whirring noise from the electronics coolant loop"],2,3,["P2E7A","P2E42","P0CEA","P2BD7"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E7A:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump C Overspeed","P2E7A means the third electronics coolant pump spins faster than the speed it was given. A centrifugal pump that draws air instead of liquid loses its load and races, so a low coolant level, a leak or a poorly bled loop come first, a slipping impeller or false speed feedback later. No manufacturer documents P2E7A.",["Coolant level low or air pocket at the pump inlet","Leak or defective seal in the electronics coolant loop","Impeller loose on its shaft or broken","Faulty speed feedback from the pump electronics"],["Coolant or hybrid system warning, possibly MIL","Coolant reservoir level dropping, traces of leakage","Pump runs loud or churns; power or charging may be reduced"],2,3,["P2E79","P2E48","P2E46","P2C67","P2D0B"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ C — מהירות יתר"],P2E7B:["Drive Motor A Excitation Current Sensor Circuit","P2E7B is the general circuit fault of the measuring element for the DC field current in the rotor of drive motor A. It exists only in electrically excited synchronous motors, whose rotor field comes from a winding, as in Renault's Megane E-Tech, Nissan's Ariya and BMW's fifth-generation eDrive. The controller stores P2E7B when the signal is missing or unusable without a clear low or high reading, e.g.",["Supply or reference of the excitation current sensor lost","Open or corroded connection between sensor and motor controller","Excitation current sensor or its isolated amplifier failed","Measuring input inside the inverter or motor controller defective"],["Electric drive warning lamp and MIL","Noticeably reduced power or no drive from motor A","Vehicle may refuse to enter ready mode"],4,3,["P2E28","P2E29","P2E2A","P2E2B","P0A78"],"חיישן זרם עירור מנוע הנעה‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E7C:["A/C Compressor Control Module Internal Temperature Sensor B Circuit","P2E7C covers the second internal temperature sensor in the control electronics of an electric A/C compressor. Their inverter sits on the housing: a Mitsubishi Heavy Industries patent places a sensor next to the power switches, Denso measures at the switches and at the motor stator, and TI's compressor inverter reference feeds IGBT temperature back for overheat protection. The maker decides what B denotes;",["Sensor B or its circuit on the compressor control board defective","Compressor controller fails to evaluate or transmit the value","Unstable 12 V supply, ground or data link to the compressor"],["A/C cools weakly or switches off","On plug-in hybrids and EVs, battery cooling and fast charging may be limited","Warning message on the climate display; MIL depends on the manufacturer"],4,0,["P2E7D","P2E7E","P2E7F","P2E80","P0D70","P0D75"],"חיישן טמפרטורה פנימית מודול בקרת מדחס מזגן‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E7D:["A/C Compressor Control Module Internal Temperature Sensor B Performance","P2E7D is the plausibility check for internal temperature sensor B of the electric A/C compressor controller: the reading is electrically in range yet conflicts with other temperatures. The test runs after a long rest, when all sensors should read alike. No manufacturer documents P2E7D.",["Sensor B drifted or poorly coupled to its measuring point","Comparison value wrong, e.g. outside air or second internal sensor faulty","Compressor still warm from recent use or preconditioning when the test ran"],["Usually no noticeable effect at first; fault stored after a cold start","Compressor may derate early or shut off on a wrong temperature","MIL on some vehicles after two drive cycles"],4,1,["P2E7C","P2E7E","P2E7F","P0D71","P0D76"],"חיישן טמפרטורה פנימית מודול בקרת מדחס מזגן‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E7E:["A/C Compressor Control Module Internal Temperature Sensor B Circuit High","P2E7E reports that internal temperature sensor B of the A/C compressor controller delivers a signal above its valid range. Most sensors of this kind produce a voltage that falls as temperature rises; TI's compressor inverter reference uses such an analog part, so a high signal stands for an impossibly cold reading.",["Sensor B path open, e.g. cracked solder joint on the board","Reference or ground of the measuring circuit lost inside the module","Analog input of the compressor controller defective"],["Compressor runs restricted or not at all","Cabin and, where present, battery cooling weaker","MIL possible after two drive cycles depending on manufacturer"],4,1,["P2E7F","P2E7C","P2E7D","P0D72","P0D77"],"חיישן טמפרטורה פנימית מודול בקרת מדחס מזגן‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E7F:["A/C Compressor Control Module Internal Temperature Sensor B Circuit Low","P2E7F is the low-signal counterpart: sensor B inside the compressor control module reports a value below its valid band, which for a sensor with falling output means an impossibly hot reading. GM's comparable code on the compressor IGBT sensor is P0D78: the 2011 Volt fails above 274 °C, the 2018 and 2019 tables above 150 °C, with the compressor detecting the condition itself and passing it on over GMLAN, Type B.",["Short circuit in the sensor B path on the control board","Measuring circuit of the compressor controller defective","Power stage genuinely overheating, e.g. low refrigerant charge"],["Compressor derates or shuts down for overheat protection","Air conditioning blows warm, battery cooling may be limited","MIL possible after two drive cycles depending on manufacturer"],4,1,["P2E7E","P2E7C","P2E7D","P0D73","P0D78"],"חיישן טמפרטורה פנימית מודול בקרת מדחס מזגן‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E80:["A/C Compressor Control Module Internal Temperature Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","With P2E80 the controller sees the reading of sensor B, a second internal thermometer in the compressor electronics, flicker: values leap or vanish for an instant and then look normal again. Set criteria for P2E80 are not published by any manufacturer. For the 2019 Volt, GM lists the IGBT counterpart P0D79 merely as a code that must be inactive before its rationality check P0D76 starts.",["Loose contact or cold solder joint in the sensor B circuit","Electrical interference from the inverter switching on the measuring line","Fluctuating 12 V supply or ground of the compressor controller"],["A/C cuts out and recovers sporadically","Fault may be stored without any noticeable effect"],4,0,["P2E7C","P2E7D","P0D74","P0D79"],"חיישן טמפרטורה פנימית מודול בקרת מדחס מזגן‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2E81:["Cold Start Engine Coolant Bypass Valve D Stuck Closed","P2E81 is the cold-start version of P26C2 for valve D, which GM uses as the block rotary valve between two mechanical end stops. Its 2025 ECM tables (25OBDG03B) count a failure when commanded and measured position differ by more than 5° while raw feedback stays below 50°, i.e. on the closed side, in 4 of 5 seconds; Type B, MIL after two trips.",["Block rotary valve stuck on the closed side (deposits, wear)","Valve actuator too weak to turn the valve when coolant is cold and thick","Chafed or corroded harness to the valve actuator","Invalid end-stop learn values after repair or battery disconnect"],["Check engine light after two trips","Engine temperature rising faster or unevenly after a cold start","Usually no driveability change"],2,1,["P2DE8","P26C2","P26C0","P2DE7","P2E82"],"שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע התנעה קרה‏ D — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2E82:["Cold Start Engine Coolant Pump Overspeed","P2E82 flags an electric main coolant pump that spins faster than requested while the cold-start warm-up strategy runs. GM's 2025 ECM tables (25OBDG03B) subtract reported from requested speed, filter the result and fail the test when it falls below −200 rpm in 8 of 10 seconds; Type B, MIL after two trips.",["Low coolant level or air trapped after service, so the impeller runs dry","Impeller loose or damaged, so the motor turns without load","Faulty pump electronics or speed feedback signal","Flow path blocked by a stuck valve, changing the pump load"],["Check engine light after two trips","Gurgling noises or weak heater output","Rising engine temperature if coolant is missing"],2,3,["P26CE","P2DE9","P2B85","P2C37","P2E81"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע התנעה קרה — מהירות יתר"],P2E83:["Fuel Rail Pressure Performance - Engine Off","P2E83 covers a fuel rail pressure check that runs once the engine is shut down: the residual pressure in the rail falls too fast, stays too high or behaves implausibly. No manufacturer documents the code publicly. For monitors active at standstill, CARB extends the driving cycle through the shutdown period until the next start.",["Injector leaking into the cylinder, so rail pressure decays too quickly","Leaking pump check valve or pressure relief valve","Rail pressure sensor with offset or drift, implausible at rest","Pressure rising after shutdown from heat soak with no way to relieve it"],["Check engine light","Long cranking or rough start after the car has stood","Possible fuel smell or smoke right after starting"],3,1,["P0087","P0088","P0191","P228C","P00C6","P053F"],""],P2E84:["Battery Charger B Input Voltage Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2E84 questions the plausibility of the grid voltage that charger B reads at its input: the sensor answers within its electrical limits, yet the figure does not suit the moment, such as a voltage with no supply connected or a value that contradicts other readings. No manufacturer documents P2E84 publicly.",["Voltage sensing inside charger B drifting or faulty","Corroded or loose AC contacts between charge inlet and charger B","Unstable or unusual supply from the charging station or house circuit","Charger software misjudging the reading"],["AC charging does not start or stops after a short time","DC fast charging still works normally","Charging fault message in the instrument cluster or app"],3,0,["P0E8B","P2E85","P2E86","P0D3E","P0E86","P0E87"],"חיישן מתח כניסת מטען סוללה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E85:["Battery Charger B Input Voltage Sensor Circuit Low","P2E85 means the input voltage signal of charger B sits too low, so the car sees little or no grid voltage while it expects AC. GM uses the code on its battery-electric models, from the 2017 Bolt EV to the Lyriq, Hummer EV, Blazer, Equinox and Silverado EV and BrightDrop vans, under the wording input voltage sensor circuit low voltage.",["DC-only NACS adapter used on an AC charger","Charging station or house circuit not delivering AC voltage","Open or high-resistance AC path between inlet and charger B","Sensing circuit inside charger B shorted to ground"],["Vehicle does not charge on a Level 1 or Level 2 AC charger","DC fast charging works without the adapter problem","Further charger codes such as P0D3F or P0F71 stored"],2,0,["P0E8B","P2E84","P2E86","P0D3F","P0E86"],"חיישן מתח כניסת מטען סוללה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E86:["Battery Charger B Input Voltage Sensor Circuit High","P2E86 flags an input voltage signal of charger B above the highest value the measurement can plausibly produce. Home sockets and AC stations stay far below that, so the fault normally lies in the sensing path or its signal line, rarely in the grid. No manufacturer documents P2E86 publicly.",["Voltage sensing circuit inside charger B faulty","Sensor signal line shorted to a supply voltage","Lost reference ground of the measurement"],["AC charging refused or ended immediately","Charging system warning in the cluster","Fault returns at once after clearing, even on a known good charger"],3,0,["P0E8B","P2E84","P2E85","P0D40","P0E87"],"חיישן מתח כניסת מטען סוללה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E87:["Proximity Detection Circuit B","P2E87 is the general fault of a second plug-detection circuit, B, whose job is to tell the vehicle that a connector is seated in an inlet. Under SAE J1772 this proximity pin is tied to earth through resistors and a switch in the latch button, so the car can lock out driving and wind down current before the plug comes out; CHAdeMO inlets have their own proximity contact for the same interlock.",["Damaged or corroded proximity contact in inlet B","Open or poorly seated connector between inlet B and the controller","Faulty charging cable or plug resistor","Evaluation circuit in the charger or control unit faulty"],["No charging through the affected inlet","Plug not recognised or vehicle reports a cable while none is fitted","Vehicle may refuse to enter drive readiness"],2,0,["P2E88","P2E89","P2E8A","P2E8B","P0D56"],""],P2E88:["Proximity Detection Circuit B Range/Performance","P2E88 flags plug sensing on circuit B whose value is electrically valid but makes no sense, typically a voltage that falls between the defined steps for no plug, plug latched and release button pressed. Those steps come from fixed resistors: J1772 uses 150 Ω plus 330 Ω once the latch is opened, and IEC 62196 cables code their current rating with values from about 100 Ω to 1.5 kΩ, each read within a tolerance band.",["Worn or dirty proximity contact raising the resistance","Charging cable or adapter with off-standard coding resistor","Moisture in inlet B creating leakage paths","Control software judging the signal wrongly"],["Charging aborts or the current is limited unexpectedly","Plug status changes without anyone touching the connector","Fault appears only with certain cables"],2,0,["P2E87","P2E89","P2E8A","P2E8B","P0D57"],""],P2E89:["Proximity Detection Circuit B Low","P2E89 stands for a voltage on proximity circuit B below the band the controller accepts in a state where no plug can be present. The rule for circuit A shows how this is judged: GM's Volt checks the line with the charge door closed or while driving out of Park and sets P0D58 below 4.2 V, in 2011 after 30 failures out of 50, in the 2019 tables after 240 out of 400 samples above 20 km/h, as a Type A code with MIL.",["Proximity line of circuit B chafed and shorted to ground","Water or dirt in inlet B bridging the contact to earth","Defective charging cable left in the inlet","Input stage in the evaluating control unit damaged"],["Message that a charging cable is connected although none is","Vehicle cannot be put into drive mode","Warning lamp, depending on manufacturer the MIL"],2,0,["P2E87","P2E88","P2E8A","P2E8B","P0D58"],""],P2E8A:["Proximity Detection Circuit B High","P2E8A is the opposite of P2E89: the proximity line of circuit B sits above the accepted band. Because the evaluating controller usually pulls the pin up to a reference such as 5 V, as described for Watt & Well's EVCC, an open wire or a missing earth path reads high just like a short to a supply.",["Broken proximity wire or unplugged connector at inlet B","Missing protective-earth path in inlet or cable","Proximity line shorted to a supply voltage","Evaluating control unit faulty"],["Charging cable on inlet B is not detected","Charging does not start on that inlet","Warning lamp, depending on manufacturer the MIL"],2,0,["P2E87","P2E88","P2E89","P2E8B","P0D59"],""],P2E8B:["Proximity Detection Circuit B Intermittent/Erratic","P2E8B describes a plug-detection signal on circuit B that drops out or jumps for moments, so the car sees a connector appear and vanish although nobody touched it. The consequences follow from the purpose of the line: under SAE J1772 the proximity state is what lets the vehicle stop drawing current before the plug is released and block driving off while connected, so a flickering signal can end charging for no…",["Loose low-voltage connector on the proximity line","Worn proximity contact in inlet B or on the cable plug","Chafed wire with intermittent contact to ground","Moisture in the inlet after rain or washing"],["Charging stops and restarts at random","Cable-connected message appears and disappears","Fault more frequent at the start or end of charging"],2,0,["P2E87","P2E88","P2E89","P2E8A","P0D5A"],""],P2E8C:["Battery Charger B Charge Sequence Signal 1 Circuit High","Charge sequence signals 1 and 2 belong to DC fast charging to CHAdeMO, used for example on the Nissan Leaf, the Mitsubishi i-MiEV and the Outlander PHEV. Signal 1 runs over connector pin 2: the station closes its switch d1 and applies 12 V to the line, which tells the car it is ready and starts the CAN dialogue.",["Sequence signal 1 line shorted to a 12 V source","Moisture or debris in the DC inlet bridging pins","Faulty input stage in the evaluating control unit","Station switch d1 not opening at the end of a session"],["DC fast charging refused or ending with an error","AC charging continues to work","Charging fault message in the cluster"],2,0,["P2E8D","P2E8E","P2E8F","P2E87"],"אות רצף טעינת מטען סוללה‏ B 1 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E8D:["Battery Charger B Charge Sequence Signal 1 Circuit Low","P2E8D means the vehicle finds the first CHAdeMO sequence line low while the fast charger should be driving it. Signal 1 is the opening move of a session: once the plug is detected the station closes d1 and applies 12 V, and only after that does the CAN exchange of battery limits begin. If the vehicle side sees no voltage, the session stalls before any current flows.",["Sequence signal 1 line shorted to ground","Open wire or damaged pin 2 in the DC inlet","Fast charger not closing its switch d1","Faulty input stage in the evaluating control unit"],["DC fast charging does not start","Station reports a communication or vehicle error","AC charging unaffected"],2,0,["P2E8C","P2E8E","P2E8F"],"אות רצף טעינת מטען סוללה‏ B 1 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E8E:["Battery Charger B Charge Sequence Signal 2 Circuit High","P2E8E concerns the second CHAdeMO sequence line, which works differently from the first: the station closes switch d2 to tie the line to ground, completing the circuit that sequence signal 1 feeds, and only then may the vehicle close its high-voltage contactors. Before that the connector has been latched and the vehicle has given charge permission.",["Open wire or damaged pin 10 in the DC inlet","Fast charger switch d2 not closing","Sequence signal 2 line shorted to a supply voltage","Faulty input stage in the evaluating control unit"],["DC session stops after insulation test without current flowing","Station shows a vehicle-side error","AC charging still possible"],2,0,["P2E8F","P2E8C","P2E8D"],"אות רצף טעינת מטען סוללה‏ B 2 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E8F:["Battery Charger B Charge Sequence Signal 2 Circuit Low","P2E8F reports the second CHAdeMO sequence line pulled low at a time it should be released. Because the station uses d2 to connect this line to ground as the very last step before the vehicle closes its contactors, and opens d2 first when the session ends, a line already at ground early, or still at ground once d2 is open, contradicts the sequence.",["Sequence signal 2 line shorted to ground","Fast charger switch d2 stuck closed","Water or dirt in the DC inlet","Faulty input stage in the evaluating control unit"],["DC fast charging refused right after plugging in","Session ends with an error instead of a normal stop","AC charging unaffected"],2,0,["P2E8E","P2E8C","P2E8D"],"אות רצף טעינת מטען סוללה‏ B 2 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E90:["Battery Charger A Internal Power Supply Performance","P2E90 says the internal power supply of charger A, the rails that feed its control and gate-driver electronics, does not behave as intended. Kia uses the code: technical bulletin ELE409 (service action SA639, December 2025) covers 2025 EV6 and 2026 EV9 built between 21 February and 18 September 2025 that store P2E9092, performance or incorrect operation, and can no longer charge on Level 1 or 2;",["Internal supply stage of charger A or the ICCU failed","Weak 12 V feed or loose low-voltage connector at the charger","Charger software fault"],["No AC charging at home or on Level 2 stations","DC fast charging may still work","Charging system warning in the cluster"],4,0,["P2E91","P0D67","P0E5E","P2E2C"],"אספקת מתח פנימית מטען סוללה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E91:["Battery Charger B Internal Power Supply Performance","P2E91 is the same verdict for charger B: one of its internally generated supply voltages is wrong, so the charger cannot run its power stages safely. Polestar uses the code on the Polestar 3, whose grid-to-high-voltage converter GHCA reports as charger B.",["Internal supply stage of charger B failed","Loose low-voltage connector or weak 12 V feed at charger B","Charger software fault"],["AC charging fails while DC fast charging still works","Charging time much longer or charging stops early","Charging socket light signals a fault"],4,0,["P2E90","P2E2F","P0E8B","P2DB7"],"אספקת מתח פנימית מטען סוללה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2E92:["Charge Port Door B Open Request Switch Wake-Up Circuit","P2E92 concerns cars with a second electrically opened charge door. Its open-request switch or sensor must be able to rouse sleeping control units, so besides its normal signal it drives a wake-up line, and P2E92 records that the two disagree. Porsche's Taycan campaign WLK2 shows the naming, door A at the driver and door B at the passenger side, both opened by a hand gesture over a sensor;",["Open or shorted wake-up wire between switch and control unit","Worn switch or sensor at door B giving mismatched signals","Water ingress or corrosion at the door B connector","Wake-up input of the control unit faulty"],["Charge door B does not open on request every time","Door opens only from the screen or the other side works normally","Increased standby drain if the line keeps waking modules"],2,0,["P0CC6","P2E93","P2E94","P2E98"],""],P2E93:["Charge Port Door B Open Request Switch Circuit","P2E93 is the basic circuit fault of the input with which the driver asks the second charge flap to open. On cars with a flap on each side this input is usually a touch or wipe sensor on the flap itself: Porsche's Taycan and Cayenne Electric open each flap when a hand passes over a sensor area at its rear, and Porsche's WLK2 parts list calls the passenger-side flap door B. No manufacturer documents P2E93 publicly.",["Touch or wipe sensor of flap B with a wrong internal resistance","Partly broken or corroded signal wire to the flap B sensor","Moisture in the connector at the flap module","Faulty input stage in the control unit reading the sensor"],["Charge flap B does not react to touch or hand gesture","Flap B still opens via the central display or app","Charging flap warning in the instrument cluster"],2,0,["P2E92","P2E94","P2E95","P2E96","P2E97","P0CC7"],""],P2E94:["Charge Port Door B Open Request Switch Circuit Performance","With P2E94 the open request input of charge flap B is electrically sound, yet its behaviour cannot be right, for example a request that stays active for far too long. Audi describes exactly this pattern for the Q6 e-tron in bulletin 2076776/1: tension in the left or right flap module can deform the flap so that it sinks into the body and the button inside the module stays pressed;",["Deformed or recessed flap B keeping the request button pressed","Sensor of flap B shifted or not seated correctly","Ice or dirt acting on the sensor area"],["Flap B cannot be opened from outside","Opening via the display or charging menu still works","Flap B sits deeper than the surrounding body panel"],2,0,["P2E93","P2E95","P2E96","P2E97","P0CC8"],""],P2E95:["Charge Port Door B Open Request Switch Circuit Low","P2E95 says the request signal from charge flap B has dropped under the bottom of its permitted range. Usual reasons are a signal wire touching ground, water bridging the connector pins or an internally shorted sensor. Depending on the wiring, the control unit may take this as a button held down all the time. No manufacturer documents P2E95 publicly.",["Signal wire of the flap B sensor shorted to ground","Water in the flap B connector bridging the contacts","Request sensor of flap B failed short internally"],["Flap B does not open on touch, or only with the manual release","Control unit may stay awake longer, raising standby drain","Charging flap warning displayed"],2,0,["P2E93","P2E94","P2E96","P2E97","P0CC9"],""],P2E96:["Charge Port Door B Open Request Switch Circuit High","P2E96 is stored when the request signal of charge flap B climbs past the top of its permitted range. Contact with a 12 V supply raises it, and so does a broken sensor ground or switch path that lets a pulled-up input float. The control unit then usually sees a request that never arrives. No manufacturer documents P2E96 publicly.",["Sensor signal wire shorted to a 12 V supply","Interrupted ground or switch path at the flap B sensor","Pushed-back or loose pin in the flap module connector"],["Flap B never reacts to the hand or touch","Opening from the centre console or display still works","Warning that the charging flap is impaired"],2,0,["P2E93","P2E94","P2E95","P2E97","P0CCA"],""],P2E97:["Charge Port Door B Open Request Switch Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2E97 points to a request signal from charge flap B that briefly vanishes or jumps, while no permanent fault can be found. A real case with the same sensor type comes from Porsche: on the Macan Electric of model years 2023 to 2025 the optional electric flaps open when a flat hand rests on the rear third, and bulletin WRP7 explains that production tolerances could make the gesture go undetected now and then;",["Sensor on flap B not held firmly, adhesive strip loosened","Loose terminal in the flap B connector","Harness to flap B damaged by repeated movement"],["Flap B opens only on some attempts","Code stored without a lasting fault in the workshop"],2,0,["P2E93","P2E94","P2E95","P2E96","P0CCB"],""],P2E98:["Charge Port Door B Position Sensor Circuit","P2E98 is the general circuit code for the sensor that reports whether charge flap B is open or shut. Mercedes-Benz documents it: in its plug-in hybrids the separate DC charging socket has its own flap, and information LI47.70-P-078563 lists P2E9873 for a supposed electrical fault of that flap's position sensor, stored in the DC charge-connection unit N116/5 and the powertrain controller, with the MIL lit and the…",["Software fault in the DC charging unit reporting a false sensor fault (Mercedes)","Position sensor of flap B with a wrong internal resistance","Damaged wire or connector between sensor and control unit"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on, charging and starting normal (Mercedes)","Flap B may stay shut or show a wrong status"],4,1,["P2E99","P2E9A","P2E9B","P2E9C","P2E9D","P0CCC"],"חיישן מצב דלת פתח טעינה‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2E99:["Charge Port Door B Position Sensor Circuit Performance","P2E99 means the position signal of charge flap B is within its electrical limits yet contradicts what the flap is doing, for instance closed although the flap was just opened. On cars with two flaps such an error has side effects, because the flaps lock each other: Porsche found on the 2020 Taycan that a bad sensor signal led to a wrong end-position decision, which then blocked the flap on the other side, and…",["Position sensor or its harness giving a wrong end-position signal","Oxidation or particles in the flap actuator that houses the detection","Software misreading the flap state at start-up"],["Message asking to close a charging flap although both are closed","Opposite flap A locked and not operable","Charging refused"],4,0,["P2E98","P2E9A","P2E9B","P2E9C","P2E9E","P0CCD"],"חיישן מצב דלת פתח טעינה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2E9A:["Charge Port Door B Position Sensor Circuit Low","P2E9A reports that the flap B position signal has fallen under its lowest valid value. A signal wire chafed against ground, water in the connector or an internally shorted sensor are the usual reasons. Tesla's latch patent shows a common build in which a reed or Hall element inside the latch senses a magnet disc on the door, so the signal follows the gap between them. No manufacturer documents P2E9A publicly.",["Position signal wire of flap B shorted to ground","Water in the sensor connector at flap B","Position sensor failed short internally"],["Flap B status in the display does not change","Charging blocked or charging flap warning"],2,0,["P2E98","P2E99","P2E9B","P2E9C","P0CCE"],"חיישן מצב דלת פתח טעינה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2E9B:["Charge Port Door B Position Sensor Circuit High","P2E9B is the high-side position fault of charge flap B: the reading lies above anything a working sensor can deliver. A signal wire touching 12 V, or a missing sensor ground, letting the input drift upwards, are typical explanations. No manufacturer documents P2E9B publicly.",["Position signal wire shorted to a 12 V feed","Broken ground wire of the flap B position sensor","Corroded or loose connector at the flap module"],["Permanent message that a charging flap is open","Charging not possible on either side"],2,0,["P2E98","P2E99","P2E9A","P2E9C","P0CCF"],"חיישן מצב דלת פתח טעינה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2E9C:["Charge Port Door B Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2E9C covers a flap B position signal that flickers or drops out briefly instead of failing for good. Common sources are loose terminals, a harness bent at every flap movement, or a sensor sitting loose in its holder. No manufacturer documents P2E9C publicly. Two official cases show how fragile this signal path can be on two-flap cars.",["Loose terminal in the position sensor connector","Harness to flap B strained or chafed by flap movement","Oxidation or particles in the flap actuator with integrated detection"],["Flap status in the display switches without reason","Sporadic charging flap warnings or interrupted charging"],2,0,["P2E98","P2E99","P2E9A","P2E9B","P0CD0"],"חיישן מצב דלת פתח טעינה‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2E9D:["Charge Port Door B Unlock Control Circuit","P2E9D concerns the output that releases or drives charge flap B, not its sensors. Depending on the design this is a latch actuator or a small motor: Audi's e-tron family uses lock actuators F496 and F497 for its high-voltage charging flaps on the two sides, and Porsche's Taycan a servo motor per charge port door. No manufacturer documents P2E9D publicly.",["Flap B actuator or motor winding open or shorted","Damaged control wire or connector to the flap B actuator","Faulty output stage in the control unit"],["Flap B does not unlock or move at all","Charging only possible on the other side","Charging flap warning in the cluster"],2,0,["P2E9E","P2E9F","P2EA0","P2E98","P0CD1"],""],P2E9E:["Charge Port Door B Unlock Control Circuit Performance","P2E9E is a function check: the control unit commands flap B to unlock and then expects the position sensor to confirm an open flap. GM's tables for the A flap of the Volt set P0CD2 when that report is missing after 5 seconds (2011) or 13 seconds (2013, only above minus 12 °C), skip the test while position or output codes are active, and use Type B.",["Flap B lock actuator or motor gears broken, often after force on the flap","Flap B frozen, dirty or binding in its housing","Software sequencing error between the two flaps","Position sensor not reporting the opened flap"],["Flap B pops slightly or rocks but does not open fully","Flap B moves freely by hand because the actuator is broken","Charging flap warning, charging only on the other side"],2,0,["P2E9D","P2E9F","P2EA0","P2E99","P0CD2"],""],P2E9F:["Charge Port Door B Unlock Control Circuit Low","P2E9F is the low-voltage form of the flap B release output fault: the driver stage measures its control line close to 0 V where a higher level is expected. A control wire chafed to body ground or an actuator winding that has shorted are the usual culprits, and a protective fuse or driver shutdown can follow. No manufacturer documents P2E9F publicly.",["Control wire of the flap B actuator shorted to ground","Shorted winding in the flap B actuator or motor","Water in the actuator connector"],["Flap B does not release on any request","Blown fuse for the flap circuit possible"],2,0,["P2E9D","P2E9E","P2EA0","P0CD3"],""],P2EA0:["Charge Port Door B Unlock Control Circuit High","P2EA0 marks the opposite case at the flap B release output: the line sits at a high voltage while the driver stage should be pulling it down or keeping it off. Contact with a 12 V circuit does this, and on low-side switched outputs an interrupted actuator or wire gives the same reading. No manufacturer documents P2EA0 publicly.",["Control wire of the flap B actuator shorted to 12 V","Open actuator winding or broken wire on a low-side driven output","Output stage in the control unit stuck on"],["Flap B never releases, only the manual release helps","Actuator may run warm if powered permanently"],2,0,["P2E9D","P2E9E","P2E9F","P0CD4"],""],P2EA1:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Bank 1 Sensor 6","P2EA1 is the general electrical fault of a sixth exhaust temperature probe on bank 1, counting from the engine towards the tailpipe. No manufacturer documents this code publicly: the diesel tables that are published stop at probe 5, which GM's 2025 table 25OBDG04A places behind the particulate filter.",["Corroded or heat-damaged plug of the sixth probe near the exhaust","Probe lead or internal wire broken by exhaust vibration","Harness chafed or melted along the aftertreatment","Faulty input stage or temperature evaluation module"],["Check engine lamp on","Particulate filter regeneration delayed or blocked","Live data for probe 6 missing or jumping"],2,1,["P2EA2","P2EA3","P2EA5","P2480","P2484"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1, חיישן 6)"],P2EA2:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit High Bank 1 Sensor 6","P2EA2 says the signal of the sixth bank 1 exhaust probe sits above its upper electrical limit. Which temperature that implies depends on the element. Most probes form a voltage divider with a pull-up resistor in the module; an open lead then drives the input to the reference, which an NTC part reads as extreme cold and a platinum (PTC) part as extreme heat.",["Open signal or ground lead, or connector not latched","Probe element burnt open after overheating or vibration","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage"],["Check engine lamp, often after a single trip","Probe 6 shows an impossible extreme value in live data","Filter regeneration or SCR dosing restricted"],2,1,["P2EA1","P2EA3","P2EA5","P2482"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 6)"],P2EA3:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Low Bank 1 Sensor 6","With P2EA3 the input of the sixth bank 1 exhaust probe drops below the lowest value a healthy circuit can deliver. Electrically this is nearly always a short: the signal wire touching ground or the exhaust, or an element whose insulation has broken down. What the module displays differs by type, as Hella explains for divider circuits: a shorted NTC probe looks red hot, a shorted platinum (PTC) probe looks frozen.",["Signal wire chafed through to ground or to the exhaust pipe","Probe with internal short after thermal or mechanical damage","Water or road salt bridging the connector pins"],["Check engine lamp after the second faulty trip","Probe 6 reads far too hot or far too cold depending on type","Regeneration or SCR dosing held back"],2,1,["P2EA1","P2EA2","P2EA5","P2481"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 6)"],P2EA5:["Exhaust Gas Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1 Sensor 6","P2EA5 is the plausibility fault of the sixth bank 1 exhaust probe: the voltage is electrically valid, yet the temperature does not match what the exhaust is doing. California's rule 13 CCR 1968.2, section (e)(15.2.1), like §1971.1 for heavy-duty engines, asks for two-sided rationality checks and names exhaust temperature sensors that steer a catalyst temperature strategy. No manufacturer publishes P2EA5.",["Probe loose or pulled from its boss after exhaust work","Drifting element or soot-coated tip reacting too slowly","Neighbouring probes swapped at their connectors","Contact resistance in the connector shifting the reading"],["Check engine lamp after two trips","Probe 6 stays flat or lags while other probes heat up","Regeneration interrupted or not started"],2,1,["P2EA1","P2EA2","P2EA3","P2483"],"חיישן טמפרטורת גזי פליטה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 6)"],P2EA6:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit","P2EA6 is the general circuit fault of the temperature sensor in the charge pipe between the turbo compressor and the charge air cooler. Squeezing the air heats it a lot; Cummins notes in patent US6401457 that excessive outlet temperature can melt the compressor housing or harm the wheel, and still estimated the value in 2001 because no series sensor lasted there.",["Loose or corroded connector on the charge pipe sensor","Wire breaking intermittently near the hot turbocharger","Sensor element failing internally","Faulty input in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Compressor outlet temperature missing or jumping in live data","Boost limitation at high load possibly less refined"],2,1,["P2EC0","P2EC1","P2EC2","P2B6E"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2EA7:["DC/AC Converter A Input Voltage Too Low","A DC/AC converter turns direct current into household AC for sockets in the vehicle. P2EA7 means the DC voltage reaching converter A is below the range in which it is allowed to run. Which supply that is depends on the design: Toyota Industries' patent US10050558 describes a 12 V-fed unit that only works between about 11 and 16 V, pauses its output when a weak or aged battery pulls the input down and restarts on its…",["Weak, discharged or aged 12 V battery","Voltage drop at the supply fuse, cable or ground point of the converter","Hybrid high-voltage supply restricted, for example at very low state of charge","Faulty input voltage measurement inside the converter"],["AC sockets in the vehicle deliver no power or cut out","Message about the power outlet or inverter in the cluster","Problem appears mainly with engine off or at low battery charge"],2,0,["P2EA8","P2EA9","P2DA8","P0364","U0288"],"מתח כניסת ממיר DC/AC‏ A — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2EA8:["DC/AC Converter A Input Voltage Too High","P2EA8 is the reverse of P2EA7: the DC input of converter A lies above its permitted window. In the 12 V design of Toyota Industries' patent US10050558 the inverter stops once the battery side exceeds about 16 V, for example after a jump start from a 24 V source or with a failed alternator regulator.",["Charging system overvoltage from a faulty alternator regulator or DC/DC converter","Jump start or charging with too high a voltage","Faulty input voltage measurement inside the converter"],["AC sockets switch off and stay off until a restart","Other overvoltage messages or flickering lights"],2,0,["P2EA7","P2EA9","P0563","U0288"],"מתח כניסת ממיר DC/AC‏ A — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2EA9:["DC/AC Converter A Over Temperature","P2EA9 reports that converter A has become too hot. The converter watches the power devices that switch and invert the current – MOSFETs, diodes and transistors – and in Toyota Industries' patent US10050558 it stops once their temperature passes a set limit, then waits for a manual reset, the same handling as an input overvoltage.",["Long operation near the rated power","Cooling air path blocked or cooling fan failed","High temperature at the mounting location","Faulty temperature sensing or power stage in the converter"],["AC sockets switch off under load","Output only returns after cooling and a restart"],2,0,["P2EA7","P2EA8","P2DA8","U0288"],"ממיר DC/AC‏ A — חום יתר"],P2EAA:["Active Radiator Air Flow Control Module A Control Circuit Performance","The active radiator air flow system meters cooling air with motor-driven flaps between bumper opening and radiator; J2012 keeps its control module apart from the grille shutter modules (P05C0, U0284). Hyundai and Kia's patent US11225900 shows such a system with two flap zones, each moved by its own actuator according to vehicle speed, outside and coolant temperature and refrigerant pressure.",["Corroded or loose connector in the exposed front-end area","Supply or ground of the module outside its range","Internal fault in control module A"],["Check engine lamp on, where the maker assigns a MIL","Flaps stay in one position","Slower warm-up or slightly higher fuel consumption"],2,1,["P2EAB","P2EAC","U02C0","U05C1","P05A3"],"מודול בקרת זרימת אוויר רדיאטור פעיל‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2EAB:["Active Radiator Air Flow Control Module A Over Temperature","P2EAB means module A of the active radiator air flow system reports that its own electronics have overheated. Such smart actuators carry their motor driver on board and protect it: J2012 records the matching case for the grille shutter as P05C0, where the actuator switches its output stage off when the chip runs too hot.",["Flaps blocked by ice, dirt or a damaged linkage, motor overloaded","High heat at the mounting place near the radiator","Internal fault in the module or its temperature sensing"],["Check engine lamp on, where the maker assigns a MIL","Flaps stop moving for a while","Higher coolant temperature under load if the flaps are stuck closed"],2,1,["P2EAA","P2EAC","U02C0","P05C0"],"מודול בקרת זרימת אוויר רדיאטור פעיל‏ A — חום יתר"],P2EAC:["Active Radiator Air Flow Control Module A Performance","P2EAC is the general performance fault of module A: the module can be reached, but the flap system does not do what it is told. GM's check of the comparable smart shutter actuator on the 3.0 L diesel LZ0 shows the approach: a gap of more than 5 % between commanded and reported position starts repeated attempts to free the flaps, and only after a calibrated number of failed retries is the fault confirmed, type B with…",["Flaps frozen or blocked by debris","Broken or detached flap linkage","Worn gearbox or motor in the actuator"],["Check engine lamp on, where the maker assigns a MIL","Flaps do not open or close, sometimes only in frost","Warmer engine under load or slower warm-up"],2,1,["P2EAA","P2EAB","U02C0","P059F"],"מודול בקרת זרימת אוויר רדיאטור פעיל‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2EAD:["Reductant Metering Unit 2 Performance","Some diesels dose DEF at two points, each with its own metering unit or injector. P2EAD means the second one no longer delivers what it should. GM documents it for the 3.0 L Duramax LZ0, where its table calls it injector 2 performance with low consumption: the control unit compares the pressure drop expected while the second injector doses with what it measures and builds a correction factor;",["Second DEF injector crusted or partly blocked by urea crystals","Kinked, frozen or blocked line to the second injector","Engine control software needing an update (GM LZ0 2023)","Weak DEF pump or pressure sensor deviation"],["Check engine lamp on","DEF warning and, if not repaired, speed limitation","Higher NOx emissions"],3,3,["P20FE","P2EAE","P2EAF","P2053"],"יחידת מינון אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ 2 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2EAE:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1 Unit 2","P2EAE concerns the second DEF injector on bank 1. Open, low and high circuit faults have their own codes, P2053 to P2055; here the circuit works, yet its signal does not fit a properly moving valve.",["Armature of the second injector sticking from urea crystals","Corroded contacts distorting the current trace","Injector coil with changed characteristics"],["Check engine lamp on","DEF system warning","Higher NOx emissions"],2,3,["P2EB9","P2EAF","P2053","P2054","P2055","P202E"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2EAF:["Reductant Injection Valve Stuck Closed Bank 1 Unit 2","P2EAF means the second DEF injector on bank 1 stays shut although it is commanded open, so the SCR stage it serves gets no reductant. It is the unit 2 counterpart of P208E. Control units spot the case in two ways. One looks at the coil current: when the armature lifts, the trace shows a small kink, and Delphi's patent US11280245 describes finding it even with chopped drive voltage.",["Needle held by crystallised DEF","Corrosion inside the injector after poor fluid or long standstill","Blocked or frozen supply line to the second injector"],["Check engine lamp on","DEF warning with countdown to speed limitation","Higher NOx emissions"],2,3,["P208E","P2EAE","P2EAD","P2053"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקוע במצב סגור (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2EB0:["Throttle Valve Intake Air Pressure Sensor Circuit","P2EB0 concerns the sensor that measures air pressure at the inlet of the throttle valve, i.e. between charger or air filter and throttle. On turbo engines this is the reading Ford calls TIP and GM TIAP; both makers, however, report faults of that sensor under the boost sensor codes P0236–P0238, and no manufacturer documents P2EB0 publicly.",["Loose, corroded or oil-wetted connector at the sensor","Intermittent break in signal, reference or ground wire","Failed sensor electronics, e.g. SENT output"],["Check engine lamp on","Reduced boost or hesitant acceleration if a substitute value is used","Other air system checks such as the PCV monitor may not run"],1,3,["P2EB1","P2EB2","P2EB3","P0235"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר יניקה שסתום מצערת — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2EB1:["Throttle Valve Intake Air Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P2EB1 says the pressure signal at the throttle inlet is below the lowest valid voltage. These sensors are linear: Ford's transfer curve gives about 0.4 V at 20 kPa and 4.5 V at 300 kPa, so a low voltage reads as an absurdly low pressure. A missing 5 V reference, a signal shorted to ground or a failed sensor are the usual causes. No manufacturer documents P2EB1;",["5 V reference open or shorted, often shared with other sensors","Signal wire shorted to ground","Pressure sensor failed"],["Check engine lamp, often after the first trip","Noticeable loss of power under load","Pressure reading far below ambient in live data"],1,3,["P2EB0","P2EB2","P2EB3","P0237"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר יניקה שסתום מצערת — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2EB2:["Throttle Valve Intake Air Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P2EB2 is stored when the throttle inlet pressure signal exceeds its upper limit. Since voltage climbs with pressure, the module would read a boost no charger can deliver. Electrically this points to a signal wire touching the 5 V reference or battery voltage, or to an open sensor ground that lets the output float up. No manufacturer documents P2EB2 publicly.",["Open sensor ground or corroded ground pin","Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Pressure sensor failed high"],["Check engine lamp, often after the first trip","Boost limited, sluggish response","Pressure reading far above ambient with the engine off"],1,3,["P2EB0","P2EB1","P2EB3","P0238"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר יניקה שסתום מצערת — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2EB3:["Throttle Valve Intake Air Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2EB3 covers a throttle inlet pressure that is electrically fine but wrong. With the engine stopped, the pressure ahead of the throttle must equal manifold and barometric pressure; Ford checks this at key-up after at least 10 s off, allowing about 2.7 inHg between boost and manifold sensor. While running, GM compares its TIAP reading with an airflow model and fails it if the gap exceeds 30 kPa, reported as P0236.",["Sensor offset or drift with age","Pressure port blocked by oil residue or ice","Leak in the charge air path upsetting the model comparison","Contact resistance in the connector"],["Check engine lamp on","Pressure reading differs from manifold and barometric pressure with engine off","Uneven boost or reduced power"],2,3,["P2EB0","P2EB1","P2EB2","P0236","P2227"],"חיישן לחץ אוויר יניקה שסתום מצערת — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2EB4:["Hybrid/EV Battery Inductive Charger High Voltage Interlock Circuit/Open","With inductive charging, the vehicle coil picks up high-frequency power from a ground pad and an on-board rectifier turns it into DC for the traction battery; SAE J2954 defines classes up to 11 kW around 85 kHz. Because this path carries high voltage, its plugs and covers sit in a high voltage interlock loop, a low-voltage signal wire that breaks as soon as a connector is pulled or a lid removed.",["HV connector or cover of the charger not fully latched","Bent or pushed-back interlock pin","Broken or chafed interlock wire","Fault in the interlock evaluation of the module"],["Inductive charging does not start or stops","Charging fault message"],4,0,["P2D35","P2D33","P0D15","P0A0A"],"נעילת בטיחות מתח גבוה מטען אינדוקטיבי סוללת מתח גבוה — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2EB5:["Hybrid/EV Battery Inductive Charger Input Voltage Low","P2EB5 reports that the input of the inductive charger receives too little voltage during power transfer. That input is the AC the vehicle coil collects from the ground pad across the air gap, so the level depends on alignment, gap and the power sent by the ground side. For its reference coil SAE J2954 allows vertical gaps of up to about 250 mm and a sideways offset of up to 100 mm.",["Vehicle not parked accurately over the ground pad","Object or ice between ground pad and vehicle coil","Ground unit delivering too little power","Faulty input voltage measurement in the charger"],["Inductive charging slow or interrupted","Charging fault message"],4,0,["P2EB6","P2D37","P2D36","P2D33"],"כניסת מטען אינדוקטיבי סוללת מתח גבוה — מתח נמוך"],P2EB6:["Hybrid/EV Battery Inductive Charger Input Voltage High","P2EB6 is the counterpart to P2EB5: the voltage at the input of the inductive charger is higher than its electronics accept. Too much induced voltage can stem from a ground unit sending more power than requested, a ride height that shifts the coupling, for example when the vehicle is loaded or unloaded during charging, or a control loop between both sides that has lost step.",["Ground unit sending more power than requested","Coupling changed by ride height or position during charging","Disturbed communication between vehicle and ground unit","Faulty input voltage measurement in the charger"],["Inductive charging stops shortly after starting","Charging fault message"],4,0,["P2EB5","P2D37","P2D36","P2D33"],"כניסת מטען אינדוקטיבי סוללת מתח גבוה — מתח גבוה"],P2EB7:["Replace 12V Battery","P2EB7 is a request rather than a classic fault: the vehicle considers its 12 V battery due for replacement. Energy management judges battery condition through a sensor or a battery with its own electronics on the LIN bus; HELLA's intelligent battery sensor, for example, measures voltage, current and temperature and works out state of charge, health and function.",["12 V battery worn, low remaining capacity","Brief LIN communication fault with the battery module (Bentley 2025)","New battery fitted but not registered or of the wrong type","Faulty battery sensor"],["Code stored without warning lamp","Possibly weak starting or reduced start-stop operation"],1,0,["P0562","P0563"],""],P2EB9:["Reductant Injection Valve Circuit Range/Performance Bank 2 Unit 2","P2EB9 is the bank 2 twin of P2EAE: the circuit of the second DEF injector on the second exhaust bank works electrically, but its signal does not match a valve that opens and closes as it should. Bank 2 implies a separate exhaust line for the second cylinder bank, and unit 2 a further dosing point on that line. No manufacturer documents P2EB9 publicly.",["Armature sticking from urea crystals","Corroded contacts distorting the current trace","Injector coil with changed characteristics"],["Check engine lamp on","DEF system warning","Higher NOx emissions"],2,3,["P2EAE","P2056","P2057","P2058","P201A"],"שסתום הזרקת אוריאה (AdBlue) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P2EBB:["Crankcase Temperature Sensor Circuit","P2EBB is the general circuit fault of a sensor that reports the temperature inside the crankcase, i.e. of the blow-by gas or the space above the oil. Patents show what engines do with it: Ford (US9228557) feeds exhaust-heated air into the crankcase, checks the arrival with such a sensor and stores a code, possibly with MIL, if the reading stays below the expected value;",["Connector loose or contaminated with engine oil","Harness wire breaking intermittently on the engine block","Sensor element failed internally"],["Check engine lamp on","Crankcase temperature missing or jumping in live data","No noticeable change in how the engine runs"],1,1,["P2EBC","P2EBD","P2EBE","P04DB"],"חיישן טמפרטורת בית גל הארכובה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2EBC:["Crankcase Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2EBC means the crankcase temperature sensor delivers an electrically valid value that does not suit the engine state: it may stick, react too slowly or sit far from the coolant and oil temperatures after a long stop. The CARB rule 13 CCR 1968.2 calls in (e)(15.2.1) for rationality checks that catch readings that are wrongly high as well as wrongly low.",["Sensor drifted or slow because of sludge or oil coking on the tip","Contact resistance in the connector shifting the value","Replacement sensor with a different characteristic fitted"],["Check engine lamp after the fault is confirmed","Crankcase reading disagrees with oil and coolant temperature on a cold start","Crankcase ventilation checks may not complete"],1,1,["P2EBB","P2EBD","P2EBE","P0196"],"חיישן טמפרטורת בית גל הארכובה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2EBD:["Crankcase Temperature Sensor Circuit High","P2EBD is set when the crankcase temperature signal rises above its highest valid voltage. With the usual pull-up arrangement this happens when the current path through the sensor is interrupted, for example by an unplugged or oil-soaked connector, a broken wire or an open element, or when the signal touches the 5 V reference or battery voltage.",["Connector unplugged, oil-soaked or with spread terminals","Signal or ground wire broken","Sensor element open circuit","Signal shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage"],["Check engine lamp on","Crankcase temperature fixed at an extreme value","Engine runs normally"],1,1,["P2EBB","P2EBC","P2EBE"],"חיישן טמפרטורת בית גל הארכובה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2EBE:["Crankcase Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","P2EBE reports a crankcase temperature signal below the lowest voltage the circuit can produce when intact. In practice a short is behind it: either the signal lead has rubbed through to ground on the engine block, or the insulation inside the sensor has given way, for instance after oil has crept into the housing.",["Signal wire chafed through to ground on the engine","Sensor shorted internally after oil ingress","Faulty input stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine lamp on","Live data shows an implausible crankcase temperature","Crankcase heating or ventilation checks suspended"],1,1,["P2EBB","P2EBC","P2EBD"],"חיישן טמפרטורת בית גל הארכובה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2EBF:["Battery Charging Mode Switch Stuck","P2EBF reports that the control used to select a battery charging mode stays in one state, most likely a button that reads as permanently pressed. On plug-in hybrids such a control makes the engine recharge the traction battery while driving: Mitsubishi's Outlander PHEV had a separate Battery Charge (CHRG) switch that runs the engine until about 80 percent state of charge, and the 2026 model reaches the same mode…",["Button mechanically jammed or contact welded in the pressed state","Spilled liquid or dirt in the console switch panel","Short in the switch signal wire imitating a held button"],["Engine keeps running to charge the traction battery","Charging mode cannot be switched on or off","Higher fuel use and less electric driving"],2,1,["P0E60","P05D0","P05D3"],"מתג מצב טעינת סוללה — תקוע"],P2EC0:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","P2EC0 reports that the compressor outlet temperature signal has fallen under the lowest valid voltage. Air temperature sensors on the intake side are usually NTC thermistors, as Bosch states for its combined boost pressure and temperature sensor; their resistance shrinks as they warm, so a signal pulled towards ground is read as extreme heat.",["Signal wire shorted to ground, e.g. chafed on the charge pipe","Sensor shorted internally","Oil or moisture bridging the connector pins"],["Check engine lamp on","Live data shows an implausibly hot charge air temperature","Possible loss of power if a substitute value limits boost"],1,1,["P2EA6","P2EC1","P2EC2","P2B6F"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2EC1:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit High","P2EC1 is set when the compressor outlet temperature sensor delivers a voltage above its permitted window. Because the module feeds the sensor through a pull-up resistor, any break in the current path lifts the input to the reference: an unplugged or corroded connector, a cracked wire or a burnt-out element. A short to 5 V or battery voltage has the same effect.",["Connector unplugged, corroded or with spread terminals","Signal or ground wire broken","Sensor element open circuit","Signal shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage"],["Check engine lamp on","Live data shows a fixed extreme value","Usually no noticeable change in driving"],1,1,["P2EA6","P2EC0","P2EC2","P2B70"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2EC2:["Turbocharger Compressor Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2EC2 flags a compressor outlet temperature that is electrically valid but does not fit the operating point. A reference is easy to build: Cummins (US6401457) derives the outlet temperature from inlet temperature and pressure, turbo speed, air mass and pressure ratio, and after a long soak the sensor should also agree with intake and ambient readings.",["Sensor drifted or reacting too slowly","Tip coated with oil from crankcase or turbo seals","Sensor loose or not reaching into the air stream","Contact resistance at the connector"],["Check engine lamp after the fault is confirmed","Reading disagrees with intake and ambient temperature after a cold soak","Charge air cooler diagnosis may be suspended"],2,1,["P2EA6","P2EC0","P2EC1","P2B71","P026A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מדחס מגדש טורבו — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"]};export{e as default};
